window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6501,"title":"Chapter 6501: Chapter 6499: Looks Like We Have Escaped","paragraphs":["Chapter 6499: Looks Like We Have Escaped","“What should we do? Are you still going to enter?” Eggy didn’t want to proceed any further.","“We’re already here. Let’s take a look. My heart will feel uneasy if I don’t give it my all,” Chu Feng replied as he ventured into the lair.","The true dragon’s aura was overwhelmingly powerful, but fortunately, it didn’t exert its oppressive might. Otherwise, Chu Feng would have struggled to have taken even a step forward.","Chu Feng proceeded carefully despite having thoroughly concealed himself. He was not confident that his concealment means would work against an expert of this caliber.","Fortunately, after he ventured some distance in, he heard snoring sounds.","The true dragon appeared to be asleep. Chu Feng saw a glimmer of hope.","He ventured further in, and the snores got even louder. Even the lair began to shake.","Some time later, he finally encountered the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness. It was shaped like a dragon and spanned a hundred meters long, but it was a translucent soul entity that emanated a faint light.","It laid in the center of the lair, coiled around a gleaming, golden orb. The orb emanated a powerful dragon aura, and it seemed to harness special powers.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness, despite being asleep, would instinctively sniff the orb now and then.","Soon, Chu Feng discovered a pattern.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was slowly growing dimmer, but each time it sniffed the orb, it would regain its brightness.","“While this lair harnesses energy beneficial to the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness, what truly sustains it is that orb. If I steal that orb, I might be able to lure it out of the lair,” Chu Feng said.","“How do you intend to do that? It’s too dangerous to approach it directly,\" Eggy asked.","“I’ll use a teleportation formation. I’ll have to construct it in the lair to ensure that the formation takes in the lair’s aura, and I can’t leave until it is activated. This is necessary to avoid the true dragon’s detection,” Chu Feng said as he retreated from where the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was resting to an area he believed was relatively safer.","To avoid alarming the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness, Chu Feng constructed the teleportation formation inside his body, and he needed to absorb the dragon lair’s aura now and then. This made the process extremely convoluted, so it took him rather long.","Fortunately, he succeeded in constructing the teleportation formation.","Now, he just needed to transfer the teleportation formation onto the orb, leave the dragon lair, and activate the teleportation formation. That should bring the orb out of the lair right away.","So, he returned to where the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was resting and carefully layered his teleportation formation on the orb. Cold sweat drenched his back. He was extremely nervous.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was simply too powerful. If not for the Divine Deer, he wouldn’t have been able to escape from it at all.","To his relief, everything went well. He successfully enveloped his teleportation formation on the orb.","Without any hesitation, Chu Feng began flitting out of the lair. It would be a success once he stepped out of the lair. It was nerve-wracking as well, but it didn’t take long for the exit to appear within sight.","“It’s done!” Eggy was overjoyed.","The next second, her smile froze in place.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness had appeared at the exit. It was no longer asleep but was instead glaring at Chu Feng with a vile sneer.","“Elder,” Chu Feng called the Divine Deer.","But the Divine Deer’s response chilled Chu Feng’s and Eggy’s hearts.","“Oh no, Chu Feng! I’m unable to use my power!”","Meanwhile, Shangguan Fengquan and Sikong Changsheng were spectating the situation from above.","“That true dragon’s fragmented consciousness is still as fond of toying with others as before,” Shangguan Fengquan remarked with a smile.","Sikong Changsheng didn’t utter a word. His conscience felt uneasy, but he tried not to show it. He had known this would happen. The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness always toyed with anyone who stepped into its lair before murdering them.","He felt uneasy bringing about the downfall of someone as talented as Chu Feng.","“Brat, you have quite the means. Looks like you’re a talented world spiritist,” the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness said.","“You were awake all this while?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course. It has been so long that I almost miss being disturbed. I wanted to play with you a little longer, but you ran faster than I expected.” The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness looked at Chu Feng with a mocking gaze.","“Elder, could there be a misunderstanding?” Chu Feng asked.","“Misunderstanding? You’re attempting to lure me out of my lair. What misunderstanding can there be? I shall use you to replenish my dragon orb’s energy.” The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness unfurled its claw, revealing the orb within.","Not only had the orb removed Chu Feng’s teleportation formation, but it was also emanating an eerie aura.","Now that Chu Feng was getting a closer look at the orb, he saw countless skeletons that had their origin energies siphoned clean.","Weng!","A spirit formation gate opened before Chu Feng, and Eggy stepped out.","She was well aware that she didn’t stand a chance, but she couldn’t turn a blind eye to Chu Feng’s plight. They were already cornered, but she would rather struggle with all her might than to resign to fate.","But as soon as Eggy unleashed her black aura, a surge of spirit power sealed her black aura back in. That plunged her into despair.","But just then, Shangguan Fengquan’s voice echoed from behind, “You don’t need to put your life on the line to deal with that.”","Shangguan Fengquan had unknowingly flitted behind Chu Feng, and while she was speaking, she had already walked forward to stand in front of them.","“Elder?” Chu Feng was surprised.","Shangguan Fengquan had previously instructed him to lure the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness out of the lair, stating that she wouldn’t be able to do anything about it otherwise. The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was not out of its lair yet.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness assessed Shangguan Fengquan.","“Dumb dragon, you don’t recognize me anymore?” Shangguan Fengquan asked with a smile.","“You are... that lass? You’re quite the tenacious one. I’m surprised you’re still alive.” The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness laughed, but its eyes turned increasingly viler and colder. “You were lucky to have gotten away the last time, but I won’t let you escape this time.”","The true dragon opened its mouth and unleashed a breath of golden light at Shangguan Fengquan, Chu Feng, and Eggy. However, the breath of golden light was deflected by an invisible barrier.","It was Shangguan Fengquan’s doing.","Shangguan Fengquan changed her hand seal. Chains rose from the ground and coiled around the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness. These chains were extremely strong, so much so that they distorted the other party’s body.","It looked as if the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness would be ripped apart from the sheer force.","“Hahahahaha...” The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness burst into laughter. “Lass, you have improved, but have you forgotten that I’m invincible in this lair?”","The lair emanated a brilliant golden glow, significantly amplifying the strength of the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness. Its twisted body recovered to normal, and its physique began to enlarge.","The chains wrapped around it creaked. It was only a matter of time before they shattered.","“Dumb dragon. Even if I can’t defeat you, I can always flee.” Shangguan Fengquan took out a golden talisman paper and set it ablaze. The golden talisman paper transformed into a surge of golden teleportation energy that enveloped her, Chu Feng, and Eggy.","But at the same time, tremendous martial power sealed off the lair.","“Trying to escape? Do you think you can get away?” the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness replied confidently.","What happened next left the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness dazed.","The teleportation energy worked as per intended. Shangguan Fengquan, Chu Feng, and Eggy appeared outside the lair.","“Looks like we have escaped,” Shangguan Fengquan replied with a smirk."]},{"number":6502,"title":"Chapter 6502: Chapter 6500: The One Who Ruled the Earlier Years of the Present Era","paragraphs":["Chapter 6500: The One Who Ruled the Earlier Years of the Present Era","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was infuriated by Shangguan Fengquan’s taunts.","GRAR!","It opened its mouth wide and unleashed a devastating dragon breath, but the breath grew significantly weaker as soon as it left the perimeter of the lair. Shangguan Fengquan easily dissipated it with a wave of her hand.","“Tsk tsk. Is that all you have? Come out and have a fight with me. Or are you intimidated by me? You aren’t a true dragon at all. You’re a turtle who spends its days holed in its shell,” Shangguan Fengquan cheerily mocked the true dragon like a mischievous grandmother.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was infuriated. Overwhelming killing intent gushed from the lair.","But Chu Feng was fearless. He felt absolutely safe, now that Shangguan Fengquan was protecting him.","“Lass, you’ll never obtain my power!” the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness spat before returning into the dragon lair.","As soon as the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness left, Shangguan Fengquan’s body slumped. She didn’t even have the strength to stand upright. Chu Feng’s hand quickly shot out to support her.","“Lord Sectmaster!” Sikong Changsheng rushed over with worried eyes.","Shangguan Fengquan’s soul body had become much dimmer. Even her aura was nowhere as strong as before. Despite taunting the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness, her intervention had taken a toll on her.","“It’s fine. I wouldn’t have lasted long in the first place. This treasure is barely sustaining my consciousness.” Shangguan Fengquan waved her hand nonchalantly. She turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Do you have alcohol?”","“Elder, I have top-quality Dragon Spring.” Chu Feng took out an exquisite jade bottle.","This was the Dragon Spring refined personally by Long Mucheng. It couldn’t be bought even in the Dragon Breath Spring Chamber.","But Shangguan Fengquan rolled her eyes in disdain. “Pui! I want alcohol. Alcohol! Who wants that goddamned Dragon Spring?”","“Yes, I have alcohol as well.” Chu Feng stowed away the Dragon Spring and pulled out thousands of vats, gourds, and bottles that floated around them. He opened every single one of them, allowing their aroma to waft out.","“Brat, you have quite the collection.”","Shangguan Fengquan revealed a bright smile. She first took a sniff before grabbing a nearby vat and downing its contents. It only took a few gulps for her to finish the entire vat. It was as if she were a ravenous ghost.","But that wasn’t enough to hit the sweet spot.","She downed three more vats of alcohol before wiping her mouth with a satisfied smile. These four vats were not the best alcohol in Chu Feng’s collection, be it in terms of fragrance or age. However, they shared a commonality.","They were all alcohol from the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","“That was satisfying! There’s no better alcohol than those from home!” Shangguan Fengquan looked intoxicated. The nostalgic fragrance of the alcohol evoked old memories, reminding her of past affairs.","But Chu Feng felt bitter.","Shangguan Fengquan’s body was growing increasingly fainter. She wouldn’t last long at this rate. She could have lasted longer if she hadn’t entered the dragon lair to save him.","He knew that this was merely a fragment of her consciousness, and its dissipation wouldn’t affect her main body, but he still felt guilt-ridden.","But Shangguan Fengquan showed no displeasure whatsoever. She glanced at Eggy with her intoxicated eyes before remarking to Chu Feng, “You have a fine world spirit.”","She turned back to Eggy and asked, “Lass, what do I call you?”","“You can call me Milady Queen,” Eggy replied haughtily, albeit with a smile. She rarely smiled at others, but Shangguan Fengquan had saved Chu Feng, after all.","Shangguan Fengquan replied with a beaming smile, “What an adorable lass.”","She tossed a vat to Eggy. “Come, Milady Queen. Let’s toast to your bravery!”","Eggy glanced at the potent alcohol in the vat and frowned. She was a drinker, but she wasn’t fond of potent alcohol. Nevertheless, she still took the vat. “Thank you for saving Chu Feng.”","She downed its contents.","“The means you used earlier is impressive, but your little body won’t be able to withstand it if you unleash that power in its entirety. You’ll lose your life. Don’t you fear death?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","“I didn’t think that much,” Eggy replied.","Shangguan Fengquan revealed a deep smile. You didn’t think that much? You think I’d believe such words?","“It’s rare to come across such a good world spirit in the world. Chu Feng, I’d say that your greatest fortuitous encounter is none other than her,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“I think so too.”","Chu Feng had always thought that way. He took a vat as well and said, “Elder, allow me to toast you.”","“Very well.” Shangguan Fengquan raised a vat with a smile.","The two gulped down the alcohol.","Sikong Changsheng appeared to have made up his mind as well. He took a vat and said, “Lord Sectmaster, allow me to toast you as well.”","“Don’t bother. You don’t even know how to pick your alcohol. Don’t force yourself if you don’t know how to drink.” Shangguan Fengquan rolled her eyes. She turned back to Chu Feng and said, “Chu Feng, I revealed myself because of you, but you didn’t complete your mission. Do you know what I mean?”","“Yes, I understand. I’ll back down here,” Chu Feng said.","“This is a bonus opportunity. You can still obtain the legacy if you gather all the key fragments,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“I understand.” Chu Feng nodded.","“If I’m not mistaken, you’re a member of the Enigma Sect, right?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","“Enigma Sect? I have never joined the Enigma Sect.” Chu Feng was perplexed, for he didn’t think that someone of Shangguan Fengquan’s stature would spout nonsense. But he had never even heard about the Enigma Sect, let alone join it.","“I am too accustomed to calling it by its old name. It should be known as the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect now,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“Was the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect known as the Enigma Sect in the earlier years of the present era?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s a long story. It was believed that the strongest powers in the earlier years of the present era were the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect and the Myriad Dao Sect, but in truth, the Ancestral Martial Galaxy had another mysterious sect.","“This sect rarely competed for anything, but no one was a match for them whenever they appeared. Even the Myriad Dao Sect and my Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect shied away from conflict with them.","“On the surface, the Myriad Dao Sect was the strongest cultivator power, and our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect is the strongest world spiritist power, but we all know the greatest power in the world of cultivation is none other than the Enigma Sect.","“The Enigma Sect is none other than the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, though I’m used to calling it the Enigma Sect,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“Woah. The Hidden Dragon Martial Sect was the true ruler in the earlier years of the present era?” Eggy was astonished.","“Yes, that’s right,” Shangguan Fengquan replied affirmatively."]},{"number":6503,"title":"Chapter 6503: Chapter 6501: Joining the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6501: Joining the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect","“Elder, are you acquainted with the elders of my Hidden Dragon Martial Sect?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course. We’re from the same world of cultivation.” Shangguan Fengquan suddenly looked melancholic. “Your Hidden Dragon Martial Sect wouldn’t have landed in its current plight if those two were still around. The whole world of cultivation owes your Hidden Dragon Martial Sect.”","Both Chu Feng and Sikong Changsheng looked curious. Shangguan Fengquan clearly knew things that no one else knew.","“The Immemorial Domain of Gods shines the brightest in the Nine Galaxies. All cultivators naturally look forward to it. Cultivators have ventured into the Ninth Galaxy right from the very start, but none returned. That’s how the Ninth Galaxy gained its reputation as the Immemorial Purgatory.","“It may seem like the cultivators of my generation have reached the peak of prosperity, but in truth, we all knew that we had uncovered most remnants, and our resources are on the verge of drying out. Our growth speeds, be it the older ones or the younger ones, have greatly slowed. At this rate, we’ll all begin to decline.","“We knew something had to change, so all powers resumed their exploration of the Ninth Galaxy. We made thorough preparations, but still, no one returned. Even meticulously prepared communication means failed. The Ninth Galaxy felt like an independent space isolated from the rest of the world of cultivation.","“At that point, all powers had decided to give up on the Ninth Galaxy, till something happened.","“A mysterious remnant suddenly appeared. It stirred a huge phenomenon when it surfaced, sending tremors through the world of cultivation. It bears a striking resemblance to the present God’s Era, but there is no record of such a remnant in history.","“All powers saw a glimmer of hope in that. We wondered if there were more resources in the world of cultivation that simply haven’t been uncovered. Activating the remnant proved tough, so we put aside our grudges and joined forces for once.","“We succeeded in activating the remnant, but it turned out that the remnant didn’t contain treasures and fortuitous encounters. No, it contained a sinister power that threatened to destroy the world of cultivation. By activating the remnant, we awakened that dormant power.","“As soon as we realized that something was amiss, we did everything we could to set things right, but that power was so strong that we couldn’t suppress it with our combined prowess. In the end, two experts from the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect used a secret skill that cost them their lives to dispel that power.”","Sikong Changsheng trembled. “Lord Sectmaster, was the crisis back then resolved by the elders of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect?”","He was young when the crisis happened, but everyone in the world of cultivation could sense the impending threat coming from the remnant. Even he thought that the world of cultivation was on the verge of destruction.","But then, that threat abruptly vanished as if nothing had happened.","Those who participated in the remnant claimed that they had worked together to overcome the power. That was how the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, the Myriad Dao Sect, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, and the other powers became heroes.","The Enigma Sect, also the present-day Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, remained under the cover. Not even the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect mentioned its name.","Shangguan Fengquan looked at Chu Feng and continued, “We didn’t withhold the truth to steal the credit. It’s what your two Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s elders wanted. They didn’t care about what the world thought. They merely wanted to quietly guard the Ancestral Martial Galaxy. They told us not to tell it to others.”","“I trust you, elder.” Chu Feng didn’t think Shangguan Fengquan had any reason to lie. He only felt awe for the two elders from the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. “Elder, do you know the names of the two elders?”","“They have instructed us to keep mum about the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, but they did tell us their names before they passed away. They are Ye Wuhen and Song Wuya.”","“Ye Wuhen and Song Wuya.” Chu Feng noted down those names.","“That incident made us realize that while the current world of cultivation may contain more fortuitous encounters, there may also be destructive forces beyond our control. We cannot be content with the status quo, or else it might spell our annihilation.","“Thus, all the top powers then gathered the older generation and younger prodigies to venture into the Ninth Galaxy. Some powers left descendants in the eight galaxies, whereas some went all out and brought their entire clan into the Ninth Galaxy.","“Our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect opted to bring everyone into the Ninth Galaxy, and from the looks of it now, that was the correct decision to make,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","Chu Feng nodded in agreement.","Had those powers not entered the Ninth Galaxy, they were bound to spiral into decline once powerhouses like Shangguan Fengquan and the others passed away.","“Elder, are there truly many fortuitous encounters in the Ninth Galaxy?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course.” Shangguan Fengquan nodded.","“Are there Ancient Era’s powers in the Ninth Galaxy?”","“There are, and they are very powerful.”","“How are the powers that had entered the Ninth Galaxy back then faring?”","“Some have been destroyed. Some fell into decline. Some rose through the ranks.”","“The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect must have risen through the ranks.”","“That goes without saying. I’m the one leading the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, after all,” Shangguan Fengquan remarked gleefully before her expression turned serious once more. “Chu Feng, are you willing to join our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect?”","The abrupt change in topic surprised Sikong Changsheng. He looked at Chu Feng nervously.","“I’m willing,” Chu Feng replied.","Sikong Changsheng’s lower jaw fell, for Chu Feng replied without any hesitation as if he had already made up his mind.","Chu Feng harbored goodwill toward the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect right from the start, mainly because they had their roots in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy as well. He cared about his roots and hoped for the prosperity of the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, and the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect was the representative power of the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s world spiritists.","Furthermore, the two elders he had met from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect were decent people.","“Very well. You’re a member of our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect from now on. If you ever require help after entering the Ninth Galaxy, you may take this token and look for anyone from our sect.”","Shangguan Fengquan compressed her formidable spirit power to form a token, and the token floated toward Chu Feng.","Chu Feng took the token and inspected it. Written on its front was ‘Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’. Inscribed on the back were the words ‘Fengquan’s Bestowment’."]},{"number":6504,"title":"Chapter 6504: Chapter 6502: The Loser Grandfather Appears","paragraphs":["Chapter 6502: The Loser Grandfather Appears","The token carried a hint of Shangguan Fengquan’s aura.","Manifesting the token caused Shangguan Fengquan to grow fainter. Even the seven-colored gemstone on her forehead had grown dim.","Chu Feng half-kneeled on the ground and bowed deeply to Shangguan Fengquan. “Thank you for your special bestowment, Lord Sectmaster. I’ll not let you down.”","“Don’t be in a rush to thank me. It won’t be that easy for you to find us even after you enter the Ninth Galaxy. You have to work hard in your cultivation. The Ninth Galaxy is not that friendly to juniors like you. Rather, old folks like us benefit more from it,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“It sounds like there’s a distinction between juniors and elders in the Ninth Galaxy. May I know the reason behind that?” Chu Feng asked.","“Cultivation is built upon accumulation and epiphanies.","“The natural energies in the eight galaxies are far weaker than the Ninth Galaxy, and our generation has depleted the resources left behind from the Ancient Era. Those who come after us have to rely on natural energies for their cultivation, but the limitations of their resources and talent doomed them to slow growth.”","Chu Feng strongly agreed with that. He had relied a lot on resources to advance his cultivation. If he had cultivated solely using natural energies, there was no way he could reach his current level at his age.","“But hard work is bound to reap rewards in cultivation.","“Cultivators who have been limited by the world of cultivation, upon entering the Ninth Galaxy and encountering richer natural energies, will find their accumulation bearing fruit. Their cultivation will surge at a rapid pace until they deplete their accumulation, then their cultivation will revert to its normal speed.","“Young prodigies like you possess exceptional intelligence and encounter fewer bottlenecks in your cultivation, but that also means that you lack accumulation,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“The longer someone has cultivated here, the more rewards they will reap upon entering the Ninth Galaxy?” Chu Feng asked.","“Those who have cultivated long enough here will enjoy a growth spurt in the Ninth Galaxy. Nevertheless, talent is still the most important element for both cultivators and world spiritists. Even if two people have cultivated for the same time, the difference in talent may result in a difference in the rewards they reap from the Ninth Galaxy.","“I can tell you straight that your grandfather possesses both talent and accumulation. He is limited by his resources. Someone like him is bound to enjoy rapid growth upon entering the Ninth Galaxy,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","Eggy took this chance to ask, “Jie Tianran is a terrible person. Since Chu Feng is a member of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect now, why don’t you kill him before your soul dissipates?”","“Milady Queen, I’m at my limit. My soul will dissipate before I can even look for Jie Tianran.” Shangguan Fengquan chuckled. She turned to Chu Feng and continued, “Chu Feng, the compensation given to the older generation only goes that far, but talent will take you further. You might not receive any compensation, but given your talent, they might not necessarily grow any faster than you in the Ninth Galaxy.","“Once I return, I’m going to brag all about you and tell those old monsters to tone it down. A formidable prodigy is about to join our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect soon.”","Shangguan Fengquan looked at Chu Feng with expectant eyes before her silhouette disintegrated into an aura.","“Farewell, Lord Sectmaster.”","Chu Feng and Sikong Changsheng bowed. In particular, Sikong Changsheng’s eyes were filled with yearning.","Suddenly, Sikong Changsheng’s face darkened. He turned to Chu Feng and said, “Chu Feng, you have to leave right now.”","Before Chu Feng could utter a word, teleportation energy enveloped him.","He was transported not back to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, but back to space, where he had channeled the key fragments. Eggy stood right beside him.","The two of them widened their eyes in unease.","Countless people were gathered in the space around them. Among them were many familiar faces.","Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, their parents, and the Totem Dragon Clan’s experts.","The Totem’s Nine Daoists, Huahua, and Xia Xingchen.","Jie Shanxian, Jie Tiannian, and Daoist Starseizer.","What was worth mentioning was that no one from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan was present here.","All these people were shackled with formation collars that were linked together with a single chain, and the one holding the end of the chain was none other than Jie Tianran.","“Chu Feng, the key fragments have been activated. I know you’re here. Come out, or else I’ll start killing them,” Jie Tianran’s voice echoed.","The experts of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion assessed the surroundings, searching for Chu Feng’s whereabouts.","“Chu Feng, shall I make a move?” the Divine Deer asked.","The Divine Deer had the power to save everyone.","Before Chu Feng could answer, Jie Tianran tightened his grip on the chain and channeled spirit power through it. A bundle of light shone in the captives’ dantians. A gu harnessing tremendous power had grasped all their souls.","“That is... a Soul Sealing Gu. I’m afraid I’m unable to do anything about that. I can free them from those shackles, but I cannot dispel the Soul Sealing Gu,” the Divine Deer said.","Jie Tianran couldn’t stop the Divine Deer from saving everyone, but everyone would still die once Jie Tianran activated the Soul Sealing Gu.","“Chu Feng, I can try saving them.”","Eggy knew that Chu Feng wouldn’t sit still and watch as harm befell his family and friends, but Chu Feng didn’t have the power to oppose Jie Tianran. This meant that she would have to do something about the situation.","“Hold on, Eggy. Let me think of a solution first,” Chu Feng said as he flew into the distance."]},{"number":6505,"title":"Chapter 6505: Chapter 6503: Forcing Chu Feng to Concede","paragraphs":["Chapter 6503: Forcing Chu Feng to Concede","Chu Feng had previously constructed a teleportation formation inside his body to steal the dragon orb, but he didn’t get to use it in the end.","So, he first made his way to a place that was relatively safer and set it as the destination of the teleportation formation. Then, he left a powerful teleportation talisman paper on the spot so that they could continue teleporting off to somewhere even safer.","Once he was done with his preparations, he returned to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","By then, Jie Tianran was already getting impatient. “Chu Feng, aren’t you going to show yourself? Do you not care about your friends anymore?”","As Jie Tianran spoke, the shackles binding Chu Feng’s friends and family suddenly pulsated with incredible energy, inflicting excruciating pain on them.","“Jie Tianran!” Chu Feng roared as his figure appeared.","In truth, he was still a far distance away from Jie Tianran. He had to amplify his voice using a talisman paper to relay his message over, or else his words would have faded to silence before reaching.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion immediately used their observation formation to lock onto Chu Feng’s position.","Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, Xia Xingchen and the others looked worried. They felt indebted to Chu Feng, so much so that they thought that it would be right for them to die over Chu Feng. The last thing they wanted was for them to become baggage to him.","None of them could speak or relay their voices to Chu Feng due to the shackles.","Even if not for that restriction, the distance was so great that only Heavenly God level cultivators or Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists could have relayed their voices over to Chu Feng.","The members of Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were prepared to set off to capture Chu Feng, but Jie Tianran raised his hand and stopped them from making a reckless move. Even he wasn’t confident of capturing Chu Feng from this distance away.","But Jie Tianran didn’t lose his composure. He looked at Chu Feng with a gleeful smirk.","“You’re here, Chu Feng,” Jie Tianran said.","“Jie Tianran, have you fallen so low as to bring in uninvolved parties into our grudge?” Chu Feng asked.","“Uninvolved parties? They are your friends, and they will stand against me and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion for your sake. They are very much involved in this. I’d be clearing future threats for our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion by killing all of them today.”","Jie Tianran briefly paused before adding, “But you don’t have to worry. I’m in a good mood today, and don’t intend to go on a massacre. I can even spare your life. You know, I have given it some thought, and I believe your words make sense. Nurture is indeed more important than plunder.”","Jie Tianran hooked his finger.","Two chains dragged Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer to his sides and made them kneel to him. The two of them might have regained consciousness, but they were still in terrible states. Powerless against Jie Tianran, they kneeled to him like pitiful dogs.","But their conditions evoked no sympathy from Jie Tianran. He glanced at the two of them, and his smile widened. “I might not have been able to dig out and capture all your allies in a single swoop had I not tested my location talismans on them back then.”","Jie Tianran grinned as he said those words.","Chu Feng realized he had still been underestimating Jie Tianran.","It might have been a coincidence that Jie Tianran had planted a location gu in Daoist Starseizer and Jie Shanxian’s bodies, but if that were true, it would be shocking. Long Zhuoyan had been present when he was treating Daoist Starseizer and the others.","Long Zhuoyan’s spirit power had severely regressed due to the injuries she sustained in the Ancient Era, but she had been one of the top experts of the Ancient Era. Few could match her means and her experience. Yet, she didn’t notice Jie Tianran’s location gus.","That showed that Jie Tianran’s means were more formidable than he had expected.","“Jie Tianran, you went through so much trouble simply because you want these, right?” Chu Feng said as he took out three key fragments.","“Smart. I’m more interested in your Ruler’s Bloodline and Genesis Bloodline, but I know you won’t throw away your life for them. So, I’ll only demand those three key fragments today. Hand the key fragments over, and I’ll let them go,” Jie Tianran said.","Chu Feng flicked his wrist, and a surge of light flew toward Jie Tianran.","However, the light stopped in the midpoint between them before expanding into a spirit formation gate. That was the teleportation formation Chu Feng had prepared beforehand.","“Release them first. Once you release a number of them, I’ll hand you the first key fragment. Also, you have to release the Soul Sealing Gu on them before releasing them,” Chu Feng said.","“Sure.” Jie Tianran accepted the deal without haggling.","He waved his sleeves, and a third of the people he had captured had their Soul Sealing Gu released and the shackles around their necks shattered.","He even constructed a teleportation formation to transport those people straight to where Chu Feng’s spirit formation gate was waiting. The teleportation passageway was transparent, so that those outside could see what was happening inside.","Once those people were a safe distance away from Jie Tianran, Chu Feng tossed the first key fragment over.","After Jie Tianran obtained the first key fragment, he did the same thing as he did before and freed another half of the remaining people.","It was worth noting that Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, Huahua, Xia Xingchen, the Totem’s Nine Daoists, Daoist Starseizer, Jie Shanxian, and those who were closer to Chu Feng remained imprisoned. Jie Tianran didn’t free any of them.","Chu Feng tossed the second key fragment to Jie Tianran.","Upon obtaining the second key fragment, Jie Tianran finally removed the Soul Sealing Gu and shackles on Long Chengyu and the others.","“Chu Feng.” Long Chengyu and the others looked at Chu Feng with conflicted eyes.","“Don’t worry. He can’t do anything to me. You can leave without any worries,” Chu Feng said.","The others did as they were told, knowing they would only be a burden to Chu Feng if they stayed behind. Their only choice was to trust Chu Feng’s means. They obediently entered Jie Tianran’s teleportation formation, which led to Chu Feng’s spirit formation gate.","“Will your grandfather obediently release them?” Eggy didn’t trust Jie Tianran’s character.","And her concerns proved not to be unfounded.","When Long Chengyu arrived at the other end of Jie Tianran’s teleportation passageway and was about to leave, Jie Tianran suddenly changed his hand seal and trapped them within.","“Chu Feng, I don’t trust you. Hand the final key to me first. I’ll only let them go once I fuse the key fragments,” Jie Tianran said.","“I trust you even less,” Chu Feng snorted.","“I don’t want to bother arguing with you. You don’t have a choice here,” Jie Tianran replied confidently, knowing that Chu Feng had no choice but to concede here."]},{"number":6506,"title":"Chapter 6506: Chapter 6504: Chu Feng’s Backing","paragraphs":["Chapter 6504: Chu Feng’s Backing","“Let’s hope you can be a human for once.”","Chu Feng didn’t hesitate for long. He tossed the final key to Jie Tianran. At the same time, he told the Divine Deer, “Elder, please make a move if Jie Tianran tries to harm my friends.”","“I know.” The Divine Deer nodded.","It couldn’t make a move before because it couldn’t lift the Soul Sealing Gu. Now that the Soul Sealing Gus had been released, nothing was standing in its way. The only reason Chu Feng hadn’t told the Divine Deer to make a move yet was that he wanted to save this move until the situation was truly desperate.","It would be ideal if Jie Tianran kept his promise and released the others. Otherwise, it was not too late for the Divine Deer to intervene then.","The final key fragment fell into Jie Tianran’s hand. He took out his two key fragments and fused the five of them into a complete key.","“Jie Tianran, it’s time for you to free them,” Chu Feng urged.","“No rush. Aren’t you curious to know the legacy left behind by the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect?” Jie Tianran said as he channeled the key.","Weng!","The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city suddenly began glowing brightly as if a sacred land, illuminating its surroundings. Everyone in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, including Jie Tianran, looked at the main city with a different gaze.","Even Chu Feng’s eyes were locked on the main city.","As world spiritists, they were instinctively excited to see what the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect had to offer.","“It’s all a show,” Jie Tianran scoffed. He was excited as well, but he didn’t like this.","He had always thought that the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect became the strongest world spiritist power because they were the firstcomers and plundered all the resources in the earlier years of the present era.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","Light rays shot out from the main city and began revolving around it. Each one contained a rune. As more light rays appeared, the light radiating from the main city faded, and even the main city itself started to turn incorporeal.","It was as if the main city’s energy had all been fused inside the runes.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","These light rays suddenly morphed into a comet rain and surged toward Jie Tianran.","“Let me see the legacy left behind by the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect,” Jie Tianran murmured with eyes gleaming in excitement.","It was apparent to him that the light rays were the legacy.","The next moment, his expression stiffened. Everyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was dumbstruck.","The light rays shot past Jie Tianran and headed straight toward Chu Feng!","Jie Tianran quickly released his spirit power to stop the light rays, but it was all futile. The light rays were so fast that they arrived before Chu Feng in the blink of an eye. By then, the light rays had already shrunk.","They circled around Chu Feng as if acknowledging him as their master.","Chu Feng had inherited the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy.","“Chu Feng, could it be...” Eggy’s eyes lit up.","Chu Feng laughed in glee. He turned to Jie Tianran and said, “Even the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy knows that you’re a despicable scum and refuses to acknowledge you. It knows that I am of superior character and chooses me instead. I can only say that the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy has good judgment!”","Jie Tianran’s eyes reddened, and his killing intent flared. He thought that Chu Feng had tampered with the key fragments.","“Elder.” Chu Feng knew that Jie Tianran was about to go on a killing spree, so he hurriedly called out to the Divine Deer.","But the Divine Deer didn’t make a move. “There’s no need for me to make a move.”","Chu Feng widened his eyes in shock.","Jie Tianran had already made his move. He channeled his formation to massacre Long Chengyu and everyone else who was trapped in his teleportation passageway, but no matter how the teleportation passageway warped, the people inside it remained unharmed.","A great power was protecting them.","“Chu Feng!!!” Jie Tianran glared at Chu Feng while flying toward him at his fastest speed.","If not for them being too far away, he would have made a move straight to snap Chu Feng’s neck there and then.","All of a sudden, Chu Feng vanished and reappeared at the entrance of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s entrance. The same happened to Long Chengyu and the others, as well as those who had entered Chu Feng’s spirit formation gate and left this place.","They had all been assembled here.","It happened so abruptly that everyone was dazed.","Just then, a person appeared next to Chu Feng. It was Sikong Changsheng.","“Don’t blame Chu Feng. This has nothing to do with him. I was the one who made the decision,” Sikong Changsheng told Jie Tianran.","“Are you the one who stood up for Chu Feng?” Jie Tianran asked.","“I am from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, Sikong Changsheng.”","“Sikong Changsheng?”","That name alarmed not just Jie Tianran but some of the older experts of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion as well. They had heard about Sikong Changsheng. That was the name of a famed junior in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect before they left for the Ninth Galaxy.","To think someone from that era had survived to this day! Just how powerful could he be then?","No one from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was confident of dealing with someone like that.","“But you’re right to say that I’m standing up for Chu Feng. He is a member of our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect now,” Sikong Changsheng continued.","“He is a member of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect?”","Those words shocked not just those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion but even Long Chengyu and the others as well.","“Hahahahaha...” Jie Tianran sneered as his eyes grew increasingly colder. He remained fearless even against this legendary figure. “You want to be Chu Feng’s backing? You might have been able to do so if the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect was still here, but do you think you have the power to do it alone?”","“Are you challenging me now?” Sikong Changsheng’s robe fluttered as overwhelming spirit power flared from him and rippled across space.","Wails ensued. Everyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was subjected to immense pain.","Even Jie Tianran frowned as well. His muscles were being squeezed, and his bones creaked. Clearly, Sikong Changsheng was stronger than him.","And Sikong Changsheng was not even tapping into the power of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city."]},{"number":6507,"title":"Chapter 6507: Chapter 6505: The Sectmaster Reappears","paragraphs":["Chapter 6505: The Sectmaster Reappears","“Do you take me for a pushover?” Jie Tianran refused to back down. His eyes hardened in determination.","“Jie Tianran, it’s not worthwhile to use that here. You can settle the scores with him in the future. There’s no need to rush,” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body said.","“But the Ruler’s Bloodline is right in front of us.” Jie Tianran refused to concede.","His goal was not just the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy but Chu Feng as well.","“He has the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city behind him. Are you confident that you can bring him down if he can tap into that remnant’s power as well?” the old entity asked.","Jie Tianran’s killing intent slowly faded.","“Old man, why don’t you kill him since you have already made a move? You’d only be giving him a chance to exact vengeance on you if you let him go now,” Eggy urged Sikong Changsheng.","“His character might be flawed, but he’s still Jie Ranqing’s father and Chu Feng’s grandfather,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“Consider him vermin. Elder, go ahead and kill him,” Chu Feng said.","Sikong Changsheng was rendered speechless.","Weng!","Powerful teleportation energy flowed from Jie Tianran’s body, completely disregarding Sikong Changsheng’s oppressive might to wrap everyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","In the blink of an eye, everyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion vanished.","But Jie Tianran’s voice echoed, “Chu Feng, flee to the Ninth Galaxy if you’re frightened. A mere Sikong Changsheng can’t protect you if you remain here.”","Long Chengyu spat, “Aren’t you talking big despite being the one running away?”","Xia Xingchen piled on, “You’re even more shameless than that withered prune from the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect!”","But Jie Tianran didn’t reply. He had already left and couldn’t hear their retorts.","“Chu Feng, come with me,” Sikong Changsheng said.","Teleportation energy enveloped Chu Feng and Eggy, and the duo were transported back into the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. The outside remained illusory, but the main city looked the same as ever.","“Cough cough...” Sikong Changsheng clasped his mouth and coughed violently. His complexion paled, and fresh blood seeped through his fingers.","“What’s wrong, elder?” Chu Feng rushed forward and grabbed Sikong Changsheng’s wrist.","Much to his shock, Sikong Changsheng’s energies were in disarray. Even his bloodline was damaged. He was afflicted with many old injuries.","“I’m fine. It’s just an old ailment,” Sikong Changsheng replied with a smile. He took a pill and meditated for a while to recuperate. Slowly, his rampant energies calmed down, though he felt weaker than before.","“Chu Feng, it’s not that I don’t want to help you clear the obstacles in your way, but I don’t have the ability to do that right now. My soul and bloodline were impaired a long time ago, and that prevented me from using spirit power for a prolonged time. Otherwise, I would have gone to the Ninth Galaxy with the others instead of staying behind in the main city.","“All I can do is to intimidate Jie Tianran. I won’t be a match for him if we fight it out. Your grandfather isn’t as simple as he appears on the surface,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“Is it because of that old monster inside of him?” Chu Feng asked.","That old entity couldn’t do much inside the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant because they were limited to their consciousness, but who knew how powerful that old thing was in his main body?","“I can’t tell for sure, but that one is tricky as well,” Sikong Changsheng replied.","“Don’t worry, elder. I’ll deal with them myself.”","“Mm. That will be for the best. Chu Feng, I have already handed the legacy to you. You should hurry up and grasp it.”","Chu Feng grinned. “Elder, I thought you weren’t going to give this legacy to me?”","“Why would I give it to that outsider instead of you? Cut the crap and quickly study it,” Sikong Changsheng urged.","“All right.”","Chu Feng sat down with crossed legs. He might have acquired the legacy, but it would only be useful if he could comprehend it.","Weng!","The energy shrouding Chu Feng suddenly transformed. A black aura appeared out of nowhere and surged toward Eggy like a shooting star before revolving around her.","Sikong Changsheng’s eyebrows shot up.","“Elder, is this part of the legacy as well?” Chu Feng asked.","“It appears so.” Sikong Changsheng sounded unsure.","“Eggy?” Chu Feng couldn’t decipher the energy revolving around Eggy, but he had a feeling she would have a better sense of it.","“It is a legacy, but it’s an unusual one. Come, let’s do it together,” Eggy said with a sweet smile as she sat down and began cultivating.","“All right.”","Chu Feng formed a hand seal, closed his eyes, and began cultivating.","Thus, the energies revolving around Chu Feng and Eggy began to fuse into them. Once they fully absorbed the energies, the legacy would be theirs.","Sikong Changsheng looked at the black aura revolving around Eggy with complicated eyes.","Just then, a voice echoed in Sikong Changsheng’s ears. “You have done well to hand the legacy to Chu Feng.”","Sikong Changsheng was overjoyed to hear the voice. He quickly flitted to the depths of the main city, where he was met with a familiar figure—Shangguan Fengquan.","She was still a soul entity, but her body was nowhere as thin as it appeared before.","“Lord Sectmaster, you...”","“The Dragon Prison Orb,” Shangguang Fengquan interjected.","As soon as Sikong Changsheng took out the Dragon Prison Orb, he was transported into the realm inside the orb and into the dragon lair, where the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was right in front of him.","He wasn’t capable of moving that quickly. It was Shangguan Fengquan dragging him along.","“Hm?”","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was surprised to see Shangguan Fengquan, but its eyes soon twisted in malevolence. “Lass, you must be tired of living. Do you think I’d give you a second chance?”","It picked up the dragon orb and took a huge whiff from it. Energy flowed visibly from the dragon orb into its body.","An instant later, the dragon lair glowed with incredible radiance. Waves of dragon aura seeped from the walls of the lair and gushed into the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness grew larger, and its intangible body grew corporeal. Its power also visibly grew.","This time, the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness didn’t hold back. It was exerting its full prowess.","The overwhelming power emanated by it made Sikong Changsheng succumb to despair.","“Is that your limit, dumb dragon? I’m terribly disappointed.”","But Shangguan Fengquan reacted with scorn."]},{"number":6508,"title":"Chapter 6508: Chapter 6506: The Strength of a Dominator","paragraphs":["Chapter 6506: The Strength of a Dominator","Kacha!","The seven-colored gemstone embedded on Shangguan Fengquan’s forehead cracked.","A small spirit formation gate formed on her palm. From it, over a hundred dragon orbs flew forth, each one containing energy far surpassing that of the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness’s one.","These dragon orbs flew toward the true dragons’ fragmented consciousness.","“Lass, what do you mean by this?” The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was stunned.","“Assimilate them,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness frowned, thinking that it had to be a trap. Yet, it could tell that these dragon orbs were all the real deal.","“What are you up to?”","“You talk too much.”","Shangguan Fengquan lost her patience. She pointed her finger at the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness and casually flicked it downward.","Boom!","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was slammed to the ground, unable to move.","It was oppressive might, and the oppressive might was coming from Shangguan Fengquan!","This made the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness realize that it was in a weaker position and had no other option, even if it was a trap. So, it opened its mouth and devoured the hundred dragon orbs.","Its body quickly became corporeal and grew larger, soon reaching a point where even the dragon lair was too small to contain its hulking stature. However, the dragon lair reacted to it and shattered apart, transforming into an aura that fused into the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness.","By the time the two completed their fusion, the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was already large enough to be one with the realm. The realm even began to crack. It looked as if the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness could finally shatter its prison and be free.","“Hahahaha... Lass, it looks like you came down here to help me recover my strength. Speak, what wish do you have? This god will fulfill it,” the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness said as the realm began to crumble.","Even Sikong Changsheng trembled a little in the face of its might. It was not because he was timid, but this suppression came from the depths of his soul.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness had undergone a metamorphosis after taking in the hundred dragon orbs and the dragon lair. It had reached a new height compared to before. With its current strength, it could disintegrate Sikong Changsheng’s soul with a mere glance.","Shangguan Fengquan had nurtured a monster that could destroy the world of cultivation. If the dragon were to escape from here, it would be a huge disaster.","“Don’t address yourself as a god. Don’t you get it, dumb dragon? You’re just a cultivation resource,” Shangguan Fengquan snorted.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness narrowed its eyes in anger.","“Lass, watch your words! Don’t think that I won’t kill you just because you helped me.”","Just its cold gaze caused the space around Shangguan Fengquan and Sikong Changsheng to distort and crumble.","Shangguan Fengquan raised her hand and directed it at the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness, which had become so humongous that it covered the sky. “Dumb dragon, I’ll give you a chance. I’ll spare your life if you manage to escape from my grasp.”","She opened her palm.","The realm finally completely collapsed. The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was plunged into boundless space.","It remained as big as ever, comparable to a realm, but it found itself confronted with a humongous hand that was approaching from afar. Furious winds assaulted it, and it felt like even space was rustling.","Extreme fear seeped into its eyes. It was less than a grain of sand before this humongous hand.","So, it tried to escape.","But the hand was as fast as it was humongous. It arrived before the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness in the blink of an eye and grasped it tightly.","The true dragon’s fragmented consciousness cried in agony. “I was wrong, I was wrong! I know that I was wrong now! Lass—no, milord! Milord, please spare me. I’m willing to be your servant!”","“I’ll grant your wish,” Shangguan Fengquan’s voice echoed from above. Her voice resonated powerfully, as if she was the universe itself. “I’ll turn you into Sikong Changsheng’s cultivation resource.”","She clenched her fist and crushed the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness into bits.","Sikong Changsheng witnessed everything in shock.","The next moment, he was transported out of this space and the Dragon Prison Orb, back into the depths of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. Shangguan Fengquan was standing beside him.","Sikong Changsheng gasped for air. He knew what he had witnessed wasn’t an illusion but a glimpse of what Shangguan Fengquan was capable of.","If the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness could lay waste upon the world of cultivation, Shangguan Fengquan would be an absolute god who could vanquish anyone or anything at her whim.","“Lord Sectmaster, y-your cultivation?” Sikong Changsheng looked at Shangguan Fengquan with awed eyes as if she was a god.","“How can I carve out a space for the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect in the Ninth Galaxy if I can’t even pull this off?” Shangguan Fengquan replied with a smile. She presented her clenched fist to Sikong Changsheng. “Here, take it and use it to strengthen your bloodline. It should heal your injuries.”","She opened her fist and revealed a bundle of aura that was coiled like a dragon.","It was the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness, but it had passed out and had been refined into a cultivation resource.","“Lord Sectmaster, this is too valuable. I can’t accept this.” Sikong Changsheng anxiously turned down the gift.","He understood how powerful the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness was. This was the power that countless predecessors of his Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect coveted, including the old Shangguan Fengquan.","Yet, Shangguan Fengquan was giving it to him now that she had obtained it? He didn’t think he was qualified to receive it.","“What are you saying? This is nothing. There are far more valuable things in the Ninth Galaxy, but I’m unable to bring it here to you due to the restrictions. I’ll compensate you well once you return to the sect,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“Lord Sectmaster, such treasure should go to Chu Feng instead,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“Did you hurt your brain as well? Chu Feng possesses the Ruler’s Bloodline. Giving him this is as good as pouring a pail of shitty slop into a bowl of immortal spring water. Isn’t that sabotaging him?” Shangguan Fengquan scoffed.","“Um...” Sikong Changsheng found himself at a loss for words.","You’re describing a treasure like this as a pail of shitty slop? Is that appropriate? But I guess this also means that the present Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect doesn’t lack resources.","“Take it.”","Shangguan Fengquan placed her palm on Sikong Changsheng’s dantian and pumped the energy right into it.","Sikong Changsheng couldn’t turn down the gift anymore even if he wanted to. He quickly bowed to Shangguan Fengquan and expressed his utmost gratitude. “Thank you, Lord Sectmaster.”","“You have completed your mission. Someone has claimed the legacy. It’s time for you to enter the Ninth Galaxy and join us,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“Lord Sectmaster, I don’t think Chu Feng is planning to enter the Ninth Galaxy yet, but Jie Tianran is eyeing Chu Feng’s Ruler’s Bloodline. I wish to remain here for the time being,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“Chu Feng doesn’t need anyone to... It matters not. You may stay behind if you wish to,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“Lord Sectmaster, did you possess such strength from the very start? You were only pretending to be no match for the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness earlier?” Sikong Changsheng asked out of curiosity.","“Of course. That true dragon’s fragmented consciousness is nothing to me. I held back my strength to put on an act before Chu Feng. It’s the carrot and not the stick that works better on people like Chu Feng. If you do him a favor, he’ll return it several fold. I sacrificed myself to pique his guilt, so that he would feel greater goodwill toward our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect,” Shangguan Fengquan said with a smirk."]},{"number":6509,"title":"Chapter 6509: Chapter 6507: Milady Queen’s Decision","paragraphs":["Chapter 6507: Milady Queen’s Decision","“That explains why Lord Sectmaster sent Chu Feng into the dragon lair despite the huge risk, only to step in and save him afterward. I thought...”","“You thought I was planning to eliminate Chu Feng?” Shangguan Fengquan asked.","“Um... This...” Sikong Changsheng dared not to speak his mind.","“It’s normal for you to have such concerns. I also don’t know if I’d have made a move against him if he had refused to join our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“Lord Sectmaster, about the world spirit’s legacy...”","“It’s a bonus for Chu Feng’s world spirit,” Shangguan Fengquan said as she glanced in Eggy’s direction.","Eggy was oblivious to it, but Shangguan Fengquan could see it clearly. Eggy had already absorbed the energy around her body, but the energy around Chu Feng’s body continued to swirl.","“Oh? Is that her decision? It’s truly hard to find a world spirit as good as her. Very well, I shall satisfy your wish,” Shangguan Fengquan said. She closed her eyes and formed a hand seal.","Sikong Changsheng looked uneasy.","As Shangguan Fengquan channeled her powers, more cracks appeared on the seven-colored gemstone on her forehead. Even her body began growing thinner. It was unlikely that she was putting on an act this time. She was at her limit.","A moment later, Shangguan Fengquan released her hand seal.","By then, her seven-colored gemstone was covered in cracks, and her body had turned gaseous. It would only take a light wind for her to disintegrate.","“Looks like it’s time for me to leave,” Shangguan Fengquan examined her own condition and remarked. She turned to Sikong Changsheng and continued, “What are you crying for? I’m not dead. I’m doing well in the Ninth Galaxy right now!”","Sikong Changsheng was secretly wiping off his tears.","“I don’t know when I’ll get to meet Lord Sectmaster again.”","“Enough, enough. We’ll meet again. Go treat your injuries with that true dragon’s fragmented consciousness and reinforce your bloodline. With your talent, you should be able to rise to great heights in the Ninth Galaxy,” Shangguan Fengquan consoled.","“I won’t let you down, Lord Sectmaster,” Sikong Changsheng replied as his tears fell on the ground.","“Let me take one last look at the world of cultivation,” Shangguan Fengquan said as her pupils gleamed with a mysterious glow.","It felt like the entire world of cultivation was reflected in her eyes, but in truth, she was gazing upon a land not too far away. It was the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Hidden Dragon Martial Sect.","Seconds later, her eyes widened in shock.","I still can’t see through it? Who’s the founder of the Enigma Sect?!","...","Deep in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, a massive dragon silhouette awoken—Lord Long Xie.","“That Shangguan lass has grown a lot. At this rate, it’s only a matter before she catches up with me. She’s at least qualified to snatch my Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s disciple now,” Long Xie smiled before closing his eyes.","Shangguan Fengquan was oblivious to Long Xie’s observation. She had already cast her gaze elsewhere, but the more she peered, the more shocked she felt.","“I have underestimated the world of cultivation.”","She revealed a surprised but delighted smile.","“Interesting. How interesting. To think there are monsters of Chu Feng’s caliber in this world of cultivation. The top prodigies of Ninth Galaxy won’t be able to remain on their high horses once those monsters head over,” Shangguan Fengquan remarked with a hearty laugh.","Sikong Changsheng was curious to know who was deserving of such high praises from Shangguan Fengquan. “Lord Sectmaster, who are you referring to? Is it Xianhai Yu’er?”","“I’ll give you a clue. It’s two female juniors whose beauty is on par with me,” Shangguan Fengquan replied.","“Two?” Sikong Changsheng was surprised.","“You have been here all this while. Shouldn’t you have a good grasp of the prodigies here?”","“I have been residing in the main city all this while, and I couldn’t use my observation means due to my injuries, so I’m afraid I don’t know much about the juniors. But I do know that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan has a shockingly talented offspring named Xianhai Yu’er, and she’s on good terms with Chu Feng.","“Her elder brother is formidable as well, though his talent is slightly weaker than Xianhai Yu’er’s and Chu Feng’s, and he is a man.","“If it’s a female junior... Ah, I do know of a lady named Xian Miaomiao. She is also on good terms with Chu Feng, and she has acquired the legendary Soul Fog. Are you referring to her, Lord Sectmaster?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","Shangguan Fengquan’s eyes widened in astonishment. “Another lass has obtained the Soul Fog?”","“Were you not referring to her?” Sikong Changsheng realized that Shangguan Fengquan was not talking about Xian Miaomiao.","“That makes things more interesting. Let those arrogant relics from the Ancient Era see how strong our present-era cultivators are.”","“Lord Sectmaster, are we not going to take them into our sect?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","“As talented as they are, our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect is ultimately a world spiritist power. We shouldn’t be forcing others to join our ranks just because they are talented. Not only are we flouting our rules, but we’ll be holding them back as well,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“I was short-sighted,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“Don’t worry, I know you are speaking with the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s welfare in mind. It doesn’t matter, since we have already secured the biggest fish here.”","Shangguan Fengquan turned her eyes to Chu Feng once more.","Sikong Changsheng did the same.","Light rays continued to revolve around Chu Feng, but they couldn’t enter his body. The runes inside the rays began to flicker chaotically.","“Lord Sectmaster, do you think Chu Feng can claim the full legacy?” Sikong Changsheng asked."]},{"number":6510,"title":"Chapter 6510: Chapter 6508: Excitement","paragraphs":["Chapter 6508: Excitement","This legacy was demanding on the individual’s talent, intelligence, and competency. Just because an individual obtained the legacy didn’t mean that they would obtain the full benefits of it.","“It is extremely difficult to take in the entire legacy, but it shouldn’t be a problem for Chu Feng.”","Chu Feng soon emanated a powerful aura that shook the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city a little. It was the Ruler’s Bloodline!","Under the influence of the Ruler’s Bloodline, the runes revolving around Chu Feng began to pulsate in sync as if becoming one.","“He succeeded!” Sikong Changsheng exclaimed in excitement. “I wonder how far his spirit power will grow.”","“Building up a solid foundation is of utmost importance in cultivation. This legacy does more than strengthen one’s psyche; it reinforces one’s foundation. Its true benefits will only show in the future, when Chu Feng advances further in his spirit power cultivation.","“But that brat’s talent is indeed astounding. His fusion with the legacy is impeccable. It shouldn’t be a problem for him to advance straight to rank seven True Dragon.”","“Rank seven True Dragon?” Sikong Changsheng was shocked.","Having a strong foundation was even more important for world spiritists than for cultivators, which was why advancing even a single rank as a world spiritist was tough.","Chu Feng was at rank three True Dragon. Reaching rank seven True Dragon meant to make four consecutive breakthroughs. This was a ridiculous feat that Sikong Changsheng had never seen before.","But on second thought, the predecessors of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect couldn’t withstand the legacy, either. Even Shangguan Fengquan, dubbed to be the most talented individual in the history of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, failed to obtain this legacy back then.","This showed how extraordinary the legacy was.","Thus, it was not too shocking if Chu Feng advanced to rank seven True Dragon through the legacy.","“Hm?”","Shangguan Fengquan and Sikong Changsheng widened their eyes.","All the light rays and runes had begun fusing, brightening up even the sky of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. It was a phenomenon!","Sikong Changsheng was dumbstruck. Shangguan Fengquan was jumping with joy.","“He’s fused with the legacy to this extent? If so, rank seven True Dragon won’t be the cap. Our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect has picked up a treasure this time around!”","Just then, the seven-colored gemstone shattered, and Shangguan Fengquan’s body dissipated.","“Farewell, Lord Sectmaster!” Sikong Changsheng bowed deeply with tears in his eyes.","He knew that their sectmaster had left for good this time. The only way they could be reunited was for him to enter the Ninth Galaxy.","...","In the Ninth Galaxy, there existed a colossal starfield, where even the smallest realm was roughly comparable to the largest realm in the other eight galaxies. Some of the larger realms were even on par with entire starfields.","In its entirety, this starfield was no smaller than the eight galaxies combined, yet this vast expanse was enveloped by powerful spirit power.","Someone was using this colossal starfield as the foundation of a teleportation formation.","This teleportation formation emanated an aura similar to the spirit formation gate Shangguan Fengquan had manifested in the Dragon Prison Orb.","Thousands of powerful world spiritists sat in the formation core, each one wielding strength above Heavenly Dragon. Yet, all of them looked exhausted and were gasping for air as if they had depleted themselves.","Countless dragon orbs floated above the formation core. They were identical to the ones that the true dragon’s fragmented consciousness had assimilated, just that there were millions of them gathered here. It was truly a sea of dragon orbs.","Aside from the dragon orbs, there were also other more valuable treasures lying around.","“How useless. I went to great lengths to construct this teleportation formation, but you only transported a hundred dragon orbs over,” a woman’s voice echoed.","A magnificent throne floated right outside the formation core. On it sat a beautiful woman dressed in a gorgeous dress.","This woman had succulent lips, seductive eyes that drew others in, and vibrant seven-colored hair strands. She sat leisurely on the throne, her legs crossed and her right hand supporting her head.","She was Shangguan Fengquan.","Upon realizing that Shangguan Fengquan had awoken, the world spiritists channeling the formation core hurriedly stopped what they were doing and knelt. Their eyes were filled with fear.","They knew they had failed to satisfy Shangguan Fengquan, so they dared not utter a word.","Standing beside Shangguan Fengquan’s throne was an old man who was dressed like a carefree immortal but was bald except for a few strands of hair. He first bowed deeply before speaking up, “Old ancestor, the restrictions are too great. It wasn’t easy for them to transport a hundred dragon orbs over.”","“Shut up.” A glance from Shangguan Fengquan silenced the bald old man. “Do you think I’m oblivious to the restriction? I entrusted this formation to them to train them. How many resources do you think Jie Ranqing can send over if she channels this formation?”","The crowd fell silent. They had witnessed Jie Ranqing’s means, and they knew they were no match for her.","“You are nothing on her even when banded together,” Shangguan Fengquan snorted.","The world spiritists shuddered even more, but they replied in unison, “Old ancestor, please punish us for our incompetence.”","They understood how Shangguan Fengquan operated. She was extremely strict when it came to rewards and punishments. They had wasted this elaborately constructed formation and thus deserved to be punished.","But what Shangguan Fengquan said next stunned them.","“Forget it. You’re dismissed. Head back and rest up.”","There was a hint of a smile on Shangguan Fengquan’s face.","The world spiritists were surprised, but they knew better than to question her. They thanked her before hurriedly leaving the scene.","“Old ancestor, you seem to be in a good mood. Is that lad, Changsheng, still alive?” the bald old man asked fawningly.","“Sikong Changsheng is indeed still alive. He’s injured, but that isn’t an issue. I have instructed him to head over to the Ninth Galaxy to look for us,” Shangguan Fengquan said.","“That’s good. That’s good.” The bald old man was relieved.","“But my good mood has nothing to do with Sikong Changsheng,” Shangguan Fengquan added.","The bald old man was taken aback. It has nothing to do with Sikong Changsheng?","After moving to the Ninth Galaxy, it had become clear to them that the world of cultivation was practically a withered well; it was holding them back. What good thing could possibly be found there?","“I have seen the future of our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. With him around, our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect can shake even the Ancient Era’s God Clans,” Shangguan Fengquan said with expectant eyes.","The bald old man’s eyes widened in shock. He knew of two unwavering facts.","1: The Ancient Era’s God Clans are so powerful that it’s impossible to shake their positions.","2: Shangguan Fengquan never boasts.","He couldn’t help but wonder what kind of future the old ancestor had seen. Despite not knowing a thing at all, he could already feel his blood pumping."]},{"number":6511,"title":"Chapter 6511: Chapter 6509: Rank Nine True Dragon World Spiritist","paragraphs":["Chapter 6509: Rank Nine True Dragon World Spiritist","The light rays revolving around Chu Feng began to seep into his body. His spirit power flared, revealing his current level of strength before swiftly growing.","Rank four True Dragon.","Rank five True Dragon.","Rank six True Dragon.","Rank seven True Dragon.","Rank eight True Dragon.","Rank nine True Dragon.","As Shangguan Fengquan had predicted, Chu Feng didn’t just stop at rank seven True Dragon. Instead, he pushed to rank nine True Dragon in a single breath. He was now only a step off from reaching Heavenly Dragon.","Sikong Changsheng was flabbergasted.","“He made so many breakthroughs?”","Chu Feng stood up and inspected the changes in him. Despite having made so many breakthroughs within a short span of time, he found that he could easily channel his rank nine True Dragon World Spiritist’s psyche.","“That legacy is incredible!”","Even Chu Feng was awed.","In truth, he had intentionally tried to slow his breakthrough earlier, knowing that advancing too fast could destabilize his foundation. Even when a shortcut to reach greater heights dangled in front of him, he still made sure to advance slow and steadily lest problems emerged.","Despite his carefulness, he still advanced straight to rank nine True Dragon World Spiritist.","But when he realized that the legacy was so powerful that it didn’t even destabilize his foundation, he immediately regretted pacing himself. If he had just gone all out, there might have been a chance he could reach Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","Granted that such a breakthrough would likely result in an unstable foundation, and that might come back to bite him in the future, but his objective for seeking the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy was to reach Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","That was the minimum requirement for him to contract with the Spirit God Clansmen, so that they could release their sealed power and recover.","However, that regret only remained for an instant.","There was no point crying over what couldn’t be changed. Not to mention, the Spirit God Clansmen wouldn’t have wanted Chu Feng to compromise his potential to save them, especially since there was still time to spare.","“How are you feeling, Chu Feng?” Sikong Changsheng made his way to Chu Feng’s side.","“Elder, this legacy is formidable. I made six breakthroughs in a single shot and am now at rank nine True Dragon.” Chu Feng opened his palm and revealed his spirit power.","“Of course. Do you know how many of our experts died to obtain this power? You got lucky,” Sikong Changsheng said.","He neglected to mention that none of the experts of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect had been able to assimilate the legacy.","Just then, Eggy opened her eyes. Her following words made Sikong Changsheng so mad that he nearly collapsed to the floor.","“Chu Feng, why are you only at rank nine True Dragon?”","“Only... What do you mean by only? Chu Feng raised his spirit power from rank three True Dragon to rank nine! Do you know how long it took those rank nine True Dragon World Spiritists out there to reach their current level?” Sikong Changsheng questioned.","“Old man, I know that rank nine True Dragon World Spiritists are incredible. It’s because it is your Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect that I harbor higher expectations... but I guess rank nine True Dragon is not too bad. It’s acceptable,” Eggy replied with a smile.","Sikong Changsheng didn’t know how to respond. This was neither a compliment nor a praise.","“Old man, we’re only a step away from reaching Heavenly Dragon now. If you have anything good, take it out and help Chu Feng advance to Heavenly Dragon,” Eggy said.","“Lass, don’t get too greedy. Steady progress is the key to building a strong foundation for the future. I believe Chu Feng understands that as well, right?”","Sikong Changsheng looked at Chu Feng, only to see the latter looking at him with expectant eyes.","“Elder, my foundation is very sturdy. I’m more than happy to accept anything you have that can help me advance my spirit power,” Chu Feng said.","“You two... are really... Birds of the feather flock together!” Sikong Changsheng sighed.","But Chu Feng still pressed on. “Do you have it or not, elder?”","“Of course not! You grew up in the world of cultivation; you should know what it means to be a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. How can it be that easy to reach that level? It’s only a matter of time before you reach that level, so there’s no need to rush,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“But I’m in a rush, elder,” Chu Feng said.","“There’s nothing I can do. You’re on your own,” Sikong Changsheng replied helplessly.","Chu Feng chuckled. He turned to Eggy and asked, “What about you, Eggy? Did you get anything good?”","“We’ll talk later.” Eggy opened the gate to his World Spirit Space and stepped in.","“How mysterious,” Sikong Changsheng remarked.","Chu Feng looked at Sikong Changsheng and asked, “Elder, what legacy did she obtain?”","“I’m curious to know as well,” Sikong Changsheng replied.","“All right. I’ll ask her.”","Chu Feng projected his consciousness into his World Spirit Space, only to see Eggy holding a scroll. Eggy had blocked the name of the scroll with her energy, so Chu Feng couldn’t tell what it was.","“Is that what you got, Eggy?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yup.” Eggy nodded.","“Is it a world spirit’s martial skill?”","“You can consider it so.”","“Why are you keeping me in suspense? What kind of skill is it?”","“It’s a secret. You just have to know that I’m satisfied with this.”","Eggy’s smile was so sweet that Chu Feng thought his heart would melt. Her face was so beautiful that he could spend his entire life staring at it.","“Fine. As long as our Eggy is satisfied.”","“Chu Feng, don’t you have other matters to attend to? You should go out and check on your friends. Shoo shoo, I’m going to cultivate now,” Eggy said as she unfurled the scroll.","“Yes, Milady Queen. I’ll be taking my leave.” Chu Feng retracted his consciousness from his World Spirit Space.","Sikong Changsheng stared intently at Chu Feng. “So, what is it?”","All he knew about Eggy’s legacy was that it was Shangguan Fengquan’s means. Having witnessed Shangguan Fengquan’s true strength, he was extremely curious about what that legacy entailed.","“It’s a world spirit’s martial skill, but my Eggy refuses to elaborate on the details. It should be quite powerful.”","“Definitely powerful,” Sikong Changsheng replied affirmatively.","“Elder, I’d like to meet my friends.”","“Follow me.”","Sikong Changsheng rose into the air, and Chu Feng followed him."]},{"number":6512,"title":"Chapter 6512: Chapter 6510: Chu Feng’s Capability","paragraphs":["Chapter 6510: Chu Feng’s Capability","This time, Chu Feng was able to venture deeper into the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city without being teleported back to his starting point. He passed through dense clusters of buildings and finally arrived before a square.","The square was enveloped in a formidable power, and in it were Long Chengyu and the others.","“Chu Feng, how are you?” Long Chengyu and the others, despite being in the middle of their treatment, rushed up to Chu Feng to enquire about his condition.","“I’m fine,” Chu Feng replied as he revealed his spirit power.","“You are... at rank nine True Dragon?”","Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, Xia Xingcheng, the Totem’s Nine Daoists, and the others were shocked. In particular, the Totem’s Nine Daoists were in disbelief.","“If you have reached rank nine True Dragon at such a young age, I can’t even imagine the heights you’ll attain in the future. How vexing it is to be born in the same era as you! ” Daoist Ninth Dragon remarked with an exaggerated expression.","“It’s the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy, after all. That’s the true behemoth of the world of cultivation right there! I wouldn’t have expected anything less from them,” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Exactly! The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion only began pulling their weight after the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect left. If the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect was still here, I bet the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion wouldn’t even dare let out a squeak!” Xia Xingchen exclaimed.","“Hahaha!”","The others burst into laughter.","Even though they had nearly lost their lives earlier, they were safe now. The remarks thrown back and forth lightened the atmosphere, and learning that Chu Feng had joined the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect was yet another cause of celebration.","But Chu Feng’s gaze fell upon Huahua. The latter usually enjoyed commotions, but she was brooding over something right now. She was examining Daoist Starseizer’s condition, and Jie Shanxian was lying next to Daoist Starseizer as well.","Chu Feng flitted through the crowd and went to Daoist Starseizer’s and Jie Shanxian’s side.","“Chu Feng, I only ended up troubling you.”","“Don’t say that, elder. I know you returned to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion for my sake. If anyone is to be blamed, it is Jie Tianran. You can be assured that I’ll eventually settle the scores with Jie Tianran over this,” Chu Feng declared as he looked at Jie Shanxian and Jie Tiannian.","Their poor conditions left him with a heavy heart.","“Chu Feng, I can’t find the location gu in my master’s body,” Huahua said.","She was looking for the location gu in Daoist Starseizer’s body. Until the location gu was extracted, they wouldn’t be safe.","“Let me give it a try.”","Chu Feng grabbed Daoist Starseizer’s wrist to search for the location gu, but he couldn’t find anything at all.","“Allow me.”","Sikong Changsheng suddenly appeared. He placed his spirit power-infused palm on Daoist Starseizer’s dantian, suffusing the latter’s body with light.","The crowd gasped in shock. This legendary elder was indeed formidable.","But Sikong Changsheng soon replied, “I can’t find anything.”","“Was Jie Tianran lying?” Xia Xingchen asked.","“That is very likely.”","Sikong Changsheng was stronger than Jie Tianran. If even he couldn’t find the so-called location gu, the chances were that the location gu didn’t exist at all.","“Let me try again,” Chu Feng said.","He formed a hand seal and activated the Three Realms Divine Eyes.","Moments later, he said, “I found it.”","“The location gu?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","“That’s right.”","Chu Feng proceeded to inspect Jie Shanxian and Jie Tiannian. Jie Tiannian didn’t have the location gu, but both Daoist Starseizer and Jie Shanxian had been planted with location gus.","“Chu Feng, are you certain about it?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","He was confident in his observation means. It didn’t bode well if the location gus truly existed, as if meant that Jie Tianran’s means were above his despite his weaker spirit power.","“Yes, the location gus exist. They are very discreetly hidden,” Chu Feng replied. He wouldn’t have found the location gus either if not for his Three Realms Divine Eyes.","“Where are they?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","“They are constantly moving along with the soul,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s bizarre!”","“Let me try removing them.”","Chu Feng supported Daoist Starseizer and Jie Shanxian till they were sitting upright. He placed his palm on their backs, hoping to use Qin Jiu’s Hundred Methods of Gu Control to remove their location gus.","This method allowed him to track the location gus, but he was unable to remove them.","“My spirit power is still too weak. I need to reach Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist at minimum,” Chu Feng replied with a sigh.","The Hundred Methods of Gu Control did work on Jie Tianran’s location gu, but the gap in their spirit power was too great.","“Chu Feng, are there location gus planted on the others?” Jie Shanxian weakly asked.","Those words left a bitter taste in Chu Feng’s mouth. Both Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer had shown great kindness to him, but because of Jie Tianran, they lost their spirit power. That was fatal for someone of their age; their days were numbered.","“Elder, there are no location gus on the others,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s good, that’s good. You can stop frowning now. Starseizer and I, we know that our days are numbered. Rather than dragging you down, we’d rather you send us on our way so that we can depart with a dignified front,” Jie Shanxian said.","The crowd was stunned.","Jie Tiannian anxiously exclaimed, “Elder, you mustn’t!”","She had utmost respect for Jie Shanxian.","“Master...” Huahua tightly held Daoist Starseizer’s hand. She had a feeling that her master shared the same thought as Jie Shanxian.","“Huahua, Lord Jie Shanxian’s will is also my will. I was useless. Not only was I of no help, but I was even exploited by Jie Tianran and nearly caused your deaths. I can’t continue dragging you down anymore,” Daoist Starseizer said.","“Enough. What’s with all this melancholy? It’s not as if the location gu can’t be lifted. Didn’t Chu Feng already say that he can lift it once he reaches Heavenly Dragon?” Sikong Changsheng said.","“Elder.” Jie Shanxian looked at Sikong Changsheng with respect.","Even she, who was practically a living fossil in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, had to address Sikong Changsheng as ‘elder’.","“I trust that Chu Feng will eventually reach Heavenly Dragon, but Jie Tianran will not wait that long to make a move,” Jie Shanxian said.","“I know what you’re worried about. So be it if you have location gus in your body. You can stay in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. He can’t get in here anyway, so there’s nothing to fear,” Sikong Changsheng said.","Everyone’s eyes lit up, including Chu Feng.","“Elder, can they stay here?” Chu Feng asked.","“Did I say that I’d chase them off?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","“Thank you, elder!” Chu Feng grinned.","“Elder, you’re dashing,” Xia Xingchen added.","Others dared not speak so casually to Sikong Changsheng out of deference for him, but their joy was palpable, especially for Huahua.","Not even Jie Tianran could breach the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, or else he wouldn’t have gone through the trouble of collecting the key fragments. If they could stay here, they would be safe from Jie Tianran.","“You can thank Chu Feng for that.” Sikong Changsheng handed a key to Chu Feng. “From now on, you can enter this city whenever you like.”"]},{"number":6513,"title":"Chapter 6513: Chapter 6511: The Undying Starfield Appears","paragraphs":["Chapter 6511: The Undying Starfield Appears","“Sure!” Chu Feng took the key.","“Feed this to the three of them.”","Sikong Changsheng handed three pills that prolonged longevity to Chu Feng. That was exactly what Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer urgently needed right now.","“Elder, you’re a wonderful person,” Chu Feng said gratefully as he took the pills.","“Don’t try to flatter me.” Sikong Changsheng rolled his eyes.","Chu Feng quickly fed the pills to Jie Shanxian, Daoist Starseizer, and Jie Tiannian.","The pills were more potent than he had imagined. Not only did it increase their lifespans, but their complexions also looked much better.","“Thank you, elder. Thank you.” Huahua kowtowed to Sikong Changsheng out of gratitude.","“If you want to thank someone, thank Chu Feng instead. I wouldn’t have intervened if not for him. Also, you aren’t allowed to leave this square. Just because I took you in doesn’t mean that you can act as you please,” Sikong Changsheng said as he took his leave.","Huahua wiped off her tears and beamed a smile at Chu Feng. “I shan’t thank you yet. I’ll do it when you remove the location gu from my master.”","“Sure.” Chu Feng nodded. He turned his gaze to the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and the others, “Elder, where is Bai Yunqing and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan?”","They were probably fine, or else Long Chengyu and the others would have told them by now, but he still had to ask for his heart to be at ease.","“Ah, I nearly forgot to tell you. Bai Yunqing, Miss Yu’er, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, and the others returned after the Immemorial Cemetery closed. Shortly after, Miss Yu’er and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan told us that they needed to leave for a while due to a matter in the clan.","“Before they left, they left me with a letter for you,” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief said.","He handed the letter to Chu Feng.","It was a unique letter that could only be opened with Chu Feng’s aura. Chu Feng opened the letter, and its contents flowed through his palm into his head. Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, their parents, and grandfather appeared in his head.","“Young friend Chu Feng, our clansmen have received a summons urging us to return to our ancestral land,” Little Fishy’s father said.","“But you don’t have to worry about us. This summons likely symbolizes something good,” Little Fishy’s mother added.","“ Likely ? It is definitely something good, grandson-in-law,” Little Fishy’s grandfather said.","“My grandfather is right, big brother. You don’t need to worry about us. We’ll look for you once we’re done here,” Little Fishy said with a vibrant smile.","“You just have to wait for us!” Xianhai Shaoyu grinned.","All of them were in high spirits, probably because they knew it was something good.","“What’s going on, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","Only Chu Feng could see the earlier message, so Eggy couldn’t help but be worried. She had always been more concerned about Little Fishy.","Chu Feng told Eggy about the message.","“Again? There must be something special about their ancestral land?” Eggy said.","“What about Bai Yunqing?” Chu Feng continued probing.","“Young friend Bai Yunqing mentioned that he had to leave for a while to attend to other matters as well. He has also left a letter for you,” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief said as he handed over a letter.","It was an ordinary letter containing a simple message.","Big brother Chu Feng, I wish to pay a visit to Miss Wu. Please don’t worry about me. I’ll be back as soon as possible.","—Your beloved little brother, Bai Yunqing.","“How did Bai Yunqing get into contact with the Black-feathered Specter?” Eggy remarked.","Bai Yunqing had a crush on a lady named Miss Wu, but Chu Feng suspected that Miss Wu was the Black-feathered Specter who cursed Bai Liluo.","“I think it’s a good thing, no matter how they got into contact with each other,” Chu Feng said with a smile.","He had interacted with Li Wu; she didn’t seem to be a bad person despite being an enigmatic figure. Otherwise, she wouldn’t have handed the power to lift Bai Liluo’s curse to him. It wouldn’t be a bad thing if Bai Yunqing could win Li Wu’s heart.","“Chu Feng.”","Sikong Changsheng, who had left the square earlier, suddenly rushed back.","“What’s wrong, elder?” Chu Feng asked.","The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and the others immediately tensed up. Something must have happened, given Sikong Changsheng’s grim expression, and the chances were that it was related to Jie Tianran.","“Come with me,” Sikong Changsheng said as he walked away from the square.","A barrier had been constructed around the square to prevent Long Chengyu and the others from wandering around the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, but it didn’t obstruct Chu Feng’s movements.","Chu Feng followed Sikong Changsheng to a great tower that rose into the sky. As soon as they stepped into the tower, they were transported to its peak.","It felt like they had left the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city to arrive in outer space. Everything could be clearly seen in this space. It was a humongous observation formation that could be used to keep track of everything ongoing in the world of cultivation!","This observation formation was not sharp enough to peer into individual realms, but it allowed one to keep tabs on major events happening in the world of cultivation.","Two conspicuous phenomena could be seen right away.","One was God’s Era.","Its humongous silhouette continued to tower over the Seven Realms Galaxy, shining brighter than ever. A visible energy spiral could be seen swirling within the silhouette. Three gates could be vaguely seen within the energy spiral, each one larger than a starfield.","However, the gates looked intangible, and it was uncertain whether one could enter them or not.","The other one was coming from the Bloodline Galaxy.","An incredible spirit power was raging within a humongous formation. Shockingly, the humongous formation contained several stars inside, or perhaps, it might be more accurate to say that it contained an entire starfield.","“The Undying Starfield,” Chu Feng murmured.","“Indeed, it is the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Undying Starfield. Someone took it away a while back and did something remarkable with it using the Bloodline Galaxy,” Sikong Changsheng said.","And indeed, the humongous formation was siphoning energy from the entire Bloodline Galaxy."]},{"number":6514,"title":"Chapter 6514: Chapter 6512: Pointing Toward the Chu Heavenly Clan’s Forbidden Land","paragraphs":["Chapter 6512: Pointing Toward the Chu Heavenly Clan’s Forbidden Land","“It’s the Netherworld Sect,” Chu Feng said.","He knew that the Netherworld Sect had taken the Undying Starfield, and that they planned to use it for something. He told Sikong Changsheng everything he knew, including the fact that the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy was in the Undying Starfield’s Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","“The Netherworld Sect has lain low until this day. They must be up to something huge,” Sikong Changsheng remarked.","“Elder, are you familiar with the Netherworld Sect?” Chu Feng asked.","Someone who had lived through the ages was bound to be much more knowledgeable.","“There were traces of the Netherworld Sect even in the earlier years of the current era. They were already mysterious back then. They didn’t occupy any territories, and they didn’t compete for remnants, either. But I know they were strong; they just chose to maintain a low profile.","“Even after our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect left for the Ninth Galaxy, the Netherworld Sect continued to maintain a low profile. It’s only a thousand years ago that they suddenly changed their demeanor. They began to scourge young prodigies by planting their so-called Netherworld Embryos in their bodies at a large scale.","“There isn’t much information about them from the earlier years of the present era due to their limited activity. Later on, I couldn’t observe much in the world of cultivation due to my injuries, so I’m afraid my understanding of them is limited.","“I suspect that the Netherworld Sect is at least on par with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, if not stronger. It’s no easy feat to pull off something of this scale,” Sikong Changsheng said as he examined the revealed Undying Starfield.","“The Netherworld Sect is indeed unfathomable, but it matters not to me as long as they don’t provoke me. I only want the legacy in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm,” Chu Feng said.","“Are you planning to head to the Undying Starfield?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Chu Feng, I have a doubt.”","“Feel free to speak.”","“Do you have no interest in God’s Era’s power?”","“How can anyone possibly not be interested in God’s Era’s power?”","“If so, why do you want to visit the Undying Starfield’s Flowersea Ordinary Realm first when there is already a stir in God’s Era?","“I have heard of the Great Monster Slayer Emperor. Yes, he made a name for himself in the earlier years of the present era with his Monster Slayer Sword, but that’s all there is to it. The legacy he left behind can’t be better than our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s.","“You have two choices here—God’s Era or the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy. No matter how I look at it, God’s Era is the wiser choice,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“I possess the Monster Slayer Sword, which is the key to opening the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s tomb. Only I can retrieve the legacy now. Since the Great Monster Slayer Emperor has chosen me, I ought to claim the legacy even if it’s not of any help to me. I can’t let his legacy remain buried like that,” Chu Feng said.","“You’re quite the sentimental one.” Sikong Changsheng couldn’t say anything to that, but he still asked, “Why did you suddenly give up on God’s Era halfway through the last time?”","Chu Feng had entered God’s Era when it last opened. He triggered the Heaven Ladder and induced a huge phenomenon. Given his accomplishments, it felt like he could have benefited from God’s Era if he had continued, but he had chosen to give up.","“Elder, you can tell that I gave up?” Chu Feng asked.","While those outside God’s Era could see the situation inside then, they were unable to see through the details. Most thought that Chu Feng had failed the challenge and was eliminated.","“Do I look like a fool to you?” Sikong Changsheng glared at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng chuckled before continuing, “I vaguely sensed God’s Era’s true power at the end of the path I have chosen.”","“Why did you give up then?!” Sikong Changsheng felt shocked and angered.","“I know my limits. I was not remotely confident of obtaining that power. Advancing further will bring me nothing but pain, so I gave up,” Chu Feng replied.","Chu Feng didn’t reveal everything he knew.","Before entering God’s Era, he had already deciphered that he needed to first obtain an activation item before he could obtain God’s Era’s final power. Without the activation item, his efforts were doomed to be in vain.","Chu Feng tried searching for the activation item but to no avail. Knowing it was futile to proceed, he chose to give up.","Consequently, this was also why he didn’t think Jie Tianran could obtain God’s Era’s final power. He was confident that Jie Tianran couldn’t find the activation item when it had eluded him.","“I see.”","Sikong Changsheng breathed a sigh of relief, knowing that Chu Feng’s brain was still functioning well. Only a fool wouldn’t claim God’s Era’s final power when it was within sight.","“I’ll enter God’s Era if it opens again. I’m hoping to obtain its power as well,” Chu Feng said.","“It’s not without reason that even powerhouses from the Ancient Era failed to obtain God’s Era’s power. It is indeed an extremely challenging trial. Nevertheless, obtaining such a power is bound to serve you well in the future. You shouldn’t miss it if a chance presents itself,” Sikong Changsheng advised.","All of a sudden, Chu Feng sensed something from his Dao Creation Palace.","He had ventured into the Immemorial Land of Dao Creation with Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu. The others had constructed Dao Creation Pavilions, but he had constructed a Dao Creation Palace.","No more than ten people had constructed Dao Creation Pavilions in the Ancient Era.","And as for Dao Creation Palaces? None.","That was how significant Chu Feng’s Dao Creation Palace was.","Little Fishy and the others had received benefits from their Dao Creation Pavilions, but Chu Feng’s Dao Creation Palace hadn’t given him anything yet. Despite having obtained the biggest treasure, it turned out to be useless.","A while back, Chu Feng suddenly received guidance from his Dao Creation Palace. It pointed him to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, but it didn’t go any further than that.","Now, the guidance has become much more precise. It was pointing to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Ancestral Martial Lower Realm, the Chu Heavenly Clan’s forbidden land.","“Eggy, the Dao Creation Palace has given me precise guidance,” Chu Feng hurriedly said.","“Guidance? To where?” Eggy asked.","“To the Chu Heavenly Clan’s forbidden land,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6515,"title":"Chapter 6515: Chapter 6513: Returning to the Eastern Sea Region","paragraphs":["Chapter 6513: Returning to the Eastern Sea Region","“The Chu Heavenly Clan’s forbidden land? Haven’t you already visited that place with Zi Ling, but there was nothing there? Could it be that you have reached the required level to obtain the legacy and awaken your bloodline? Quick, let’s stop dawdling and head there!” Eggy’s eyes gleamed with excitement.","“My thoughts exactly.”","Having made up his mind, Chu Feng bade farewell to Sikong Changsheng, Long Chengyu, and the others.","As Long Chengyu and the others were limited to the square, only Sikong Changsheng was able to send Chu Feng off.","“Here’s a gift, Chu Feng.”","Sikong Changsheng pulled out a bamboo tube and a bamboo boat with a wave of his sleeves. The bamboo tube was the controlling tool for the bamboo boat, and the words ‘Qin Jiu’ were inscribed on it.","“Woah, the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect really has all kinds of good stuff!” Eggy exclaimed in awe.","Jie Shanxian had a similar bamboo boat, and it moved faster than ordinary teleportation formations. With it, there was no need to rely on teleportation formations anymore. One could simply channel the bamboo boat and head anywhere they wanted.","And this bamboo boat was larger than Jie Shanxian’s, spanning around ten meters in length. Needless to say, it was more valuable. It was a bona fide treasure.","“Elder, you’re giving this to me?” Chu Feng was astonished, though he continued looking at Sikong Changsheng with hopeful eyes.","This treasure was too valuable, though it didn’t change the fact that he wanted it.","“It is my own possession. Consider it a personal gift,” Sikong Changsheng emphasized.","“Elder, you treat me too well. I’ll surely take care of you till you age away!” Chu Feng was so excited that he leaped forward to embrace Sikong Changsheng.","“Those are words of filial piety, but somehow, I feel uncomfortable hearing them from you. Enough. You should hurry along. Be careful. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has people stationed all over the eight galaxies. Who knows what they are planning?” Sikong Changsheng said.","“I’ll be careful.”","Chu Feng channeled the bamboo boat and made his way to the Chu Heavenly Clan.","Even as Chu Feng’s silhouette vanished into space, Sikong Changsheng continued staring in his direction. Moments later, he made up his mind and murmured, “Now that he’s a junior of our Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, I can’t turn a blind eye to his affairs anymore. Lord Sectmaster, I’ll do everything I can to protect him.”","With that, Sikong Changsheng entered a training forbidden land in the main city. His priority at hand was to repair his bloodline, treat his injuries, and recover his strength.","...","A massive warship carrying the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s flag floated amid space. Gathered on this warship were members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion who had been at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city earlier.","This warship was equipped with an observation formation, and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s experts were observing God’s Era and the Undying Starfield through it.","Jie Tianran was also onboard this warship.","“God’s Era is reacting more strongly than before. There will be a new home for its power very soon,” the old entity told Jie Tianran.","“Head to the Bloodline Galaxy, where the starfield has appeared,” Jie Tianran ordered.","The warship immediately changed its direction.","“You aren’t going to God’s Era?” the old entity asked in confusion.","“God’s Era isn’t fully opened yet. There’s no point heading there now. Besides, I’m the only one who can obtain its power. Rather, I’m more curious to know what the Netherworld Sect is hiding. They are our greatest rival here,” Jie Tianran said.","“Do you intend to foil their awakening?” the old entity asked.","“No, I’ll help them and, in the process of doing so, control them. They shall fall under my command,” Jie Tianran declared confidently.","His earlier failure at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city didn’t seem to faze him.","...","Chu Feng arrived before a raging sea.","It was the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm’s Eastern Sea Region.","He had been here with Zi Ling not too long ago, but whenever he stood above this sea and experienced the familiar sea breeze, he couldn’t help but reminisce about the past.","He would think about the first time he ventured into this Eastern Sea Region with Eggy, his first meeting with Little Fishy, his battle with the Immortal Execution Archipelago, and Jiang Qisha.","The strong foes that he had nearly succumbed to were now not worth a mention, but those memories continued to occupy his mind. He had gone through a lot here and met many friends.","Though his friends and kin were nowhere to be seen now. They were all trapped at a place where Chu Feng hadn’t been able to find yet. He didn’t think that the person who captured them had bad intentions, but it was inevitable that he would worry about them until he finally found them.","Chu Feng suddenly felt bitter.","He thought about Su Rou and Su Mei. Those two had been captured by the Moon Immortal, and he hadn’t heard from them in a long time. I wonder where they are.","A gate suddenly appeared, and Eggy walked out. She first stretched her back before remarking, “Of all the sea breezes I have felt, the Eastern Sea Region’s one is still the most comfortable. It would have been better if Yu’er and Zi Ling were here as well. We could have had a drink.”","“Milady Queen, have you gotten addicted to alcohol after sharing a drink with Sectmaster Shangguan?” Chu Feng asked with a smile.","“I’m still not fond of drinking, though it’s not too bad drinking with people I’m fond of.” Eggy looked at Chu Feng with a subtly sweet smile.","“Sure, let’s have a drink with them one day. It won’t be just Zi Ling and Yu’er but Su Rou, Su Mei, and my other friends as well. But Milady Queen, you’ll have to first return for now,” Chu Feng said.","“Are you entering now? All the best. I hope that you’ll get something good out of it this time.”","The Chu Heavenly Clan’s forbidden land was surrounded by a barrier that restricted access to all but him. So, Eggy had to return to his World Spirit Space in order to tag along.","“This seems to be it.”","Upon entering the forbidden land, Chu Feng felt a response from his Dao Creation Palace.","“Do you feel the energy to awaken your bloodline?” Eggy asked.","“Let me try sensing it.”","Chu Feng had learned from experience how to locate the energy hidden in this place. He sat down with crossed legs and focused. He couldn’t feel anything at first, but over time, the energy hidden here slowly became salient to him.","It was as if he had come into contact with a brand-new world. That was how tremendous the energy was. He felt like a fish entering an ocean; he could hardly tell how huge the ocean was.","It was unfathomable in the truest sense of the word.","But that appeared to be Chu Feng’s current limit. He couldn’t decipher anything else from the energy or commune with it. It was as if an invisible gate was standing in his way, blocking his path.","“I still can’t overcome this hurdle despite having advanced my cultivation so much?” Chu Feng frowned.","Just then, his Dao Creation Palace quivered, and his surroundings changed."]},{"number":6516,"title":"Chapter 6516: Chapter 6514: A Palace That Can House the World of Cultivation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6514: A Palace That Can House the World of Cultivation","Chu Feng’s consciousness was transported to above a golden ocean.","The waves here were much calmer compared to the Eastern Sea Region, for its water was suffusing with concentrated natural energies, to the point where they condensed to form this boundless golden ocean.","Chu Feng had never felt such rich natural energies before.","No cultivator could withstand this temptation.","Chu Feng quickly formed a hand seal and attempted to assimilate the natural energies.","“Fuck.”","Chu Feng rarely cursed. He had expected as much, but he still felt incredibly displeased when he confirmed that he was unable to tap into the natural energies here for his cultivation.","“Hm?”","Chu Feng’s eyebrows suddenly shot up. He noticed the natural energies were flowing toward a common direction.","So, he got up and quickly found the place where the natural energies were converging at.","The sheer amount of natural energies here was so great that he heard a wondrous yet earth-shattering roaring sound.","It was more than just a sound; it was the majesty behind it. It felt like a terrible hurricane raging through the lands, a massive waterfall gushing from the sky, and two armies tearing each other apart. That was the grandeur he felt from it.","The sound was loud but not noisy. If anything, Chu Feng felt energized and excited.","This was all natural energies!","But he was unable to approach the natural energies any further. An invisible layer of energy blocked his path as if a barrier. He couldn’t reach the center of the converging natural energies.","Boom!","Something suddenly exploded within Chu Feng’s dantian.","The sky stirred. The white fog scattered, revealing the vast space hiding beneath it. This space was devoid of stars, but it was incredibly familiar to Chu Feng.","This was the world within Chu Feng’s dantian, just that it didn’t contain the nine-colored lightning or the Sacred Tree Seed.","Just then, a massive silhouette appeared in the sky. It was initially blurry, but it slowly grew clearer as it descended.","It was a black palace that emanated an air of majesty, shrouded in a black aura that crackled with nine-colored lightning. It felt divine yet demonic at the same time, and the air of loftiness it exuded signalled that of its extraordinariness.","Two words were inscribed on the palace’s plaque—Asura Palace!","“Asura Palace?”","Chu Feng recognized this palace. He had personally constructed and named it, after all. It was his Dao Creation Palace.","The Asura Palace landed behind Chu Feng.","Whoosh!","The doors opened, revealing another realm within. It was chaotic, boundless, and filled with endless possibilities.","“This feeling... Is it beckoning me in?”","Chu Feng felt a tug from the door, so he made his way over. But when he walked up to the door, he realized that he was unable to step into the Asura Palace’s chaotic and unformed world.","Weng!","Energy suddenly pulsated from the gate, rippling outward to form a path of clearly partitioned black aura and nine-colored lightning.","“My path is related to the energy inside the Chu Heavenly Clan’s forbidden land.”","Chu Feng could see why his Dao Creation Palace guided him here.","The path soon collided with the barrier blocking Chu Feng’s path, causing the black aura and nine-colored lightning to abruptly erupt upward. However, the path didn’t stop there just because of that. It relentlessly crashed against the barrier, determined to pave a way forward.","At the same time, a huge vortex began to swirl as a result of the clash. As the vortex spun faster, it created something reminiscent of a window that allowed Chu Feng to glimpse into the areas that he was unable to access.","It was an incomparably colossal palace, so much so that it could house the entire world of cultivation. Realms that housed many mountains, rivers, and countless lives looked insignificant as if a speck of dust inside the colossal palace.","Even Chu Feng, who thought that he had seen much of what the world had to offer, felt his heartbeat hastening. He instinctively felt excited and nervous.","To think that there’s something this huge in the world!","He felt like he had seen a different side to the world of cultivation, but at the same time, he couldn’t help but wonder who resided inside this colossal palace.","GRAR!","A lightning beast suddenly roared.","The path extending from the Asura Palace immediately collapsed, and the Asura Palace disintegrated. The sky reverted to its original state. Chu Feng’s consciousness also returned to its main body.","“What a powerful lightning beast. To think that our Chu Heavenly Clan’s forbidden land possesses such tremendous power!” Chu Feng was excited.","“What are you saying, Chu Feng? What did you see?” Eggy asked out of curiosity as she was unaware of what Chu Feng had just witnessed.","Chu Feng told her what he had just seen.","“I see. That vast energy must be the legacy that can help you awaken your Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. But you still can’t obtain it, not even with the aid of the Dao Creation Palace?” Eggy asked.","“I’ll give it another try,” Chu Feng said.","He tried sensing the surrounding energy once more. The same situation happened, but his consciousness was once again transported back to his main body when the lightning beast roared.","He made a few more attempts, but the outcome was the same.","“It’s not working. My cultivation might still be too weak to obtain the legacy. I’ll have to try again after reaching Heavenly God level.” Despite failing to obtain anything, Chu Feng remained in a good mood.","He had his guesses in the past, but this was the first time he had gotten a glimpse into how formidable the energy inside the forbidden land was. He couldn’t wait to awaken his bloodline and harness all this energy.","Following that, Chu Feng made his way to the Bloodline Galaxy, though he didn’t enter the Undying Starfield right away. He had already inspected the vicinity; the Netherworld Sect had constructed a tight barrier around the Undying Starfield.","The barrier was constructed using powerful treasures and was nigh impossible to breach.","Chu Feng would have to find another way in.","So, he made his way to the agreed meeting location to look for Wen Xue. The latter had promised to find a way to bring him in."]},{"number":6517,"title":"Chapter 6517: Chapter 6515: The Cheeky Senior Sister","paragraphs":["Chapter 6515: The Cheeky Senior Sister","Wen Xue was nowhere to be found when Chu Feng arrived. Instead, a nearby commotion caught his attention.","A large group of people from different factions was gathered together.","Among them, an old man with a pockmarked face spat, “The bastard Netherworld Sect thinks that they are the masters of the Bloodline Galaxy now, doing as they please here. Those scum caused my cultivation speed to slow down by so much. They should pray that they never fall into my hands, or else I’m going to pull out their tendons and skin them alive! I’d eat their meat as well, but I bet beasts like them have sour meat!”","The crowd burst into laughter.","They were talking about the Undying Starfield. By now, they had already learned about the relationship between the Undying Starfield and the Netherworld Sect, as well as the fact that the Undying Starfield had been siphoning energy away from the Bloodline Galaxy.","They had noticed a slowdown in their cultivation speed in recent years, much to their distress. Who could have thought it would be due to the Netherworld Sect stealing their natural energies? That was as good as robbing the potential of the Bloodline Galaxy’s cultivators!","Even so, they only dared to grumble. None dared to confront the Netherworld Sect. The only thing they would do was to leave the Bloodline Galaxy and develop elsewhere.","“You’re slow, junior,” a voice echoed.","Shockingly, it was from the pockmarked old man who berated the Netherworld Sect with great anger. He parted ways from the crowd and flew away.","Chu Feng quickly followed that old man.","Once there was no one else around them, the pockmarked old man waved his sleeves and shrouded the two of them in an isolation barrier.","“Senior.”","Chu Feng was certain the pockmarked old man was Wen Xue.","“It’s me,” Wen Xue turned around and replied.","“Why did you transform into this look?”","Chu Feng was taken aback by Wen Xue’s means. He couldn’t sense Wen Xue’s aura at all even now when he was right in front of her. Her ability to disguise herself was extraordinary.","“I am now a traitor of the Netherworld Sect. They have put a bounty on me. If I don’t disguise myself, should I sit around and wait for them to capture me instead?” Wen Xue asked.","Those words made sense, so Chu Feng changed the topic and remarked, “You came back fast.”","“That’s because I’m efficient.”","“Does that mean that you have found a way to enter the Undying Starfield?’","“Of course,” Wen Xue replied gleefully.","“How?” Chu Feng’s interest was piqued.","“Wear this.”","Wen Xue took out two sets of Netherworld Sect’s robes and bamboo veil hats.","“That’s all?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yup, that’s all.”","“But there’s a sealing formation around the Undying Starfield. Normal Netherworld Sectmembers can’t pass through the formation except through specific entrances.”","“Don’t you trust me?”","“Well... You didn’t help me in my fight against Jie Tianran inside the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant when you were capable of doing so. I still remember that clearly.”","“Tsk. Are you bringing up old scores now? Just trust me. It’ll work.”","“Fine.”","Chu Feng put on the Netherworld Sect’s clothes.","“All right. Let’s go,” Wen Xue said.","She dispelled the isolation barrier and concealed the two of them.","Just as Wen Xue was about to move, Chu Feng asked, “Senior, where are we heading to?”","“A teleportation formation, of course. We’re still some distance away from the Undying Starfield. It’d be too slow to travel there manually,” Wen Xue replied.","“There’s no need for that. I have something good,” Chu Feng said as he took out Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat. That was the gift he had just received from Sikong Changsheng.","“Woah! You have something this good?” Wen Xue exclaimed the moment she saw the boat.","“I just obtained it.”","“What else did you get? Let me open my eyes.”","“Spirit power.”","Chu Feng revealed his spirit power.","“No way. Rank nine True Dragon?”","Wen Xue’s eyes nearly bulged out as she punched Chu Feng’s arm. She didn’t hold back her strength. Chu Feng groaned in pain.","“What are you doing, senior?” Chu Feng rubbed his arm as he complained.","“You complained about me being untrustworthy, but aren’t you the same too? You hid your spirit power from me. You liar!” Wen Xue complained.","“I didn’t hide it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Are you seriously telling me that you made a breakthrough to rank nine True Dragon in the short span while you’re away?”","“It sounds shocking, but it’ll make perfect sense once you hear my story.”","Chu Feng told Wen Xue about what he had been through in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","“That makes a bit more sense now, but it still sounds ridiculous,” Wen Xue grumbled.","She quickly thought of something and began touching Chu Feng all around.","“What are you doing, senior?” Chu Feng was flustered.","“Junior, don’t you think you’re being too reckless with your breakthroughs? Let me check if that left any detrimental side effects on your body,” Wen Xue said with a grin.","Those words would have been more convincing if Wen Xue didn’t have a mischievous smile on, which signalled that she was up to no good.","“Stop messing around, senior. There’s more important matters at hand,” Chu Feng urged.","“Fine. I lack charm, and my junior isn’t drawn to women. That’s why other things are more important than this,” Wen Xue grumbled in dissatisfaction while boarding the bamboo boat.","Chu Feng channeled the bamboo boat, and it began to move.","“Milord, it’s not me! It’s not me! I was framed! Noooooo~~”","Cries of misery echoed from the surroundings.","Fights and deaths were commonplace in the world of cultivation. With Chu Feng’s sharp senses, he could easily pick up on all sorts of noises in his surroundings. He usually paid no attention to them, but this time, he looked over out of curiosity.","A pockmarked old man was lying on the ground, being beaten up by a group of Netherworld Sectmembers.","“You said that you’ll rip out our tendons and skin us alive? Try it then!”","The Netherworld Sectmembers struck the pockmarked old man with a thorned whip, leaving bloody gashes on his back. The pockmarked old man soon lost even the energy to scream, and it looked like he was on the verge of breathing his last.","Chu Feng recognized the pockmarked old man to be the same person Wen Xue had disguised herself as earlier.","“Senior, I thought that was just a random disguise,” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course not. That old man is a terrible person who commits all kinds of atrocities. I’m merely delivering justice to him,” Wen Xue replied with a cheeky grin.","That confirmed it.","Wen Xue had publicly insulted the Netherworld Sect not just to vent her anger but also to scheme against this old man. The old man likely deserved his punishment, since Wen Xue had said so."]},{"number":6518,"title":"Chapter 6518: Chapter 6516: Senior Sister’s Confidence","paragraphs":["Chapter 6516: Senior Sister’s Confidence","“How is your boat so fast?!”","Wen Xue’s eyes gleamed with excitement as the bamboo boat surged across space. She was so excited that she actually stood up.","“Sit still, senior,” Chu Feng advised, considering the small size of the boat.","“Yes sir.”","Wen Xue sat on the edge of the boat, with her legs dangling and kicking about outside the boat. Despite being an old monster, she was as mischievous as a child.","Chu Feng could do nothing about her.","“Junior, I heard you have a Netherworld Embryo implanted in you as well,” Wen Xue said.","“I do.” Chu Feng nodded.","“I happen to know a secret skill that utilizes the Netherworld Embryo to accelerate your cultivation speed. Do you want me to teach you?” Wen Xue asked.","“I’ll pass.” Chu Feng shook his head.","“What’s wrong? Are you not confident of learning it? Your talent is definitely up to scratch, so I think you should be able to grasp it quickly.”","“I have learned a method that focuses solely on my bloodline power. I can’t use other methods other than my bloodline to raise my cultivation.”","He was referring to the Dao of Specialization.","He possessed the Four Symbols Divine Body as well, but he no longer used it because of the Dao of Specialization. It was a huge tradeoff, but he wouldn’t have become this powerful if not for the Dao of Specialization, too.","“All right.” Wen Xue nodded. “What’s that method of yours? Why don’t you teach me?”","“I can’t teach you, or else I’d have already done so. You should also know that I’m not the kind to keep good things to myself. Speaking of which, how is your study of the Hundred Methods of Gu Control going?” Chu Feng asked.","“Will you believe me if I say that I have reached an even higher mastery in it than you?” Wen Xue asked with a smirk.","“I believe you,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Before long, Chu Feng and Wen Xue were already in the vicinity of the Undying Starfield’s entrance.","“Senior, do we really enter just like that? Are you sure it’ll work?” Chu Feng looked at Wen Xue with questioning eyes.","“Of course it won’t work, but there’s nothing to fear. I have a treasure,” Wen Xue replied.","“What treasure? It’s about time to take it out.”","“It’s a treasure that allows me to impeccably reconstruct others.”","Wen Xue waved her sleeves, and an individual appeared between the two of them.","Chu Feng took a few steps back out of shock. It was a familiar face. It was Wen Xue’s master, Netherworld Marshall Wuma Hanshuang.","While Chu Feng was confused, Wuma Hanshuang knelt to Chu Feng and kowtowed. “Wuma Hanshuang pays respect to Lord Chu Feng.”","“Did you construct her using the treasure?” Chu Feng looked at Wen Xue in astonishment.","The person before him looked and felt like Wuma Hanshuang, but she clearly wasn’t the real Wuma Hanshuang.","“It looks exactly like her, doesn’t it?” Wen Xue asked.","“Yeah. It’s perfectly identical.”","Chu Feng even tried touching the figure, but he couldn’t find any flaws in it. The other party felt exactly like Wuma Hanshuang.","“Chu Feng, this is unbelievable!” Eggy remarked.","“Seems like my senior is still hiding many things.” Chu Feng chuckled.","Little did they know that this Wuma Hanshuang was not a reconstructed figure; it was Wuma Hanshuang in the flesh. That was why the ‘impersonation’ was impeccable.","Wuma Hanshuang led the way forward, while Chu Feng and Wen Xue followed her as her lackeys.","“Senior, there’s a barrier in front.”","Before approaching the entrance, Chu Feng noticed through his Divine Eyes that the Undying Starfield was enveloped in an invisible barrier. They would be noticed as soon as they came into contact with the barrier.","The Undying Starfield was a smaller starfield compared to the others in the world of cultivation, but it was still an entire starfield and not a realm. It was a formidable feat to construct a barrier at this scale. It would take more than a single Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist to pull this off.","“A barrier? I don’t see it,” Wen Xue said.","“I wouldn’t lie to you about this,” Chu Feng replied.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion must have joined hands with the Netherworld Sect,” Wen Xue deduced.","“Is the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion the only power that has that many Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists?” Eggy asked.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is a powerhouse that has been around since the earlier years of the present era, after all. It has been steadily accruing power ever since the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect left for the Ninth Galaxy, and it is now the strongest power in the world of cultivation.","“World spiritists have the advantage when it comes to deciphering remnants. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion must have secured many legacies and cultivation resources over the years. They were weaker before because they were withholding their resources from the older generation.","“Given the accumulation of their world spiritists, they were bound to quickly reach Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists once they acquired the necessary resources,” Chu Feng said.","“Your analysis makes sense, but this doesn’t bode well for us,” Eggy grumbled.","She was worried about Chu Feng.","They had seen Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion aside from Jie Tianran back at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. Who could have thought that they would have even more Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists here?","On top of that, many forces had joined forces with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion now. Even Ancient Era’s powers struggled to rival them","“I’m fine. I have Elder Divine Deer’s protection. Mere Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists can’t hope to faze me. Besides, I’m not that far off from reaching Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist anymore,” Chu Feng smiled.","“That’s true.” Eggy nodded.","The rate at which Chu Feng was growing was amazing.","Once Chu Feng reached Heavenly Dragon or Heavenly God, it would be time to settle old scores.","Chu Feng turned to Wen Xue and asked, “Senior, did you not hear what I’m saying?”","He had warned Wen Xue about the barrier, but the latter didn’t slow in the least. “Aren’t you trying to say that there are powerful world spiritists helping the Netherworld Sect, right? That’s exactly what I told you—the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has joined hands with them.”","“That’s not what I mean. We’ll be discovered if we touch the barrier, senior. Someone from the Netherworld Sect will immediately head over to stop us. Are you sure your impersonated Wuma Hanshuang can intimidate them?” Chu Feng asked.","He was worried. He could already spot some experts from the Netherworld Sect in the vicinity, and they were bound to have formed an encirclement around the Undying Starfield. This hinted that the entire Netherworld Sect was practically here.","If they failed to enter this time, the Netherworld Sect would only further tighten their guard, making it harder for them to enter the next time.","“Don’t worry. Nothing will go wrong,” Wen Xue replied confidently."]},{"number":6519,"title":"Chapter 6519: Chapter 6517: I Feel It","paragraphs":["Chapter 6517: I Feel It","As soon as they came into contact with the barrier, teleportation energy swiftly converged in front of them and manifested into a spirit formation gate.","“I have underestimated the formation,” Chu Feng murmured.","To think that the barrier was equipped with a teleportation formation as well! The security around the Undying Starfield was at an astonishing level.","Several Netherworld Sectmembers emerged from the spirit formation gate and encircled them. One of them was a Heavenly God.","“Paying respect to Lord Wuma.”","When they realized it was Wuma Hanshuang, they hurriedly bowed deferentially to her.","“What a lineup. Are you here to apprehend me?” Wuma Hanshuang coldly asked.","“Milord, this is the formation constructed by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. A spirit formation gate will be automatically manifested whenever someone comes into contact with the barrier. Please pardon us if we have offended you,” the Heavenly God explained.","Wuma Hanshuang smiled. “You don’t need to be so tense. I’m joking with you. This place is of utmost importance to our Netherworld Sect. Trouble might come knocking now that it is revealed to the world, so it is only right for you to do your due diligence.”","“We will not let our guard down!” the Netherworld Sectmembers said in unison.","“What’s the current situation inside the starfield?” Wuma Hanshuang asked.","“Milord, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists are indeed capable. Not only did they reinforce our control over the Undying Starfield, but they even used the special nature of the Netherworld Embryo to construct a detection formation.","“Anyone who appears in the Undying Starfield without a Netherworld Embryo will be immediately detected and tracked,” the Heavenly God reported.","“Guarding against intruders is important, but what’s more crucial is awakening the power here. How is it going?” Wuma Hanshuang pressed on.","“Milord, we’re only responsible for guarding the formation. I’m afraid we don’t know what’s happening inside the starfield. However, I’ve heard that the sacred item has appeared, just that we haven’t been able to fully awaken its power yet.","“I’ve also heard that the natural oddity we captured a while back is finally working under the effects of the sacred item. That has greatly boosted the strength of our lords and prodigious juniors,” the Heavenly God reported.","“Good.” Wuma Hanshuang nodded.","“Lord Wuma, Lord Baili and Lord Xiahou are currently at the formation core. Are you going to look for them?” the Heavenly God asked.","“I’ll first check on the sacred treasure before paying respect to Lord Baili. Keep an eye here. Send a signal if anyone tries to barge in,” Wuma Hanshuang instructed.","“Understood.”","The Netherworld Sectmembers bowed respectfully.","With that, Wuma Hanshuang led Chu Feng and Wen Xue into the Undying Starfield.","The Netherworld Sectmembers didn’t even dare to look at Chu Feng or Wen Xue, let alone ask about their identities.","“Not bad. I can see that Wen Xue wasn’t slacking around while she was with Wuma Hanshuang. Her impersonation of the latter is impressive.” Eggy complimented her.","Wen Xue was able to extract useful information from the Netherworld Sectmembers in their earlier conversation.","“Indeed.” Chu Feng nodded while keeping a close eye on Wuma Hanshuang. This Wuma Hanshuang looks far too realistic.","“Senior, isn’t it weird how the Netherworld Sect suddenly has so many Heavenly God level cultivators?” Chu Feng asked in confusion.","He had clashed with the Netherworld Sect before, but it didn’t have so many experts back then.","Otherwise, Baili Zilin, as Baili Xukong’s son, should have far stronger experts guarding him rather than just Jimo Qianzhou. The only explanation was that the Netherworld Sect, like the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, had undergone a metamorphosis in recent days.","“Until a while back, the experts of the conservative faction, the new faction, and the neutral faction were still in closed-door training. They have gone into such closed-door training many times before, but they have always ended in failure. This time, however, they succeeded.","“They grasped a new method to further utilize the Netherworld Embryo’s power, which is the secret skill I wanted to teach you earlier. The Netherworld Sectmembers grew considerably stronger as a result,” Wen Xue explained.","It was pretty much the same as what Chu Feng had expected.","“However, the Netherworld Sect remains an enigmatic power. They refuse to divulge some information no matter how close you are to them, so what I know about them remains limited. It’s not just me. Take Wuma Hanshuang for instance, her position is only second to Baili Xukong in the new faction, but there are still many things that she doesn’t know about.","“That’s just how the Netherworld Sect operates,” Wen Xue said.","“Senior, do you know about the natural oddity they talked about?” Chu Feng asked.","“I heard my master mention it, but I didn’t expect them to really do it.”","“What is it?”","“While the Undying Starfield’s power hasn’t been fully awakened, its energy is already seeping out, just that it can’t be utilized. Thus, they have been thinking of ways to use the energy. This way, they would still benefit from this operation even if they fail to awaken the sacred item in the end.","“Baili Xukong has a godson named Zhao Feng. That fellow likes to dabble in unorthodox methods, and he found a way to utilize the energy. In gist, it involves using a medium to tap into the sacred item’s power. There are some risks involved, but some cultivators can accept that.","“The natural oddity is the most suited medium for that. It has unlocked its sentience and has started cultivating, just like me. It is the perfect medium to use,” Wen Xue said.","“I doubt the natural oddity is faring well after becoming a medium for someone else’s cultivation,” Chu Feng remarked.","“Of course. It’s the worst.”","“The Netherworld Sect still had the cheek to say that it wasn’t an unorthodox sect. Look at everything it has done,” Chu Feng spat.","“The conservative faction is still decent. It’s mainly the new faction that is messing around,” Wen Xue replied.","Soon, they arrived at the entrance of the Undying Starfield.","Many experts from the Netherworld Sect were gathered here. At a glance, Chu Feng could already spot many rank one Heavenly God level cultivators. There were bound to be stronger individuals hidden in the shadows.","Wuma Hanshuang could pass without a hitch thanks to her lofty stature.","As soon as Chu Feng entered a certain range of the Undying Starfield, he suddenly felt something.","“I feel it, Eggy,” Chu Feng said."]},{"number":6520,"title":"Chapter 6520: Chapter 6518: You Came All The Way Here For a Date?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6518: You Came All The Way Here For a Date?","“The Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s legacy?” Eggy asked.","“Yes, I can sense its position through the Monster Slayer Sword, but it might not be easy to reach it.”","As he sensed the location of the legacy, Chu Feng could also see with his eyes the arduous feat he had to undertake in order to reach it.","The Undying Starfield had been remodeled by powerful formations.","There were dark red light paths that could accelerate one’s movement speed to a level surpassing teleportation formation. However, all other locations aside from those that could be reached via these dark red light paths had been sealed off.","Chu Feng couldn’t unravel the seal with his current strength.","It just so happened that the Flowersea Ordinary Realm was located in a sealed region.","“Junior, where should we head to?” Wen Xue asked.","She was here to help Chu Feng acquire his legacy, so she was ready to listen to his dispatch.","“The area I want to head to has been sealed off,” Chu Feng relayed his observations to Wen Xue and Eggy.","“Not even a rank nine True Dragon World Spiritist like you can breach the seal?” Wen Xue asked.","“That’s no simple spirit power. It’s linked to a treasure. On top of that, I fear that I’d be discovered as soon as I attempt to breach it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Is that formation that formidable? Is it linked to that sacred item?” Wen Xue asked.","“Most likely so.”","Chu Feng looked at the dark red energy suffusing the starfield. It gave off an eerie feeling reminiscent of the Netherworld Embryo, but it was stronger and more unnerving.","“What should we do? Should we retreat? They might give up on the Undying Starfield once they awaken their sacred item. It’s not too late for us to return and retrieve the legacy then,” Wen Xue said.","“I don’t think the sacred item could have modified the Undying Starfield to this extent. The Netherworld Sect or the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion probably channeled the sacred item to achieve this effect. If I can come into contact with the sacred item, I should be able to alter its properties,” Chu Feng said.","“I know where the sacred item is,” Wen Xue said.","“I’ll be counting on you to lead me there,” Chu Feng replied with a grin.","The sacred item was very discreetly hidden. It would take him some time if he had to find it manually. He could opt to use the Three Realms Divine Eyes, but it was a borrowed power that would eventually run out. It would be best to only use it when absolutely necessary.","So, Chu Feng followed Wen Xue.","Even though the dark red light paths greatly accelerated one’s movement speed, it still took some time to travel across a starfield.","In the meantime, Wen Xue asked, “Junior Chu Feng, when do you plan to head to the Ninth Galaxy?”","“I want to find my friends and family first. What about you, senior?”","“I’ll be heading there once you acquire what you want here. Don’t miss me too much,” Wen Xue replied with a grin.","“God’s Era is about to open again. Aren’t you interested in it?”","“I am not a junior anymore.”","“You aren’t?”","“What I mean is that I’m not a junior in the truest sense of the word. I heard God’s Era’s power can only be obtained by a junior.”","“You never know for sure. I’m always skeptical about such prophecies.”","“You can just tell me that you miss me and don’t want me to leave. I’ll probably return to the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect one last time and bid a farewell to my master first,” Wen Xue replied.","“I’ll accompany you,” Chu Feng offered.","“There’s no need for that. You’re a busy man. Go do whatever you need to do instead.”","The two of them chatted a lot along the way, starting with questions about the Netherworld Sect. Even though they had Wuma Hanshuang as a shield, Chu Feng was still worried that they might bump into higher-ups along the way. He would give them away if he couldn’t aptly answer their questions.","Chu Feng needed to come up with a reasonable identity.","Thankfully, the Netherworld Sect was not tight-knit. Most sectmembers were left to their own devices, and only the outstanding ones were noticed by the higher-ups. This was helpful to Chu Feng in coming up with his identity.","After settling their agenda, the rest was all idle chatter.","Chu Feng’s impression of Wen Xue had changed after their encounter at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant. He let his guard down around her and thought of her as a true friend. It might have just been idle chatter, but he still enjoyed the conversation.","As they ventured deeper into the starfield, they spotted more Netherworld Sectmembers. All of them stood guard vigilantly.","“Looks like we’re drawing close?” Chu Feng asked Wen Xue.","“We should be arriving soon,” Wen Xue replied.","Weng!","A powerful surge of spirit power suddenly flew past Chu Feng. It was a visible pulse, flying past them and speeding off into the distance. It looked as if it would envelop the entire starfield.","“Looks like the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has successfully constructed their detection formation based on the Netherworld Embryo,” Wen Xue said.","“Indeed.” Chu Feng could tell as much.","All of a sudden, a burst of killing intent could be felt in the distance.","A teleportation gate appeared not too far away, and an army of experts dashed out and rushed in Chu Feng and Wen Xue’s direction.","“Senior, did they see through us?” Chu Feng’s heart clenched up.","“That shouldn’t be! We have Netherworld Embryos in us.” Wen Xue was unsure about what was going on as well. “Don’t worry. We should be fine even if they have discovered us.”","Soon, Chu Feng and Wen Xue realized that those people weren’t after them. They flew off using the dark red light path and headed elsewhere.","“See, I told you we’re safe. We have Netherworld Embryos inside us, after all,” Wen Xue said.","“It looks like something has happened. Let’s take a look,” Chu Feng said.","So, the two of them followed the army of experts and soon heard fighting sounds. From the ruckus and the shockwaves, they could tell that it was a huge battle involving many cultivators.","“It seems like intruders have slipped into the Undying Starfield, and they are fairly powerful,” Wen Xue said.","Despite being some distance away, they could deduce from the shockwaves that the intruders were Heavenly God level cultivators. On top of that, they weren’t just rank one Heavenly Gods.","“They don’t seem like normal cultivators.”","They got a closer glimpse of what was going on as they approached the battlefield.","One of them wielded a powerful and terrifying black aura. This was not a usual cultivator skill, and it wasn’t the Netherworld Sect’s means.","Wen Xue was excited. She relished in such commotions.","“That aura!”","Looking at the raging black aura and the spirit power, Chu Feng suddenly realized something and sped up. Soon, he saw the master of the black aura.","It was a beautiful woman dressed in a blue skirt. She gave off an air of coldness, but her face was warped in savagery. She was a rank four Heavenly God level cultivator.","She was accompanied by a man, who was constructing formations to ward off the experts surrounding them. He was a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“Chu Feng, isn’t that the Black-feathered Specter and Bai Yunqing? Are they having their date here?” Eggy exclaimed in astonishment.","Her words were intended as a joke, but those two were indeed Li Wu and Bai Yunqing."]},{"number":6521,"title":"Chapter 6521: Chapter 6519: The Opponent is a Rank Five Heavenly God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6519: The Opponent is a Rank Five Heavenly God","“They wouldn’t come here for no reason. Something must have happened,” Chu Feng murmured.","Wen Xue finally got a good look at Li Wu and remarked, “Woah! A beautiful lady dishing out such vicious moves. The feeling she gives me... Is she a natural oddity? Tsk tsk. The world of cultivation is filled with all kinds of experts.”","Wen Xue assessed Li Wu with a peculiar gleam in her eyes.","Just then, a spirit formation gate opened, and powerful individuals emerged from within.","There were now more than twenty Heavenly Gods involved in the fight, and three of them had reached rank four Heavenly God. It was evident from their conditions that they had raised their cultivation through means, but it was no easy feat to raise one’s cultivation at Heavenly God.","And these were just the people who had rushed here thus far.","More experts from the Netherworld Sect were converging at this place.","“Those who dare to barge into our Netherworld Sect’s territory will be killed!” a furious roar echoed.","A humongous embryo reminiscent of a demon god suddenly rose from the crowd, and it loftily gazed upon the battlefield from its towering stature. It was a Netherworld Sect’s formation, and it greatly enhanced the strength of Netherworld Sectmembers.","“Li Wu is injured. She won’t last long at this rate,” Eggy said.","Chu Feng’s Heaven’s Eyes had grown more potent following his breakthrough to rank nine True Dragon World Spiritist. He could now follow a fight involving Heavenly Gods despite his weaker cultivation.","Eggy was right. Li Wu was injured and could hardly withstand the coordinated offense coming from the Netherworld Sectmembers.","While Bai Yunqing had made some advancements in his spirit power, and he could rival world spiritists one rank stronger than him, he was still no match for rank four Heavenly Gods.","While Chu Feng made his way over, more glaring wounds were inflicted on Li Wu’s body.","That caused Bai Yunqing’s eyes to turn red, and he went into a frenzy. However, the huge disparity in their spirit power only rendered his efforts futile.","The duo was cornered.","“Senior, use Wuma Hanshuang to order the Netherworld Sectmembers to capture the two of them alive,” Chu Feng told Wen Xue.","“Junior, you shouldn’t be going after other girls. I’ll tell Zi Ling about this!” Wen Xue looked at Chu Feng confused.","“What are you thinking? Those two are my friends,” Chu Feng explained.","“Again? Why do you have so many friends?”","Wen Xue was baffled, but she still made her move.","Wuma Hanshuang stepped forward and roared, “That woman is a natural oddity. She’ll be of great help to our sect. Capture them alive!”","The Netherworld Sectmembers looked over to confirm Wuma Hanshuang’s identity.","The three rank four Heavenly Gods shouted at the same time, “Capture them alive.”","The Netherworld Sect’s formation changed. Their killing intent diminished, and they began moving to curb Li Wu and Bai Yunqing instead. However, that was proving to be a difficult task as Li Wu and Bai Yunqing were struggling with all their might.","“Brother, it’s me. I can take the two of you out. Have Miss Li Wu feign weakness and let them capture you,” Chu Feng sent a voice transmission to Bai Yunqing.","Moments later, Li Wu and Bai Yunqing began showing signs of weakness, and the experts of the Netherworld Sect took this opportunity to capture them.","The three rank four Heavenly Gods flitted up to Wuma Hanshuang to make their report. “Lord Wuma, we have apprehended the intruders alive.”","“Hand them to me. I’ll deal with them,” Wuma Hanshuang replied.","“Understood.”","One of the rank four Heavenly Gods took out a formation token to report that they had apprehended the intruders and handed them to Wuma Hanshuang. With that, the Netherworld Sectmembers gathered in the area and those making their way over swiftly scattered.","Now that the battle was over, their auras also waned. The cultivation of the rank four Heavenly Gods regressed to rank three Heavenly God level. They had indeed been using special means to raise their cultivation.","However, Li Wu’s cultivation underwent a more drastic change, regressing from rank four Heavenly God level to rank one Heavenly God.","“She raised her cultivation by three ranks at Heavenly God level? Junior Chu Feng, your friend is terrifyingly powerful!” Wen Xue exclaimed.","It would have been a formidable feat if a Heavenly God could raise their cultivation by a single rank. It would take a true monster to raise one’s cultivation by three whole ranks!","Chu Feng was also awed by Li Wu’s strength, but now was not the time to fuss about that.","By now, Bai Yunqing had ascertained that the person standing before him was indeed Chu Feng, but he was curious to know how Chu Feng had gotten involved with the Netherworld Sect, even securing the support of such a powerful expert from the Netherworld Sect.","Chu Feng started off by explaining his motive here before clarifying that the Wuma Hanshuang before them was not the real Wuma Hanshuang but a clone created by Wen Xue.","“What about you? What are you doing here?” Chu Feng asked.","“We’re here to save Feng Ling,” Li Wu replied.","“Feng Ling? What happened to her?” Chu Feng hurriedly asked.","He was on closer terms with Feng Ling than Li Wu. They had fought alongside each other in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith and ventured into the Immemorial Land of Dao Creation together.","It turned out that both Li Wu and Feng Ling were natural oddities. They were ancient entities, and they had known each other for a long time now. Li Wu’s cultivation had regressed severely due to events that happened in the Ancient Era, whereas Feng Ling, similar to Wen Xue, had used a special means and was cultivating from scratch as a junior.","The Netherworld Sect had previously used a natural oddity as a medium to construct a trap specifically designed against natural oddities. The trap emitted energy that only natural oddities could sense.","Feng Ling fell for the trap and was captured by the Netherworld Sect.","Li Wu was able to sense Feng Ling’s position. It was through that ability that she realized that Feng Ling could be in danger. Bai Yunqing happened to visit Li Wu during that time and learned about the matter, so the two of them made their way over to search for Feng Ling.","Upon reaching the vicinity, they spent some time investigating the situation before designing a plan to rescue Feng Ling.","Everything initially went smoothly, but the Netherworld Sect suddenly activated a powerful detection formation. Unfortunately, neither of them had the Netherworld Embryo within them, resulting in them being discovered.","“Can you tell me Feng Ling’s current position?” Chu Feng asked Li Wu.","“Big brother Chu Feng, Miss Feng Ling should be near the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item, but there are no structures or realms in the vicinity. So, we deduced that she’s in a spatial formation. We don’t know the situation in the spatial formation, but many powerful experts are guarding the area around the sacred item,” Bai Yunqing replied.","“What’s their cultivation level?” Chu Feng asked.","“Probably rank five Heavenly God level,” Bai Yunqing replied."]},{"number":6522,"title":"Chapter 6522: Chapter 6520: That Works","paragraphs":["Chapter 6520: That Works","“That is a problem.” Chu Feng frowned. He turned to Wen Xue and asked, “Senior, do you know the rank five Heavenly Gods in the Netherworld Sect?”","He spoke via voice transmission, though he relayed his words to Li Wu and Bai Yunqing as well.","“Baili Xukong is the only one in the new faction who has reached this level. I don’t know the people in the conservative faction, but since they can stand their ground against the new faction, I’d assume they have at least one rank five Heavenly God as well.","“The neutral faction only has a few old fellows, but I’m sure some of them have reached rank five Heavenly God as well. It might even be possible that all of them are at rank five Heavenly God level,” Wen Xue replied.","“They have so many experts?” Chu Feng realized that the situation was going to be tricky. “What if you encounter someone of that level? Can Wuma Hanshuang rescue a hostage from their grasp?”","“Of course not. In fact, I suspect someone stronger might come down very soon to question Wuma Hanshuang for capturing these two people. That can potentially expose us before we can save anyone,” Wen Xue said grudgingly.","The odds were stacked against them in the first place. The Undying Starfield was enveloped in the Netherworld Sect’s formation. It was easy for them to track and hunt anyone down.","Bai Yunqing said, “Big brother, you should leave first.”","“What are you talking about? I still have business here, and Feng Ling is my friend. I can’t turn a blind eye to her plight. You came up with a plan, right? Tell me about it,” Chu Feng said.","“I’ll tell him,” Li Wu said.","It turned out that Li Wu and Bai Yunqing had been here for some time now. They couldn’t ascertain whether Feng Ling was imprisoned in a spatial realm or not, but they had devised a countermeasure.","Their plan was to grasp control of the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item.","Of course, the sacred item was nowhere near enough to curb all the Netherworld Sect’s experts, but they could at least use it to suppress their cultivation. As long as they could make the enemies weaker than them, they would be able to easily rescue Feng Ling.","“That’s easier said than done. Even the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion struggle to grasp control of the sacred item, but those two think that they can use their sacred item to curb them?” Eggy scoffed.","“Brother, that’s too dangerous,” Chu Feng replied.","It was not to imply that the plan was completely hopeless, but it was too difficult to pull off.","“Big brother Chu Feng, I know this would be an impossible feat otherwise, but there’s a good chance of pulling it off with Miss Li Wu here,” Bai Yunqing said as he looked at Li Wu.","Chu Feng and Wen Xue turned their gazes to Li Wu.","“I felt a peculiar sense of familiarity with the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item, though I can’t remember where I have seen it. However, I’m certain that my power can resonate with the sacred item. I might not be able to control the sacred item, but I can at least tap into its power to construct a formation and fuse it into a suppression formation to suppress the Netherworld Sectmembers’ cultivation,” Li Wu explained.","It turned out that Li Wu was in a weakened state not because she was injured by the Netherworld Sectmembers but because she had extracted a portion of her energy and fused it into the formation Bai Yunqing had prepared beforehand.","That greatly weakened her fighting prowess, or else she could have at least stood her ground longer against the three rank four Heavenly Gods.","While chatting, they made their way to a remote area.","“Show me the formation,” Chu Feng said.","“Big brother Chu Feng, this is the formation.” Bai Yunqing took out an item that resembled a Cosmos Sack, but that was merely a disguise for the formation.","Chu Feng inspected the formation, and his eyes lit up.","This formation had potential. There were flaws in it, but he could teach Bai Yunqing how to resolve those problems. More importantly, Li Wu’s incomparably powerful curse energy had grown much more potent than before. It was extremely permeative, so there was a high chance it could permeate the sacred item.","The formation also contained a golden talisman paper that wielded the power to suppress the cultivation of others. The talisman paper looked new, but it emanated an aura even older than the Ancient Era. It was clearly from the Immemorial Era.","However, this talisman paper was an incomplete product. It couldn’t directly suppress one’s cultivation; it needed to be channeled through a powerful treasure.","So, the plan was for Li Wu to take control of the sacred item with her curse energy before utilizing the sacred item’s energy to channel the suppression talisman.","This suppression talisman worked against both cultivators and world spiritists alike.","“Miss Li Wu, you are actually the Black-feathered Specter, aren’t you?” Chu Feng asked.","He wanted to verify it despite already having the answer to the question. Before they parted ways, Li Wu gave Chu Feng a box that not only harnessed the Black-feathered Specter’s aura but also had the power to lift Bai Liluo’s curse energy.","“Isn’t the clue I gave you obvious enough?” Li Wu asked.","“It is obvious enough.” Chu Feng chuckled. “Your power is unique and formidable, Miss Li Wu.”","“Do you think it’s feasible?” Li Wu asked.","“It is feasible, but we have to first make some changes,” Chu Feng said.","“How?”","“Add my bloodline to your curse energy. That will enhance my control.”","“There’s no need for that. I can sense it when you activate the formation. I’ll channel my energy to coordinate with you then.”","“What if you’re unable to do so?”","“The energy I infused into the formation is special. It’s intricately linked to me. I can channel it even from outside the Undying Starfield, as long as I’m not too far away,” Li Wu said.","“I understand, but there’s another reason I suggested adding my bloodline to your energy. There’s a Netherworld Embryo in me. I suspect that the sacred item may reject external entities, since it’s from the Netherworld Sect, but we can minimize the rejection using the Netherworld Embryo’s aura,” Chu Feng replied.","“Fine.” Li Wu nodded.","Following that, Chu Feng told Bai Yunqing the adjustments that needed to be done to the formation to perfect it. Granted that he could do it himself, it was easier for Bai Yunqing to do it given his stronger spirit power.","So, Chu Feng gave the command, while Bai Yunqing carried out the orders. Li Wu also cooperated with them.","Some time later, Bai Yunqing finally completed the formation.","Chu Feng stowed the formation away and told Li Wu, “Miss Li Wu, tell me Feng Ling’s location.”","Li Wu took out a small white stone and handed it to Chu Feng. The stone glowed and pulsated like a mini heart. “This is Feng Ling’s life stone. It can lock onto her location. She is near the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item, but there are too many people guarding the area. We dare not make a reckless move.”","“Leave it to me.” Chu Feng turned to Wen Xue and said, “Senior, please take the two of them out of here.”","The three of them were startled.","“You’re staying here alone?” Wen Xue asked."]},{"number":6523,"title":"Chapter 6523: Chapter 6521: I Was Worried You Had a Bad Impression of Me","paragraphs":["Chapter 6521: I Was Worried You Had a Bad Impression of Me","Before Chu Feng could reply, Bai Yunqing said, ‘Big brother Chu Feng, let me stay behind.”","“I want to stay behind as well. This formation is built on my energy. I can remedy the situation if anything happens,” Li Wu said.","“Neither of you can stay. You don’t have the Netherworld Embryo inside you. You’ll be caught by the detection formation. Do you think the Netherworld Sect will turn a blind eye as you approach their sacred item? You’ll only become a hindrance to me rescuing Feng Ling,” Chu Feng said.","Bai Yunqing and Li Wu fell silent. They had to agree with Chu Feng’s words. They had already been exposed, and staying here would only increase the difficulty of the rescue operation.","But Bai Yunqing still said, “Big brother Chu Feng, I have done my calculations. The suppression talisman can only suppress their cultivation down to rank one Heavenly God level and rank one Heavenly Dragon. With your current cultivation level...”","He feared that Chu Feng couldn’t deal with them.","“Yes, I’m unable to deal with rank one Heavenly Gods and rank one Heavenly Dragons, but it won’t be easy for them to capture me either. Besides, what if I suppress their cultivation down to True God level and True Dragon?” Chu Feng proposed with a smile.","Bai Yunqing laughed.","If he had been the one to channel the formation, rank one Heavenly God level and rank one Heavenly Dragon would have indeed been the limit. But there was a chance that Chu Feng could achieve more than that.","While Bai Yunqing had the advantage in terms of spirit power, Chu Feng’s understanding of formations and world spiritist techniques far surpassed him. The latter might just be able to pull off what was impossible for him.","“Listen to me. The two of you have already done your part. The formation has been perfected, and Miss Li Wu has already said that she can cooperate with me even from outside the Undying Starfield. You can still help me even after leaving this place,” Chu Feng said.","Bai Yunqing and Li Wu nodded.","“Junior, I’ll escort them out before returning to look for you. It should help to have Wuma Hanshuang around,” Wen Xue said.","“Indeed. Senior, why don’t you leave Wuma Hanshuang behind for me instead and teach me how to control her? You don’t need to come back afterward,” Chu Feng suggested.","“That won’t do.”","“Why?”","“Only I can control her.”","“Only you?” Chu Feng narrowed his eyes.","Just then, Chu Feng noticed Netherworld Sectmembers rushing toward them from all directions. Chu Feng quickly grabbed Bai Yunqing’s rope, and Wen Xue grabbed Li Wu’s rope.","Leading the Netherworld Sectmembers was one of the rank three Heavenly God level cultivators from before.","“Paying respect to Lord Wuma,” the rank three Heavenly God bowed respectfully to Wuma Hanshuang despite bringing such a huge procession over.","“What’s the matter?” Wuma Hanshuang asked.","“My apologies, Lord Wuma. I mean no offense, but Lord Xiahou Jue commanded me to ask you how you intend to deal with the intruders.”","“Do I need to report my business to you?”","“I dare not, but this is Lord Xiahou’s command. He also told me to... Lord Xiahou wants me to verify your identity,” the rank three Heavenly God trembled as he spoke.","Bai Yunqing, Li Wu, and Chu Feng tensed up, knowing that this Wuma Hanshuang was a clone created by Wen Xue. Wuma Hanshuang would have to reveal her strength to prove her identity, but how could a clone possibly wield Wuma Hanshuang’s strength?","This put them in a spot.","“He doesn’t trust me and thinks I’m a fake, huh?” Wuma Hanshuang sneered.","The rank three Heavenly God gulped as he asked with a quivering voice, “Lord Wuma, I don’t mean to disrespect you, but this is Lord Xiahou’s command. I dare not defy him.”","“Tell Xiahou Jue to come here in person to verify it,” Wuma Hanshuang snorted.","“Milord, this...”","The rank three Heavenly God looked conflicted. He was clearly terrified of both Wuma Hanshuang and Xiahou Jue, despite being a fellow Netherworld Marshal.","Just then, a rank one Heavenly God level Netherworld General stepped forward and said, “Pardon me, Lord Wuma.”","Only the ignorant could be so brave.","The Netherworld General charged forth to grab Wuma Hanshuang’s throat. This was as good as courting death.","Pah!","Wuma Hanshuang grabbed his wrist and squeezed it. Kacha! The wrist was snapped into two.","Boom!","A powerful aura burst forth. It was the aura of a rank four Heavenly God.","“How else do you want to verify my identity? Tell me,” Wuma Hanshuang questioned in derision.","The Netherworld General screamed in agony. “Lord Wuma, I am merely following orders. Please have mercy on me!”","“Scram!” Wuma Hanshuang harrumphed.","She tugged out the Netherworld General’s arm, causing fresh blood to spurt. The Netherworld Sectmembers hurriedly retreated afterward.","Chu Feng and the others looked at Wen Xue.","“I told you that I’m the only one who can control her,” Wen Xue replied cheerily.","“Senior, what’s going on? How did you place the Wuma Hanshuang under your control?” Chu Feng asked via voice transmission.","He had already been harboring doubts, but the earlier situation proved that the Wuma Hanshuang traveling with them was not a mere clone but the real deal. Wen Xue was somehow controlling the real Wuma Hanshuang.","“Fine, I shan’t continue my lie. This person right here is indeed my master in the Netherworld Sect, Wuma Hanshuang, in the flesh. I used some means to control her. I didn’t tell you because I’m worried that it’ll frighten you. It might give you a bad impression of me. You’re already quite guarded against me due to our history,” Wen Xue replied casually, though her words hinted that she was aware that Chu Feng didn’t trust her."]},{"number":6524,"title":"Chapter 6524: Chapter 6522: The Netherworld Sect’s Sacred Item","paragraphs":["Chapter 6522: The Netherworld Sect’s Sacred Item","“Senior, it’s normal for me not to trust you after what you did to me back then, but I have a conscience. You have saved and helped me. I’d be an ingrate if I continue putting up my guard against you,” Chu Feng said.","“Eesh, I just didn’t want to scare you. Shall we be honest with each other from now on?” Wen Xue asked.","“All right. Senior, how many more means do you possess that I don’t know about?” Chu Feng asked.","Even if Wen Xue had resorted to special means, Wuma Hanshuang was still a rank four Heavenly God. Chu Feng couldn’t even imagine what it would take to control such a powerful individual.","“I am a person of many means,” Wen Xue replied with a shrug.","“Senior, aren’t we going to be honest with each other?”","“Be good and stop asking. You have your secrets too, right?”","“Fine, I shan’t probe. Senior, you should be able to safely escort them out of here, right?” Chu Feng emphasized the word ‘safely’ here.","“No problem.” Wen Xue nodded. “I’ll return to join you after escorting them out.”","“You don’t have to. There’s not much Wuma Hanshuang can do beyond this point.”","“Hmph! That’s not what you said earlier.”","Chu Feng chuckled. “Don’t worry, I’ll be fine. I’ll be honest with you. I have tricks up my sleeve. The Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion won’t be able to catch me, even if I don’t suppress their cultivation. I’m more worried about the rest of you.","“Senior, take them out of the Undying Starfield to somewhere safe, where Miss Li Wu can channel her energy with ease of mind and aid me in grasping control over the sacred item. Following that, bring them to where we first met. I’ll meet you all there once I’m done settling things here.”","“Take care, junior,” Wen Xue said. She turned to Li Wu and Bai Yunqing and said, “Let’s go. We’re all baggage here. Let’s not become a hindrance to my junior.”","Li Wu looked at Chu Feng apologetically. “Chu Feng, even though we didn’t know each other back then, I apologize for harming your friend, and I’ll find a way to make it up for that. Feng Ling is the most important person to me in this world, so...”","“Don’t worry, Feng Ling is my friend as well. Even if not for that, your relationship with my brother makes you my sister-in-law. I’ll definitely rescue Feng Ling.”","Bai Yunqing grinned at those words, but that only prompted Li Wu to shoot him a cold glare.","Bai Yunqing quickly clarified, “N-not yet, big brother. She’s not your sister-in-law yet.”","Chu Feng could tell that Li Wu wasn’t fond of such jokes, so he responded with an awkward smile. “Miss Li Wu, I was just trying to lighten up the situation. I didn’t mean anything by that. I hope you don’t take it to heart.","“It’s fine. I know you don’t mean harm. I’ll entrust Feng Ling to you then,” Li Wu said.","Wen Xue began leading Li Wu and Bai Yunqing out of the Undying Starfield. It didn’t take long for their silhouettes to disappear amid the vast expanse of space, leaving Chu Feng alone.","“We’re back to fighting by ourselves. Chu Feng, do you think Wen Xue was telling the truth? She was able to control someone as powerful as Wuma Hanshuang. What kind of ridiculous ability is that? Could she be much stronger than what we see?” Eggy asked.","She had a much better impression of Wen Xue after their encounter at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant, but even so, she found it inconceivable how Wen Xue could control Wuma Hanshuang.","It would be terrifying to make an enemy out of Wen Xue.","“My senior is an enigmatic one. I don’t think she was scheming anything when she obediently joined the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect; it did look like she was forced into it. I don’t think she was that powerful then. She might have grown after going through some fortuitous encounters. Personally, I think it’s a good thing.”","Chu Feng didn’t think much of it. While he was initially guarded against Wen Xue, she had helped him a lot afterward. He could most definitely sense the goodwill she harbored for him. That was enough reason for him to trust her.","He wasn’t too bothered about Wen Xue’s strength.","Every cultivator was bound to have their fortuitous encounters, just like how Chu Feng was swiftly growing through his fortuitous encounters. Besides, Wen Xue was an old monster who had lived through the ages. The knowledge she had accrued was bound to serve her well, and she might have also prepared many hands in the meantime.","She was bound to have an advantage over Chu Feng when it came to cultivation.","Chu Feng continued his journey forward and soon saw the so-called sacred item that the Netherworld Sect was trying to awaken.","It was a towering black door, standing at a height of over hundreds of thousands of meters, making it conspicuous even from far away.","The door was closed, but it was shrouded in an eerie dark red aura. It was fused into the surrounding space. It resembled a bottomless hole as energy from the surroundings flowed ceaselessly into it.","That was no ordinary energy; it was the Bloodline Galaxy’s galactic energy.","Chu Feng finally understood why the Netherworld Sect had sealed off the Undying Starfield. That was not just a simple seal; it doubled as an auxiliary formation. It siphoned energy away from the Bloodline Galaxy to feed the sacred item.","“To think that the sacred item the Netherworld Sect seeks to awaken is a door. What a sinister door this is,” Eggy assessed the door with widened eyes.","“It is quite sinister.” Chu Feng felt uneasy just looking at the door.","If the door could already stir such unease in him, whatever power is in it must be worse.","Chu Feng’s greatest enemy at the moment was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but he felt like the one who might bring devastation upon the world of cultivation was the Netherworld Sect. This realization sparked a thought in him.","If possible, I’ll stop the Netherworld Sect from awakening the power inside the door."]},{"number":6525,"title":"Chapter 6525: Chapter 6523: Lord Cang Li","paragraphs":["Chapter 6523: Lord Cang Li","But as Chu Feng got closer, he realized that ie would be tough to even approach the sacred item, let alone stop it. The sacred item was placed in a bizarre container, and it was protected by the formation enveloping the Undying Starfield.","The formation was formed using the sacred item’s energy, whereas the container was collecting the dark red aura emanated by the sacred item.","There were also many Netherworld Sectmembers gathered in the area to protect the sacred item. They didn’t reveal their cultivation, but Chu Feng could tell that there were many Heavenly Gods among them.","The ones who had attacked Li Wu and Bai Yunqing earlier were here as well.","But what was more noteworthy were the four thrones floating on platforms located in the four cardinal directions of the sacred item.","Four Netherworld Marshals sat upon these thrones, but they weren’t just any Netherworld Marshals. The fact that the three rank three Heavenly Gods who attacked Li Wu were just standing with the crowd, whereas these four people were seated spoke as much.","These four Netherworld Marshals wore veils that concealed their appearances, but their snowy beards indicated that they were from the older generation.","“The ones guarding the immediate vicinity of the sacred item must be even stronger than the others. Are all of them rank five Heavenly Gods? But why are there so many of them here? Are some of them from the neutral faction?” Eggy asked.","“That’s likely the case,” Chu Feng replied.","“The Netherworld Sect looks even stronger than the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Their partnership isn’t a good thing for us. We’ll be in trouble if they join forces to deal with you. Chu Feng, we mustn’t let them acquire the power inside the door.” Eggy shared the same thought as Chu Feng.","“My thoughts exactly.”","“Chu Feng, can you fuse the formation into the sacred item this far away?”","“If the ones guarding the sacred items were weaker, I could have concealed the formation and secretly transmitted it over. But I don’t think it’s feasible with so many experts present here. It’s nigh impossible. I’ll have to find a way to approach the sacred item.”","Just then, a spirit formation gate manifested outside the Netherworld Sect’s encirclement perimeter of the sacred item.","24 world spiritists from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion emerged from the spirit formation gate. They were all Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. They made their way toward the sacred item, and the Netherworld Sectmembers stepped aside to let them pass.","These world spiritists were all rank one Heavenly Dragons, and none of them were Saint-tier elders. It was still a formidable line-up, but it looked weak compared to the Netherworld Sect’s army.","“Is the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion going to work on the sacred item?” Eggy asked.","“It does look like they are here to probe the sacred item. It should be safe to assume that Jie Tianran is here as well,” Chu Feng said.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists didn’t immediately construct formations after getting close to the sacred item. Instead, they took out formidable treasures that exuded power surpassing their own.","These rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists were incapable of channeling these formidable treasures; someone stronger must have been doing it from afar. Of the entire Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, the only ones capable of this feat were Jie Tianran and Jie Mubai.","Song Yun had killed Jie Mubai, so that left only Jie Tianran.","“Does the Netherworld Sect trust the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion that much?” Eggy was baffled.","“The Netherworld Sect probably has its considerations.”","“Can’t you impersonate a Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritist and sneak your way over?” Right after Eggy blurted out those words, she refuted that possibility. “That won’t work. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s observation formation is surveying the Undying Starfield. Their world spiritists don’t have Netherworld Embryos inside them, but you do.”","“I’ll have to find another way.” Chu Feng nodded.","He was only able to advance this far thanks to Wuma Hanshuang’s cover, but the latter’s influence could only bring him this far. If he wanted to get any closer to the sacred item, he would have to assume another identity—a Netherworld General, at least.","He was about to leave the place to obtain the clothes of a Netherworld General when another figure stepped out from the teleportation formation.","This time, it was a Netherworld Sectmember.","He was ten meters tall and had a muscular physique that bulged even under his robe, resembling a human-shaped beast. He wore a veil, but the white beard extending from the veil hinted that he was from the older generation. His robe was embroidered with the words ‘Netherworld Marshal’.","This muscular old man carried a hundred meters tall copper door engraved with dark red runes. The copper door felt like an invaluable treasure.","All Netherworld Sectmembers greeted this muscular old man, addressing him as Lie Shan. From the surrounding discussions, Chu Feng learned that Lie Shan was from the neutral faction.","The old man named Lie Shan placed the copper door down.","Clang!","A massive shockwave rippled from the copper door, causing space to quake and shatter. The copper door must have been frighteningly heavy.","Lie Shan stood upright with the copper door in hand, not uttering a word.","Just then, a resonant, elderly voice echoed from the distance, “All juniors of the Netherworld Sect are to head to where Lord Lie Shan is to undergo the selection required for awakening the sacred item.”","The voice had been amplified by a formation so that it could reach every nook and cranny of the Undying Starfield.","Spirit formation gates appeared all around, and Netherworld Sectmembers emerged from them. These Netherworld Sectmembers were all juniors.","These juniors quickly made their way toward where Lie Shan was.","The dark red runes engraved on the copper door began to move, and before long, the copper door morphed into a hundred-meter-tall spirit formation gate.","“Chu Feng, could that be a trap?” Eggy asked.","Chu Feng was still in the midst of figuring out a way to approach the sacred item when the Netherworld Sect suddenly presented an opportunity to him. This was so coincidental that Eggy wondered if it was a scheme instead.","“It doesn’t seem to be a scheme. This operation appears to be a collaboration between the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Juniors emanate a unique aura that those from the older generation are unable to emulate, and that unique aura is often used when leaving legacies behind to ensure that they are inherited by juniors. That could be the reason they are opting to use juniors’ Netherworld Embryos in the formation instead,” Chu Feng analyzed.","“That makes sense. It looks like you have deciphered it all,” Eggy said with a smile.","Chu Feng’s grasp of formations had already far surpassed hers.","It was not that Eggy was lacking in talent, but that she had grown up in the Asura Spirit World, so her understanding of formations was based on hearsay. In contrast, Chu Feng had built up his foundation from the ground and slowly reinforced his understanding of formations.","While there were still many experts towering above Chu Feng, he was definitely qualified to be considered a master world spiritist in the world of cultivation now.","“It’s all thanks to Milady Queen’s teaching,” Chu Feng replied.","“That goes without saying.” Eggy’s face beamed gleefully. She was satisfied with his answer.","Chu Feng followed the junior Netherworld Sectmembers and made his way toward the copper door as well. He was not worried about catching anyone’s attention as there were Netherworld Sectmembers rushing here from afar as well.","While the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation encompassed the entire Undying Starfield, there was a limit to the energy it harnessed. Only those who were further away were teleported over. Those who were closer were expected to travel over on foot.","On that note, Chu Feng couldn’t help but note that the Netherworld Sectmembers were being teleported extremely quickly, almost to the point of it being instantaneous. He wondered if it was due to the sacred item or that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion truly possessed such means.","...","Chu Feng entered the spirit formation gate and was transported into a palace.","The palace was constructed out of copper, and it was covered in dark red runes.","At the palace’s center, there was an old man lying on a platform. This old man wore the Netherworld Sect’s robe, but it didn’t contain the word ‘Netherworld Marshal’. He didn’t wear a veiled bamboo hat either, leaving his face open for all to see.","His appearance was... unseemly. It didn’t help that he was only 1.5 meters tall and was a hunchback. Despite being before a crowd, he showed no concern for his image and scratched his armpit while picking his nose. That only made him look more unkempt.","“Paying respect to Lord Cang Li.”","Just then, more juniors stepped in and bowed respectfully to the old man on the platform.","But that old man roared back, “Paying respect your head!”"]},{"number":6526,"title":"Chapter 6526: Chapter 6524: Plump Chen Hui","paragraphs":["Chapter 6524: Plump Chen Hui","“Haven’t I said that I don’t like anyone paying respect to me? Try to butter me up once more, and I’ll break your leg!”","That explained why the juniors, who were already present in the palace, didn’t pay respect to the old man. They must have already been aware of this.","But there was still a steady stream of juniors who didn’t know better and greeted the old man. The old man would berate them for it, but it came to a point where he was sick of repeating the same point. He went straight to remotely slapping those who infringed on his rule, toppling them to the ground.","The juniors in this space were all decently talented. They would have shone like brilliant stars anywhere else in the world of cultivation. The Netherworld Sect must have carefully picked the juniors qualified to enter the Undying Starfield.","A man draped in the robe of a Netherworld Marshal entered and greeted, “Lord Cang Li.”","It was a familiar face—Jimo Qianzhou, Baili Xukong’s lackey.","He was the Netherworld Marshal who had protected Baili Zilin when the latter tried to mess with Chu Feng.","When Chu Feng and Little Fishy were in the Immemorial Massacre Sea, he led a group of Netherworld Sectmembers to capture him. Unfortunately, he bumped into the God Clan’s Shen Bai, and the two of them got into an argument before coming to blows.","Jimo Qianzhou was outmatched and sustained severe damage. Yet, he was fully recovered now. The Netherworld Sectmember must have accumulated many invaluable resources over the years to be able to heal him up.","Even if Chu Feng had not defeated the God Clan, the powerhouses of the Netherworld Sect would have probably vanquished them once they were out of their closed-door training.","“What is it?” The old man named Cang Li continued picking his nose, not bothering to spare a glance at Jimo Qianzhou.","“Lord Cang Li, it’s about time. We can begin now,” Jimo Qianzhou said.","“Begin what?” Cang Li asked.","“The selection of our juniors.”","“What’s the point of beginning the selection when not everyone is here yet?”","“Lord Cang Li, most of our juniors are already here.”","“What do you mean? The conservation faction’s Chen Hui isn’t here. Neither is your new faction’s Baili Zilin. Are they not planning to come? Are you hiding your own faction’s prodigy because awakening the sacred item comes with risks? Screw that. Are you saying that those without backing should shoulder all the danger, while those with backing reap the rewards while shaking their legs from the back?” Cang Li spat in disdain.","“Milord, that’s not it. Young master Zilin is in closed-door training and is unable to make it,” Jimo Qianzhou explained.","“Scram, you lapdog! Are you trying to pull one over on me? Do I look like a fool?” Cang Li sneered.","Jimo Qianzhou dared not to respond to that or even continue explaining himself.","“Well said. Jimo Qianzhou deserves a scolding,” Eggy said merrily before adding, “Chu Feng, didn’t you meet a person named Chen Hui a while back? Could it be the same person?”","Some time ago, Chu Feng participated in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s entrance examination to obtain a Saint-tier treasure that he needed to save Eggy. There, he met a fair-skinned, chubby man named Chen Hui.","“There are plenty of people with the same name in the world. It can’t be that coincidental.” Chu Feng shrugged off Eggy’s remark as a joke, and Eggy did mean it as a joke as well.","Just then, a group of people stepped into the palace.","The man leading the group placed his hands on his hips and declared loudly, “Lord Cang Li, I, Chen Hui, am here.”","That man was not wearing a veil, and his familiar face caused Chu Feng’s lower jaw to slacken. “Holy shit! It really is Chen Hui! He is a Netherworld Sectmember?!”","Chu Feng was shocked beyond words.","Chen Hui had left without saying farewell during the entrance examination. Chu Feng didn’t think that they would meet again in the Netherworld Sectmember, and judging from Chen Hui’s entourage, he was likely of considerable stature here.","“If he’s from the conservation faction as well, he might be acquainted with Song Yun. Is it possible that he participated in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s entrance examination because he had heard about you from Song Yun and wanted to probe you?” Eggy deduced.","“Milady Queen, you might have hit the nail on the head.” Chu Feng thought that made a lot of sense.","“Lord Cang Li, Disciple Chen Hui has brought the conservation faction’s juniors here to participate in the selection,” Chen Hui said.","The other juniors behind him bowed to Cang Li.","Jimo Qianzhou’s face darkened. That Chen Hui came at such a bad timing. He’s obviously doing it on purpose.","“Open your eyes and take a good look at the conservative faction!” Cang Li glared at Jimo Qianzhou.","Jimo Qianzhou could only smile awkwardly in response. No matter what, it was a fact that the prodigies of the conservative faction had come to participate in the selection, whereas the new faction had hidden their most talented prodigies.","“Forget it. Even if I wait until the world ends, I doubt that Baili Zilin will be here.” Cang Li stretched his back as he stood up.","He turned to the juniors present and said, “To put it nicely, you are gathered here to play your part for the Netherworld Sect. But to be frank, you’re just here because you don’t have backing, so no one cares if anything happens to you. So, you'd better buck up. If you don’t have backing, you’ll have to become strong to become your own backing and that of your descendants. How else can you survive in the world of cultivation?”","“All right, the selection begins now. Sit down and prepare yourself. It’ll be a trial of willpower. As long as your willpower is firm enough to clear the trial, you’ll be rewarded. You may begin now.”","Cang Li took out a token infused with a dark red aura. It was the same dark red aura that the sacred item emanated.","The juniors quickly sat down.","Cang Li formed a hand seal, and the dark red aura in the token surged into the sky and fused with the palace’s ceiling. The dark red runes in the surroundings morphed into spirit power.","It turned out that the palace was a formation.","A dark red aura suffused the palace. Instantly, the juniors frowned, and their breathing hastened. Even Jimo Qianzhou hurriedly stood up and flitted over to the platform where Cang Li stood.","Only Cang Li’s platform was free from the dark red aura’s influence.","“What’s wrong? Are you afraid that you’ll succumb and embarrass yourself?” Cang Li cast a cold glance at Jimo Qianzhou.","Jimo Qianzhou responded with a bitter smile.","“Stop being an eyesore and get lost!” Cang Li roared.","Jimo Qianzhou wanted to observe the situation, but he was forced to leave. Cang Li was the most difficult one to deal with among the elders of the neutral faction. Even Baili Xukong would be nagged at by him. Jimo Qianzhou dared not to offend him.","Just then, a harrumph echoed. Some juniors collapsed to the ground, and the number only soared with time.","“Why are you still standing there like an idiot? Move the juniors who can’t hold on anymore out! Are you going to watch as they die in here?” Cang Li berated.","Jimo Qianzhou felt wronged. Didn’t you just tell me to leave?"]},{"number":6527,"title":"Chapter 6527: Chapter 6525: I’ll Remember You","paragraphs":["Chapter 6525: I’ll Remember You","But Jimo Qianzhou dared not speak against Cang Li. He channeled his martial power from the platform and remotely transported the fainted juniors out of the copper palace.","As time passed, the fainted juniors’ symptoms worsened. Many spewed white froth while convulsing nonstop.","“Grow a brain! If you’re at your limit, stand up and walk out. What’s more embarrassing than being weak is to adamantly hold on despite being at your limit. You’ll only impair your foundation and limit your future potential as a cultivator. That would be sheer dumbness,” Cang Li shouted.","After hearing his words, many juniors, upon reaching their limit, stood up and left on their own accord. Nevertheless, there were still juniors who held on till they fainted.","“Damn it. Who knows if the lousy idea cracked by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is reliable or not?” Cang Li cursed with a darkened face.","There had been tens of thousands of juniors gathered in this copper palace earlier, but within moments, less than three thousand of them remained.","Cang Li formed a hand seal, and the dark red aura scattered. He waved his sleeve, and Cosmos Sacks flew out and landed in the hands of Chu Feng and the others.","“Not bad. Those who remain have exceptional willpower. Congratulations on clearing the selection. You’ll be able to contribute to our Netherworld Sect in the awakening of the sacred item. Whether we succeed in awakening the sacred item or not, you are all the pride of our Netherworld Sect. We’ll be raising the stakes now.”","Cang Li took out a vat inscribed with the words ‘Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’. He triggered the vat’s mechanism, and countless glowing bubbles rose into the sky and filled up the palace. Each of these bubbles was a formation.","“The next step is to fuse these formations into your Netherworld Embryos. These formations were prepared by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, so, to be honest, I have no idea how reliable they are. Give it a try, but raise your hand if you feel unwell; I’ll personally dispel the formation for you. If you’re able to adapt to it, try to fuse as many formations as possible. You may begin,” Cang Li said.","Chu Feng reached out and grabbed a bubble formation. He carefully examined the formation, fearing that there might be a trap in it.","“Jimo Qianzhou, I heard that a lad beat up Baili Zilin, and that person appears to be Jie Tianran’s grandson? Is that true?” Cang Li suddenly asked.","“Um...” Jimo Qianzhou’s face darkened. He didn’t want to talk about Baili Zilin’s dark history in public, but he dared not to refute Cang Li. So, he had no choice but to reply politely, “Yes, Lord Cang Li. That is true.”","“I heard that lad is skilled in world spiritist techniques, and he has a Netherworld Embryo in him as well. I wonder how many formations he can fuse with if he is here,” Cang Li murmured.","The corners of Jimo Qianzhou’s lips twitched.","You sure heard plenty of things. You’re choosing to ask me now to put me in a spot.","But Jimo Qianzhou still politely replied, “Yes, he is a skilled world spiritist. He has inherited his mother’s Ruler’s Bloodline. However, the rumors that he has a Netherworld Embryo in him are not credible.”","Chen Hui suddenly spoke up, “Lord Cang Li, Chu Feng does have a Netherworld Embryo in him, and he has received the Guidance of the Divine Vat.”","Jimo Qianzhou’s face turned cold, and he furiously roared, “You heard that from Song Yun, didn’t you? Shouldn’t you people know better what kind of person Song Yun is? She has killed many of our Netherworld Sectmembers. How can you trust her?”","It was a stark contrast to his timid behavior when addressing Cang Li.","“Even if Song Yun isn’t credible, shouldn’t the Netherworld Envoy who brought her back be?” Chen Hui asked.","“That Netherworld Envoy has been beguiled by Song Yun. There are plenty of people in our Netherworld Sect who have been beguiled by her, no?” Jimo Qianzhou snorted.","Chen Hui had been a stalwart supporter of Song Yun.","Upon hearing those words, Chen Hui fell silent and continued fusing the formation into his Netherworld Embryo.","Cang Li smiled at their bicker as if he was a third party watching the commotion.","Eggy’s eyes lit up upon hearing those words. \"You hear that, Chu Feng? I was right. Chen Hui must be on close terms with Song Yun. He must have known about your ties with her and was curious about you.”","Just then, Cang Li turned to Jimo Qianzhou and asked, “What’s the name of the lad who beat up Baili Zilin?”","“Chu Feng,” Jimo Qinazhou replied.","I don’t know how strong he is, but that’s an awful name,” Cang Li remarked.","Chu Feng was unfazed by the discussion about him. He continued observing the formation. Only after confirming that the formation didn’t contain energy detrimental to him did he finally fuse it into his Netherworld Embryo. He grabbed a few more and did the same.","It didn’t take long for him to fuse five formations in, and that was him intentionally slowing down his pace. He made sure to lag behind Chen Hui, who was the fastest one of the juniors present. Even so, he still caught Cang Li’s attention.","“Lad, take off your bamboo veil and show me your face,” Cang Li said.","Chu Feng took off his bamboo veil. He had already altered his face into an ordinary-looking one.","“What’s your name?” Cang Li asked.","“Milord, my name is Feng Chu,” Chu Feng replied.","“Feng Chu? You look so-so, but you have a wonderful name. Are you from the new faction or the conservative faction?”","“I am from the new faction.”","“Oh? The new faction still has talent like you?” Cang Li was surprised.","“Lord Cang Li, our new faction has no lack of talents,” Jimo Qianzhou remarked with a grin.","“Am I talking to you? Stop butting your way into our conversation. Do you know anything about Feng Chu?” Cang Li sharply criticized Jimo Qianzhou, rendering the latter speechless. “Feng Chu, you are a true talent. I’ll remember you. Do your best. No matter what the outcome is, I’ll ensure that you’ll get the resources you require in the Netherworld Sect.”","“Thank you, milord,” Chu Feng said before continuing to fuse more formations into his Netherworld Embryo.","He wasn’t worried about Cang Li or Jimo Qianzhou probing deeper into his background. He had already come up with a reasonable identity with Wen Xue.","“Brother Feng, I am also from the new faction. Please guide me along.”","Chu Feng received several voice transmissions. They were from members of the new faction seeking to get on close terms with him. He didn’t expect the Netherworld Sect to be so political.","“Lad, you’re Feng Chu, right? You better keep a low profile, do you hear me?” another voice transmission was relayed to Chu Feng."]},{"number":6528,"title":"Chapter 6528: Chapter 6526: What a Prodigy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6526: What a Prodigy","It was coming from a dark-skinned man not too far behind Chu Feng. He was a junior who had stepped into this copper palace together with Chen Hui.","Chu Feng paid him no heed.","“I’m talking to you. Do you hear me, or are you pretending to be deaf? I’ll cripple you if you dare to steal young master Chen Hui’s accomplishment,” that man continued his threats.","Ultimately, he was just worried about Chu Feng stealing attention from Chen Hui.","“That skunk has quite the nasty mouth. I’d have ripped his mouth out if not for that old man over there.” Eggy clenched her fists in anger. She wouldn’t stand for anyone speaking to Chu Feng in such a tone.","“Don’t waste your time with such scum. You’d only be dirtying your hands for nothing,” Chu Feng replied as he continued fusing more formations.","He didn’t slow down in his pacing, but Chen Hui began to lose steam.","“I didn’t expect there to be such a figure in the new faction.”","Chen Hui didn’t notice Chu Feng at the start. He only shot Chu Feng a glance when Cang Li publicly praised him. It was only now that he was taking a proper look at the prodigy from the new faction.","The difficulty level suddenly soared for him after fusing fifteen formations. At this rate, eighteen formations would be his limit.","And his prediction was on the mark. He was unable to fuse any more formations after the eighteenth one. Meanwhile, Chu Feng had also fused the eighteenth formation, just like him.","“Chu Feng, why are you fusing so many formations? You might draw unwanted attention if you surpass Chen Hui here,” Eggy reminded.","By the time Chen Hui reached his limit, the other prodigies present had long reached their limit and stopped fusing formations into their Netherworld Embryo. Chu Feng was the only one who was still doing so. That made him the center of attention.","“Eggy, something is off. The more formations I fuse into my Netherworld Embryo, the stronger the peculiar feeling I’m getting. It’s not that these prodigies are at their limits, but that there’s a fundamental limit imposed on the formation. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is scheming something, but I’ll have to break the limit to decipher their true intention.”","Chu Feng sensed that this matter was more important than not being the center of attention, so he grabbed the nineteenth formation and began fusing it.","“You bastard! You don’t know what’s good, huh? Young master Chen Hui has personally graced this place, yet you dare to steal the attention from him? Continue fusing more formations, and I’ll chop off your hands!” the dark-skinned man roared via voice transmission.","Of course, Chu Feng was unfazed. He fused the nineteenth formation and moved on to the twentieth.","“Indeed, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion harbors an ulterior motive,” Chu Feng told Eggy.","“What’s hidden in the formations?” Eggy asked.","“Hidden within the formations is energy that will allow them to take control of the sacred item. It is discreetly hidden. Even a person with sharp senses would have to gather a certain number of formations before the energy becomes barely perceptible.","“While the purpose of these formations is to aid the Netherworld Sect in taking control of the sacred item, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is going beyond that by slipping in this discreet energy,” Chu Feng said.","“That loser grandfather of yours wouldn’t help the Netherworld Sect for no reason. I bet he’s trying to exploit them for what they are worth.” Eggy wasn’t surprised in the least.","“Now that you mention it, I do sense a sliver of Jie Tianran’s aura in the formations,” Chu Feng said.","“That confirms it. Your loser grandfather is up to something.”","“Yeah.”","Chu Feng was unsure at first, but this discovery confirmed his previous guess that Jie Tianran was here.","“Your grandfather might be a loser, but his means are troublesome to deal with. Chu Feng, are you confident of pulling it off? Is Li Wu’s formation reliable?” Eggy was worried.","Chu Feng would have been in huge trouble at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city if Sikong Changsheng hadn’t stepped in to help him back then.","“To be honest, I wasn’t sure if things would work out even if I managed to get to the sacred item and impeccably fuse Li Wu’s formation into it. But with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation, I’m confident that it’ll work now. Jie Tianran’s ambitions worked ot my advantage,” Chu Feng replied.","“I wonder if your grandfather will die of anger if he learns that you’re exploiting him here as well.” Eggy laughed in mischief.","Chu Feng continued fusing more formations into his Netherworld Embryo. He was already the center of attention, so he might as well go all the way and complete his agenda.","It would be best if he could use the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation to conceal Li Wu’s formation. That way, he could openly fuse Li Wu’s formation into the sacred item without fearing repercussions.","All in all, Chu Feng fused a total of 231 formations into his Netherworld Embryo. That was ten times Chen Hui’s amount, but it was still nowhere near his limit. He had only stopped because he had fused enough formations for his use.","Even Jimo Qianzhou’s mouth was agape in shock, let alone the other juniors. A monster had emerged among this group of prodigies.","Pah!","Someone suddenly slapped Jimo Qianzhou. It was Cang Li.","“And you call yourself a Netherworld Marshal! You’re worse than trash! How did your new faction fail to notice a prodigy of this caliber? You must have been too busy fawning on that useless Baili Zilin and squandering our resources on him!” Cang Li spat.","“Milord, it’s precisely because we have unearthed his talent that Feng Chu is here!” Jimo Qianzhou clasped his cheek while replying indignantly.","He didn’t expect to be completely humbled by Cang Li in public.","Pah!","Cang Li slapped Jimo Qianzhou once more.","“How dare you talk back to me! Your new faction wouldn’t have sent him here if you truly thought he was a prodigy!” Cang Li berated.","Jimo Qianzhou was speechless, but it was a fact that they had hidden Baili Zilin and all the top prodigies of the new factions. They were worried that this faction would hinder their future.","“Your new faction was the one who pushed for a partnership with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but you’re playing games at a time like this. Tell Baili Xukong that the juniors here are the future of our Netherworld Sect. If anything happens to them, I’ll never forgive him!” Cang Li roared.","Jimo Qianzhou dared not utter a word despite being reprimanded.","The neutral faction’s stance was extremely important within the Netherworld Sect, and Cang Li wielded extraordinary say within the neutral faction.","Conducting a selection for the juniors to cooperate with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was a trivial issue that Jimo Qianzhou could have handled, but Cang Li intervened and dragged Lord Lie Shan into it as well.","Jimo Qianzhou regretted hiding the prodigies of the new faction. Whether the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation would harm their prodigies or not, this act had already worsened Cang Li’s impression of the new faction.","The only silver lining was that this was Baili Xukong’s decision, so Jimo Qianzhou didn’t have to shoulder the blame.","After Cang Li berated Jimo Qianzhou, he turned to address Chu Feng and the other juniors, “You people should also wise up. Later, in the formation core, when you find yourself reaching your limit, just stand up and leave. There’s nothing more important than staying alive. No one will remember you if you throw your life away here. The Cosmos Sack I gave you contains not just cultivation resources but a blue pill as well. Take some time to recuperate, and we’ll head out afterward.”","The crowd did as they were told.","Chu Feng didn’t need to recuperate, but he ate the pill to avoid attracting attention. Just then, someone appeared before him.","It was Chen Hui."]},{"number":6529,"title":"Chapter 6529: Chapter 6527: I’m Only Worried That You Don’t Want Me","paragraphs":["Chapter 6527: I’m Only Worried That You Don’t Want Me","As Chen Hui made his way over, the dark-skinned man and the other juniors from the conservative faction stood up and took their positions behind him. It was quite the display.","“Brother, I am Chen Hui,” Chen Hui said with a grin.","“I have heard about you,” Chu Feng replied.","“Heard, your head! Greet young master Chen Hui!” the dark-skinned man pointed a finger at Chu Feng and said.","Pah!","The dark-skinned man flew across the room and slammed into the palace walls. His body was fine, but there was a fiery red hand print on his face.","“Just because he’s your young master doesn’t mean that he is other people’s young master. Just try oppressing others once more, and I’ll rip your mouth apart!” Cang Li glared coldly at the dark-skinned man.","Needless to say, he was the one who slapped the dark-skinned man.","The dark-skinned man felt wronged, but he dared not to protest against it.","“Don’t hold it against him. That’s the kind of person he is,” Chen Hui said.","Chu Feng merely smiled without saying anything.","“Brother Feng Chu is an amazing prodigy, but it's a pity that the new faction doesn’t appreciate your talent. If you join our conservative faction, I guarantee you that you’ll never lack resources from this day forth.” Chen Hui thumped his chest reassuringly.","“I’m more worried that your conservative faction dares not to accept me,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Oblivious to Chu Feng’s true identity, Chen Hui replied with a confident chuckle, “Our conservative faction welcomes you as long as you’re willing to join us. You need not worry about the new faction. We won’t allow any of them to exact vengeance on you.”","He even revealed his cultivation as proof of that—he had reached rank seven True God level.","“Woah!”","Shocked exclamations could be heard from all around.","Even Cang Li was momentarily surprised before revealing a heartened smile. In contrast, Jimo Qianzhou didn’t look good at all. They had no idea Chen Hui had reached this level.","“What’s he showing off for? It’s all through unorthodox means,” Eggy snorted. She doubted that Chen Hui could have reached this level by cultivating normally.","“Young master Chen Hui has grown rapidly, but I heard that you are on extremely close terms with Song Yun. She even met you before escaping. Did young master Chen Hui, like Song Yun, use the flesh and blood of our brethren for your cultivation?” Jimo Qianzhou sneered.","“Song Yun has committed an unforgivable sin. Our conservative faction is after her as well. However, you, as a Netherworld Marshal, should not speak carelessly without evidence. You claim that I have used the flesh and blood of our brethren for my cultivation. Prove it,” Chen Hui demanded.","“Hmph.” Jimo Qianzhou harrumphed coldly.","He was just about to continue speaking when Cang Li interjected, “Enough. Why is an old thing like you interfering with a conversation among juniors?”","“Lord Cang Li, Chen Hui dares to publicly poach our new faction’s prodigy. Am I supposed to...”","“Supposed to what? Conservative faction, new faction—they are all from our Netherworld Sect. Our members can choose wherever they want to go. Do you intend to tie him down with force? Are we still the Netherworld Sect or the new faction?” Cang Li asked sharply.","“Of course we’re the Netherworld Sect.” Jimo Qianzhou dared not to retort anymore. He knew that Cang Li had a bad impression of him, so he could only lower his head and back down.","“Brother Feng Chu, this is an earnest invitation from our conservative faction. There are many eyes here, so spare a thought for my reputation, won’t you?” Chen Hui asked with a grin.","Looking at Chen Hui’s wily yet earnest expression reminded Chu Feng of the days they had spent reaping crops on the fields in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s entrance examination.","Back then, when Chen Hui departed without saying farewell, he thought that they would never meet again. The world of cultivation was a huge place, after all. Who could have expected them to reunite in the Netherworld Sect?","Chu Feng did have a good impression of Chen Hui, but learning that Chen Hui had approached him with an ulterior motive made him feel an urge to get back at him. At the very least, he ought to even things out.","“Sure. I’ll join the conservative faction once we’re done awakening the sacred item,” Chu Feng said.","“It’s a deal.” Chen Hui was overjoyed.","“Yes, it’s a deal,” Chu Feng replied.","With that, the entire group left the copper palace and made their way closer to the sacred item.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had already begun channeling their treasures to construct a massive formation. Each treasure emanated a powerful aura, showing that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had gone all out for this operation.","The formation was as big as a miniature realm, and it enveloped the massive sacred item.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists continued to linger in the area, but they were just for show. The ones truly channeling the formation were the experts hidden in the shadow.","Within the formation was an empty formation core that was prepared for Chu Feng and the others.","“Young friends, I’ll have to trouble you to step into the formation core. When the formation is completely activated, it’ll siphon away the formation energy inside your bodies. As the formation energy is already bound to your Netherworld Embryo, so the process will inevitably cause you pain, though it should be bearable. As long as you endure it, your job will be done,” a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion explained.","Chu Feng and the others stepped into the formation core and sat down.","“Chu Feng, let’s flee if the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion tries anything funny. We can always return another day to claim the legacy. You have the Divine Deer anyway. They won’t be able to stop you from rescuing Feng Ling.” Eggy was worried.","“All right. I’ll flee right away if I sense that something is amiss,” Chu Feng replied.","There was no discomfort initially. All of a sudden, a brilliant light shone, and a powerful surge of spirit power gushed toward the sacred item.","Boom!","Space shook. The sacred item emanated an even denser congregation of dark red aura, but this time, the dark red aura formed a protective barrier around itself to stop the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s spirit power.","Wu!","Groans echoed around Chu Feng. The formation had begun siphoning the formations from the junior Netherworld Sectmembers’ bodies.","“How are you feeling, Chu Feng?” Eggy was worried.","“I feel nothing at all,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He didn’t say that just to reassure Eggy; he truly felt nothing. It could be because the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was worried about the Netherworld Sectmembers’ safety or that they had other plans in mind, but they didn’t siphon the formations quickly.","Meanwhile Chu Feng got to work. It looked as if he was cooperating with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation on the surface, but in truth, he was secretly using Heaven’s Eyes to observe the nature of the formation.","He could now use Heaven’s Eyes even with his eyes closed. It wasn’t as powerful as its usual state, but it was enough.","“I am right. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is trying to gain control over the sacred item. That works to my advantage.”","Chu Feng began secretly channeling the formation constructed by Li Wu and Bai Yunqing before discreetly fusing it into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation. It was a good thing that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was siphoning out the formations inside their Netherworld Embryo slowly, so Chu Feng could do a more thorough job with the fusion.","As the formations siphoned away from the Netherworld Sectmembers’ Netherworld Embryos fused with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation, the dark red aura emanated by the sacred item gradually thinned.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s plan was a success. The junior Netherworld Sectmembers’ Netherworld Embryo could indeed circumvent the sacred item’s defenses.","Finally, the dark red aura blocking the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation dissipated, allowing the formation’s spirit power to flow into the sacred item.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion managed to pull it off!” Chu Feng was thrilled.","The sacred item had a defense mechanism to repel hostile energies. Even if Chu Feng had found another opportunity to approach the sacred item and fuse Bai Yunqing’s formation into it, there was a chance that the sacred item might have just repelled it.","It was a good thing that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had foreseen that and used the junior Netherworld Sectmembers’ Netherworld Embryos to circumvent that defense mechanism.","The pieces were falling into place."]},{"number":6530,"title":"Chapter 6530: Chapter 6528: The Number One Under Heavenly God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6528: The Number One Under Heavenly God","Chu Feng had fused Bai Yunqing’s formation into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation, and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation was pumping its spirit power into the sacred item.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s greed ended up helping Chu Feng.","Even if the sacred item went amok, everyone would only think that the culprit was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion instead of Chu Feng.","...","There was a spatial realm located in proximity to the sacred item. In the spatial realm was a black mountain made from a cultivation treasure. At the peak of the mountain was a sealed cavern.","At the foot of the mountain was an extravagant palace. The palace emanated a dark red aura that flowed toward the mountain cavern.","The dark red aura was clearly the sacred item’s aura, but it had been refined into energy that could be used for cultivation.","A Netherworld Sectmember floated above the palace. He had a dashing appearance, but his ghastly pale face made him look eerie. He was Zhao Feng, Baili Xukong’s godson.","He was the one who had discovered the method to refine the sacred item’s energy using a natural oddity as a medium, processing it into a cultivation resource.","“As expected of my godfather’s blood-related son. Little brother Zilin is truly talented. His cultivation will grow by leaps and bounds after this,” Zhao Feng looked at the cavern as he remarked.","Boom!","Shockwaves rippled from the cavern. At the same time, the dark red aura flowing toward the cavern slowed.","“Looks like that’s all for now.”","Zhao Feng knew that Baili Zilin had reached his limit and couldn’t absorb any more dark red aura, so he flitted into the palace.","The moment he stepped into the palace, he heard multiple groans of agony, but he ignored them. These were all the victims he had schemed to capture. Despite the palace’s extravagant appearance, it was actually a prison.","The entire place felt eerie.","Zhao Feng opened one of the cell doors, and on the other side of the door was a different scenery. It was a well-decorated room, resembling that of a young lady. Desserts and fruits were placed on the table, though they were completely untouched.","After Zhao Feng walked into the room, he quickly closed the door, fearing that the noises outside would reach here. He glanced at the untouched food and sighed before casting his gaze at the corner of the room.","A woman sat there cross-legged, cultivating. She had an innocent face and wore a white dress. No man could resist the urge to take a second look at her. A set of wind chimes was fastened at her waist, making her look lively.","She was Feng Ling.","“Miss Feng Ling, you don’t have to cultivate on the ground,” Zhao Feng said with a smile.","“You’d have let me leave if you truly cared about me. Don’t you think it’s hypocritical of you to feign concern while locking me in here?” Feng Ling sneered.","“You have misunderstood me, Miss Feng Ling.” Zhao Feng opened the door, allowing the cries of agony to reach the room. “Don’t you think I’m already treating you very well? You would have been suffering with the others if not for my protection.”","Zhao Feng closed the door after finishing his words.","The screams were so intense that Feng Ling looked nowhere as calm as before.","“What do you want from me?” Feng Ling asked.","“Miss Feng Ling, are my intentions not clear enough? I have told you that I have seen you a long time ago, but it wasn’t convenient for me to reveal my face due to our sect’s rules. Back then, you were already a renowned prodigy of the Bloodline Galaxy. The moment I saw you, I could no longer tear my eyes away from you. You are my dream lover.","“What I want is very simple. I just want you to marry me and become my wife. But I’m afraid there are complications now.” Zhao Feng looked troubled.","Feng Ling frowned. Marrying you is not easy at all for me. You don’t catch my eye. Nevertheless, she asked, “What complications are there?”","“Do you know who I am? Allow me to reintroduce myself. I am Zhao Feng, one of the leading figures of the Netherworld Sect’s new faction, Baili Xukong’s godson. My little brother, Baili Zilin, has a grudge with that lad named Chu Feng.","“Not only are you acquainted with Chu Feng, but the two of you are also on close terms. That makes it difficult for me to take you as my wife. However, it’s still possible to resolve this matter.","“As long as you join our Netherworld Sect and tell little brother Zilin that you aren’t good friends with Chu Feng and that you’re willing to deal with Chu Feng for me, I promise that you’ll leave this place safe and sound and receive cultivation resources beyond your imagination. With your talent, I’m sure you can become a formidable figure just like me.","“And if you do help us deal with Chu Feng, that would be a huge accomplishment. That would lay the groundwork for you to marry me,” Zhao Feng said.","“Is Baili Zilin here as well?” Feng Ling asked.","“Yes, he’s about to emerge from this closed-door training. Let’s meet him together,” Zhao Feng said.","“All right.” Feng Ling nodded as she rose to her feet.","Zhao Feng was overjoyed to hear that. He tried to grab her hand, but she dodged it.","“You’ll have to respect me if you want to marry me. I won’t have physical contact with any men before marriage,” Feng Ling said.","Zhao Feng frowned.","In response, Feng Ling smiled sweetly at him, and that loosened his frown.","“Young master Zhao, you understand me, right? I’m sure you don’t like a woman who has no boundaries,” Feng Ling spoke in a much gentler tone, which made Zhao Feng smile.","“Of course. I am a gentleman.”","Zhao Feng led the way for Feng Ling.","As they walked out of the palace, a man emerged from the cavern. It was Baili Zilin.","Zhao Feng quickly flitted to the top of the mountain, and Feng Ling followed him.","Baili Zilin was displeased to see Feng Ling. This might be their first meeting, but Baili Zilin had already seen paintings of her. To be exact, he had seen paintings of everyone acquainted with Chu Feng.","He also knew that Feng Ling was imprisoned here, and she was being treated well because of Zhao Feng’s intervention.","“Little brother Zilin, congratulations on your successful closed-door training. You have reached rank seven True God level in a single breath,” Zhao Feng said.","“It’s a pity that I have failed to reach rank nine True God level,” Baili Zilin remarked.","“You can’t say that. As important as cultivation levels are, fighting prowess is also equally important. With little brother Zilin’s talent and strength, even as a rank seven True God level cultivator, your fighting prowess easily makes you the strongest man beneath Heavenly Gods,” Zhao Feng said."]},{"number":6531,"title":"Chapter 6531: Chapter 6529: Zhao Feng’s Pride","paragraphs":["Chapter 6529: Zhao Feng’s Pride","“Indeed, I have made considerable advancements in my cultivation. I ought to thank you for this, godbrother,” Baili Zilin said.","“You’re being too distant. I was only a 99-year-old child when my parents passed away. I wouldn’t be the man I am now if not for godfather taking me in and nurturing me. Despite being less than two hundred years of age, I have surpassed my parents to become a Heavenly God level cultivator. On top of that, I can rival enemies a rank stronger than me.","“I know that I’m talented, but I also know that I’d have never reached this level if not for godfather,” Zhao Feng said.","Baili Zilin squeezed out a smile, though his smile was strained. “Godbrother, I heard that you have been looking for the man named Chu Xuanyan?”","“Yes, that’s the man who inflicted the severe injuries on my parents that eventually resulted in their deaths. Now that I have reached Heavenly God level, I am more than capable of exacting vengeance on him. However, Chu Xuanyan seems to have completely disappeared from the face of the world. I can’t find any news about him at all. I wonder if he had also sustained severe injuries during his fight against my parents as well and died.” Zhao Feng stroked his lower jaw contemplatively.","“Godbrother, I understand your desire to avenge your parents, but you mustn’t forget our Netherworld Sect’s rules. The Netherworld Sect should always come first. You’re splitting your energy across different matters; that’ll inevitably slow your work. For instance, I have a grudge against Chu Feng as well, but I didn’t tap into the Netherworld Sect’s resources to kill him.”","At this point, Baili Zilin turned to Feng Ling and remarked, “Why does this lady look so familiar? Is she Feng Ling?”","Baili Zilin took a step up to Feng Ling. “Isn’t she the one who fought alongside Chu Feng in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith?”","Zhao Feng became nervous, but Feng Ling replied sweetly, “Yes, that’s me.”","Baili Zilin turned to Zhao Feng and asked, “Godbrother, what do you mean by this? You know that I was defeated by Chu Feng, so you brought his friend over to irk me?”","“What are you saying, little brother Zilin? Please don’t misunderstand me. Yes, Miss Feng Ling is acquainted with Chu Feng, but the happenings on the Nine Heavens’ Zenith are mere rumors. Miss Feng Ling was forced to work with Chu Feng; their relationship is nowhere near as intimate as the rumors make them out of be.","“The truth is that Miss Feng Ling harbors a grudge against Chu Feng and wishes to help us deal with him. Isn’t that right, Miss Feng Ling?” Zhao Feng shot a look at Feng Ling.","“Well...”","Feng Ling chuckled as she unleashed the aura of a rank seven True God level cultivator. At the same time, a powerful aura gushed forth from her body, and her cultivation surged beyond rank nine True God level.","As she revealed her cultivation, she also made her move.","She was so close to Baili Zilin that Zhao Feng had no time to react. Her left hand grabbed Baili Zilin’s wrist and pinned it behind his back, while her right hand grabbed Baili Zilin’s neck.","“I’m afraid that the rumors are true. Chu Feng is my friend, and we are... very close,” Feng Ling said.","“You!!!” Infuriated, Zhao Feng unleashed his aura as a rank one Heavenly God.","“Do you want him to die?”","Feng Ling wasn’t intimidated. She tightened her grip, and her fingers sank into Baili Zilin’s neck like sharp knives. Fresh blood flowed down her fingers.","“Feng Ling, you fooled me?” Zhao Feng’s eyes turned bloodshot, and he clenched his teeth.","Despite having sealed Feng Ling’s paths of escape with his rank one Heavenly God level oppressive might, he dared not to make a reckless move now that Baili Zilin was in Feng Ling’s clutches.","“Yes, I fooled you. I suggest you take a good look in the mirror. You have no backbone at all. Look at how you bend your back and fawn upon everyone! Someone who has no pride wants me to marry him? Dream on!","“And you wanted me to badmouth my friend? Pui! Who do you take me to be? Do you think I’m as disgusting as you lot? You call him your godbrother, but all there is between the two of you are ties of mutual interest. There’s no loyalty whatsoever.","“Let me go, or else I’ll rip apart your godbrother’s throat. Let’s see if your godfather will still take care of you once that happens!” Feng Ling uttered insults as if she was hurling punches at Zhao Feng.","Zhao Feng’s veins popped out of sheer anger, but he dared not make a move.","“Hahaha...” Baili Zilin suddenly burst into laughter. “My dear godbrother, it looks like your puppy love isn’t being reciprocated. Feng Ling, do you think you can kill me?”","Baili Zilin unleashed a powerful aura, pushing the fingers sinking into his neck out.","Feng Ling immediately understood that the situation had gone awry and drew her God Armament. Despite the increment in her fighting prowess, her hand that was holding Baili Zilin hostage was still ricocheted off.","It was spirit power! Baili Zilin was protected by a powerful treasure!","Feng Ling tried to escape, but Zhao Feng swiftly exerted his oppressive might and crushed Feng Ling to the ground.","Uwa!","“You little bitch. I’ll murder you!”","Zhao Feng marched up and grabbed Feng Ling’s head. He smashed her head against the ground several times, causing her to bleed nonstop. It looked as if he would beat her to death.","“There’s no need to do that.” Baili Zilin stepped forward and smiled at Feng Ling. “Miss Feng Ling is indeed extraordinarily powerful. To think that she can raise her cultivation by four ranks at True God level. I would have been in trouble if not for my father’s protective treasure.”","“That’s all you are good for—your father,” Feng Ling sneered.","“Shut up!” Zhao Feng roared.","Just as he was about to smash Feng Ling’s head more, Baili Zilin raised his hand and interjected, “There’s no need for that, godbrother. Our Netherworld Sect cherishes talent, and Miss Feng Ling is indeed talented. She’s stronger than the rumors put her out to be. Given our relationship, I’m more than willing to support her entry into the Netherworld Sect as long as she’s willing to marry you... but I only fear that she’s unwilling to do so.”","“Little brother Zilin, how can I marry someone who dares hurt you?” Zhao Feng asked.","“Godbrother, you should really reflect on yourself if Miss Feng Ling would rather die than to marry you. Or do you rather not try at all because you don’t have confidence in your charm? If so, I can only say that you’re letting my father down,” Baili Zilin said.","Zhao Feng’s hands shook, knowing that Baili Zilin was mocking him. He might fawn on Baili Zilin, but he was still someone with pride. The anger on his face faded, but his expression only grew increasingly colder."]},{"number":6532,"title":"Chapter 6532: Chapter 6530: Vindictive","paragraphs":["Chapter 6530: Vindictive","“Give me a moment, little brother Zilin.”","Zhao Feng lifted Feng Ling as if he was holding a little chick and flitted down the mountain, returning to the palace.","Baili Zilin wasn’t worried about Zhao Feng freeing Feng Ling. Instead, he touched his neck as anger flickered across his eyes. His anger was not directed at Feng Ling but Zhao Feng.","“You know that I have a grudge against Chu Feng, yet you want to marry his friend. Are you challenging the limits of my patience? Your parents were loyal to my father, and they died in the middle of a mission issued by my father. My father only took you as his godson out of guilt.","“A mere godson can never measure up to me. You’ll be my lapdog for life.”","He wasn’t worried about Zhao Feng overhearing his words. In his view, he was already showing Zhao Feng a lot of respect by speaking softly.","...","Over on Chu Feng’s side, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation energy flowed steadily into the sacred item. At the same time, Bai Yunqing and Li Wu’s formation was being simultaneously transferred over.","But Chu Feng didn’t make a move right away. He was waiting for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to make the first move, so when things finally went awry, they would just think that their formation had gone awry.","No one would doubt Chu Feng.","The aura of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation suddenly changed, causing the sacred item to tremble. The formation grew increasingly powerful, radiating a brilliant light as if it were the sun.","Now, the weaker cultivators couldn’t even see the sacred item.","“Looks like the sacred item’s door is opening.”","“It’s working!”","“Is that the prowess of world spiritists?”","“I understand now why they say that world spiritists are indispensable for remnants.”","The eyes of the Netherworld Sect’s experts glowed in delight. They thought that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was earnestly helping them to awaken the sacred item, but in truth, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had just begun stealing control of the sacred item.","“The show has finally begun. Let’s see who can take control of the sacred item’s power.”","Chu Feng closed his eyes. His expression was unchanged, but in truth, he had secretly begun channeling Bai Yunqing and Li Wu’s formation.","Moments later, his heart swelled in delight.","Indeed, it was not easy to take control of the sacred item, but thanks to Li Wu’s unique curse energy, he succeeded in gaining control over a portion of the sacred item’s power.","“Now, I have claimed the initiative.”","Boom!","The sacred item’s door suddenly opened. It was just a small slit of a few centimeters, an insignificant gap compared to the sheer size of the sacred item, but it made everyone’s heart shudder.","All the cultivators present sensed incomparable power.","But before they could analyze what was within the door, a dark red light shot out from the gap, causing the hearts of the Netherworld Sect’s and Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s experts to clench up.","Even the Netherworld Sect’s experts seated on the four thrones around the sacred item stood up at the same time.","The dark red light moved so fast that it pierced through the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation and enveloped Chu Feng and the other juniors before anyone could make a move.","“What is that?”","The Netherworld Sect’s juniors were all flustered.","“Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, what the hell are you all up to?” the neutral faction’s Cang Li roared furiously.","The dark red light didn’t kill Chu Feng or any of the juniors, but it inflicted excruciating pain on them. On top of that, it also isolated them from the rest of the world. Those inside couldn’t leave, and those outside couldn’t enter.","“Chu Feng!” Eggy called out worriedly.","“Don’t worry, I’m the one behind this. I constructed this protective formation out of the sacred item’s energy,” Chu Feng replied.","“You have gained control over the sacred item?” Eggy was delighted to hear that.","But Chu Feng replied, “Not yet. The sacred item’s power is unfathomably great and enigmatic. It’s easy to awaken it, but exerting control over it proves to be extremely difficult. This is the limit of what I can do at the moment.","“I constructed this protective formation to protect me in case they notice my tampering, but above that, it also serves to confuse both the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. It’ll mislead them into thinking that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation has incurred the sacred item’s backlash, prompting it to attack the Netherworld Sect’s juniors.”","Eggy’s eyes lit up in delight. “So, you’re intentionally inflicting pain on them?”","Most of the Netherworld Sect’s juniors were frowning in pain.","“We shouldn’t half-ass the show, after all. But this is just the beginning. You’ll see the climax when I gain control over more of the sacred item’s energy,” Chu Feng replied.","“Oh? What are you planning to do?” Eggy was intrigued.","“No rush. You’ll know in a jiffy.”","“Tsk. Keeping me in suspense, huh?” Eggy pouted, though her eyes gleamed in anticipation.","Chu Feng opened his eyes because he needed to feign pain as well.","Out of curiosity, Eggy also watched the other juniors via his eyes. All of a sudden, her gaze fell upon Chen Hui’s lackey, the dark-skinned man who kept secretly threatening Chu Feng while he was busy fusing formations into his Netherworld Embryo.","The dark-skinned man had completely dropped his earlier arrogance. He clutched his head while rolling all around the ground. He was in so much pain that his mouth was crooked and his eyes were rolled up.","Chen Hui anxiously rushed to his side and fed him some invaluable pills, but that did little to alleviate the dark-skinned man’s pain.","“Y-y-young master Chen Hui, I have brought you shame,” the dark-skinned man said with a stutter as tears streamed from his eyes.","He was faring the worst of all the juniors gathered here. He had no idea why that was the case, but it made him appear as the weakest one here. He felt embarrassed because of that.","Chen Hui was perplexed. He was also enduring the sacred item’s energy, but he didn’t think it was that unbearable. He couldn’t understand why his companion was acting in such a manner.","“Hahaha! Chu Feng, isn’t that lad in far greater pain compared to the others? You must have taken special care of him,” Eggy asked with a hearty laugh.","“Of course.”","“Didn’t you tell me that he’s not worth my attention?” Eggy’s lips twisted in mischief.","“He isn’t worth your attention, but I am a man who returns favors,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6533,"title":"Chapter 6533: Chapter 6531: Ambition Revealed?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6531: Ambition Revealed?","Ignorant of the truth, Cang Li flitted up to the formation and grabbed a Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. “Free our juniors right now!”","“I-I can’t do it. We’re not the ones controlling the formation. Our Mansion Master is the one controlling the formation!” the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist blurted out. This confirmed that Jie Tianran was the one channeling the formation.","“Damn it!”","Cang Li shoved the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist aside and smashed his fist into the dark red barrier imprisoning Chu Feng and the other Netherworld Sect’s juniors. His punch was so strong that it caused shockwaves, but the barrier didn’t even shake.","The fury in Cang Li’s eyes blazed, but he didn’t continue attacking the barrier.","Instead, he took out a talisman paper and activated it. A spirit formation gate manifested.","He stepped into the spirit formation gate and entered a teleportation passageway. The teleportation passageway was quite short; it didn’t take him long to reach the other end, where he was transported into a vast spatial realm.","This spatial realm was located at the topmost region of the Undying Starfield. There was no scenery to be seen in this spatial realm. Rather, it was filled with formations and huge swathes of people, both from the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Cang Li rushed to the center of the spatial realm, where the formation cores were located.","There were many Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists sitting in each of the formation cores, but there was only one person in the centermost formation core—Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran’s eyes were shut. His left hand formed hand seals, while his right hand operated a golden compass. The golden compass was ancient and had a unique design. It was designed not for searching treasures but to probe formations.","Golden talisman papers emanating the Immemorial Era’s aura floated above Jie Tianran. Each one harnessed a powerful formation, making them extremely valuable, but there were over ten thousand of them gathered here.","Whenever Jie Tianran flicked his finger, a golden talisman would descend into the golden compass, and the golden compass would temporarily emit a mystical glow.","“Jie Tianran, release our Netherworld Sect’s juniors right now!” Cang Li roared at Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran raised his head and glanced at Cang Li before closing his eyes once more. He continued forming hand seals while replying, “To think that you’re an elder in the Netherworld Sect. Can’t you tell that the barrier was made from your sacred item’s energy? What does it have to do with me?”","His impatient voice indicated that he had no respect for Cang Li whatsoever.","“I don’t care about that. It might be our sacred item’s energy, but you’re the one who caused it. You better find a solution right now!” Cang Li growled.","“My Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has come here to help you to awaken your sacred item. You can tell me directly if you don’t need our help. We’ll leave right away,” Jie Tianran said.","“Leave? Don’t even think about leaving until you have freed our juniors,” Cang Li spat coldly.","Everyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, except for Jie Tianran, directed displeased looks at Cang Li.","Just then, a figure flitted up to Cang Li. It was Baili Xukong.","“Lord Cang Li.” Even the esteemed leader of the new faction respectfully greeted Cang Li before continuing, “I know you’re worried about our juniors, but our juniors are still faring fine right now.”","Baili Xukong gestured toward an observation formation beneath them, which reflected the situation around the sacred item. Even though the juniors shrouded in the dark red barrier were clearly in pain, they didn’t seem to be in danger yet.","Except for the dark-skinned man.","“Look at that dark-skinned lad. He’s on the verge of death!” Cang Li pointed out.","“But the others are fine. That fellow from the conservative faction is probably weaker than the others. I hate to say this, but we’re dealing with the sacred item here. It’s inevitable that we’ll incur some sacrifices while trying to awaken it,” Baili Xukong said.","“So you also know that we’re dealing with the sacred item here, Baili Xukong. I’d be more than willing to die for its awakening, but can you guarantee that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion can pull it off?” Cang Li asked.","Jie Tianran immediately replied, “The fact that I’m here shows that I’m confident.”","Cang Li pointed at Jie Tianran, wanting to say more, but Baili Xukong dragged him away.","“Lord Cang Li, I know you don’t trust the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but we have already tried everything to awaken the sacred item. If there was any other choice, we would have never sought their help. This is our last resort. We’re doing this for our Netherworld Sect’s future,” Baili Xukong told Cang Li via voice transmission.","“Baili Xukong, I don’t agree with how you do things, but I acknowledge your loyalty to the Netherworld Sect. However, Jie Tianran is a man blinded by ambition. He would kill even his daughter and his grandson if they stood in his way. Someone like him wouldn’t sincerely help our Netherworld Sect.","“We have tried everything to awaken the sacred item, and while we have never succeeded, we have never been attacked by the sacred item either. The sacred item belongs to us even though we’re unable to harness its powers. Unless blasphemed, there’s no reason for the sacred item to attack any of our sectmembers,” Cang Li revealed his thoughts via voice transmission.","He wasn’t just worried about the juniors. He had a feeling that something was amiss as well.","“Lord Cang Li, are you saying that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is secretly tampering with the sacred item without our knowledge, and that provoked its aggression?” Baili Xukong asked.","“What if Jie Tianran plants a gu inside the sacred item? That could become a huge disaster in the future even if we successfully awaken the sacred item and harness its power,” Cang Li said.","Baili Xukong frowned. That prompted him to take another look at the observation formation, which showed the trapped Netherworld Sect’s juniors.","He was no fool. In truth, he had already considered the possibility that Cang Li had proposed, but he went ahead with the plan because he trusted the sacred item. He didn’t believe that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion could grasp control of it even if they tried.","That said, he still wouldn’t forgive the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if they were up to something behind his back.","Uwa!","Just then, all the Netherworld Sect’s juniors trapped inside the red aura barrier, including Chu Feng and the dark-skinned man, grabbed their heads and screamed in pain. Even Chen Hui did the same.","As if they had been hypnotized, they kneeled, kowtowed to the sacred item, and spoke in unison, “Lord Sacred Item, please spare us. We merely wished to borrow your power. We didn’t mean to control you. Please spare us.”","Then, they kowtowed once more.","“What’s going on?”","The expressions of the Netherworld Sectmembers warped. Many of their experts stood up and surrounded the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. Something was clearly amiss.","The sacred item must have relayed some information to the juniors for them to apologize.","Cang Li pointed a finger at Jie Tianran and berated, “Look at what you have done, Jie Tianran! Are you trying to control our sect’s sacred item through your formation?”","Even Baili Xukong’s eyes turned cold. “I expect an explanation, Mansion Master.”","The Netherworld Sectmembers whipped out their weapons while eyeing the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in animosity."]},{"number":6534,"title":"Chapter 6534: Chapter 6532: Utter Scum","paragraphs":["Chapter 6532: Utter Scum","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists revealed flustered looks, especially the elites gathered in the formation core below.","They knew that they were attempting to control the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item via the formation, and they didn’t think that the sacred item could communicate with the Netherworld Sect’s juniors. This would expose them.","A battle would be inevitable.","But one person in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion remained unfazed, and that was Jie Tianran.","“You fools. I don’t need to go one big round just to deal with the Netherworld Sect,” Jie Tianran said.","“We have tried many ways to awaken our sacred item, but not once has such a situation happened. You were the one channeling the formation. Shouldn’t you know better than any of us what’s going on?” Baili Xukong questioned.","“Someone is indeed trying to take control of your sacred item. That person has even tapped into your sacred item’s power to beguile your juniors, forcing them to utter such slander. That person isn’t from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Jie Tianran stated.","“What a joke. The only ones here other than our Netherworld Sect is your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Are you saying that our sectmember has taken control of your formation?” Cang Li sneered.","“That is precisely what I’m saying.”","Jie Tianran flung his right hand, and the compass in his grasp rose into the sky. A ray of light shot out of the compass into the observation formation, locking onto Chu Feng and the juniors trapped inside the red aura barrier.","Through the observation formation, the light gushed into the Undying Starfield.","From the viewpoint of Chu Feng and the others, it looked like the light had descended out of nowhere and enveloped them.","“What is that?”","Even the relaxed Eggy rose to her feet. Her instincts told her that something bad was about to happen.","Chu Feng frowned as well, but he didn’t panic. Instead, he remarked with a sigh, “I have underestimated that old thing Jie Tianran.”","...","Cang Li had no idea what Jie Tianran was trying to do, so he further probed, “What do you mean by this?”","“The person seeking to control the sacred item is among them,” Jie Tianran declared, his voice echoing not just in the spatial realm but throughout the Undying Starfield.","The golden talisman papers floating above Jie Tianran surged toward the glowing compass, amplifying its prowess. The light enveloping Chu Feng and the others narrowed down to shroud just a single person—Chu Feng.","“Feng Chu?” Cang Li’s eyes narrowed.","Jie Tianran sneered, “Take a good look. This is the man who is trying to control your Netherworld Sect’s sacred item. Are you going to continue maligning my Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?”","“Cut the bullshit! You want to frame our Netherworld Sectmember with just a random formation?” Cang Li didn’t trust Jie Tianran, especially since the latter was accusing a sectmember who wielded immense potential.","Even Baili Xukong narrowed his eyes in skepticism.","Jie Tianran’s formation might have looked formidable, but none of them could discern if he was telling the truth. This might just be all an act.","“My means aren’t to be disputed by the likes of you. Reveal yourself!”","Jie Tianran changed his hand seal. Several talisman papers flew into the compass before flowing along with the light like a school of fish, descending from the sky. As they landed on Chu Feng, the space around him began to distort.","Even the Netherworld Sect’s veil and cloak, which boasted great concealment prowess, turned transparent.","“What’s that, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","“Jie Tianran’s formation is more potent than I thought. At this rate, he’s going to strip away my disguise and lock onto my bond with the sacred item. It looks like I can’t hide it anymore.”","Knowing that he would soon be revealed, Chu Feng decided to drop the act and stand up. Instead of waiting for his clothes to become transparent and appear bare naked before the crowd, he would rather preserve his dignity.","“Jie Tianran, there’s no need for this unnecessary move.”","Chu Feng waved his sleeves and took off his veil. Beneath it was no longer his altered appearance but his true face.","“Chu Feng?!”","Chen Hui, Cang Li, Jimo Qianzhou, Baili Xukong, and all Netherworld Sectmembers were horrified.","Even Jie Tianran, who had remained composed all this while, shot to his feet, and his face reflected his utmost shock. He didn’t think that the person hindering him was Chu Feng.","“Feng Chu? Chu Feng? After all that has happened, it turns out that he’s Chu Feng?” Cang Li had complicated feelings about this situation.","It was the same for Chen Hui as well. He thought that a monstrous prodigy had appeared in the Netherworld Sect, but the other party turned out to be Chu Feng.","However, he couldn’t speak to Chu Feng. He needed to draw a line between him and Chu Feng, or else he would implicate not just himself but the entire conservative faction.","Just then, a voice transmission was relayed to Chen Hui. “Brother Chen Hui, will your conservative faction dare take me in if I join you right now?”","It was from Chu Feng. He was looking at Chen Hui with a mischievous smile.","“Chu Feng! To think that I took you as my brother! As if fooling me wasn’t enough, you even want to drag me down right now?” Chen Hui replied via voice transmission.","“Brother? Did you really take me as a brother during the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s entrance examination? Or were you just curious to see me?” Chu Feng replied.","“I admit that I was curious about the man who has charmed Song Yun, but after meeting you... Forget it, it’s all in the past. What are you doing right now? Is Jie Tianran speaking the truth? Are you behind the sacred item’s backlash? Are you trying to steal our sacred item right now?” Chen Hui asked.","“What do you plan to do if I covet your Netherworld Sect’s sacred item?” Chu Feng asked.","“Then you shouldn’t blame me for turning against you.”","Chen Hui’s gaze turned cold. He endured the pain and struggled to his feet. Killing intent seeped out from him.","Uwa!","Chen Hui barely lifted himself up before falling heavily back onto the ground.","“You don’t have the strength to stop me now,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Now that he wielded some of the sacred item’s power, he could suppress even Heavenly God level cultivators in the vicinity, let alone Chen Hui.","While he was talking to Chen Hui, the Netherworld Sectmembers finally snapped out of their shock. They drew their weapons and encircled Chu Feng.","Similarly, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists teleported over and joined forces to construct a sealing formation to trap Chu Feng.","Both powers already had an agenda against Chu Feng, and this matter only further worsened their ties.","But Jie Tianran continued staring at the observation formation without uttering a word.","His heart had remained as calm as still water during the sacred item’s backlash and the Netherworld Sect’s questioning, knowing that everything was under control. But when he saw Chu Feng’s face, his emotions went amok. Fury washed over him, especially when he recalled how the latter had stolen the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy from him not too long ago.","Just then, Chu Feng raised his head to look at the sky, specifically where Jie Tianran was.","“What are you doing now, Jie Tianran? I infiltrated the Netherworld Sect on your behalf so that you can attain full control over the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item. Are you framing it all on me now that you can get away scot-free? You truly are a scum,” Chu Feng berated."]},{"number":6535,"title":"Chapter 6535: Chapter 6533: A Clash of Formations","paragraphs":["Chapter 6533: A Clash of Formations","Upon hearing Chu Feng’s words, the Netherworld Sect eyed the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion with renewed wariness.","In the spatial realm, Baili Xukong and Cang Li also turned to look at Jie Tianran. They were aware that Chu Feng was attempting to drive a wedge in their relationship, but at the same time, the sacred item was so important to them that they couldn’t allow anything to go wrong.","Jie Tianran would have to prove his innocence to them.","Jie Tianran hadn’t expected Chu Feng to be this shameless, and that further fanned his anger. Even so, he kept his temper in and replied, “Chu Feng, there’s no one in the world of cultivation who doesn’t know about our ties. You are the one person whom I’ll never work with, so save your effort!”","His words echoed loudly across the Undying Starfield.","“Jie Tianran, there’s no one in the world of cultivation who doesn’t know about your despicable nature. There’s no deed beyond you. You even backstabbed your daughter in the name of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s interests. Naturally, you’re only going to deny our relationship to the bitter end.”","It was not without reason that Chu Feng insisted that he was colluding with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. In truth, Jie Tianran’s formation was powerful, to the point where he could have potentially gained control of the sacred item if granted more time.","Currently, the two of them were vying for control over the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item.","Both parties were still far from success, but the competition was already on.","It wouldn’t be a problem if that was all, but if Jie Tianran learned that Chu Feng’s true intention was not to gain full control of the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item but instead borrow its energy to channel a formation and suppress their cultivation, he might change his strategy and move to curb Chu Feng.","Jie Tianran’s means couldn’t be underestimated. He could lock onto Chu Feng even when the latter was already using the sacred item’s power to protect himself. There was no such thing as excessive caution when dealing with Jie Tianran.","So, Chu Feng was hoping to use this matter to mislead Jie Tianran. He wanted to let the other party think that he was driving a wedge in his ties with the Netherworld Sect to distract him so that he would fall behind him in the competition to control the sacred item.","“Chu Feng, we are all world spiritists here. Such lowly tricks are meaningless. If you want to control the sacred item, speak with your skills. But let me warn you. This isn’t the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. There are no old things here to ensure fairness,” Jie Tianran spoke with a voice dripping in disdain.","He was also channeling the formation to take control of the sacred item. He glanced at Baili Xukong and Cang Li. “Don’t disturb us from channeling our formation if you don’t want your sacred item to be under that little bastard’s control. All you have to do is to seal off the area and don’t let that little bastard escape.”","Jie Tianran flung his sleeves.","The talisman papers floating above him descended and fused into the bodies of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists. The world spiritists began emanating divine lights.","“Channel the formation with me!”","The remaining talisman papers fused into the formation.","Even the nature of the formation changed as a result. It became less radiant, but it exuded an ancient, overwhelming power that everyone in the sacred item’s vicinity could feel.","Cang Li narrowed his eyes in skepticism, but he didn’t stop them.","“Lord Cang Li, there have been clashes between Chu Feng and our Netherworld Sect. I don't know how he slipped into the Undying Starfield, but he is definitely up to no good. If I have to choose between the two of them, I’d rather trust Jie Tianran,” Baili Xukong said before he went off to make arrangements.","He gathered the Netherworld Sect’s experts to form a seal around the sacred item to block Chu Feng’s escape routes.","Cang Li understood where Baili Xukong was coming from. Given the current circumstances, they had no choice but to go with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","His eyes glanced at the detection formation constructed by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. It encompassed the entire Undying Starfield, and while it couldn’t see what every individual was doing, it showed whether they harnessed a Netherworld Embryo in them. It was reflected in the formation that Chu Feng had a Netherworld Embryo.","“The rumors are true. He has fused with a Netherworld Embryo. If only he was brought into our sect together with Song Yun... Haa! But there are no ifs in this world,” Cang Li sighed.","He had heard about Chu Feng—the latter was known to be loyal to his friends. He could have become a huge asset that would bulk up their Netherworld Sect, but their paths crossed only to diverge.","...","Chu Feng could see experts from the Netherworld Sect encircling him. They whipped out treasures and cooperated with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists to seal off the area around him, forming an inescapable net.","But he didn’t have the spare energy to deal with that. He had to put his full attention into controlling the sacred item, to the point where he was starting to get flustered.","He couldn’t tell whether it was due to Li Wu’s curse energy or Jie Tianran’s formation, but the power lying dormant in the sacred item had fully awakened. If he wanted to, he could activate the sacred item right away for the Netherworld Sect’s use.","He could already tell that the sacred item’s power had the ability to metamorphose the Netherworld Embryo. He could hardly imagine how strong the Netherworld Embryo would become if the Netherworld Sect obtained this power.","Awakening the sacred item was effortless, but stopping its power from being used was a tall order.","“This is a headache.” Chu Feng felt stressed.","It would be terrible if Jie Tianran changed his mind and attempted to activate the sacred item instead of controlling it. He could only pray that Jie Tianran wouldn’t do that. If he could sense the sacred item’s power, Jie Tianran must be able to feel it as well.","Under normal circumstances, someone as selfish as Jie Tianran wouldn’t fulfill the Netherworld Sect’s wish. But again, there was no way to tell what Jie Tianran would do.","Chu Feng suddenly frowned. “I knew that old thing wouldn’t let the peace remain for long.”","Jie Tianran had found Chu Feng’s formation and was launching a two-pronged attack against it. He attempted to siphon spirit power away from Chu Feng’s formation while inflicting damage at its very core.","But Chu Feng didn’t panic. He had prepared countermeasures.","Instead, it was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists who frowned. They discovered that Chu Feng had bound his formation to theirs, making it hard for them to siphon spirit power away from Chu Feng’s formation. Moreover, damaging Chu Feng’s formation would cause greater damage to their own.","“How is that little bastard so troublesome to deal with? Isn’t he just a True Dragon World Spiritist?”","The elite world spiritists of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion tasted despair. In their opinion, there was no way to purge Chu Feng’s formation.","All of a sudden, the world quaked.","Everyone turned their eyes to Jie Tianran.","The cause of the quake was an ancient red talisman paper in Jie Tianran’s hand. The talisman paper squirmed as if it had a life of its own. More importantly, it harnessed great spirit power.","Even Cang Li narrowed his eyes. “The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has many secret hands.”","Jie Tianran’s voice boomed within the Undying Starfield. “Chu Feng, do you think I can’t do anything about you just because you’re holing up in my formation?”","He was about to fuse the red talisman paper into the formation when he suddenly stopped moving."]},{"number":6536,"title":"Chapter 6536: Chapter 6534: Inner Demon","paragraphs":["Chapter 6534: Inner Demon","Chu Feng’s eyes widened. He noticed that his formation was suddenly seeping into the sacred item faster than before. The curse energy in his formation had become stronger.","“Miss Li Wu, please hold on a little longer.”","Chu Feng knew that Li Wu must have made a move.","Meanwhile, there was a concealed warship parked not too far away from the Undying Starfield. Sitting with crossed legs on the ship were Li Wu and Bai Yunqing. The former was channeling her energy, whereas the latter was supporting her with his formation.","Their efforts greatly reinforced the formation over on Chu Feng’s side, though it also suffused the warship with curse energy as well.","Wen Xue stood by the corner. She reached out and grabbed a sliver of curse energy. As Li Wu was consciously controlling the curse energy, it didn’t hurt Wen Xue.","“What formidable curse energy.” Wen Xue examined the curse energy before turning her eyes back to Li Wu. “I wonder what kind of entity you are to wield such tremendous power.”","A guess popped into her head, and the corners of her lips curled into a bizarre smile. Viciousness, vileness, and greed, traits that were at odds with her innocent face, surfaced in her eyes.","But Bai Yunqing and Li Wu were too focused on helping Chu Feng reinforce the formation that they didn’t notice it.","...","On Chu Feng’s side, Jie Tianran continued attempting to remove Chu Feng’s formation away from his, but he didn’t double down on his efforts. To curb Jie Tianran, Chu Feng deepened the link between his formation and Jie Tianran’s.","“I see. That old thing sure is scheming.” Chu Feng suddenly realized something.","Jie Tianran must have realized that Li Wu’s curse energy was more effective at assimilating the sacred item, so he wanted to exploit it. As both formations were tied together, Jie Tianran could, to some extent, tap into Li Wu’s curse energy as well if he utilized the correct methods.","He had wanted to remove Chu Feng’s formation earlier because he didn’t want Chu Feng to take advantage of him, but upon realizing that Chu Feng’s formation was more effective, he had decided to take advantage of Chu Feng instead.","He had made a perfunctory effort to remove Chu Feng’s formation to pull wool over Chu Feng’s eyes.","“Old thing, you must think that you’re taking advantage of me, but I bet you don’t know that you’re just playing into my hand.”","While Chu Feng was dissatisfied with Jie Tianran’s underhanded move, the last thing he wanted was for Jie Tianran to interfere with his efforts. This worked out for him. His true goal was not to control the sacred item but to tap into its power to activate the suppression talisman paper.","The talisman paper Jie Tianran had taken out earlier was still floating next to him; he hadn’t used it yet.","“Jie Tianran, you can’t bear to use your treasure?” Cang Li questioned.","It was obvious to anyone watching that Jie Tianran had planned to activate the talisman paper to strengthen the formation to deal with Chu Feng, but Jie Tianran had refrained from activating it in the end.","Cang Li assumed that Jie Tianran couldn’t bear to use it.","“Keep your thoughts to yourself. It’s beyond you to interfere with the affairs of world spiritists. I have my own intentions,” Jie Tianran snorted impatiently.","Chu Feng was right. Jie Tianran had stopped removing Chu Feng’s formation because he realized that Chu Feng’s formation quickened the assimilation of the sacred item. He simply wanted to make use of Chu Feng.","But he couldn’t possibly tell Cang Li that.","“What powerful curse energy. It’s very compatible with the sacred item. Your grandson has quite the means to obtain something like that,” the old entity told Jie Tianran.","“He’s just paving the way for me,” Jie Tianran snorted.","“Jie Tianran, your grandson is a cunning one. It’s not your first time crossing blows with him. When have you managed to take advantage of him? You’re using his formation to hasten the assimilation of the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item, but do you think he doesn’t know that?”","“You’re saying that little bastard is doing it on purpose?”","“I can’t say for sure. On the surface, it looks like you’re taking advantage of that brat, but something feels off.”","“Hahaha...” Jie Tianran suddenly burst into laughter.","“What are you laughing at?” The old monster was displeased.","“You’re letting your fear get ahead of you. Just because that little bastard outdid us several times, you overestimate his capabilities and doubt your own ability. As for me, I don’t let my emotions get in the way of my judgment. No matter the situation, I’ll face it with confidence,” Jie Tianran replied.","“Jie Tianran, confidence is a virtue, but conceit is a bane. Your overconfidence might just lead you into another one of your grandson’s traps. People like you, who have been in a position of power for a long time, are exceptionally prone to that. I have been through that myself,” the old entity said.","“My confidence is founded on concrete grounds, and I have you here with me. I won’t let Chu Feng get away this time,” Jie Tianran replied.","“Indeed. Now that your grandson knows about my existence, I’ll be humiliated as well if he outdoes you. I’ll lend you my strength,” the old entity said.","A surge of energy flowed into Jie Tianran’s body, and his formation was enhanced without activating the formation paper.","However, Jie Tianran said, “Leave this formation to me. If you want to make a move... why don’t you construct a sealing formation just in case?”","“Hasn’t the Netherworld Sect already constructed a tight net?” the old entity asked.","“The Netherworld Sect? The fact that Chu Feng slipped in here is a testament to their incompetence. Besides, Chu Feng possesses strong escape means. That’s why he remains calm despite being surrounded. We can’t count on them to capture Chu Feng,” Jie Tianran said.","“That makes sense. I’m confident of trapping Chu Feng here as long as he doesn’t use the sacred item to flee,” the old entity said.","“Don’t worry, I won’t let him have the sacred item’s power. It is mine,” Jie Tianran replied confidently."]},{"number":6537,"title":"Chapter 6537: Chapter 6535: Betrayal","paragraphs":["Chapter 6535: Betrayal","As time passed, Li Wu’s curse energy weakened, and the rate of assimilation of Chu Feng’s formation began to slow.","“That little bastard is at his limit. It’s time to dump him.”","Seeing that he had squeezed Chu Feng’s value dry, Jie Tianran flicked his finger.","The red talisman paper that he had taken out earlier but hadn’t used yet descended and fused into his formation. The control formation swiftly turned red throughout, and it took only an instant for it to eject Chu Feng’s formation from it.","“That old thing is quite skilled at backstabbing,” Chu Feng scoffed.","“It’s time to show the Netherworld Sect what we, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, are capable of,” Jie Tianran declared. He waved his sleeves, and another twenty talisman papers flew forth.","Ten of these talisman papers were golden, and the other ten were black. They harnessed spirit power that was nowhere weaker than the red talisman paper, but they moved as if they had a life of their own. Clearly, they were invaluable treasures.","The golden talisman papers emanated fierce auras, whereas the black talisman papers emanated sinister auras. They had different uses.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has benefited a lot from ruling over the world of cultivation for so many years.” Cang Li frowned.","He might not be a world spiritist, but he could tell that Jie Tianran’s talisman papers were invaluable treasures. Even possessing one was already a huge thing, but Jie Tianran used twenty of them in a single shot without batting an eyelid.","And this was nothing but a glimpse of Jie Tianran’s wealth. Jie Tianran wouldn’t stake all his assets to help the Netherworld Sect. It only went to say that he possessed many more of such talisman papers.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was much wealthier than the Netherworld Sect had thought.","Shoosh!","The golden and the black talisman papers fused into the control formation. The red energy faded, replaced by an amalgamation of black energy and golden energy.","“This feeling... That old thing has a few tricks up his sleeve.”","Chu Feng sensed Jie Tianran’s control formation becoming stronger in real time. The latter wasn’t about to leave any room for Chu Feng to make a comeback. At this rate, it was only a matter of time before Jie Tianran’s formation became stronger than Chu Feng’s.","But the greatest threat to Chu Feng was not Jie Tianran gaining greater control over the sacred item than him, but that Jie Tianran was simultaneously suppressing Chu Feng’s control over the sacred item as well.","So, Chu Feng stopped reinforcing his control over the sacred item and instead channeled his spirit power to fend against Jie Tianran’s suppression.","“That little bastard is still too young. Even if you guard your current progress, it means nothing when my control over the sacred item surpasses you,” Jie Tianran sneered.","Everything was going according to his plan. He had successfully distracted Chu Feng from reinforcing his control over the sacred item. While Chu Feng’s progress had stagnated, Jie Tianran made quick progress and soon overtook him.","But Jie Tianran wasn’t content with just this. He took out ten more golden talisman papers with a wave of his sleeves and fused them into the formation.","Cang Li began wiping the cold sweat off his forehead. “That Jie Tianran isn’t one to strike a losing deal. How much does he intend to get out of our Netherworld Sect if he’s expending so many treasures to help us awaken our sacred item?”","He was previously worried that Jie Tianran couldn’t bear to use his treasures, but now, he was worried about Jie Tianran using too many treasures. After all, Jie Tianran would surely settle the bills with their Netherworld Sect afterward.","“What’s the situation, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","She couldn’t see the situation with the sacred item, but she could sense the changes in Jie Tianran’s control formation. Jie Tianran’s control formation had begun emanating the sacred item’s aura, a sign that both had begun to assimilate.","This wasn’t good news.","“Jie Tianran has used treasures to reinforce his control formation, and his control over the sacred item has now surpassed mine. However, he isn’t going all out yet; he seems to be secretly doing something on the side. I don’t know what that old thing is planning, but you don’t have to worry. He won’t gain control of that sacred item so easily.”","In contrast, Chu Feng wasn’t very worried.","Eggy’s heart was set at ease. She knew Chu Feng well, and the latter wasn’t one to feign composure. He must be confident.","“What do we do now?” Eggy asked.","“We can already channel the suppression talisman paper,” Chu Feng replied.","“Why aren’t you channeling it yet then?” As Eggy said those words, her eyes suddenly widened, and a mischievous smile formed on her face. “I know. You must be up to no good. Are you going to pull one over on your grandfather again? Let’s infuriate that old thing to death this time.”","“Infuriate him to death? That would be a fitting death for him,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Jie Tianran couldn’t hear Chu Feng and Eggy’s conversation. He just thought that everything was going according to plan. All of a sudden, he turned to Cang Li and said, “Cang Li, take a good look and judge for yourself whether I’m helping your Netherworld Sect or not.”","Jie Tianran suddenly changed his hand seal, and the Undying Starfield shook.","Two golden formation hands extended from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s control formation and grasped the sacred item’s door.","Boom!","The two formation hands exerted force, and the door began to slowly open.","A strong but sinister dark red aura gushed out from the sacred item. It looked as if tens of thousands of ghosts were gushing out from the gates of hell to suffuse the surroundings."]},{"number":6538,"title":"Chapter 6538: Chapter 6536: Suppression","paragraphs":["Chapter 6536: Suppression","“The sacred item has awakened! The sacred item has awakened! Did the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion succeed?” The Netherworld Sectmembers were overjoyed.","When the dark red aura gushed out from the sacred item, the Netherworld Sectmembers felt a calling from their Netherworld Embryos. There had to be a connection between the two. If it were possible to further evolve the Netherworld Embryo, it would be through the sacred item.","“Jie Tianran lives up to his reputation as the strongest world spiritist in the world of cultivation.” Even Cang Li, who had been guarded against Jie Tianran, had to acknowledge the latter.","The Netherworld Sect had tried many ways to awaken the sacred item, but nothing worked. While the sacred item hadn’t fully awakened yet, they could at least see hope in it now.","Jie Tianran’s voice boomed across the Undying Starfield, “Chu Feng, you exploited a slip-up from the Netherworld Sect to infiltrate my control formation, hoping to stop me from awakening the Netherworld Sect’s treasure. But this isn’t the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. There is no entity here to enforce fairness between us. Now, you can only watch helplessly as I awaken the Netherworld Sect’s treasure. Do you understand your place now?”","He had intentionally flaunted his progress to taunt Chu Feng.","This was at odds with Jie Tianran’s character. He was a proud person, and he viewed it beneath himself to taunt others. But he had suffered so many setbacks at Chu Feng’s hands that he felt like he had to get even.","He had claimed earlier that the old entity had grown afraid of Chu Feng, but the truth was that he was the one who had grown afraid of Chu Feng. That was why he wanted to prove himself by outdoing Chu Feng here.","He had to thoroughly crush Chu Feng here to expel his inner demon and regain his confidence. This would be extremely beneficial to his future growth.","“You speak as if you have already won, Jie Tianran. I’m still here. What can you do about me?” Chu Feng said as he stood up.","Even though it might seem that the light emanating from the sacred item had trapped Chu Feng, in truth, it was protecting him. This barrier was the basis of his confidence.","“Take a good look. I’ll show you what I can do,” Jie Tianran declared.","His control formation flickered, and the barrier protecting Chu Feng began to weaken. This greatly bolstered the confidence of those from the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","In their view, Jie Tianran was slowly removing Chu Feng’s grasp over the sacred item.","Chu Feng even heard the mocking laughter of some Netherworld Sectmembers.","“Aren’t you celebrating too early? I’m able to tap into the sacred item’s power because I have grasped some control of it. Jie Tianran doesn’t have the power to remove my control of your sacred item. He can only unravel the barrier because he possesses greater control over the sacred item than I do at the moment. Do you think he’s truly helping you awaken your sacred item? How naive. His goal is to gain full control of the sacred item. All of you will become his puppets,” Chu Feng said.","That was the greatest worry of the Netherworld Sect at hand. None of them could laugh anymore after hearing Chu Feng’s words.","“Chu Feng, you can’t escape your crimes by driving a wedge between us. Today is the day you’re going down,” Baili Xukong declared. His words made it clear that he was standing on the side of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Oh?”","Chu Feng raised his hand. He dragged all the Netherworld Sect’s juniors, including Chen Hui, before him using the sacred item’s energy. “You said that I’m going down. Are you intending to forsake your people?”","Chu Feng looked at Baili Xukong.","“Chu Feng, blaspheming our sacred item is already a death sentence. If you obediently surrender, I can still consider leaving you with an intact corpse. Otherwise, we’ll kill you and everyone associated with you,” Baili Xukong said.","“I see. Chen Hui’s life must be unimportant to you. Let’s do this then.”","Chu Feng shot out a formation chain that pierced Chen Hui’s body, but the latter didn’t sustain any injuries. It was a one-sided life binding formation.","Chen Hui’s death would not affect Chu Feng, but if Chu Feng died, Chen Hui would suffer the same plight as well.","“Brother Chu Feng, we’re at least acquainted with each other, no? I-I-I-I haven’t lived long enough yet!” Chen Hui anxiously sent Chu Feng a voice transmission.","“It’s a misunderstanding, Brother Chen Hui. I don’t intend to drag you down. I’m merely using this opportunity to see how much the Netherworld Sect cares about you. If they are willing to abandon you, I suggest you stop risking your life for the Netherworld Sect and join me instead,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission.","“That fellow named Baili Xukong is Baili Zilin’s father, as well as the leader of the new faction. He wants nothing more than our deaths. Your binding our lives together works to his advantage,” Chen Hui exclaimed.","“Don’t worry, neither of us is dying here,” Chu Feng replied.","“Chu Feng, you’re already a dead man. Stop playing such underhanded games. Why don’t you just step out and face your death like a true man?” Baili Xukong said.","He did hope for Chen Hui’s death, but he couldn’t make it too obvious.","“I’m already a dead man?”","Chu Feng pulled Chen Hui into a formation realm inside his palm before revealing a confident smirk. The Netherworld Sectmembers who didn’t know Chu Feng well might find him laughable. It was futile to threaten Baili Xukong with Chen Hui’s life.","But those familiar with Chu Feng felt their nerves becoming taut. Even Jie Tianran shuddered, as he quickly racked his brain to wonder what was off.","Chu Feng was clearly scheming something.","And indeed, Chu Feng raised his head to look at Jie Tianran. “Jie Tianran, you must think that you’re very clever to exploit my formation to reinforce your control over the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item. It does sound like the perfect plan.","“I can tell you right now that my true goal is neither to hinder the sacred item’s awakening nor to gain full control over the sacred item. I only want to borrow the sacred item’s power to suppress all of you.”","“Suppress all of us?”","The Netherworld Sectmembers were first taken aback by Chu Feng’s declaration, then they found his words utterly hilarious. How could Chu Feng even think about using their sacred item to suppress them? That was ridiculous!","Chu Feng formed a hand seal, and smiles vanished from everyone’s faces.","The sacred item emanated immense pressure that enveloped the Undying Starfield. The weaker ones didn’t suffer as huge of a backlash, but experts like Baili Xukong and the four elders seated on the platforms frowned. Some of them even let out pained groans.","All Heavenly God level cultivators and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists felt the pressure seeping into them and crushing their bodies and souls, plunging them into unbearable pain. There was only one way to escape this pain, and that was to lower their cultivation."]},{"number":6539,"title":"Chapter 6539: Chapter 6537: Take a Good Look","paragraphs":["Chapter 6537: Take a Good Look","“Hurry up and suppress your cultivation!” Baili Xukong used the formation to relay his voice throughout the entire Undying Starfield.","Thus, all Heavenly God level experts began suppressing their cultivation. As they lowered their cultivation, the terrifying pain subsided.","But Baili Xukong and the others felt no relief whatsoever. The suppression grew stronger with each passing moment. If they wanted to avoid the unbearable pain, they would have to continue suppressing their cultivation.","Chu Feng was right.","Who could have thought that the top experts from the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion would be suppressed by a mere junior?","“What’s happening, Jie Tianran?” Cang Li questioned.","He, Jie Tianran, and the others were in a formation realm outside the Undying Starfield, but they could sense the suppression imposed on the Undying Starfield. What was even more shocking was that Chu Feng was indeed pulling it off using their sacred item!","This was unacceptable to the Netherworld Sect.","“It is Chu Feng’s doing. Why are you asking me? Do you think I was the one who ordered him to do that?” Jie Tianran glared at Cang Li.","Cang Li was rendered speechless.","Indeed, Chu Feng was the one causing trouble, so Jie Tianran shouldn’t take blame for this. However, Cang Li still didn’t trust Jie Tianran, and he doubted that a single junior could pull off such a huge feat by himself.","He suspected that Jie Tianran had played a part in this.","“What’s his motive for doing this? What does he stand to gain by risking his life to infiltrate the Undying Starfield just to suppress our cultivation?” Cang Li asked.","“His cultivation is too weak. He isn’t a match for us. He probably thinks that he can act as he pleases once he suppresses our cultivation with the sacred item’s power. As for his motive, doesn’t he have a grudge against your Netherworld Sect? He must be here for vengeance.”","Jie Tianran shirked all responsibility to the Netherworld Sect.","“He must have an agenda even if he’s not here for vengeance. As long as he suppresses everyone’s cultivation to a level beneath him in the Undying Starfield, he would be free to do whatever he wants,” Jie Tianran added.","“Do you have a countermeasure? We can’t let him act as he pleases. It’s not just about our Netherworld Sect anymore; your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion's reputation is at stake,” Cang Li said.","The Netherworld Sect was indeed powerless before this situation. They could only bank their hopes on Jie Tianran.","If Jie Tianran stopped Chu Feng, he would be freed from suspicions of colluding with Chu Feng.","“Calm down. Leave it to me,” Jie Tianran said.","He issued an order for more Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to enter the Undying Starfield. They were to gather around the sacred item to construct a new formation.","At the same time, he began constructing another smaller but intricate formation. It was connected to the formation constructed by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists, but his was the main body.","But this also meant that his formation was more difficult to construct.","Even after the other world spiritists completed their formation, Jie Tianran still hadn’t completed his smaller formation yet.","Meanwhile, the sacred item’s suppression energy had already lowered everyone’s cultivation down to rank one Heavenly God and rank one Heavenly Dragon.","“Do something, Jie Tianran!” Baili Xukong couldn’t remain calm when his cultivation was on the verge of being lowered to True God level. He shouted to Jie Tianran for help.","“Don’t worry. He won’t be able to do much as long as I’m here,” Jie Tianran said as he took out a purple talisman paper.","This purple talisman paper was more potent than the talisman papers before. The moment it was fused into Jie Tianran’s formation, the formation’s aura flared. The formation was prepared specifically for this talisman paper!","“Activate!” Jie Tianran roared.","A purple light pillar descended from above the sacred item and fused with the formation constructed by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists.","Chu Feng’s heart skipped a beat. He sensed that the purple formation was the bane of his suppression formation. He could have lowered everyone’s cultivation down to True God level, but from the moment the purple formation fused into the sacred item, he knew he couldn’t do that anymore.","That was how powerful the purple formation was!","“Chu Feng, why did your suppression stop? Is that all you’re capable of?” Jie Tianran sneered.","“To think that someone like you is the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, Jie Tianran. You rely on treasures to cross blows with a junior like me. You’re only a match for me because of the wealth your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has accumulated over the years. But given your incompetence, it’s only a matter of time before you squander everything away,” Chu Feng scoffed.","The purple formation was indeed formidable, but its true prowess stemmed from the treasure and not Jie Tianran’s skills.","“The ability to acquire resources is a skill as well. A lowly person from a wretched background like you can only be envious of me, but that’s simply your life. This is life, Chu Feng. Someone as wretched as you isn’t worthy of the Ruler’s Bloodline,” Jie Tianran said.","“Yes, this is life,” Chu Feng replied.","Jie Tianran was baffled. He was taunting Chu Feng, but he didn’t expect the latter to concede. That put him at a loss instead. But what Chu Feng said next caused him to clench his teeth, and he nearly lost his composure.","“That’s how I was able to trample on you over and over again. That’s how I punched you in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and stole your legacy from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. You won’t be able to defeat me here, either. You might have all the resources in the world, but you can only lose to me again and again. You can only helplessly watch me walk away each time. Jie Tianran, this is life. I have accepted it. Have you?” Chu Feng said.","“What a joke. Are you incapable of reading the tides? You’re cornered,” Jie Tianran sneered.","Anyone with eyes could tell that Jie Tianran was no longer as calm as he was before. His voice carried a snarl to it.","“Cornered? If you truly think so, why don’t you step into the Undying Starfield instead of holing yourself up out there? You don’t dare to do so, right? Because you know that if I can suppress the others, I can do the same to you as well,” Chu Feng said.","“Hilarious! I shall unravel the remaining control you have over the sacred item right now. Suppress me? Let’s see how you can do that!”","Jie Tianran took out another purple talisman paper and fused it into the purple formation. That greatly strengthened the purple formation.","His goal was to completely unravel Chu Feng’s suppression formation.","“Take a good look then.”","Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and groans echoed within the Undying Starfield.","“Damn it, we have fallen for his trap!” Cang Li’s face paled.","They had underestimated the prowess of Chu Feng’s suppression formation.","Just suppressing one’s cultivation was not enough. Instead, one’s true cultivation couldn’t exceed rank one Heavenly God or rank one Heavenly Dragon. Those who were suppressing their cultivation like Baili Xukong would only continue to be tortured by the suppression.","To make things worse, the suppression was extremely potent. At this rate, those who were suppressing their cultivation would die.","Cang Li attempted to activate the teleportation formation, only to realize that it was not working. That suppression formation had also suppressed the teleportation formation!","“Jie Tianran, save them!” Cang Li turned to Jie Tianran for help.","The teleportation formation came from Jie Tianran’s hand. If anyone could make the teleportation formation work, it would be Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran had noticed the problem at the same time as Cang Li. He tried to activate the teleportation formation as well, but the result was the same. Not even he could activate the teleportation formation!","“Gah!”","Miserable cries echoed from around the sacred item. They were all coming from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. Those who had been constructing the formation around the sacred item were now bleeding from their eyes, nostrils, ears, and mouth. They were in so much pain that they clutched their heads and rolled all around.","The immense suppression on them eroded their rationality, and they were on the verge of exploding from within.","“Take a good look, Jie Tianran. See who I am suppressing right now,” Chu Feng said."]},{"number":6540,"title":"Chapter 6540: Chapter 6538: Execute Him on the Spot","paragraphs":["Chapter 6538: Execute Him on the Spot","“That despicable little bastard!” Jie Tianran’s lips quivered.","Even Cang Li was flabbergasted. He had thought that Jie Tianran was incapable of displaying emotions, but it turned out that he got angry as well.","Jie Tianran didn’t expect Chu Feng to be this despicable. Not only did he suppress his teleportation formation, but he also misled all of them into thinking that they could lower their cultivation to circumvent the suppression power.","Chu Feng waited for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to dispatch more Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists into the Undying Starfield before revealing the true potency of the suppression formation.","It was fortunate that he didn’t enter, or else he would have made a fool of himself.","He took out a transparent bead with a flick of his wrist. In the bead was a door plastered with talisman papers. Each of these talisman papers harnessed powerful teleportation energy.","“Jie Tianran, that’s your life preservation means. Are you going to expend its energy just to rescue those incompetent world spiritists?” the old entity exclaimed in astonishment.","“That little bastard has mocked me again and again. If I let him get his way without doing anything at all, I wouldn’t be worthy of my position as the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master,” Jie Tianran said.","Upon hearing those words, the old monster decided not to say anything more. He understood that Jie Tianran was not doing this to rescue his world spiritists but to uphold his ego. This was critical as it could impact his future cultivation.","He needed to fight back even if it meant emptying his coffers!","“Please do not resist. I’ll take you out right now,” Jie Tianran’s voice echoed throughout the Undying Starfield.","He formed a hand seal. The door flew out from the bead and expanded to over a hundred meters in height. It was not exceptionally big, but the moment it opened, powerful teleportation energy gushed out from within.","The talisman papers plastered on the door burst into flames one after another.","Figures emerged from within the door. They included Baili Xukong and experts whose cultivation was above rank one Heavenly God and rank one Heavenly Dragon.","“Oh?”","Chu Feng also noticed that surges of teleportation energy were appearing out of thin air and rescuing the experts who were being suppressed.","“That isn’t a teleportation formation. It is a treasure, isn’t it?” Eggy asked.","“Yes, it seems so,” Chu Feng replied.","“What formidable teleportation energy. Looks like it’s another secret hand of your loser grandfather.” Eggy was surprised. She didn’t see the true form of the treasure, but she could tell from its potency how formidable it was.","“It is indeed incredible, but it’s lacking compared to my elder’s power,” Chu Feng replied.","Those words were directed at not just Eggy but the Divine Deer as well.","“I’ll save you even if you don’t flatter me,” the Divine Deer said.","“Hehe, I know. I’m just speaking the truth,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Don’t underestimate your grandfather. The treasures in his possession are something to be reckoned with. He might have other hands as well,” the Divine Deer warned.","“Elder, do you think he has treasures that can trap us here?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course not,” the Divine Deer replied.","“That’s good to hear.” That bolstered Chu Feng’s confidence.","Meanwhile, as Baili Xukong and the others entered the formation realm, they saw the door plastered with talisman papers. They realized that Jie Tianran must have used a formidable treasure to rescue them.","“Thank you for saving us, Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master.”","Baili Xukong and the others clasped their fists to thank Jie Tianran.","Even the four elders, who had been seated on the platforms, did the same as well. They were top experts from the neutral faction.","By now, it had become clear that Jie Tianran wasn’t colluding with Chu Feng. Otherwise, the suppression power inside the Undying Starfield would have been enough to take their lives.","“You’re being too polite. I’m just doing what I should,” Jie Tianran replied.","“Mansion Master, is there really no way to stop Chu Feng?” Baili Xukong asked.","“Calm down. Chu Feng hasn’t fully grasped the sacred item yet. He’s merely tapping into its power to enhance the effects of a cultivation suppression treasure. Such treasures tend to come with strict restrictions. He won’t be able to maintain the suppression for long.","“You also don’t have to worry about him gaining full control of your sacred item. In just a short while, I’ll remove his control over your sacred item and unravel the barrier protecting him. So, tell your people to prepare themselves. Don’t let him get away,” Jie Tianran instructed.","“Milords, this matter concerns our Netherworld Sect’s sacred item. Nothing must happen to the sacred item, or else we won’t be able to face Lord Netherworld Master. Chu Feng is a cunning man; there’s no knowing what treasures he has. We can’t let him catch a breather, or else it might come back to bite us in the future. I suggest killing him as soon as the energy protecting him unravels,” Baili Xukong told the neutral faction’s experts.","The meaning behind his words couldn’t be clearer. They couldn’t let Chu Feng go even if the latter held Chen Hui as a hostage.","The neutral faction’s experts fell silent. They must be secretly discussing this matter via voice transmission. Soon, one of them relayed the verdict, “Chu Feng has undermined our authority and blasphemed our sacred item. That is an unforgivable crime. Relay my order. That man is to be executed on the spot!”","Baili Xukong quickly relayed the order.","The order echoed throughout the Undying Starfield, so even Chen Hui could hear it as well.","“It’s over. Chu Feng, you must be my nemesis! I know I left without saying farewell back then, but you don’t have to do me dirty like that!” Chen Hui fell to the ground in despair. He, too, was afraid of death.","“Don’t worry, I’ll take you out of here alive,” Chu Feng replied.","He was still busy stabilizing the suppression formation. While he couldn’t further the suppression due to Jie Tianran’s interference, there would be nothing to fear if he could just stabilize it at rank one Heavenly God and rank one Heavenly Dragon.","...","Despite such a huge incident happening in the Undying Starfield, the formation realm where Feng Ling was imprisoned remained the same as ever. This formation realm was designed to be isolated from the world so that Baili Zilin could focus on his cultivation, so the voices outside couldn’t reach within.","“Why do I feel so nervous? Did something happen?” Baili Zilin looked at the horizon with contemplative eyes.","He couldn’t sense anything outside while he was inside this formation realm, but he vaguely sensed that something had happened, possibly due to his connection with his father.","Just then, Zhao Feng flew over."]},{"number":6541,"title":"Chapter 6541: Chapter 6539: The Netherworld Sect’s Determination, the Annihilation Formation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6539: The Netherworld Sect’s Determination, the Annihilation Formation","“Little brother Zilin, the deed is done. Please take a look,” Zhao Feng said.","Baili Zilin followed Zhao Feng into the palace that served as a prison. They walked into the deepest area of the palace, where a door stood. A miserable sight awaited them on the other side of the door. There was a massive cage forged out of a treasure.","Imprisoned in the cage were tens of thousands of natural oddities. Some maintained their human form, whereas some had reverted to their original appearances. All of them were injured as if they had suffered cruel torture.","The torture wasn’t just inflicted on their bodies but their souls as well. This was the result of serving as the Netherworld Sectmembers’ cultivation medium.","At this rate, all of them would be tortured to death.","Yet, two treasures inside the cage continued to emanate energy.","One was a powerful control energy that controlled their bodies, preventing them from escaping and ending their own lives.","The other healed them.","Of course, the Netherworld Sect wasn’t healing them out of the kindness of their hearts. They merely wanted the natural oddities to die slower so that they could squeeze every bit of their value out.","The healing energy became the most terrifying torture tool to the natural oddities.","Baili Zilin had grown accustomed to this sight. He wasn’t fazed in the least. He took a casual glance around before his gaze fell upon the center of the prison.","At the center of the prison was a newly constructed formation, which had a person bound in it—Feng Ling.","Zhao Feng walked up to the formation, looked at her, and said, “Feng Ling, how dare you assault my little brother Zilin? Were it left to me, I would have you killed a thousand times over. However, my magnanimous little brother Zilin is willing to grant you a second chance. I’ll ask you right now—will you take this chance or not?”","Feng Ling smiled, “I want...”","That’s all you amount to before the threat of death , Zhao Feng scoffed in his heart. Had he known that she was so afraid of death, he would have threatened her right from the start instead of treating her so politely.","But Feng Ling continued, “I want you to suffer a fate worse than death.”","Zhao Feng’s disdain was immediately replaced by anger.","“You’re asking for it.” He pointed his token at Feng Ling.","Boom!","The formation was activated.","The sacred item’s energy flowed from the formation into Feng Ling’s body, then out of her body into Zhao Feng’s palm. It only took moments for her face to turn pale. Her muscles tensed up so much that her veins could be seen.","Feng Ling was in tremendous pain. The formation siphoned away her energy and refined it into a cultivation resource for Zhao Feng.","Soon, her hair began turning white from the tip. Her skin began to wither and wrinkle. She was aging at an extremely swift pace.","Even so, she still gritted her teeth and refused to utter a word of plea or let out a groan. Instead, she glared at Zhao Feng.","“I’d like to see how long you can put on that tough front for!”","The anger in Zhao Feng’s eyes flared. He hiked up the intensity of the formation.","“Godbrother, there’s no need for that. You can marry Feng Ling straightaway if you’re truly fond of her. You don’t have to torture her like that for my sake.” Surprisingly, Baili Zilin began speaking up for Feng Ling.","Zhao Feng was taken aback.","Doesn’t Baili Zilin hope for Feng Ling’s death? Isn’t he angry at me because I want to marry Feng Ling? There’s no way someone as vindictive as him can forgive Feng Ling after the latter tried to take his life.","He must be doing it on purpose. It’s a test.","So, Zhao Feng replied with a determined expression, “Little brother Zilin, I don’t care that Feng Ling toys with my feelings, but I can’t forgive her for daring to harm you. From the moment she made a move against you, her fate was sealed. She has to die today, no matter whether she’s willing to marry me or not.”","“Forget it. You can do whatever you want.” Baili Zilin glanced at Feng Ling before walking out.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng’s expression twitched.","He sensed a crack appearing in Feng Ling’s life stone, a sign that she was in danger. At the same time, an invisible aura emerged from the crack and guided him.","“Is it there?”","Following the guidance with his gaze, it led to a place near the sacred item.","So, he formed a hand seal and unleashed a powerful wave of spirit power.","The sacred item’s light intensified. It didn’t take long for Chu Feng and the other Netherworld Sect’s juniors to be concealed under the light.","“Is he finally at his limit? It’s time for his life to come to an end.”","A cold glint flashed across Baili Xukong’s eyes. He had been waiting for this moment. While he couldn’t enter the Undying Starfield and kill Chu Feng in person due to the suppression energy, he had already stationed all available rank one Heavenly God level Netherworld Sectmembers in the sacred item’s vicinity.","In total, they had at least 700 rank one Heavenly Gods gathered here.","Even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion dispatched 59 rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","There was no way someone who hadn’t reached Heavenly God or Heavenly Dragon could escape from such an encirclement.","“Chu Feng is removing the barrier on his own accord,” Jie Tianran suddenly said.","That remark initially had everyone confused. Why would Chu Feng remove the barrier protecting him on his own accord?","“He must have realized that the sacred item’s power won’t protect him for long, so he’s looking for an opportunity to slip away,” Baili Xukong murmured. So, he projected his voice across the Undying Starfield, “Keep a close eye on him. You absolutely mustn’t allow Chu Feng to escape. Kill him as soon as the barrier unravels!”","Just then, the barrier shrouding Chu Feng and the other Netherworld Sect’s juniors dissipated.","Surprisingly, Cang Li closed his eyes at this moment.","“Now!” Baili Xukong roared.","Countless whizzing noises echoed within the Undying Starfield. Countless dark red martial power scythes of over a thousand meters in length, each one wielding tremendous destructive prowess, surged toward Chu Feng.","This was the Annihilation Formation prepared by the Netherworld Sect’s 700 Heavenly Gods. The sheer prowess of this formation was sufficient to instantly vanquish a smaller realm.","That was also the reason Cang Li closed his eyes.","The Netherworld Sect had over 700 rank one Heavenly Gods in the Undying Starfield; they could have easily killed Chu Feng with any other means, be it through oppressive might, martial power, or martial skills.","There were countless ways they could have specifically targeted Chu Feng.","But to avoid any mishaps, they chose the Annihilation Formation.","Even though they had limited its range to avoid damaging the sacred item, it would still kill all the Netherworld Sect’s juniors who were currently trapped with Chu Feng.","But Chu Feng had to die today. These were necessary sacrifices to make to uphold the Netherworld Sect’s dignity. Cang Li understood that, which was why the only thing he could do was to avert his gaze.","In the face of the Annihilation Formation, Chu Feng fearlessly muttered, “Divine Evasion.”"]},{"number":6542,"title":"Chapter 6542: Chapter 6540: This is a Divine Skill!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6540: This is a Divine Skill!","Chu Feng activated all available means to raise his cultivation, shrouding him in not just lightning but a thin layer of divine white light as well.","The unthinkable happened.","The dark red scythes ravaged the area where Chu Feng was. The Netherworld Sect’s juniors were sliced into bits before they could even react, resulting in the splattering of fresh blood all around.","But these Netherworld Sect’s juniors were merely collateral damage. The true target of the Annihilation Formation was Chu Feng.","The martial power scythes precisely sliced through Chu Feng one after another, but Chu Feng remained unharmed as if he had absorbed those attacks.","Cang Li’s eyes shot open in disbelief.","Baili Xukong and the others were horrified as well. They had gone as far as to sacrifice their juniors in order to take down Chu Feng, but Chu Feng emerged unharmed from it. How could they accept such an outcome?","“Is this all the Netherworld Sect’s Annihilation Formation is capable of? Or are you going easy on Chu Feng?” the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists surrounding Chu Feng asked.","“You say that we have gone easy on Chu Feng? You bastards! Are you blind? Can’t you see that even our juniors were caught in the crossfire?”","The Netherworld Sect’s rank one Heavenly Gods were infuriated upon hearing the question. They felt an urge to bombard the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists with their Annihilation Formation so that they would know whether they had gone easy or not.","“Heed my order, world spiritists of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Kill Chu Feng!” Jie Tianran’s voice echoed across the Undying Starfield.","A golden light sphere reminiscent of a mini realm manifested around Chu Feng, trapping him within. Light twisted and warped within the golden light sphere as destructive energy ravaged within.","This was the slaughter formation prepared by the 50 rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","But the faces of the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists soon crumbled as they realized that their formations were incapable of hurting Chu Feng.","“Hah!” Chu Feng sneered.","This was only possible because of the strongest move he had inherited from the Divine Deer—Divine Evasion.","Divine Concealment obscured his aura.","Divine Flitting enhanced his speed.","Divine Evasion made him invulnerable to attacks from even rank two Heavenly Gods, even when his cultivation was capped at rank nine True God level. And this was only what it was capable of at True God level. It would grow even stronger once he reached Heavenly God.","“He must have a treasure capable of averting all attacks. Use a sealing formation to trap him in place instead!” Jie Tianran roared.","The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists hurriedly channeled a sealing formation, filling the surroundings with light chains. At the same time, the Netherworld Sect’s Heavenly Gods also reinforced the encirclement they had laid beforehand.","“Treasure? How shallow-minded. You can’t even tell that it’s a divine skill,” Chu Feng scoffed.","He stood up and confidently strutted right through the bombardment of attacks and the sealing formation. These powerful forces were unable to faze Chu Feng as if they existed in different dimensions.","They could only watch helplessly as Chu Feng slipped past their means and flitted into the distance.","“Chase him!”","The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists and the Heavenly Gods pursued Chu Feng, but to their shock, they were unable to catch up with him. Even rank two Heavenly Gods couldn’t match the speed of Chu Feng’s Divine Flitting, let alone them.","It was thanks to the combined prowess of Divine Flitting and Divine Evasion that Chu Feng didn’t fear these rank one Heavenly Gods and rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","“Divine skill? Is he talking about the legendary divine skills?” a Netherworld Sect’s elder from the neutral faction remarked contemplatively.","“I have lived for a long time now, but I have never met a True God level cultivator escaping so easily from the encirclement of hundreds of Heavenly Gods and dozens of Heavenly Dragons. Could it be that Chu Feng has truly grasped a legendary divine skill?” Cang Li murmured as he glanced at Jie Tianran.","He was unsure about this, so he was hoping that Jie Tianran could provide a concrete answer.","“It doesn’t matter whether he has grasped a divine skill or not. The important thing is that Chu Feng has escaped. Jie Tianran, you sure have raised a fine grandson!” Baili Xukong mocked Jie Tianran.","He knew about the enmity between Jie Tianran and Chu Feng, but the blood ties between the two made him subconsciously direct his anger toward Jie Tianran.","“There are no ties between me and that little bastard. Since we’re on that topic, I also ought to say that you have raised a fine son. If I’m not mistaken, Chu Feng had no grudge against your Netherworld Sect until your son provoked him. If you’re finding someone to blame now, the first thing you should do is to drag out your son and execute him,” Jie Tianran scoffed.","Baili Xukong’s lips twitched. He couldn’t continue venting on Jie Tianran anymore, but that made him calm down instead.","“That is just hearsay, Mansion Master. He has been harboring enmity toward our Netherworld Sect ever since one of our Netherworld Envoys planted a Netherworld Embryo in him. This has nothing to do with Zilin.","“If we’re talking about conflict, he has a much deeper grudge against your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Regardless of whether that was a divine skill or not, that was not means that an ordinary cultivator ought to possess. If he’s already capable of this much as a True God, can you imagine what he can do upon reaching Heavenly God level? Are you sure your protective formations can keep him at bay?” Baili Xukong asked.","They could no longer deny that Chu Feng was a terrifying prodigy. Without a doubt, he would pose a massive threat to all of them in due time.","“Don’t worry. He won’t be able to escape from the Undying Starfield.”","Powerful teleportation energy suddenly manifested where Chu Feng and the Netherworld Sect’s juniors were previously trapped, and a figure appeared.","Jie Tianran, Cang Li, Baili Xukong, and the others exclaimed in shock, “Chu Feng?!”","Indeed, it was Chu Feng.","To make things worse, all the Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists had left the sacred item’s vicinity to pursue Chu Feng, leaving it unprotected.","“This is bad. Chu Feng must have left a teleportation talisman paper behind. He has planned this all along. He intends to continue dealing with the sacred item!” Baili Xukong exclaimed.","Everyone from the Netherworld Sect tensed up.","Contrary to what they had expected, Chu Feng flitted into a space not too far away from the sacred item and punched into thin air. His fist, imbued with spirit power, shattered space into fragments. An entrance appeared, and he stepped into it.","“I get it now. Chu Feng’s goal was never the sacred item. He is here to rescue a friend, and he tapped into the sacred item’s power to suppress our cultivation in order to do so,” Cang Li said.","Many agreed with Cang Li’s judgment. That explained all of Chu Feng’s irrational moves."]},{"number":6543,"title":"Chapter 6543: Chapter 6541: The Number One Expert Under Heavenly God?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6541: The Number One Expert Under Heavenly God?","“Chu Feng didn’t come to the Netherworld Sect in search of vengeance, and he doesn’t seek to destroy the sacred item, either. There’s just someone he wishes to rescue among the natural oddities captured.”","An old man with snowy hair appeared in the formation realm. He wore the Netherworld Sect’s robe, but he exuded an ethereal air as if he were an immortal unfazed by secular affairs. He was a rank five Heavenly God level cultivator.","He was Dongfang Hansong, the leader of the conservative faction.","Dongfang Hansong had been here all along, just that he had quietly observed the situation as a spectator instead of joining the conversation.","But now, he looked at Baili Xukong and said, “Look at what you have done, Baili Xukong. You insisted on capturing those natural oddities to use them as a medium for cultivation. That was what drew Chu Feng here.”","Baili Xukong sneered in response, “We don’t know for sure whether Chu Feng’s goal is to rescue a friend, but just his audacious attempt to control our sacred item makes him deserving of death.”","“Chu Feng deserves death, but that doesn’t change the fact that your new faction is what sparked this mess. If anything happens to the sacred item, your new faction bears as much responsibility as Chu Feng,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“No matter what happens, I, Baili Xukong, will take responsibility for this matter, but what’s important right now is to eliminate that vermin, Chu Feng. Why don’t you spend your energy coming up with ways to deal with Chu Feng instead of questioning me?”","In the meantime, Baili Xukong had already ordered the Netherworld Sect’s Heavenly Gods to return to the sacred item to kill Chu Feng.","Dongfang Hansong didn’t say anything more. He had only spoken up right now to tarnish Baili Xukong’s reputation in front of the neutral faction so that the neutral faction would side with his conservative faction.","As for eliminating Chu Feng...","He had no idea how to do so, but even if he thought of something, he wouldn’t voice it aloud. This was the ideal chance to eliminate the new faction. The more havoc Chu Feng caused, the worse the new faction’s position would be.","There was no reason for him to stop Chu Feng.","...","In the formation realm, Baili Zilin left the prison, but instead of returning to the mountain, he made his way to a remote area.","He was breathing raggedly, and his face was distorted in frenzy.","“What came over me earlier? Why did I speak up for Feng Ling? Didn’t I wish for her death? Does this mean that I subconsciously fear Chu Feng’s vengeance? No, that can’t be possible. How can I, Baili Zilin, be so cowardly? How could I possibly fear that Chu Feng? What’s wrong with me?”","Baili Zilin refuted his conjecture, but at the same time, he couldn’t make sense of why he had spoken up for Feng Ling earlier.","Just then, he felt a strong aura heading in his direction. He raised his head, only to widen his eyes in disbelief.","The lightning-clad invader was approaching him at an extremely fast speed, but he still managed to get a clear look at the other party’s face.","“Chu Feng?”","Shock and incomprehension gripped Baili Zilin. It didn’t make sense for Chu Feng to be here. The top experts of the Netherworld Sects were all protecting this area. Even his father and the neutral faction’s powerhouses were here.","Despite his confusion, he still drew his God Armament and raised his cultivation from rank seven to rank nine True God level, with heaven-defying battle power of a single rank.","That happened to match Chu Feng’s current cultivation level.","Chu Feng was at rank six True God level, but after unleashing the Lightning Mark, Lightning Armor, Lightning Wings, and Lightning Aura, his cultivation was currently also at rank nine True God level, with heaven-defying battle power of a single rank.","“Is this heaven’s will? You appeared before me right after I came out of closed-door training.”","Baili Zilin hurriedly composed himself. He knew that Chu Feng had long noticed him and was intentionally heading his way. A fight was inevitable.","“Very well. Today, I shall spill your blood to prove to the world that I, Baili Zilin, am the number one expert under the Heavenly Gods!”","As he clenched his fists, two dark red God Armament sabers appeared in his grasp. He channeled his vast reserves of martial power into the two sabers, causing the surrounding space to distort.","“Rank three God Taboo, Demon Blood Inferno Slash!”","Baili Zilin swung both sabers simultaneously, unleashing a red aura that devoured the sky. His attack covered such a vast expanse that it resembled a massive blood cloud. One could even smell a horrendous blood stench coming from it.","He had spent many years learning this move, and he had only recently mastered it. He was extremely confident in it, for this attack was not only highly destructive but also absurdly fast.","Given their current distance, Chu Feng would surely die.","Little did he know that Chu Feng could have easily dodged this attack with Divine Flitting, though he chose not to do so. Instead, he whipped out the Lightning Flame Sword.","“He isn’t channeling his martial power. Is he planning to withstand my rank three God Taboo without using martial skills?” Baili Zilin was confused.","This should have been good news to Baili Zilin, but he felt so displeased that he bellowed, “Chu Feng, are you underestimating my martial skill now? How dare you underestimate me?!”","While he was shouting, Chu Feng had already swung his Lightning Flame Sword.","Baili Zilin froze up.","With just a casual slash, Chu Feng had split open the God Taboo Martial Skill that he had spent many years mastering.","“Baili Zilin, I don’t underestimate your martial skill, but I do have a low opinion of you. Your true cultivation might have reached rank seven True God level, but your fighting prowess remains so weak. Someone who grew hastily by stacking cultivation resources can’t possibly match me.”","While Chu Feng was speaking, he arrived before Baili Zilin and swung his blade down on him.","By the time Baili Zilin snapped out of his daze, it was already too late to dodge Chu Feng’s attack. So, he raised his two God Armament sabers to withstand the attack.","What happened next made him widen his eyes in disbelief.","Chu Feng’s Lightning Flame Sword sliced through his two ‘True’ character God Armaments as easily as a heated knife slicing through butter.","But before Chu Feng could slice Baili Zilin apart, a powerful surge of spirit power sprang out from the latter’s body and protected him.","“You’re carrying quite a lot of treasures.”","Chu Feng could tell that it was a protective formation generated by a treasure.","Baili Zilin smirked in glee when he saw that Chu Feng was unable to do anything to him. “Hmph! Despite all your words, Chu Feng, you are still unable to hurt me...”","Before he could finish his words, his expression stiffened once more.","Chu Feng opened his palm to reveal two bizarre powers that swiftly enveloped Baili Zilin. They were Protection Bane and Dark Plunder.","Baili Zilin had no idea what was happening, but he could sense the spirit power protecting him being swiftly siphoned away. At the same time, he sensed that Chu Feng had taken something important away from him, though he couldn’t tell what it was."]},{"number":6544,"title":"Chapter 6544: Chapter 6542: The Netherworld Sect’s Hero","paragraphs":["Chapter 6542: The Netherworld Sect’s Hero","“What kind of vile means is that?”","Baili Zilin was flustered. His instincts told him that he was in danger, so he anxiously took out a teleportation talisman paper and activated it without hesitation.","Powerful teleportation energy gushed out from the talisman paper and enveloped Baili Zilin.","Chu Feng could tell right away that the teleportation energy was too powerful for him to seal off, so he quickly swung his sword once more.","By then, half of Baili Zilin’s body was already covered by the teleportation energy, but Chu Feng still managed to sever half of his thigh and arm.","Baili Zilin managed to escape, but Chu Feng was unfazed. He wasn’t here to look for Baili Zilin; their encounter here was a coincidence. He had only planned to hold Baili Zilin hostage.","He figured that neither the conservative faction nor the new faction could easily touch him if he were to secure both Chen Hui and Baili Zilin. Even if Baili Xukong could turn a blind eye to Chen Hui’s plight, there was no way he would watch as his son died.","His failure to capture Baili Zilin was unfortunate, but it was not significant. His true goal was to rescue Feng Ling, after all.","On that note, encountering Baili Zilin here had given Chu Feng some ideas.","Meanwhile, Baili Zilin had been teleported to a safe region within the formation realm, but his severed arm and thigh continued to spurt blood. He couldn’t stop the bleeding, no matter what he did, as Chu Feng’s attack had wounded his soul. His face and lips turned as pale as a sheet of paper.","“Damn it! Damn it! What did he do earlier? And what is he doing here in the first place?”","Everything had been so abrupt that Baili Zilin fell into a daze. In fact, he had only confronted Chu Feng out of sheer instinct.","“Could it be...”","But upon calming down, he thought of a possibility.","Is Chu Feng here to save Feng Ling?","Thus, he endured the pain and made his way toward Feng Ling’s prison.","By the time Baili Zilin understood what was going on, Chu Feng had already arrived at the deepest area of the palace, where Feng Ling and the other natural oddities were imprisoned.","Chu Feng had taken on Baili Zilin’s appearance.","He kicked the final door open, and there, he finally saw Feng Ling.","Anger gushed into his head the moment he saw her. She looked nothing like the beautiful lady he knew. Her skin was dry and wrinkled, and her black hair had turned white. Her breathing was faint, and she struggled to even open her eyes.","Standing in front of Feng Ling was Zhao Feng, who was still devouring Feng Ling’s energy through the formation.","“Little brother Zilin?” Zhao Feng was taken aback.","“Release her!” Chu Feng ordered.","Even though he was already on the verge of running amok, he forced himself to remain calm and spoke with an authoritative tone while concealing his anger. He had never met Zhao Feng before, but he could tell from the other party’s demeanor that he was afraid of Baili Zilin.","So, he walked straight up to Feng Ling without paying any heed to Zhao Feng and rescued her from the formation.","And indeed, Zhao Feng dared not to stop him. He even took a step back nervously.","Chu Feng turned his gaze toward the natural oddities imprisoned in cages. Even though his primary objective was to rescue Feng Ling, witnessing the terrible plight of these natural oddities further fanned his fury.","“Let them out,” Chu Feng ordered.","“What are you doing, little brother Zilin? We need to use them as a medium for our...” Zhao Feng tried to seek an explanation for Baili Zilin’s irrational order.","Chu Feng raised his eyebrows in displeasure as he asked, “Do I need to explain myself to you?”","“Of course not! You’re right. We don’t need these natural oddities anymore.”","Intimidated, Zhao Feng hurriedly released the natural oddities.","Chu Feng took out a treasure and stowed all the natural oddities into it before taking his leave.","He was very tempted to slay Zhao Feng right now, but the latter was a rank one Heavenly God level cultivator.","To make things worse, the Netherworld Sect was keeping track of his movements through an observation formation. It wouldn’t be long before the other experts from the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion arrived here.","So, he first took Feng Ling out of the prison. While walking out, he suddenly halted his footsteps to take one good look at Zhao Feng. Killing intent flared in his eyes. “I’ll claim your life.”","Then, he vanished in the palace.","“What has come over you, little brother Zilin? What did you mean by that? Why are you saying that you’ll claim my life?” Zhao Feng was bewildered.","He thought that Baili Zilin was probing him earlier when he said that there was no need to hurt Feng Ling, but he wasn’t so sure about that now. He could tell that Baili Zilin truly intended to kill him from his earlier gaze. He had never felt such terrifying killing intent.","Oblivious to the truth, he chased after Baili Zilin, hoping to get an explanation. I should quickly clear up any misunderstandings between us.","To his astonishment, he was unable to keep up with Baili Zilin.","“How is little brother Zilin so fast?” Zhao Feng could only watch helplessly as Baili Zilin’s figure grew further and further away from him.","“Where’s Feng Ling?”","Zhao Feng suddenly heard a voice behind him. He turned around and was stupefied.","Another Baili Zilin was heading in his direction, but this one had sustained severe injuries and didn’t have Feng Ling with him. He had lost half an arm and half a thigh.","“Little brother Zilin, who hurt you?” Zhao Feng rushed up to Baili Zilin and asked.","“I’m asking you, where’s Feng Ling!” Baili Zilin roared.","“Didn’t you just take her away?” Zhao Feng struggled to make sense of the situation in the spur of the moment.","“You fool! That wasn’t me, but Chu Feng! Chu Feng!!! He came here to rescue Feng Ling, but you let him get away with it just like that?” Baili Zilin bellowed.","“Chu Feng? Are you saying that person was Chu Feng?”","Zhao Feng’s buzzing mind immediately cleared up. That explained why the earlier ‘Baili Zilin’ had cast such a murderous glare at him before leaving.","“Was Chu Feng the one who injured you?” Zhao Feng asked on.","“I would have been dead if not for my father’s teleportation talisman paper!” Baili Zilin huffed.","“Audacious! How dare that scumbag Chu Feng hurt my little brother Zilin? Stay here and recuperate, little brother Zilin. I’ll apprehend Chu Feng right away for you to deal with!”","Zhao Feng drew his weapon and gave chase to Chu Feng. Much to his surprise, he realized that some power was hindering him from utilizing means that raised his cultivation. It was as if this space forbade the existence of cultivators above rank one Heavenly God level.","But this wasn’t the time to be thinking. Catching Chu Feng took priority.","When he left the formation realm, he could finally hear Baili Xukong’s voice.","Jie Tianran was tracking Chu Feng’s whereabouts using an observation formation. Chu Feng couldn’t circumvent the surveillance even after disguising himself as Baili Zilin.","Baili Xukong was issuing orders for the Netherworld Sectmembers to capture Chu Feng.","Zhao Feng quickly found the other Netherworld Sectmembers and asked them about the situation. The more he heard, the more shaken up he was. He couldn’t believe that Chu Feng had suppressed everyone’s cultivation using the sacred item’s power.","To think that Chu Feng would go to such lengths to rescue Feng Ling!","At the same time, Zhao Feng also felt immense relief.","Under normal circumstances, he would have to bear responsibility for his negligence for allowing Chu Feng to sneak into the formation realm, rescue Feng Ling, and injure Baili Zilin, but it was a different story if so many people were being played like a fiddle.","Even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, his godfather Baili Xukong, the leader of the conservative faction Dongfang Hansong, and the experts of the neutral faction were unable to do anything about Chu Feng.","If so, it would be unreasonable to blame him.","And it just so happened that Chu Feng had suppressed everyone’s cultivation to rank one Heavenly God level using the sacred item. This was the perfect chance for him to accrue merit. He would be making a huge contribution to the Netherworld Sect if he could capture Chu Feng.","By then, he wouldn’t just be Baili Xukong’s godson but also the Netherworld Sect’s hero."]},{"number":6545,"title":"Chapter 6545: Chapter 6543: The Fourth Divine Skill","paragraphs":["Chapter 6543: The Fourth Divine Skill","“This must be heaven’s will. Chu Feng, I shall offer your life to reinforce my standing in the Netherworld Sect!” Zhao Feng’s blood rushed as he thought about that.","Not only did he move faster, but he felt like his fighting prowess had increased a little. But now that he had rejoined the main group, he had to follow commands no matter how much he wanted to get that merit for himself.","To make things worse, he couldn’t even see Chu Feng’s silhouette. They were growing increasingly further away from Chu Feng.","Chu Feng was currently carrying Feng Ling toward the Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","“Who... are... you?” Feng Ling feebly asked. The person carrying her looked like Baili Zilin, but she knew that he couldn’t have been him.","Chu Feng knew that Jie Tianran was tracking him through the observation formation, so he reverted to his original appearance and asked with a smile, “Why don’t you take a look?”","“Chu Feng? What are you doing here?” Feng Ling’s lifeless eyes regained their gleam.","“It’s a coincidence. We must have been fated.” Chu Feng told Feng Ling everything that had transpired.","Through their conversation, he learned that the person he met earlier was Zhao Feng, and he also learned about Zhao Feng and Baili Xukong’s relationship.","“You’re incredible, Chu Feng. The Netherworld Sect has so many old monsters, and they are working with that damned grandfather of yours, but you found a way to suppress all of them. You are truly...”","Feng Ling was excited to hear Chu Feng’s story, but halfway through her words, she suddenly fell asleep without any warning.","Chu Feng sighed.","“Chu Feng, this lass is in terrible condition,” Eggy said.","Feng Ling’s earlier excitement was just a burst of energy; that was why she abruptly fell asleep after depleting her remaining strength. At this rate, she would be in grave danger.","“That Zhao Feng employed a vicious method. He siphoned away not just Feng Ling’s bloodline but her soul and origin energies as well,” Chu Feng replied.","“Does that mean that the only way to save Feng Ling is to take Zhao Feng’s life?” Eggy asked.","“That’s right.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Chu Feng, what’s the current situation with your suppression formation? Are you able to exclude me from the suppression formation?” Eggy asked.","“I should have been able to, but Jie Tianran’s interference has hindered me from making finer adjustments to the formation. As it is, I can’t exclude you from the formation.”","“It’s fine. I can just raise my cultivation to rank one Heavenly God.”","“Eggy, I don’t want you to make a move unless absolutely required. I might be unable to cure Feng Ling, but I can at least stabilize her condition. You shouldn’t forget our agenda here. Elder Great Monster Slayer Emperor might have some surprise for us,” Chu Feng replied.","He knew that Eggy possessed the means to kill Zhao Feng, but wielding power beyond one’s ability was bound to inflict immense damage to one’s body. She might even have to pay with her life.","He was the one who had decided to save Feng Ling; he didn’t want Eggy to bear the risks for his actions.","“It’ll be best if the Great Monster Slayer Emperor has left a sliver of his soul behind. He’d be able to cleave through all those small fry with a single slash,” Eggy said.","“That’d be for the best,” Chu Feng agreed with a chuckle.","“Chu Feng, your grasp of Divine Flitting has reached a higher level,” the Divine Deer said.","Chu Feng was able to shake off the rank one Heavenly Gods without utilizing the full prowess of Divine Flitting.","“Elder, isn’t it normal for me to make progress in Divine Flitting after using it so many times? How was my utilization of Divine Evasion earlier?”","“Do you want to hear the truth?”","“Of course. Please generously share your guidance with me if I’m lacking in any way.”","“I knew you won’t have trouble using Divine Evasion given your talent, but you still surprised me when you used it. It shouldn’t have been possible for a True God to maintain Divine Evasion for so long, but you pulled it off. And if I’m not mistaken, this is your first time using Divine Evasion, right?” the Divine Deer asked.","“Yes, it’s my first time using it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Were you already confident about maintaining it for a longer time before using it?”","“I can evade attacks from rank three Heavenly God if I channel Divine Evasion’s power to its maximum, but I’d only be able to maintain it for an instant. So, I lowered its prowess to lengthen the duration.”","“I never taught you that method. Did you figure it out yourself?’","“Yes, I did.”","The Divine Deer was quiet for a few seconds before continuing, “Do you know why I have never taught you such a method of utilizing Divine Evasion?”","“Why?”","“I didn’t know Divine Evasion could be used in such a way. Or rather, Divine Evasion was not intended to be used like that. A slightest lapse in adjustment, and you might risk Divine Evasion not taking effect.”","“I’ll try to avoid using Divine Evasion in that manner.”","“What nonsense are you spouting? You have already pulled it off, and I reckon you are the only one who could have pulled it off.”","“Are you praising me now, elder?”","“Yes, I am praising you. Haa! Sometimes, I am really tempted to crack open your head to see what’s inside. It’s a good thing I didn’t choose the wrong person.”","“It’s my honor to be chosen by you, elder. I’ll do my best not to disappoint you. Elder, now that I have grasped Divine Concealment, Divine Flitting, and Divine Evasion, when are you going to impart the fourth skill to me?”","“What fourth skill?” The Divine Deer sounded confused.","“Elder, you...” Chu Feng was rendered speechless.","The Divine Deer had told him that if he mastered Divine Concealment, Divine Flitting, and Divine Evasion, he would be able to learn a fourth skill. He had asked what the fourth skill was, but the Divine Deer refused to tell him.","“Chu Feng, there is a fourth skill, and it is also my ultimate move. Intelligence is of utmost importance to grasp it, but there is something more important than that. Do you know what it is?”","“Cultivation,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s right,” the Divine Deer affirmed his answer.","“How strong do I have to be to learn the fourth skill?”","“I’ll tell you when the time comes.”","While Chu Feng was chatting with the Divine Deer, Jie Tianran and the others were still in the formation realm, watching the observation formation.","Baili Xukong’s complexion turned severe.","Shortly after Chu Feng left the spatial realm with Feng Ling, his son, Baili Zilin, walked out with a gaping hole in his chest.","Jie Tianran quickly dispatched world spiritists to treat Baili Zilin, but Baili Xukong remained infuriated. He felt humiliated through and through today.","“Mansion Master, are you certain that Chu Feng won’t be able to escape from the Undying Starfield?” Baili Xukong asked.","They could at least remedy the situation if they captured Chu Feng, but they would have to swallow their grievances if Chu Feng escaped. This would be the greatest humiliation the Netherworld Sect had suffered to date."]},{"number":6546,"title":"Chapter 6546: Chapter 6544: Framing Chu Feng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6544: Framing Chu Feng","“On that note, there is one thing I need to inform all of you. You have to make a decision now,” Jie Tianran said.","“What is it?”","The Netherworld Sectmembers turned to look at Jie Tianran.","“While I was unraveling the suppression formation Chu Feng has embedded inside the sacred item, I noticed that Chu Feng has buried an Immemorial Era’s talisman paper in the formation. That talisman paper harnesses immense destructive energy. It won’t be easy to deal with it.”","The Netherworld Sectmembers visibly tensed up upon hearing that.","“I can destroy Chu Feng’s suppression formation right now, but there is a chance that the talisman paper will unleash its destructive energy in retaliation and damage your sacred item. I’m not sure if your sacred item can withstand the damage. It’ll take longer if I have to take control of the Immemorial Era’s talisman paper. By then, Chu Feng might have already gotten away. So, I ask you to quickly discuss the matter and come to a decision,” Jie Tianran said.","His meaning was clear.","He could unravel the suppression formation right away, but that came with the risk of damaging the sacred item. If he had to protect the sacred item, he would require more time to remove the suppression formation.","He was basically tossing the blame to the Netherworld Sect.","“There’s no need to discuss this matter. Protecting the sacred item takes priority,” Cang Li replied right away.","The other experts of the neutral faction, the new faction’s Baili Xukong, and the conservative faction’s Dongfang Hansong expressed their stances at the same time, “Protect the sacred item.”","To the Netherworld Sectmembers, the sacred item was more important than their lives. Everything was secondary before the sacred item.","As they gave their answer, the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body said, “Jie Tianran, you must be intimidated.”","Of course, only Jie Tianran could hear the old entity’s voice.","“What do you mean by that?” Jie Tianran asked.","“There’s no Immemorial Era’s talisman paper in Chu Feng’s suppression formation. You’re merely coming up with an excuse to fool the Netherworld Sect because you’re worried that you can’t lift the suppression formation in time and stop your grandson from leaving,” the old entity said.","“Whether we stop Chu Feng or not depends on you. Are you confident?” Jie Tianran asked.","The old entity replied, “Does that mean you’re not confident in me?”","Jie Tianran laughed. “Of course not. I am confident in your means, elder. I’m just reluctant to make a guarantee to the Netherworld Sect, else they’ll throw the blame on me if anything goes awry. I’m merely taking countermeasures just in case... though I have a more important reason for doing so.”","“Why don’t you tell me about it?”","“Based on what I have observed, the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item harnesses immense energy. If I help them awaken it, the Netherworld Sectmembers will surely enjoy a spike in their fighting prowess, if not in their cultivation. Until I gain control of the sacred item, I will not let it awaken. In other words, this awakening is doomed to fail.","“Gaining control of the sacred item is no easy feat, too. God’s Era has begun stirring, so I can’t stay here for too long. The solution is for me to fuse more Immemorial Era’s talisman papers in the control formation and let them devour the sacred item on their own accord.","“However, that will be time-consuming, and I won’t be able to stay here to keep an eye on it. Something might go awry in the process. By framing it on Chu Feng in advance, if anything happens to the sacred item now or later on, it will have nothing to do with me,” Jie Tianran said.","“Ingenious! Jie Tianran, you’re very thorough in your plans. Your grandson will be taking the blame on your behalf no matter what happens. We won’t be making a loss even if he escapes from here.” The old entity was very satisfied with Jie Tianran’s explanation.","“Did that little bastard siphon away Ranqing’s luck? How did he stumble upon so many fortuitous encounters and obtain so many treasures and formidable means? I don’t fear him even if he reaches Heavenly God, but the other world spiritists of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion won’t be a match for him.","“I need to eliminate him as soon as possible and reclaim our bloodline. If I can reclaim Ruler’s Bloodline before entering God’s Era, I’ll be able to get more from it,” Jie Tianran said.","“You’re right. I’ll need more time for my formation. It’s a good thing that your grandson is roaming around the Undying Starfield when he could have just escaped. Once I complete my formation, your grandson need not dream about escaping from here,” the old entity said.","When the Netherworld Sectmembers learned that Jie Tianran couldn’t unravel the suppression formation right away, they understood that they could only rely on their rank one Heavenly Gods to apprehend Chu Feng.","But their rank one Heavenly Gods couldn’t even catch up with Chu Feng, let alone capture him.","“Isn’t Chu Feng a True God? How is he able to maintain such a fast speed of travel?” Cang Li was confused.","“I think there’s another matter we need to worry about,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“What is it?”","“Chu Feng is here to save a friend. He has already rescued her, and none of the rank one Heavenly Gods and rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists can faze him. So, why doesn’t he just leave?”","“Perhaps he’s unable to breach the Mansion Master’s sealing formation?” someone suggested.","Dongfang Hansong shook his head. “Chu Feng has been maintaining a confident front. I don’t think it’s just bravado. Furthermore, I heard that he has a powerful escape means that allows him to instantaneously flee to a faraway place. If the rumors are true, he could have made a getaway by now.”","“Are you suggesting that he’s up to something?” Cang Li asked.","“That’s right.” Dongfang Hansong nodded.","The atmosphere grew heavy. The powerhouses gathered here could easily raise storms in the world of cultivation, but all of them felt uneasy. It was not that they were timid, but that none of them dared to continue underestimating Chu Feng after having witnessed his means."]},{"number":6547,"title":"Chapter 6547: Chapter 6545: The Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s Legacy","paragraphs":["Chapter 6545: The Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s Legacy","“Dongfang Hansong, aren’t you overthinking it? Chu Feng wouldn’t have to go through the trouble of using our sacred item to power his suppression formation if he were that capable.” Baili Xukong didn’t think that Chu Feng could come and go as he pleased.","Besides, there was nothing of note in the Undying Starfield, aside from their sacred item.","“I hope I’m overthinking it.” Dongfang Hansong couldn’t be bothered to bicker with Baili Xukong.","“Wait a minute. What’s going on? Why did Chu Feng suddenly speed up so much?” Cang Li remarked nervously.","The others tensed up as well.","Chu Feng’s silhouette on the observation formation grew faint as his movement speed reached an unimaginable level. Even rank five Heavenly Gods like them couldn’t match his speed.","“He must have used a treasure. That treasure probably takes time to activate, so he had to put some distance between him and his pursuers before using it,” Jie Tianran explained.","The Netherworld Sect did have such treasures as well, though none of them was capable of moving at such a speed.","“Chu Feng has a lot of treasures.”","The eyes of the Netherworld Sect’s elders gleamed with greed.","Chu Feng was a troublesome foe, but if they could kill or capture him, they would be able to claim all his treasures.","Jie Tianran was right. Chu Feng’s movement speed had spiked because he had activated Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat, a gift he had received from Sikong Changsheng. That bamboo boat allowed him to move faster than normal teleportation formations, greatly increasing his traveling speed.","Some time later, he finally arrived at the Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","The realm had rivers and lakes, as well as several mountains, but it was mostly filled with fields of flowers that stretched to the horizon.","“I have been to many places now, but the Ancestral Martial Galaxy still has the most beautiful scenery.” Eggy admired the Flowersea Ordinary Realm’s beauty through Chu Feng’s eyes.","Chu Feng felt a stir in his heart as well.","He should have long obtained the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy, but he had to postpone it due to the Netherworld Sect removing the entire Undying Starfield. After a long time, he had finally returned here.","Thinking about it, it had only been a few years since his meeting with the Great Monster Slayer Emperor, but it felt like a long time had passed. It only felt that way because many things had happened in between.","Time passed in a flash when living a peaceful, monotonous life, giving the impression that one had grown old in the blink of an eye.","It was the opposite for Chu Feng. He had accomplished so many memorable feats that it felt like a long time had passed, even though it had only been a few years.","Clang!","Chu Feng pulled out a rusty sword—the Monster Slayer Sword. This was the weapon that had grown famous with the Great Monster Slayer Emperor. It might not harness any power now, but it was the key to opening the latter’s tomb.","Holding the Monster Slayer Sword in hand, Chu Feng could feel himself drawing close to the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy.","“Are we almost there? Why don’t I see it? Is it buried under the sea of flowers?” Eggy asked.","“It probably is,” Chu Feng replied.","A powerful surge of teleportation energy emerged from the ground and enveloped Chu Feng. He was transported to a majestic underground palace.","The underground palace was forged out of grayish-white stone, and it felt simple but grand.","A massive sculpture holding a sword plunged into the ground stood at the center of the palace. This was the Great Monster Slayer Emperor and his Monster Slayer Sword.","While Chu Feng was observing the sculpture, it suddenly cracked. Stones fell off its surface, and a massive soul entity emerged from within.","This soul entity was also the Great Monster Slayer Emperor holding the Monster Slayer Sword with both hands. Not only did both the man and the sword look lifelike, but they also gave off powerful auras.","“Chu Feng pays respect to elder.” Chu Feng quickly bowed to the Great Monster Slayer Emperor.","“Fated one, welcome to my legacy ground,” the Great Monster Slayer Emperor said.","Chu Feng couldn’t help but feel a tinge of disappointment. He had noticed that the soul entity harnessed power, so he thought that it was a sliver of the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul.","But from the other party’s words, he could tell that the soul entity before him was not sentient.","It would appear that the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s consciousness had completely eroded when he first met Chu Feng. He was still hoping to reminisce about the past together with the other party, but it looked like his wish would never come to be.","“Fated one, your presence here signifies that you’re qualified to inherit my legacy. You may take everything I have left behind.”","The Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul sliver pulled out the Monster Slayer Sword and plunged it back into the ground. A mechanism at the center of the underground palace whirred into action, and a transparent treasure box surfaced.","Inside the treasure box were countless high-quality Exalted Armaments and three God Armament swords containing the ‘True’ character. Other than that, it also contained many martial skill and God Taboo Martial Skill manuals.","The strongest manual was a rank four God Taboo.","Above all, the treasure box was filled with gleaming beads. They were cultivation resources.","Chu Feng’s heart ached in pain.","These cultivation resources were indeed of top quality, but the formation used to store them was imperfect, resulting in the cultivation resources losing a lot of energy over time.","Boom!","The underground palace suddenly shook. Chu Feng could feel it morphing into a gigantic formation and channeling its energy toward the Monster Slayer Sword in the center of the underground palace.","“Fated one, I am bound to be long gone by the time you reach this place. I’m unable to protect you, so I can only bestow you with a self-preservation means.”","The Great Monster Slayer Emperor released his Monster Slayer Sword and pointed his finger at Chu Feng. His Monster Slayer Sword transformed into sword aura and fused into Chu Feng’s Monster Slayer Sword.","“I have taken the real Monster Slayer Sword away with me. This is a replica forged from fusing a sliver of the true Monster Slayer Sword with an immemorial treasure. It wields power comparable to a rank one Heavenly God. You’ll be able to wield this sword once you reach pinnacle True God level. When you channel it, you can tap into its powers.","“You won’t be able to tap into your bloodline skills, and your fighting prowess will be limited, but you can use all your martial skills and secret skills. It should be enough to keep you safe as long as you don’t trifle with Heavenly Gods,” the Great Monster Slayer Emperor said."]},{"number":6548,"title":"Chapter 6548: Chapter 6546: Breakthrough","paragraphs":["Chapter 6546: Breakthrough","In the formation realm above Undying Starfield, the experts of the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion continued to follow Chu Feng’s movements via the observation formation.","“Why has Chu Feng stopped moving?”","They noticed that Chu Feng had stopped moving.","“What’s that place?” Jie Tianran asked.","Baili Xukong, Dongfang Hansong, and the other higher-ups from the Netherworld Sect quickly took out a map demarcating all of Undying Starfield’s realms. There were even supplementary texts elaborating on the circumstances in each realm.","“Flowersea Ordinary Realm,” Baili Xukong said.","“Is there something related to the sacred item there?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Our sect has scoured the Undying Starfield. The Flowersea Ordinary Realm is a normal realm. It is severely lacking in resources, and there are very few people residing there. There is nothing linked to the sacred item there,” Baili Xukong replied while studying the map.","The map contained the results of the Netherworld Sect’s investigation.","“Then we need not pay it any mind. Order your men to encircle Chu Feng,” Jie Tianran said before he returned to his work.","But this time, he constructed a brand new formation that exuded the same aura as the observation formation.","Some time later, the Netherworld Sect’s Heavenly Gods and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists finally arrived at the Flowersea Ordinary Realm, where Chu Feng was.","However, they were flabbergasted. They couldn’t see or sense any trace of Chu Feng, even after whipping out their observation means. They relayed this to Jie Tianran and the others via their communication tools.","“Jie Tianran, could we have been duped by Chu Feng? Could he have already left the Undying Starfield?” Cang Li asked.","“My formation is infallible. It has already locked onto Chu Feng. There’s no way he can escape. Let me see what he’s up to.”","Jie Tianran formed a hand seal. A new projection appeared above Chu Feng’s location in the observation formation, revealing Chu Feng’s surroundings.","This was Jie Tianran’s means. Upon realizing that Chu Feng had stopped moving, he reinforced the observation formation to further pinpoint his location.","But that additional projection only made the expressions of the Netherworld Sect’s experts turn more grim. They had thought that the rank one Heavenly Gods and rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists were fooled by Chu Feng because they were too weak, but Chu Feng was nowhere to be found, even on the additional projection.","This was perplexing. Could the location pinpointed by the observation formation be off?","All of a sudden, thunder rumbled in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","“That is...?”","The experts from the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were stunned.","Dark lightning clouds had swiftly gathered around the entire Undying Starfield. They were so close to the dark clouds that they could feel the immense power contained within them. These weren’t ordinary lightning clouds; they were nine-colored lightning clouds.","“Nine-colored lightning. It’s Chu Feng.”","“He’s about to make a breakthrough.”","“Did he stop moving because he’s cultivating?”","“Yes, that must be the case.”","“Such nine-colored lightning only appears during his breakthroughs.”","The experts from the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion discussed among themselves, but all of them already knew the answer.","“Jie Tianran, your grandson is an interesting one. Not only did he not flee, but he even started cultivating and made a breakthrough. But how did he make a breakthrough all of a sudden? Does he cultivate by living life on the edge? Does that increase his speed of cultivation?” the old entity teased.","Jie Tianran stared at the nine-colored lightning with narrowed eyes. Seeing the phenomenon up close, he had to admit that it was formidable.","Many cultivators possessed the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline; their breakthroughs would also attract nine-colored lightning. Only when they withstood the lightning tribulation could they be considered to have made a true breakthrough.","But he had never seen anyone who attracted such terrifying nine-colored lightning.","GRAR!","A furious roar echoed.","Nine colossal lightning beasts appeared amidst the clouds. An overwhelming aura jolted everyone’s souls, rendering them silent. Despite their cultivation, they still felt incomparably weak and extremely fearful of the nine-colored lightning.","Of all the nine-colored lightning tribulations they had seen, this was the only one that made them feel like that.","“That’s quite the grand phenomenon. Can your grandson withstand it? Come to think about it, he causes a huge commotion each time he makes a breakthrough,” the old entity said.","They were right. Chu Feng didn’t leave right after obtaining the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s legacy. Rather, he started cultivating on the spot.","Soon, the nine-colored lightning bolted down upon Chu Feng.","This alarmed the Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists camping for Chu Feng, and they hurriedly scattered in all directions. Despite knowing that the nine-colored lightning only affected the cultivator making the breakthrough, they were still intimidated.","Even Baili Xukong and the others were shaken up, let alone these rank one Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists!","Indeed, the nine-colored lightning bolted into the underground without causing any damage to the Flowersea Ordinary Realm. It was as if the ground had swallowed the nine-colored lightning.","“Chu Feng must be cultivating below!”","The rank one Heavenly Gods deduced. They quickly got to action.","They easily destroyed the sea of flowers, but to their shock, the ground turned out to be nigh indestructible. Despite their best efforts, they were unable to breach it.","“What a strong formation!” the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists exclaimed.","Indeed, it was a strong formation that had stopped the rank one Heavenly Gods’ attacks.","“This formation... It wasn’t constructed by Chu Feng. It has been hidden here for many years. Baili Xukong, didn’t you say that the Flowersea Ordinary Realm is a normal place? Why is there such a formation there?” Jie Tianran questioned Baili Xukong."]},{"number":6549,"title":"Chapter 6549: Chapter 6547: My Current Cultivation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6547: My Current Cultivation","“Those useless things.”","Anger flickered across Baili Xukong’s eyes as he released a wisp of martial power flame from his palm, torching the map into ashes. Clearly, the Netherworld Sectmembers had failed in their investigation of the Undying Starfield.","Boom!","More nine-colored lightning appeared around the Undying Starfield.","“What’s going on? Is he making another breakthrough?”","“Consecutive breakthroughs?”","“Just how big a fortuitous encounter did that fellow find?”","“How is he able to make breakthroughs as easily as drinking water?”","The previous lightning clouds hadn’t even dissipated when stronger nine-colored lightning manifested. The crowd felt conflicted and indignant.","The person they wanted to capture was cultivating right under their watch, but they were unable to do anything about him. This made them feel incredibly stifled.","Jie Tianran’s eyes hardened with determination. He stopped channeling his control formation and instead pulled out two black talisman papers, a blank paper, and a brush from his Cosmos Sack. These items were all extraordinary treasures.","He moved the brush, and an immense amount of spirit power flowed out.","The Netherworld Sect members sensed the flow of energy at Jie Tianran’s side and turned their eyes there. Both the paper and the brush were world spiritist treasures they had never seen before, but they were more drawn to the two black talisman papers.","Jie Tianran drew a nine-colored lightning bolt on the paper before plastering a black talisman paper on it. He formed a hand seal, and the nine-colored lightning bolt floated out from the paper and fused into the black talisman paper.","Nine-colored lightning crackled around the black talisman paper.","“Mansion Master, what are you doing?” Baili Xukong asked in confusion.","Their priority should have been to channel the control formation and remove Chu Feng’s suppression formation from the sacred item. Yet, Jie Tianran was focused on constructing a new formation right now. This left Baili Xukong and the others confused.","Jie Tianran held the other black talisman paper in between his fingers and formed a hand seal. Then, he flung his sleeves, and the black talisman paper transformed into a massive formation core that floated toward Baili Xukong and the others.","Then, he tossed the black talisman paper infused with nine-colored lightning out. It swiftly fused into the nine-colored lightning induced by Chu Feng’s breakthrough.","“Mansion Master, are you planning to use the lightning tribulation against Chu Feng?” Baili Xukong could roughly guess Jie Tianran’s intention now.","“Yes, this formation allows me to greatly amplify the prowess of the lightning tribulation, but it can only be channeled by cultivators. So, I’ll require your help,” Jie Tianran finally revealed his intention.","“Is it reliable?” Cang Li asked.","The Netherworld Sectmembers present had noticed the peculiar nature of the black talisman paper.","“I won’t do anything that harms you. Chu Feng is too arrogant, using your Netherworld Sect’s sacred item to suppress you. But he let his conceit get to his head and made a breakthrough here. It just so happens that I wield the means to tamper with his lightning tribulation. Don’t you want to give him a taste of his medicine?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Are you sure it’ll work?” an elder from the neutral faction asked.","“As long as you assist me, I’ll be able to tamper with his lightning tribulation. Even if I fail to outright kill him, I can at least render his breakthrough a failure and ruin his Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. That will spell the end of his cultivation journey,” Jie Tianran said.","“All right. Chu Feng had the gall to mess with our Netherworld Sect and make consecutive breakthroughs in our presence. He ought to pay the price for his arrogance,” the elder from the neutral faction said as he stepped into the formation core.","Cang Li, Baili Xukong, and the others did the same as well.","Any doubts they harbored about the formation vanished the moment they stepped into the formation core. They could sense the lightning tribulation’s power, Jie Tianran’s power, and the formation’s power.","Indeed, the power imbued in the formation far exceeded what someone of Chu Feng’s cultivation could bear. Even rank five Heavenly Gods like them wouldn’t have been able to withstand it if this formation power was compounded with the lightning tribulation’s power.","In their opinion, Jie Tianran was playing it too safe. There was no way Chu Feng could survive this ordeal.","So, the Netherworld Sectmembers put down their wariness and channeled the formation core.","Meanwhile, in the underground palace, Chu Feng had been waiting with closed eyes for the lightning tribulation to descend, but he suddenly felt a bout of unease and raised his head to look at the sky.","“What’s wrong, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","Chu Feng usually remained focused while waiting for the lightning tribulation to descend. His attention wouldn’t be wandering like that.","“Something is amiss about the lightning tribulation,” Chu Feng said.","“How so?” Eggy asked.","“I’m not sure, either.”","Boom!","The nine-colored lightning descended.","“Forget it.”","Chu Feng formed a hand seal, closed his eyes, and prepared himself to withstand the descending lightning tribulation. What he didn’t know was that this lightning tribulation carried the consciousness of top Netherworld Sect’s experts as well.","“Die, Chu Feng!” Baili Xukong’s consciousness descended with the lightning tribulation, and he saw Chu Feng and where he was.","But when the lightning tribulation struck Chu Feng, his consciousness was pulled into a vast, pitch-black space.","“What is this place? Is it Chu Feng’s dantian world? No, this doesn’t look like a dantian world.” Baili Xukong frowned.","GRARRR!","A deafening roar that shook space echoed from the distance.","Before Baili Xukong could even see the enemy, his martial power had already begun gushing out from his body. A suction force was siphoning away his martial power!","“What is this?!”","Sensing something amiss, Baili Xukong hurriedly severed his connection with the formation. While his consciousness returned to his body, the abrupt severance with the formation resulted in a severe backlash, and he spurted blood.","But that was nothing compared to the state he was in. His body felt powerless as if he had sustained severe injuries, and his blood flow was in disarray. Worst of all, he had lost a lot of the martial power he had been accumulating.","“Jie Tianran, you dare to fool me?” Cang Li roared.","Baili Xukong realized that the others who had entered the formation core had pale faces, and blood was seeping from the corners of their lips. They were in such a weakened state that they couldn’t even maintain an upright sitting posture.","Their faces betrayed their panic, and it looked as if they had just experienced something terrifying. Clearly, they must have encountered the same entity.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng withstood the nine-colored lightning and opened his eyes, but his pupils soon widened in shock.","“How bizarre,” Chu Feng remarked.","“What’s wrong? Did you sustain injuries? Or was it a failure?” Eggy was worried.","“The breakthrough was a success.”","“You bastard, Chu Feng. Why are you acting as if something has gone wrong when your breakthrough was a success? Are you playing with me?” Eggy rolled her eyes.","“The resources from the Great Monster Slayer Emperor should have only been enough for me to reach rank eight True God level,” Chu Feng said.","“You did go through two lightning tribulations, so you should be at rank eight True God level? Are you able to make another breakthrough?”","“I can’t make another breakthrough... but for some reason, I have already reached rank nine True God level,” Chu Feng replied.","“What?” Eggy’s mouth opened agape."]},{"number":6550,"title":"Chapter 6550: Chapter 6548: Rank Nine True God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6548: Rank Nine True God","Chu Feng revealed his aura.","“You’re really at rank nine True God level. How baffling. How did that happen?” Eggy had no choice but to accept this bewildering situation after sensing Chu Feng’s aura, though she fell into contemplation as she tried to figure out the reason behind that.","“It’s the lightning tribulation,” Chu Feng and Eggy exclaimed at the same time.","Something must have been different about the lightning tribulation.","Chu Feng channeled the Three Realms Divine Eyes to examine the nine-colored lightning, which had yet to fully disperse. Indeed, he found traces of a formation. It was very discreet, such that he wouldn’t have noticed it through his Heaven’s Eyes.","He could tell that the formation’s energy originated from a treasure, and it bore a striking resemblance to the talisman papers Jie Tianran used. From that, he concluded that it had to be Jie Tianran’s doing.","“No wonder I sensed something amiss. Jie Tianran tampered with my lightning tribulation,” Chu Feng said.","“That loser grandfather of yours tried to harm you through your lightning tribulation?” Eggy asked.","“Yes, he has to be the one behind it. He must have been trying to use my lightning tribulation against me, but his efforts ended up benefiting me instead,” Chu Feng reasoned.","“That loser grandfather of yours is truly pathetic.” Eggy’s eyes reddened in anger.","It turned out to be a blessing in disguise for Chu Feng, but it didn’t change the fact that Jie Tianran had tried to harm him. In fact, Chu Feng’s breakthrough to rank nine True God level only highlighted how powerful Jie Tianran’s means were.","Meanwhile, over in the spatial formation, Baili Xukong and the others stepped out of the formation core and glared at Jie Tianran.","“Fortunately, I reacted fast, or else Chu Feng would have sucked us dry. Jie Tianran, you really can’t be trusted!” Cang Li spat.","He had preserved his cultivation rank, but that didn’t mean there were no losses. On the contrary, the losses were massive.","Cang Li had lost half of the martial power accrued after advancing to rank five Heavenly God level, and he had only lost this much because he had reacted fast. Had he been any slower, his cultivation might have regressed to rank four Heavenly God.","“Did you really lose your cultivation?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Isn’t that obvious? Why don’t you try stepping in yourself the next time Chu Feng makes a breakthrough? I truly wonder if Chu Feng was speaking the truth earlier, and that the two of you have joined hands.” Cang Li glared at Jie Tianran.","The others weren’t as fierce as Cang Li, but their faces also showed their displeasure. No one would be pleased after abruptly losing the cultivation they had amassed with great difficulty.","“Are you insinuating that I have joined hands with the likes of him? Do I have to go through such trouble just to deal with the Netherworld Sect? Don’t you remember who saved you earlier when Chu Feng used the suppression formation against you? You should know what kind of treasure I used for that. I have already gone so far for you, but you continue to doubt me?","“If so, I’ll just leave,” Jie Tianran said as he stood up.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists followed suit.","“Please calm down, Mansion Master,” Baili Xukong quickly spoke up to placate Jie Tianran.","“Mansion Master, please hear me out. We have indeed lost our cultivation when attempting to attack Chu Feng through the lightning tribulation earlier. You might be a world spiritist, but I’m sure you understand that cultivation is not easy. The others can’t help but be peeved after losing their cultivation.","“Please be assured that we don’t doubt which side you’re on, Mansion Master. We wouldn’t have requested your help or entered the formation core earlier otherwise,” Baili Xukong said.","Meanwhile, the other experts of the Netherworld Sect also calmed down.","Jie Tianran’s words made sense. If he wanted to destroy the Netherworld Sect, he could have turned a blind eye to their plights earlier when Chu Feng activated the suppression formation. There was no need for him to go through so much trouble.","Rather, they were the ones being irrational after losing some cultivation.","“Cang Li, this isn’t the Mansion Master’s fault. We can only blame Chu Feng for being too cunning,” an elder from the neutral faction said.","The others from the Netherworld Sect also spoke up to defuse the tension.","“Forget it. I was the one who stepped into the formation core on my own accord. Mansion Master, I lost my cultivation and nearly regressed to rank four Heavenly God earlier, which was why I got too agitated. Please do not mind my earlier words,” Cang Li said.","Cang Li knew that they couldn’t afford to lose Jie Tianran at this juncture, or else they wouldn’t be able to protect their sacred item from Chu Feng. Thus, he took the cue and de-escalated the situation.","“I’m not a narrow-minded person. It’s good as long as you understand that we’re on the same side. However, this situation is bewildering. Nothing should have gone wrong with the treasure I used earlier. Can you tell me in detail what you encountered earlier?” Jie Tianran asked.","“The moment the lightning struck Chu Feng’s body, I was transported into a world inside Chu Feng’s body, but it didn't feel like his dantian world. Just then, I heard a roar coming from deep within that world. It felt like a powerful entity was guarding its territory. Right after, I felt a suction force siphoning away my cultivation,” Baili Xukong shared.","“It’s the same for me, too,” the others said.","Their experiences were similar to what Baili Xukong went through.","“Chu Feng seems to be in a remnant. I saw a massive soul entity, but I couldn’t make out his appearance because of how quickly the lightning tribulation descended. Chu Feng must have gone to the Flowersea Ordinary Realm for that remnant,” Baili Xukong said.","“That remnant isn’t important now. Chu Feng must have claimed the fortuitous encounter there to have made consecutive breakthroughs. What’s more important is the world in his body... and the voice you heard. Could it be his bloodline power?” Jie Tianran pondered.","Such a thing shouldn’t have been possible at all.","Just then, the old entity told Jie Tianran, “It has to be his bloodline power. Strong bloodline powers protect their hosts when they are in danger, especially when you resort to underhanded methods like tampering with the lightning tribulations.","“That said, not all bloodline powers are capable of protecting their hosts from what you did earlier. Most bloodline powers wouldn’t even sense the anomaly. Your grandson’s Heavenly Lightning Bloodline must be extremely powerful, perhaps even reaching the legendary Saint King-tier. That would be incredibly valuable.”","The old entity sounded excited.","“Did you already know that would happen?” Jie Tianran asked.","“I wouldn’t have allowed you to do that if I had known in advance. I’m not very fond of that grandson of yours, too,” the old entity replied.","After chatting with the old entity, Jie Tianran finally explained the situation to the others, “The entity that devoured your cultivation earlier is Chu Feng’s Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. I have underestimated his bloodline power. I didn’t expect it to protect him.”","“If that’s true, could Chu Feng’s bloodline power have converted our cultivation into energy to fuel his breakthrough? If so, there is a chance he might make a breakthrough to Heavenly God.” Cang Li and the others became nervous after hearing Jie Tianran’s words.","“You’re thinking too much. His bloodline power might have devoured your cultivation, but that doesn’t mean it’s able to convert it into energy for his use. I reckon that was merely a warning from Chu Feng’s bloodline to you.","“You’re all Heavenly Gods. Your cultivation is much too domineering for Chu Feng to use as a cultivation resource,” Jie Tianran said.","“You’re right.”","The experts of the Netherworld Sect nodded, agreeing with Jie Tianran.","Boom!","Just then, something happened in the underground palace where Chu Feng dwelled.","The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists and Heavenly God stationed in the Undying Starfield noticed the anomaly through the observation formation. They didn’t know what had happened, but they sensed that Chu Feng was about to appear.","So, they quickly flitted in to encircle the Flowersea Ordinary Realm once more while employing their means to seal off the area.","What was worth mentioning was that Zhao Feng, who had wanted to use this opportunity to make a name for himself, quietly retreated to the back of the crowd. He sensed that something had gone awry.","Boom!","A blade of light shot out from the ground and split the previously nigh indestructible ground into two.","A massive soul entity slowly rose from the ground—it was the Great Monster Slayer Emperor. Rising alongside him was Chu Feng and the Monster Slayer Sword.","“That soul entity appears to be the Great Monster Slayer Emperor.”","Baili Xukong and the others widened their eyes in shock. They had researched the figures who had dominated the earlier years of the present era.","“Yes, that’s the Great Monster Slayer Emperor. The sword in Chu Feng’s hand is clearly the Monster Slayer Sword.”","The Netherworld Sectmembers became more certain about it after seeing the sword in Chu Feng’s grasp.","“Damn it. It was the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy?”","Baili Xukong and the others felt pain. The Great Monster Slayer Emperor was still a famed figure even though he was not one of the strongest ones. His legacy was bound to be valuable. To think that they had missed it despite it being right under their watch!","Chu Feng pointed his Monster Slayer Sword at the Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists surrounding him.","“You have quite a few people here. I’m here for the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy, but what are the rest of you doing here? Are you here... to court death?”","Chu Feng’s cultivation was still at True God level, but he looked at the Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists before him in contempt."]},{"number":6551,"title":"Chapter 6551: Chapter 6549: The Thick-skinned Zhao Feng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6549: The Thick-skinned Zhao Feng","“That soul entity is the Great Monster Slayer Emperor, and Chu Feng is wielding the Monster Slayer Sword. Does this mean that Chu Feng has obtained the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy?”","Upon hearing those words, the Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists surrounding Chu Feng instinctively took a step back.","Their cultivation might be beneath Baili Xukong, Jie Tianran, and the others, but most of them had lived for over a thousand years, some even tens of thousands of years. There was no lack of individuals who were knowledgeable about the past.","Some of them recognized the Great Monster Slayer Emperor and the Monster Slayer Sword. In particular, they were intimidated by the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul entity. Any hand left behind by an expert of that caliber could easily vanquish them all.","But there were also those who weren’t afraid of death.","“Who cares what he obtained? He blasphemed the sacred item. That’s an unforgivable sin. Kill him!” a Netherworld Sectmember roared as he charged forth.","A few other Netherworld Sectmembers heeded his call and rushed in as well.","Surges of martial power gushed at Chu Feng from all directions in all forms, be it sword auras, light beams, and martial skills. These were all killing moves.","“You aren’t capable of killing me,” Chu Feng sneered.","He swung his Monster Slayer Sword, unleashing waves of martial power that quaked the sky and rippled space. His counterattack blocked the Heavenly Gods’ attacks.","“Rank one Heavenly God!”","“Did he make a breakthrough to rank one Heavenly God?!”","All Netherworld Sectmembers halted their attacks upon sensing Chu Feng’s fighting prowess. They were struck by shock and confusion.","“That’s not his real cultivation. His sword must have temporarily enhanced his strength!” Baili Xukong’s voice boomed across the Undying Starfield.","“He’s merely relying on a treasure!”","The crowd widened their eyes in realization as they heaved a sigh of relief.","“So what if that’s his real cultivation? We’re all rank one Heavenly Gods, and we have him outnumbered here. We have nothing to fear! Kill him!”","The Netherworld Sectmembers charged at Chu Feng once more.","All this while, the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul entity stood behind Chu Feng with closed eyes, showing no signs of making a move. It looked more like a decoration than a helper.","That emboldened the Netherworld Sectmembers, and more people joined the fray. Even the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists also began constructing slaughter formations to attack Chu Feng.","Anyone else in Chu Feng’s place would have long collapsed under the onslaught of so many Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","But Chu Feng remained fearless because of the special nature of the Monster Slayer Sword. The fighting prowess he received from it wasn’t particularly formidable, but he noticed that the Monster Slayer Sword was stronger if he simply swung it without relying on martial skills.","That was also how he was able to cope with all the attacks and formations targeting him.","However, there was also a downside to wielding the Monster Slayer Sword—he couldn’t use Divine Flitting.","“Elder, why am I unable to use Divine Flitting?” Chu Feng asked the Divine Deer.","He could already tell what skills he could use without activating them. Most of his martial skills and secret skills could be used with the Monster Slayer Sword, and this included special ones like Protection Bane and Dark Plunder.","However, he couldn’t use Divine Flitting and Divine Evasion.","“Divine skills are unlike other skills. They originate from me. You are able to use them because you have my acknowledgment, but I have not acknowledged the Monster Slayer Sword. You are borrowing the Monster Slayer Sword’s cultivation right now, so naturally, you aren’t able to use my divine skills,” the Divine Deer replied.","“I see. That makes things tricky.”","While Chu Feng could freely deactivate the Monster Slayer Sword, there was a brief cooldown before he could activate it again. If not for this limitation, he could have swiftly alternated between activating and deactivating the Monster Slayer Sword to use Divine Flitting in between.","Divine Flitting would have greatly enhanced his fighting prowess, allowing him to deal with his enemies with much greater ease.","This limitation forced him to compromise.","In truth, there was no need for Chu Feng to confront the Netherworld Sectmembers or the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists. He only had one target—Zhao Feng.","The problem was that Zhao Feng was hiding behind everyone else. He was attacking Chu Feng as well, but he was keeping his distance. It wouldn’t be easy for Chu Feng to kill him under such circumstances.","“Zhao Feng, you must be Baili Xukong’s godson?” Chu Feng asked while dealing with incoming attacks.","“What about it?” Zhao Feng replied loftily.","“Baili Xukong sure is an interesting one. His son is trash, and he takes in a coward as his godson,” Chu Feng remarked.","“Coward? I am fighting against you, and yet you call me a coward?” Zhao Feng replied brazenly despite his evasive fighting style.","“Look at how far you are hiding from me,” Chu Feng scoffed.","“Hahaha...” Zhao Feng burst into laughter.","“Chu Feng, you might be qualified to say those words if you’re a rank two Heavenly God, but why would I fear a True God level cultivator who is barely standing against us by borrowing the power of a treasure?” Zhao Feng snorted.","“You should know better. I don’t have anything against the others here, but from the moment you tried to take Feng Ling’s life, there’s already a grudge between the two of us,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng, how dare you speak about grudges before us? You blasphemed our Netherworld Sect’s sacred item and ruined our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation. Your actions are more than deserving of death!” Zhao Feng sneered. He turned to the crowd and asked loudly, “What do the rest of you say?”","Many agreed with Zhao Feng and let out taunts against Chu Feng.","“Indeed, Chu Feng! You are the enemy of our Netherworld Sect. If you give up right now, I can plead with the Netherworld Marshal and leave you with an intact corpse. Otherwise, we’ll make sure that your soul disintegrates into nothing!”","Chu Feng sighed helplessly. He could only remark, “Fools.”","It was obvious that Zhao Feng was using the others as meat shields, but these people failed to notice such a basic fact. But on second thought, these Netherworld Sectmembers and Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members might have realized it, but they were playing along because of the huge contribution they could obtain from killing Chu Feng.","In other words, they were willing to overlook the danger for the merit.","In hindsight, Zhao Feng was smart not to get ahead of himself to vie for contribution.","“Chu Feng, that Zhao Feng is thick-skinned. Your taunts aren’t working on him. Why don’t I make a move and vanquish him instead?” Eggy said with a hint of ire.","While Chu Feng wasn’t bothered about it, Eggy couldn’t stand people like Zhao Feng prancing around Chu Feng.","“Eggy, we can’t kill Zhao Feng yet. We need to keep him alive to properly extract Feng Ling’s bloodline from his body,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6552,"title":"Chapter 6552: Chapter 6550: Transforming the Embryo Into a General","paragraphs":["Chapter 6550: Transforming the Embryo Into a General","“Chu Feng, is the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul sliver not going to help us?” Eggy asked.","“Elder Great Monster Slayer Emperor would have helped us long ago if he intended to do so. There might be a trigger in the formation for him to help us only when I’m severely injured, but there’s no guarantee that’s the case either,” Chu Feng replied.","He also couldn’t say for sure what the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul sliver was capable of.","“Doesn’t that make it tough for you to capture Zhao Feng alive? That’s more reason for me to make a move. I can capture him alive,” Eggy said.","“There’s no need for that. I taunted Zhao Feng earlier not just to provoke him, but also to create the impression that I’m cornered and am trying to hold him hostage for a chance to escape from here.","“The Netherworld Sect has many Heavenly Gods, but their fighting prowess is severely lacking. They must have made their breakthroughs recently, and they did so using special means, which resulted in their foundation being unstable. The same is also true for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","“That said, it’s still tricky to deal with so many of them at once. The Monster Slayer Sword is a powerful weapon, but it won’t be enough for me to deal with all of them. I won’t have much of an advantage against them even if I use my martial skills. That’s also the reason I’ve refrained from using martial skills thus far.","“I want them to underestimate me, so that they won’t be able to react right away when I launch a surprise assault. I want to capture Zhao Feng in a single swoop,” Chu Feng said.","This was one of Chu Feng’s commonly used ploys—feigning weakness to spring a lethal assault. However, the key to this ploy was that he had to appear weak to his enemies without being truly vulnerable.","Otherwise, it would be all for naught if the enemy exploited a weakness he revealed and took him down right away.","“Chu Feng isn’t using any martial skills. That must be a downside of using the Monster Slayer Sword.”","“Look at him! He’s sweating profusely and gasping for air. It looks like he’s about to deplete his stamina. Channeling the Monster Slayer Sword must be taking a toll on him.”","“He probably can’t last much longer at this rate.”","“We just need to encircle him and ensure that he can’t get away. It’s only a matter of time before he falls in defeat!”","“We must kill him here this time!”","The Netherworld Sectmembers secretly shared their analysis via voice transmission. They had fallen for Chu Feng’s trickery.","Chu Feng had also been observing their reactions. The moment the Netherworld Sectmembers loosened up a little, he decisively made his move.","“Divine Might! Heaven Suppression!”","Chu Feng simultaneously activated two rank three God Taboo Martial Skills to greatly weaken the Netherworld Sectmembers’ fighting prowess.","A golden light enveloped Chu Feng as he activated two more rank three God Taboo Martial Skills—the Ye Immortal Clan’s Heaven Protection and Heaven Footwork. The former raised his fighting prowess and defensive ability, whereas the latter boosted his movement speed.","With that, Chu Feng charged at Zhao Feng like a spectre.","These happened so fast that neither the Netherworld Sectmembers nor the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists had time to react. Anyone who stood in Chu Feng’s path was slashed apart by his Monster Slayer Sword.","In the blink of an eye, he was already standing before Zhao Feng.","Zhao Feng hurriedly attempted a retaliation, but his attack barely fazed Chu Feng.","Chu Feng didn’t slash Zhao Feng with his Monster Slayer Sword. Instead, he kicked his foot right into the center of Zhao Feng’s abdomen.","This kick caused Zhao Feng to spurt blood from his nose. His face distorted from sheer pain, and he let out a howl reminiscent of a pig in an abattoir. This strike might appear to be a simple physical blow, but it dealt severe damage to his soul, rendering him incapable of fighting.","This was all Chu Feng could do for the time being until he extracted Feng Ling’s soul from the latter.","“That Chu Feng!” Baili Xukong, Cang Li, and the others turned livid with anger. They shot to their feet despite their weakened states.","As powerful as Rank three God Taboo Martial Skills were, they also placed immense stress on the cultivator using them. Chu Feng’s rank three God Taboos were powerful, but they had to be extremely strenuous as well.","Yet, Chu Feng simultaneously activated four of them without showing the slightest hint of weakness. This was a testament to his incredible endurance.","But what infuriated Cang Li and the others was the realization that they had been fooled by Chu Feng. Clearly, Chu Feng had refrained from using his martial skills to mislead them into thinking that he was weaker than he truly was.","Even the sweat on Chu Feng’s face was a lie, but the act had been so convincing that none of them saw through it. They were all convinced that Chu Feng was a goner.","And that was how Chu Feng turned the tables on them in the blink of an eye.","What was even more maddening was how Chu Feng wisely chose to retreat right away.","The effects of Divine Might had worn off, but the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists were still weakened by Heaven Suppression. That made it hard for them to pursue Chu Feng.","Hesitation flickered across the faces of the Netherworld Sectmembers.","“Use the Netherworld Troop Formation!” Baili Xukong’s voice boomed.","That was an order.","All Netherworld Sectmembers cast away their hesitation and simultaneously formed a hand seal. “I offer my blood to awaken the Netherworld Embryo. I offer my bloodline to nourish the Netherworld Embryo into a weapon. Activate, Netherworld Troop Formation!”","The entire Flowersea Ordinary Realm shook. Both the sky and the earth turned blood-red as if some kind of dye had seeped into the world.","Humongous blood-red silhouettes began rising in the distance. Even though they were a far distance away, Chu Feng could still clearly see them due to their hulking stature. These giants were all emanating the Netherworld Embryos’ auras.","These giants emanated terrifying auras, and their eyes glowed menacingly. They were all armored, and they were armed with a shield in the left hand and a saber in the right hand.","They resembled troops summoned from the netherworld to the world of the living, and the number of troops matched the number of Netherworld Sectmembers.","“Is this their hidden hand? I didn’t expect them to withhold such a move,” Eggy said.","These blood-red giants had manifested in all directions, even though the ones controlling them were all behind Chu Feng at the moment. This suggested that the Netherworld Sectmembers had prepared this formation in advance to encircle him.","From the airs emanated by the blood-red giants, this Netherworld Troop Formation was far more potent than the earlier Annihilation Formation. This was the Netherworld Sect’s real hidden card!","Eggy was worried, for she knew that Chu Feng wouldn’t be able to deal with this formation even if he exerted his full strength. And to her bewilderment, Chu Feng had stopped escaping as well.","So, she prepared to make a move.","“Chu Feng, even if you’re at your limit, don’t resort to the Divine Deer’s power right away. I can take you away from here instead,” Eggy said.","But Chu Feng immediately replied, “Eggy, I feel a weird reaction from my Netherworld Embryo.”","This was the real reason he had stopped.","“A weird reaction? How so? Is this formation suppressing you through the Netherworld Embryo inside of you?” Eggy felt even more unnerved.","“No, that’s not it. I feel like... I can control those blood-red giants through my Netherworld Embryo. If their Netherworld Embryos have morphed into soldiers, I feel like mine can be morphed into... a general,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6553,"title":"Chapter 6553: Chapter 6551: The Level of a Commander","paragraphs":["Chapter 6551: Commander Level","“Oh? Does that mean that their formation doesn’t pose a threat to you?” Eggy asked.","“I believe so, but I’m not sure how I can activate my Netherworld Embryo,” Chu Feng replied.","He turned around to look at the Netherworld Sectmembers, only to see them standing completely still.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists had caught up with them, but they kept their distance, presumably because they knew that Chu Feng wouldn’t be easy to deal with.","Chu Feng ignored the world spiritists and focused on the Netherworld Sectmembers.","The Netherworld Sectmembers emitted a blood-red aura that gushed into the sky and fused with the blood-red world. This formation was beyond their current means to control; they must have used a special method and paid a heavy price to construct and activate it.","Chu Feng observed the Netherworld Sectmembers, hoping to figure out the complete formula from their current hand seals. If he could decipher the formula, he could potentially channel his Netherworld Embryo and fuse it into the formation as well.","Unfortunately, it was too difficult for even Chu Feng to figure out the complete formula from just a single hand seal.","“Ahahahaha!” Zhao Feng, who was being held hostage by Chu Feng, suddenly let out an arrogant laugh. “You’re cornered now, Chu Feng!”","An idea popped into Chu Feng’s mind. He turned to Zhao Feng and asked, “What do you mean by that?”","“This is our Netherworld Sect’s Netherworld Troop Formation. We prepared teleportation formations beforehand to transport not us but our Netherworld Embryos. What you’re seeing now is not just simple formation entities but the manifestations of our Netherworld Embryos. This is a formation that we have devoted our life force and our bloodlines to. It’s not something your martial skills can match.","“This formation is invincible within its cultivation rank! You’re cornered now, Chu Feng. If you surrender right now, I can consider speaking up on your behalf to my godfather to grant you a quick death,” Zhao Feng said.","“Is that so?” Chu Feng chuckled as he took out a pill.","“What are you planning to do, Chu Feng? My godfather won’t let you off if you dare kill me. Everyone you know will be implicated by your recklessness.” Zhao Feng thought that Chu Feng had taken out a poison pill and panicked.","The other Netherworld Sectmembers anxiously channeled the Netherworld Troops to rush over to rescue Zhao Feng.","Chu Feng forcefully stuffed the pill into Zhao Feng’s mouth.","Zhao Feng was stunned. To his bewilderment, the pill was a recovery pill. His pain was vanishing, and he was regaining his fighting prowess. Chu Feng... is treating me? Is he intimidated by my threats?","A cold sneer formed on Zhao Feng’s lips as his panic dissipated. Hmph. I guess that’s all the legendary Chu Feng amounts to. He’s ultimately a coward who fears death.","Chu Feng flung his sleeves and tossed Zhao Feng off, saying, “The Netherworld Troop Formation? It’s nothing but a show. I have nothing to fear, even if you participate in the formation as well.”","Zhao Feng was in disbelief, but it looked like Chu Feng truly wanted him to channel the Netherworld Troop Formation as well. He knew about the dangers of the Netherworld Troop Formation—not only would his cultivation regress, but he risked losing his life if the formation was maintained for too long.","He wouldn’t have channeled his formation under normal circumstances.","But he knew that Baili Xukong and the other experts of the Netherworld Sect were observing his every move.","The other Netherworld Sectmembers were already channeling the Netherworld Troop Formation. If he didn’t participate in this formation right now, he wouldn’t receive any credit if they subdued Chu Feng through this formation.","So, he had no choice but to join the formation.","“You arrogant fool. Since you seek death, I’ll grant your wish!” Zhao Feng sneered as he formed his hand seals.","Meanwhile, Cang Li and the others were confused.","“Is Chu Feng out of his mind, or does he have a trick up his sleeve?”","After witnessing what Chu Feng was capable of, they couldn’t help but feel uneasy.","“He doesn’t know how powerful our formation is. He shall pay the price of his conceit,” Baili Xukong sneered.","Zhao Feng’s voice echoed in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm, “I offer my blood to awaken the Netherworld Embryo. I offer my bloodline to nourish the Netherworld Embryo into a weapon. Activate, Netherworld Troop Formation!”","A blood-red aura erupted from Zhao Feng, and it swiftly morphed into a humongous Netherworld Troop. He didn’t channel the teleportation formation to summon his Netherworld Troop into the distance, but instead summoned it right in front of him.","Chu Feng was standing before him right now. Since he had already resorted to the Netherworld Troop Formation, he might as well kill Chu Feng right away and claim the biggest merit here.","“Thank you,” Chu Feng suddenly said.","Zhao Feng was stunned. Thank you? Why is Chu Feng thanking me?","Chu Feng flashed a bizarre smile at Zhao Feng as he began moving his hands. He formed the exact same hand seals as Zhao Feng did earlier.","In the formation realm, Baili Xukong and the others were horrified. Even Jie Tianran frowned. They noticed a reaction from the sacred item, as if it had received some kind of signal.","“This reaction... Could it mean...?”","Cang Li anxiously cast his gaze toward Chu Feng.","By then, Zhao Feng’s hulking Netherworld Troop was already swinging its mountainlike blade down on Chu Feng. Even before the blade landed, the immense pressure it harnessed caused the ground to crack.","Even so, Chu Feng remained unfazed.","When the massive blade was less than ten meters away from Chu Feng, it abruptly halted.","“Zhao Feng, kill him right now!” Baili Xukong anxiously ordered.","But Zhao Feng was confused as well. He hadn’t ordered the Netherworld Troop to stop the attack. For some reason, his Netherworld Troop had stopped obeying his command.","The same happened to all the summoned Netherworld Troops encircling Chu Feng.","The Netherworld Sectmembers were still paying the hefty price of the Netherworld Troop Formation, but for some reason, they had lost control of the formation.","While everyone was baffled, Chu Feng began emanating a blood-red aura as well. The blood-red aura manifested into a giant hand that grabbed the blade of Zhao Feng’s Netherworld Troop. The hand clenched, and the blade shattered into pieces.","Then, a humongous silhouette far surpassing that of the other Netherworld Troops manifested from Chu Feng’s blood-red aura.","“That is...!!!”","Everyone was bewildered, be it Zhao Feng and the others in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm, or Cang Li, Baili Xukong, and the other experts in the formation realm.","That humongous silhouette had manifested from a Netherworld Embryo, but it was larger, its armor was more delicate, and it wore a cape. Also, it was not wielding a shield and a saber but a spear.","Judging by appearances, the spear looked far superior to the sabers and the shields wielded by other Netherworld Troops.","That humongous silhouette was not a Netherworld Troop but a commander-level entity!"]},{"number":6554,"title":"Chapter 6554: Chapter 6552: The True Master of the Netherworld Troop Formation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6552: The True Master of the Netherworld Troop Formation","“Chu Feng, y-you...”","Zhao Feng’s pupils quivered in unease. He realized that he had been fooled by Chu Feng. The latter didn’t look down on the Netherworld Troop Formation; he merely wanted Zhao Feng to demonstrate the channeling method so that he could learn from it.","That was evident from how Chu Feng unleashed his Netherworld Embryo... but who could have known his Netherworld Embryo would be this powerful?","Zhao Feng would have to take responsibility for this. He was the one who provided Chu Feng with the channeling method.","“What’s the situation with that Chu Feng?”","In the formation realm, Cang Li and the others were in disbelief. They were well aware of the difficulty in channeling the Netherworld Troop Formation; those Netherworld Sectmembers had undergone special training. It shouldn’t have been possible for Chu Feng to use it.","“Those useless things,” Baili Xukong sneered as he took out a token.","The token emanated an aura similar to the Netherworld Troop Formation. It was the key to awakening the Netherworld Embryo and manifesting the formation. Without it, the Heavenly Gods inside the Undying Starfield wouldn’t have succeeded in constructing the formation.","Baili Xukong fused his bloodline power into the token. In response, the token emitted a blood-red aura that manifested into a mini formation core around him. He could control the Netherworld Troop Formation through the token.","However, he had to tap into the power of the Netherworld Embryo inside him to do so.","“Baili Xukong, you’re in no condition to be channeling the Netherworld Troop Formation! Do you want to die?” an elder from the neutral formation questioned.","It was not that they didn’t want to help Baili Xukong, but they were weakened from having their cultivation siphoned away from Chu Feng’s bloodline power earlier. They would sustain tremendous damage if they channeled their Netherworld Embryos in their condition.","“How can we face the world if our Netherworld Sect allows an outsider to channel our formation? We have to defend our pride here!” Baili Xukong revealed the reason he was determined to make a move despite the damage he would sustain.","The Netherworld Sect’s reputation was at stake here.","“Lord Baili, I’ll aid you.” Xiahou Jue and Baili Xukong’s other subordinates stepped into the formation core to help him channel the formation.","Meanwhile, a storm brewed in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm. A massive blood-red vortex formed in the sky. Everyone in the realm could sense that someone was attempting to interfere with this realm from the outside.","Zhao Feng and the others understood what was going on and smirked.","“Chu Feng, do you think you can control our Netherworld Troop Formation just because you summoned your Netherworld Embryo? I can tell you right now that we aren’t the true masters of this Netherworld Troop Formation. It is...”","Before Zhao Feng could finish his words, Chu Feng’s Netherworld Troop swept its spear into the sky, severing the swirling blood-red vortex into two.","Kacha!","In the formation realm, Baili Xukong’s token shattered. Everyone gathered in the formation core was sent flying in all directions, and they spurted blood profusely as they landed on the ground.","The crowd took another look at the token and noticed that its aura was swiftly dissipating.","“How is this possible?!” Baili Xukong stared at the shattered token in disbelief. At this moment, he didn’t just feel infuriated and indignant, but helplessness and despair as well.","He had been resolved to stop Chu Feng even if it meant depleting his Netherworld Embryo, but the token suddenly shattered. He wasn't even given the chance to put his life on the line.","In the Flowersea Ordinary Realm, Chu Feng turned to Zhao Feng and asked, “What did you say earlier?”","Zhao Feng quickly averted his gaze, not daring to even look at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng scoffed, “Were you trying to say that your godfather is the true master of the Netherworld Troop Formation? That might have been the case if I were not here, but it’s a pity that I’m here.”","Chu Feng raised his right hand, and his Netherworld Troop raised its spear.","The blood-red vortex descended from the sky and imbued itself into the Netherworld Troop’s spear. At this moment, it looked as if Chu Feng’s Netherworld Troop was the true ruler of this realm.","Something even more shocking happened afterward.","The other Netherworld Troops suddenly kneeled at the same time toward Chu Feng, as if kowtowing to their king.","Upon seeing this sight, the Netherworld Sectmembers inside the formation realm fell eerily silent. Other than the whirring of formations, the only sounds that could be heard were the sounds of furiously beating hearts and hastened breathing.","All of them felt goosebumps.","As much as they didn’t want to admit it, Chu Feng had thoroughly stolen control over the Netherworld Troop Formation. Chances were that he was behind the shattering of the token as well.","Chu Feng turned to Zhao Feng once more.","“Damn it!” Zhao Feng cursed under his breath as he tried to escape.","Boom!","A blood-red light descended from the sky, crushing Zhao Feng to the ground and rendering him immobile. This was the oppressive might emanated by Chu Feng’s Netherworld Troop.","“How is this possible? What kind of monster is Chu Feng?!”","The strain he was put under only made Zhao Feng’s mind clearer. He finally understood how Baili Zilin had fallen in defeat to Chu Feng. Chu Feng was strong not just because he wielded superior fighting prowess, but because his potential and talent were at an entirely different level.","It had taken Zhao Feng a long time before he could channel the Netherworld Troop Formation, but Chu Feng learned it with just a glance and even manifested his Netherworld Embryo into an entity far surpassing his.","On top of that, his control over the formation surpassed even that of Baili Xukong’s.","I didn’t know there could be such a huge difference among prodigies.","The other Netherworld Sectmembers also felt something cracking within them as well.","Even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists turned pale with fright. They were willing to lay down their lives for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but that didn’t mean that they weren’t afraid of death.","And they could tell that they were no match for the Netherworld Troop Formation.","To make things worse, they couldn’t even escape, for the Netherworld Troop Formation had isolated the space they were in, trapping them within its radius.","Chu Feng’s Netherworld Troop flung its spear.","Everyone’s heart jolted, whether they were in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm or in the formation realm.","Chu Feng had sensed the isolation property of the Netherworld Troop Formation and used it to seal off the Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","With that, Baili Xukong could no longer project his voice to the Netherworld Sectmembers anymore, and Jie Tianran’s observation formation could no longer peer into the Flowersea Ordinary Realm."]},{"number":6555,"title":"Chapter 6555: Chapter 6553: A Death Trial for the Unorthodox","paragraphs":["Chapter 6553: A Death Trial for the Unorthodox","In the formation realm, Jie Tianran took out a talisman paper and fused it into the observation formation. He was hoping to enhance the observation formation to the point where it was potent enough to peer into the Flowersea Ordinary Realm again.","Meanwhile, in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm, the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists looked at Chu Feng with nervous eyes, as if awaiting judgment.","“Chu Feng, why don’t you kill them straight?” Eggy asked.","“I have a use for them,” Chu Feng said. Moments later, he suddenly frowned and murmured, “That old thing is tenacious.”","He sensed Jie Tianran attempting to peer into the Flowersea Ordinary Realm. He looked at the Netherworld Sectmembers and Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists, who were shaken up but trying to feign composure, and an idea popped into his head.","“If that old thing wants to look so much, I should grant him his wish.”","He secretly formed a hand seal.","In the formation realm, Jie Tianran’s observation formation could suddenly peer into the Flowersea Ordinary Realm once more.","“The observation formation has been restored... but why am I still unable to contact them? Mansion Master, how much longer will it take to restore our communications?”","Cang Li, Baili Xukong, and the others looked at Jie Tianran.","“I’ll need more time, but I don’t think we’ll be able to turn the situation around even if we restore our communications with them. That little bastard Chu Feng is vicious. He won’t spare our people.” Jie Tianran said.","“That darned Chu Feng!”","Killing intent flared from the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists in the formation realm. Those in the Undying Starfield were only at rank one Heavenly God and rank one Heavenly Dragon, but they formed the bulk of their army.","It would be a huge loss to the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if they were to lose all of them here.","“What is Chu Feng up to?” Jie Tianran murmured.","He knew that the restoration of the observation formation wasn’t his doing. Rather, Chu Feng was intentionally allowing him to peer into the Flowersea Ordinary Realm. Yet, he didn’t restore their communications.","Chu Feng must be scheming something.","Chu Feng suddenly raised his head and looked straight into the observation formation. He revealed a smile before turning his gaze back to the Netherworld Sectmembers.","“I am a reasonable person. I usually avoid trouble, unless I see someone oppressing the weak. Of course, I’m also not so magnanimous as to forgive those who trifle with me. If anyone is after my life, you can be sure that I won’t let him live.”","All the Netherworld Troops suddenly emanated overwhelming killing intent, causing the hearts of the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm to turn cold.","They thought that they were going to be killed.","But to their surprise, Chu Feng didn’t kill them right away. Instead, he opened his palm and took out Feng Ling from his formation realm.","Feng Ling had gone into a deep sleep, but her miserable plight remained evident.","“You must be curious why I have gone after your Netherworld Sect’s sacred item. It’s because of Zhao Feng. He lured in many natural oddities for his cultivation, and my friend, Feng Ling, fell prey to his scheme.","“Zhao Feng was mesmerized by my friend’s beauty and lusted over her. He tried to take her as his wife. However, my friend refused to submit to him. In a fit of anger, Zhao Feng plundered my friend’s bloodline and attempted to refine her into a cultivation resource at the expense of her life.","“If I hadn’t arrived on time, my friend would have been just skin and bones by now.","“Your Netherworld Sect claims that it is an orthodox sect seeking to bring prosperity to the world, yet people like Zhao Feng continue to emerge from your ranks. You were aware of his actions, but you turned a blind eye. That makes you the same as him.","“And you dare say you aren’t an unorthodox sect?” Chu Feng sneered.","Most people in the formation realm remained nonchalant, but some people, like Cang Li, lowered their heads in shame. Despite not having participated in Zhao Feng's scheme, they felt ashamed at having failed to keep their sectmembers in line.","Zhao Feng’s deeds had sullied the Netherworld Sect’s reputation, and it conflicted with their primary goal.","“I’m not here today to exact justice for the world. All I want is justice for my friend. I’ll be magnanimous today and grant you a chance to redeem yourselves. World spiritists of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, aid me in constructing my formation. Netherworld Sectmembers, aid me in channeling the formation. If you help me, I’ll forgive you for attempting to kill me earlier and spare your lives.”","Many Netherworld Sectmembers immediately spoke up against him vehemently. “Chu Feng, you want us to aid you in killing our sectmember? Dream on!”","Some Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists also sneered, “Chu Feng, you must have a vivid imagination. I won’t help you construct your formation even if it means dying!”","Jie Tianran, Baili Xukong, and the others were satisfied with their responses.","If death was inevitable, at least their people maintained a dignified front and didn’t embarrass them.","“Chu Feng must be truly foolish to think that our Netherworld Sectmember would work for him,” Baili Xukong sneered.","Wu!","Hundreds of blood-red lights descended and enveloped those who criticized Chu Feng. Those shrouded in the blood-red lights began screaming in utmost pain. Cracks appeared all over their bodies, and blood gushed from those cracks.","The sheer pain from their bodies crumbling robbed them of their energy to insult Chu Feng. All they could do was scream endlessly.","It was so brutal that the crowd felt chills just listening to the screams.","The Netherworld Sectmembers and Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm and in the formation realm had blood on their hands, but they couldn’t bear to look at the people shrouded in the blood-red lights.","Despite their crumbling bodies, they remained very much alive. It was torture!","“I should make one thing clear. I wasn’t negotiating with you,” Chu Feng snorted.","He clenched his fist, and those shrouded by the blood-red light were reduced to blood water. Both their bodies and their souls had been vanquished.","This sight stunned the crowd.","Those who had thought they were fearless and wanted to criticize Chu Feng shivered in fear. The words sitting at the tip of their tongue refused to leave their mouths. It was only in the face of death that they finally understood how cowardly they were.","“That bastard isn’t a human! I’ll rip him into pieces!”","Killing intent flared even more intensely in the formation realm after witnessing Chu Feng’s cruel means.","Chu Feng suddenly cast his gaze at the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm. None dared to meet his eye.","“I have already blocked the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s observation formation. They are unable to see what’s happening here. If you wish, we can keep the events here a secret. Now, give me your answer. I’ll only count to three.","“I’ll promise you one thing right now. Those who refuse me will suffer a fate a hundred times worse than what you have just witnessed.”","“A hundred times?”","Those gathered in the Flowersea Ordinary Realm were so terrified that their legs wobbled like a newborn calf.","Just the fate of those who had just died was enough to terrify them. They couldn’t begin to imagine what a hundred times worse than that would be like. That could be the worst torture in the world.","Chu Feng lifted three fingers.","“One. Two.”","He lowered two fingers, not giving the others any time to think. It was almost as if he wanted to kill them.","Just as Chu Feng was about to put down the third finger...","“I’ll do it!”","More than three hundred people from the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion replied at the same time.","“I’ll do it too! I’ll do it!”","The remaining people also voiced their agreement.","This sight plunged the formation realm into silence once more."]},{"number":6556,"title":"Chapter 6556: Chapter 6554: Saving My Close Friend With Zhao Feng’s Life","paragraphs":["Chapter 6554: Saving My Close Friend With Zhao Feng’s Life","The Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members in the formation realm gnashed their teeth in anger. Chu Feng’s action was vile. It made them question the loyalty of their respective members.","The old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body was the one to break the silence.","“That brat, Chu Feng, is quite the scoundrel. He’s intentionally showing you how he manipulates your people to do his bidding.”","Though those words could only be heard by Jie Tianran.","...","“You aren’t trying to pull wool over my eyes, right? If you dare play tricks, I’ll make you regret ever being born,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng, we would have never helped you if it were anyone else, but Zhao Feng deserves to die,” an elder from the Netherworld Sect said.","“Indeed, Zhao Feng deserves to die in the first place. We’re merely punishing him on behalf of the Netherworld Sect.”","More Netherworld Sectmembers voiced their agreement, pinning all blame on Zhao Feng.","“What... nonsense are you spouting? What do you mean I deserve death? Are you going to stoop so low as to side with an outsider like Chu Feng? You cowards! The Netherworld Sect has raised you in vain! My godfather will not let you off if he learns about this!” Zhao Feng panicked.","He had known that Chu Feng wouldn’t spare him, but he didn’t expect the latter to use his fellow peers to channel his formation and kill him. To make things worse, almost everyone here had agreed to it!","“Shut up! You have no right to lecture us. Chu Feng would have never come here if you hadn’t exploited those natural oddities and captured Feng Ling for your cultivation! Our ritual to awaken our sacred item would have gone smoothly. You are the cause of this mess! You are the sinner of our Netherworld Sect!","“After your huge screw-up, Zhao Feng, do you think that the lords of our Netherworld Sect will spare you even if Chu Feng lets you go? You are already doomed, Zhao Feng!”","The Netherworld Sectmembers berated Zhao Feng.","“Nonsense!” Zhao Feng tried to argue back, but his single mouth was no match for the crowd.","Chu Feng ignored the Netherworld Sect’s internal strife and waved his sleeves.","Shoosh!","A surge of spirit power rose into the sky and unfurled into a formation blueprint.","“Construct a formation based on this blueprint,” Chu Feng commanded the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","These Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists dared not hesitate after having witnessed Chu Feng’s means and decisiveness. They knew that the latter would kill them in a heartbeat if they didn’t carry out his orders. They quickly constructed a formation based on Chu Feng’s blueprint.","“Know that my eyes see clearer than any of yours. If you dare to alter my blueprint in any way, you should be prepared to die,” Chu Feng warned.","The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists didn’t answer, but they obediently constructed Chu Feng’s formation.","Even though their fighting prowess was nothing noteworthy for rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, they displayed exceptional world spiritist techniques and coordinated well. They did an outstanding job fulfilling Chu Feng’s formation blueprint.","This showed that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion wasn’t all talk.","In the formation realm, Jie Tianran had been keeping an eye on the Flowersea Ordinary Realm using his observation formation. He appeared to have overexerted himself on the observation formation, evident from his sweaty face.","“That is an extremely complicated formation, but that brat relayed it in such a concise manner. That is a hallmark of true skills. Jie Tianran, your grandson’s grasp of formations far surpasses that of Jie Tian,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran continued channeling the formation without saying a word.","He could also tell that Chu Feng’s formation blueprint was extraordinary, but that only further stoked his annoyance. It felt as if the world was telling him that he had made the wrong choice, but it was already too late to turn back.","Moments later, a blood-red aura enveloped the Flowersea Ordinary Realm. A brilliant light emerged from the ground. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists had finished constructing Chu Feng’s formation around Zhao Feng.","“Let’s begin.”","Chu Feng looked at the Netherworld Sectmembers.","The Netherworld Sectmembers stepped into the formation cores and coordinated with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists to channel the formation.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","Light spears manifested from the formation and pierced Zhao Feng’s body.","GAHH!","Zhao Feng screamed in agony.","Whether it was because they feared Chu Feng’s punishment or that they were angered by Zhao Feng’s earlier retorts, the Netherworld Sectmembers put their all into channeling the formation.","Soon, Zhao Feng’s Netherworld Troop dissipated into a blood-red aura and returned to his body. However, that only made Zhao Feng scream in greater agony.","Chu Feng carried Feng Ling into the formation core located at the center of the formation.","Even though this formation was being channeled by the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, Chu Feng still wielded the final say in this formation.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal and pointed his finger at Zhao Feng.","Zhao Feng had been screaming with bulging eyes all along, but at this moment, his body suddenly stiffened, and he fell silent. His demeanor abruptly changed. An instant was all it took for him to feel like a dead man.","His vitals were still present, but they were so faint that one could mistake him for a corpse.","Two surges of power flowed out from Zhao Feng’s dantian.","One of the powers carried a pristine quality, a stark contrast to Zhao Feng’s aura. This was Feng Ling’s bloodline power.","However, it was much stronger than Feng Ling’s original bloodline power, and it continued to grow stronger as time passed. This was all because of the other power.","The other power was blood-red and sinister. It was a combination of Zhao Feng’s cultivation and bloodline power. This power was gradually weakening as it was being consumed to refine Feng Ling’s bloodline power.","That was why Chu Feng took the risk of engaging the help of the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","He was more than capable of saving Feng Ling alone, but with their aid, he could increase the chances of success and even enhance Feng Ling’s bloodline power."]},{"number":6557,"title":"Chapter 6557: Chapter 6555: A Feat Beyond the Netherworld Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6555: A Feat Beyond the Netherworld Sect","Under Chu Feng’s formation, Feng Ling’s condition improved while Zhao Feng grew weaker.","Zhao Feng eventually breathed his last when his bloodline power was depleted. He stopped screaming at some point, but his lips continued quivering, and his eyes were rolled up. It didn’t look like he had died a peaceful death.","One could only imagine the sheer pain he felt even at his dying breath, but no one pitied him. Even the Netherworld Sectmembers thought that Zhao Feng deserved his plight.","Now that the deed was done, the Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists was left wondering if Chu Feng would really let them off. They were also worried that others would learn that they had lent a helping hand to Chu Feng.","Just then, a voice transmission was relayed to all Netherworld Sectmembers.","“Don’t worry. We might have helped Chu Feng channel the formation to kill Zhao Feng, but it’s also a fact that Zhao Feng was the perpetrator behind this mess. He deserves to die.","“Besides, Chu Feng has also participated in the Netherworld Troop Formation. He probably doesn’t know how severe the backlash is. I don’t know how he morphed his Netherworld Embryo into such a powerful entity and gained control over the Netherworld Troop Formation, but the greater the power, the greater the backlash.","“Once the backlash settles in, Chu Feng won’t be able to escape.”","The one who spoke was the elder from the Netherworld Sect’s conservative faction.","They had done Chu Feng’s bidding because they feared death, but if Chu Feng were to be incapacitated by the backlash, they could compensate for their wrongdoing by capturing Chu Feng.","And it would be a huge merit.","Wu!","The blood-red aura covering the sky dissipated. The Netherworld Troops dissipated into blood-red auras and returned to the bodies of the Netherworld Sectmembers.","All Netherworld Sectmembers slumped to the ground as if they had lost all their energy. They became as feeble as a dying man, and their bodies grew visibly older.","This was the backlash of channeling the Netherworld Troop Formation. The Netherworld Sectmembers had known this would happen, which was why they hesitated to channel it in the first place.","“Chu Feng, how are you feeling?” Eggy asked worriedly after seeing the plights of the Netherworld Sectmembers.","“I’m... fine.”","Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo also returned to his body, but he didn’t feel any anomaly.","“That’s good.” Eggy was surprised, but she quickly shrugged it off. Chu Feng often accomplished feats that others couldn’t even imagine. She had long grown accustomed to it.","“H-how are you fine?” The Netherworld Sect’s elder stared at Chu Feng in disbelief.","The other Netherworld Sectmembers also looked at him in incredulity.. They had been waiting for Chu Feng to be incapacitated by the backlash so that they could capture him and make up for their error.","Yet, Chu Feng was perfectly unscathed! How could they make up for their wrongdoing then?","“Are you asking why I’m fine despite having channeled your formation?” Chu Feng asked.","“What else?” The elder was agitated despite being in a feeble state.","Chu Feng chuckled before replying, “While your formation isn’t easy to channel, it shouldn’t cause a backlash when properly done. You’re suffering a backlash because you lack recognition from your Netherworld Embryos. That limits the power you can borrow from them.","“You resorted to special means to forcefully siphon power away from your Netherworld Embryo to activate the Netherworld Troop Formation; the backlash is the cost your Netherworld Embryo imposed on you in exchange.","“As for the cost... I’m guessing it’s your lifespan, though I can’t tell for sure since my Netherworld Embryo doesn’t impose such a cost on me.”","The Netherworld Sectmembers were shocked beyond words.","Is that the case? Or is he spouting nonsense?","Regardless, it was a fact that Chu Feng was unaffected by the backlash.","In the formation realm, Jie Tianran, Cang Li, and the others saw that Chu Feng was unaffected by the backlash, and they heard his words as well. No one uttered a word, but the Netherworld Sectmembers frowned.","Chu Feng’s words had come as a blow to them.","Cang Li stared deeply at Chu Feng as he murmured, “Has Chu Feng seen through the crux of the Netherworld Troop Formation? He’s completely unaffected by the Netherworld Embryo. No one in our present Netherworld Sect is capable of that. We sought the sacred item to fully grasp the power of the Netherworld Embryo, a feat that was impossible otherwise. Yet, he achieved it? Haa...”","Cang Li heaved a sigh filled with complicated emotions.","That was the reason behind the Netherworld Sectmembers’ frowns.","An outsider had achieved what they, the Netherworld Sect, had been pursuing all this time.","...","In the Flowersea Ordinary Realm...","“Continue channeling the formation,” Chu Feng ordered the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","Zhao Feng was dead, and Feng Ling had been saved, but Chu Feng thought that they could do better than this.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists did as Chu Feng instructed.","The Netherworld Troop Formation had finally unraveled, but the Netherworld Sectmembers had also become incapacitated in the process. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists weren’t confident of dealing with Chu Feng by themselves.","“How... could... this...”","The elder from the Netherworld Sect’s conservative faction glared at Chu Feng before collapsing to the ground. His eyes remained bulging, and his mouth was still open, but he had breathed his last.","And he wasn’t the first casualty.","Several Netherworld Sectmembers had already succumbed to the backlash and died, though all of them were on the older side.","“Oh? I’m surprised that so many failed to withstand the backlash. Let’s not waste precious resources, especially ones from Heavenly Gods.”","Chu Feng channeled a recovery formation for Feng Ling with his left hand while swiping away the possessions of the deceased Heavenly Gods with his right hand. The origin energies were transported into his World Spirit Space, while the treasures were stowed away in his Cosmos Sack.","“Chu Feng, are you going to break your promise?”","The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists channeling the formation tensed up. The sight of Chu Feng harvesting the deceased cultivators’ possessions made them wonder if he would do the same to them as well.","“Don’t worry, I am a man of my word. I’ll spare your lives for today since you have helped me, but I should warn you that Jie Tianran has been looking at us through his observation formation. He would have seen you working for me. I wonder if he will be as magnanimous as I am and spare your lives,” Chu Feng said with a smirk."]},{"number":6558,"title":"Chapter 6558: Chapter 6556: A Massive Gap","paragraphs":["Chapter 6556: A Massive Gap","“Chu Feng, you...”","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists and the surviving Netherworld Sectmembers looked as if they had been struck by lightning.","“You can’t blame me. That old thing insisted on looking into the Flowersea Ordinary Realm,” Chu Feng remarked as he stowed Feng Ling into the formation realm in his palm.","He beamed a smile at the crowd as he continued, “I sealed off the realm with the Netherworld Troop Formation, but his means are stronger than I thought. He reinforced his observation formation and peered in. They must have witnessed the construction of the formation, Zhao Feng’s death, and Feng Ling’s recovery.”","Chu Feng shirked responsibility to Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran’s mouth twitched. He was well aware that he wasn’t the one who restored the observation formation—Chu Feng had intentionally let him in to see what was happening inside.","Chu Feng rose into the sky.","He had successfully obtained the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy and saved Feng Ling. It was time for him to leave.","Weng!","Just then, the formation realm emanated a blinding light.","Baili Xukong and the others turned to Jie Tianran. The light was coming from a scroll in Jie Tianran’s hand.","“Jie Tianran, use my sealing formation to teach that arrogant grandson of yours a lesson. Otherwise, he might think that no one can do anything about him,” the old entity told Jie Tianran.","This was the formation constructed by the old entity.","Without any hesitation, Jie Tianran tossed the scroll toward Chu Feng.","Shoosh!","The scroll flew out at an absurdly fast speed, surging out of the formation realm instantly before swiftly expanding into the size of a realm.","In the blink of an eye, it had become as huge as the entire Undying Starfield.","Such a humongous item was naturally visible to Chu Feng from the Flowersea Ordinary Realm.","“What is that?” Eggy felt unease.","Chu Feng’s eyebrows also shot up. Not even an early Heavenly God level cultivator could deploy something of this caliber.","Shoosh!","The scroll unfurled into a humongous painting that enveloped the Undying Starfield, sealing it off. Within the painting was a realm where ghastly howls and feral growls echoed from. It looked as if hell was about to be unleashed upon the world.","“Is that... the Ghost Spirit World?” Eggy asked.","She sensed the Ghost Spirit World’s aura, and the cacophony also resembled the noises made by Ghost World Spirits.","“A formation constructed using the power of the Ghost Spirit World?”","As the energy within the painting intensified, Chu Feng realized this was going to be tough to deal with. Even if he tapped into the Monster Slayer Sword's power, he still wouldn’t be able to overcome this powerful sealing formation.","“What a formidable move, Mansion Master.”","Baili Xukong and the others applauded.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists trembled in excitement. They sensed how potent the sealing formation was.","“I said that I’d stop Chu Feng from leaving.” Jie Tianran didn’t reveal the old entity’s involvement in the sealing formation, instead taking full credit for it.","Jie Tianran’s voice projected his voice across the Undying Starfield through the sealing formation, “Chu Feng, go ahead and reveal whatever tricks you have left up your sleeves. Otherwise, don’t even dream about getting out of here today.”","His voice was resounding, almost as if it had come from a god.","Countless black shadows reminiscent of an army of locusts flew out from the sealing formation. They were world spirits from the Ghost Spirit World, and they were all headed for the Flowersea Ordinary Realm. Their target? Chu Feng.","There had to be at least hundreds of millions of Ghost World Spirits.","Chu Feng knew that they were just formation entities, but these Ghost World Spirits still felt chillingly lifelike. Even the Netherworld Sectmembers lying on the ground were scared out of their wits.","Yet, Chu Feng grinned.","He had to concede that the sealing formation was too much for him to deal with, but he had no fear.","“Elder, I need your help,” Chu Feng told the Divine Deer.","But the Divine Deer didn’t make a move. “I don’t think you need my help anymore.”","Chu Feng looked into the distance, toward the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s tombstone. The Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul sliver was still floating there, but it had opened its eyes.","Chu Feng suddenly felt overwhelming power shrouding him.","The Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul sliver had flitted to his side to protect him.","Chu Feng’s body began whizzing into the sky at a speed so fast that he was out of the Flowersea Ordinary Realm before he knew it. But the Great Monster Slayer Emperor didn’t stop there. He continued guiding Chu Feng’s body toward the sealing formation.","As Chu Feng approached the sealing formation, he got a better look at it.","The shadows emerging from the sealing formation were indeed Ghost World Spirits, and they were not both countless and humongous. Each was over tens of thousands of meters, making them comparable to towering mountains.","The sealing formation felt even more terrifying close up, but Chu Feng remained perfectly composed. He trusted the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul sliver.","“Let me see who dares block the path of my successor!” the Great Monster Slayer Emperor sneered as his body enlarged.","In the blink of an eye, he grew to the size of a realm. Even the massive Ghost World Spirits looked like ants in his presence. He gathered his energy in his palm and manifested a sword.","It was a normal sword instead of the Monster Slayer Sword, but it shared the same aura as the Great Monster Slayer Emperor.","“That sword...”","Chu Feng didn’t recognize the sword, but Jie Tianran, Cang Li, and the others gathered in the formation realm recognized it.","Most people who had heard about the Great Monster Slayer Emperor would have also heard about the Monster Slayer Sword, but the Great Monster Slayer Emperor wielded another blade.","It was a perfectly ordinary sword that couldn’t even be considered an armament. It was simply known as ‘Metal Sword’.","Clang!","The Great Monster Slayer Emperor swung his Metal Sword.","A silver light devoured the surroundings.","It was a burst of sword aura and sword intent. Space quivered wherever his sword intent touched. The Ghost World Spirits vaporized as if moths flying into a silver inferno. It didn’t matter how many of them there were.","Even the sealing formation reverted into a scroll and was sliced apart. Its tatters disintegrated into wisps of spirit power and dissipated into vast space.","“Amazing!” Chu Feng was stunned.","He instinctively understood that the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s strength was at a completely different level.","Chu Feng wasn’t the only one who was shocked. In the formation realm, Baili Xukong, Cang Li, Jie Tianran, and the others fell silent. They stared at the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul sliver in a daze.","The Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had thought that they had reached the peak of the world of cultivation after their recent breakthroughs.","But after witnessing the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s blade, they realized that they still had a long way to go before they could rival the experts from the earlier years of the present era."]},{"number":6559,"title":"Chapter 6559: Chapter 6557: The Moved Chen Hui","paragraphs":["Chapter 6557: The Moved Chen Hui","The Great Monstrous Emperor Slayer’s soul sliver continued to escort Chu Feng even after escaping from the Undying Starfield. Even though it hadn’t slowed down yet, its soul sliver had already begun to disintegrate.","Chu Feng pulled out Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat in advance, so that he could activate it right away when the Great Monstrous Emperor’s soul sliver disintegrated for good. This way, he could continue his escape without slowing down.","When the Great Monstrous Emperor Slayer’s soul sliver fully disintegrated, Chu Feng felt melancholy washing over him.","Even though this soul sliver lacked sentience, it still carried the Great Monstrous Emperor Slayer’s strength and aura. Its disintegration marked the complete death of the Great Monstrous Emperor Slayer.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng waved his sleeves, and a white, plump figure rolled onto the bamboo boat.","It was Chen Hui.","“Brother, y-you...”","Chen Hui panicked. Despite being imprisoned in Chu Feng’s formation realm, he witnessed everything that had transpired earlier. Unsurprisingly, he was intimidated by Chu Feng.","“You can go,” Chu Feng said.","“You... are letting me go?” Chen Hui was taken aback.","“I have no reason to keep you around. The Netherworld Sect doesn’t care about your life and death. You’re useless as a hostage,” Chu Feng said.","“That’s why you’re letting me go? Are you sure? I-I’m really going to leave!” Chen Hui said.","“Shoo.” Chu Feng waved him off.","Chen Hui walked to the edge of the bamboo boat.","As fast as the bamboo boat was, Chen Hui had his ways of returning to the Netherworld Sect once he leaped off it. Yet, he stood at the edge of the boat with a hesitant face, not jumping off.","“Why aren’t you leaving? Are you worried that you’ll be punished when you return?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course not. I’m one of the most outstanding prodigies of the conservative faction; they’ll surely defend me. Besides, I’m a victim. There’s no reason for them to punish me just because I survived the ordeal. The Netherworld Sect isn’t that unreasonable,” Chen Hui said.","“A reasonable sect wouldn’t have committed such vile atrocities,” Chu Feng scoffed.","“The new faction has indeed gone overboard. When I take over power in the conservative faction in the future, I’ll make sure to purge all the black sheep. The Netherworld Sect will be born anew,” Chen Hui said.","“Birds of the same feather flock together. Stop being an eyesore and scram,” Chu Feng scoffed.","He had no interest in listening to Chen Hui defend the Netherworld Sect.","But Chen Hui stayed put. Instead, the hesitation on his face deepened.","“Spit out whatever you want to say. Are the prodigies of the Netherworld Sect so wishy-washy?” Chu Feng could tell that Chen Hui had something to say.","“Chu Feng, are we still friends?” Chen Hui asked.","“We’re normal friends, but don’t expect me to jump to your rescue when you’re in danger,” Chu Feng replied.","“What if I’m really in danger?” Chen Hui asked.","“Then you should pray hard that things work out for you,” Chu Feng replied.","“Haa...” Chen Hui sighed. “Did you meet little sister Yun’er afterward?”","He had heard some news from the new faction. Xiahou Jue had bumped into Song Yun, together with Chu Feng and the others, in the Immemorial Cemetery.","“Yes, I met her.”","“Do you know how Yun’er is faring, and where she is?”","“She’s no longer in these eight galaxies.”","“Does that mean that she has entered the Ninth Galaxy?”","Chu Feng didn’t respond to that question, but his silence itself was a confirmation.","“Yun’er visited me before she left. I don’t know what skill she grasped, but she killed our Netherworld Sect’s prodigies and turned them into cultivation resources. She handed some of the cultivation resources to me. I didn’t reject her gift because I didn’t know that they were our Netherworld Sectmembers.","“It’s because of little sister Yun’er that I reached my current cultivation level,” Chen Hui replied.","“So, Song Yun really killed many Netherworld Sectmembers?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s right.”","“It’s cruel, but the Netherworld Sectmembers deserve it.”","Chen Hui’s lips twitched, but he knew better than to speak up for the Netherworld Sectmembers in front of Chu Feng.","“So, what is it that you want to tell me? Is it related to Song Yun?” Chu Feng asked. His gut feeling told him that this was the reason behind Chen Hui’s hesitation.","“I guess it’s obvious. I shan’t beat around the bush then. No matter whether you see me as a friend or not, I consider you my friend. Yun’er’s cultivation resources did benefit me greatly at the start, but as time passed, the side effects began to show. My days will be numbered if I fail to overcome the side effects.","“You didn’t suffer a backlash from the Netherworld Troop Formation even though you have manifested your Netherworld Embryo into such a powerful form. This shows that you possess exceptional control over your Netherworld Embryo. So, I was wondering if you could help me... But I understand if you refuse, too!” Chen Hui said.","Chu Feng looked at the pitiful Chen Hui and sighed. He had a favorable impression of Chen Hui, and the latter wasn’t involved in the Netherworld Sect’s wrongdoings, either.","“I’ll take a look,” Chu Feng said as he placed his palm on Chen Hui’s body.","“Your condition resembles the backlash suffered by the Netherworld Sectmembers who channeled the Netherworld Troop Formation. You used special means to obtain the Netherworld Embryo’s power, but the Netherworld Embryo doesn’t recognize you, so it took something as compensation. You said that your days are numbered, so I’m guessing it took your lifespan.","“I can impart to you a cultivation method. You’ll have to spend two hours each day practicing it. It might work, but I can’t guarantee anything. You’ll have to try it yourself.”","Chu Feng tapped Chen Hui’s mind and transferred a formation into it.","The formation contained a special method to withstand the Netherworld Embryo’s backlash. However, Chu Feng had applied special restrictions to the method so that only Chen Hui could practice it. He wouldn’t be able to impart the method to anyone else.","“Brother Chu Feng, you’re the best. I knew that you still saw me as a friend. The method you imparted to me is ingenious! I think I’ll be able to survive this ordeal with it. This way, I won’t let down little sister Yun’er’s high hopes in me.” Chen Hui was so moved that tears streamed down his cheeks.","“Let me ask you a question. You mentioned that Song Yun visited you after converting some Netherworld Sectmembers into cultivation resources. Did she absorb the cultivation resources first, or did she let you do it first?” Chu Feng asked.","“She let me absorb the cultivation resources first. That’s why I was so moved. I don’t agree with little sister Yun’er’s way of doing things, but she has truly done me a huge favor,” Chen Hui said.","“What are you moved for?” Chu Feng rolled his eyes.","“Huh?” Chen Hui was confused.","“Are you an idiot?”","“I consider myself sharp-witted.”","“Have you never questioned whether Song Yun has your best intentions at heart, or that she’s just using you as a guinea pig to see if the cultivation resources can be used?” Chu Feng asked.","Chen Hui was stunned."]},{"number":6560,"title":"Chapter 6560: Chapter 6558: Three Phenomena","paragraphs":["Chapter 6558: Three Phenomena","“Brother, your words are too much.” Chen Hui clutched his chest with a pained expression. It was hard to tell whether he was truly in pain or if it was just an act.","“Hm?”","A white light suddenly shone from Chu Feng’s palm. Chen Hui looked over.","“You should leave now,” Chu Feng cued.","“All right, I’ll take my leave. Brother Chu Feng, let’s meet again.” Chen Hui knew that Chu Feng was likely going to deal with something confidential, so he didn’t hesitate to leap off the boat this time.","Embedded in Chu Feng’s palm was his formation realm. Within his formation realm lay the unconscious Feng Ling, who was recuperating in a recovery formation. However, her body was undergoing some changes. She was about to invoke a phenomenon.","Chu Feng’s formation realm was nowhere strong enough to hold in the phenomenon, which resulted in the white light spilling out.","He pulled Feng Ling out of his formation realm and placed her down on the bamboo boat.","Feng Ling’s body was shrouded in a brilliant white light, and she emanated a divine aura. The white light converged and became even more blinding. All of a sudden, the white light gushed into the sky and enveloped the surroundings.","Even though the bamboo boat, with its ridiculously fast movement speed, had already disappeared into the horizon from Chen Hui’s point of view, the blinding white light still extended to where he was and enveloped his surroundings.","It was a phenomenon, one large enough to encompass a starfield!","“What a formidable phenomenon! Is it from that lady named Feng Ling?” Chen Hui guessed, though he wasn’t certain. Chu Feng had too many secrets, after all.","The phenomenon was even more astonishing from Chu Feng’s point of view, especially since it was moving along with the bamboo boat. He saw the phenomenon far clearer than anyone else could.","The white light was not pure light—it was a cluster of pristine feathers revolving around a core. No, it was not exactly feathers but something resembling dandelion seeds. In any case, it was stunning.","It felt divine, but it didn’t feel stifling. It felt incredibly pure.","“Waaa, what an amazing phenomenon!” Eggy exclaimed aloud. She had come out on her own accord and was now standing beside Chu Feng.","On the bamboo boat whizzing through space, Chu Feng and Eggy stood side by side while admiring the pristine scenery around them. It was a truly gorgeous sight, but Chu Feng turned his gaze from the scenery to Eggy when she emerged.","“Is it beautiful?” Chu Feng asked.","“It is. Feng Ling’s phenomenon is rather special.”","Eggy stared at the phenomenon with twinkling eyes. Even she was not immune to such beautiful scenery.","“It’s beautiful, but there’s something more beautiful here,” Chu Feng said.","“Where?” Eggy looked around.","Chu Feng poked Eggy’s face with his finger. “Here.”","Eggy frowned in confusion, not knowing what Chu Feng was getting at. It was only when she noticed his mischievous smile that she realized that he was teasing her. “You’re asking for a beating, Chu Feng! How dare you tease this queen?”","She punched Chu Feng’s arm.","“Am I getting punished for speaking the truth now? My Eggy’s face is so much nicer. I can stare at it all day long and still not get enough of it.” Chu Feng clutched his arm while yelping in pain.","“Chu Feng, you’re getting from bad to worse!” Eggy hurled her fist.","“I was wrong, I was wrong!? Chu Feng retreated with a mischievous grin.","Soon, the white light converged back into Feng Ling’s body. Feng Ling’s complexion visibly reddened. She looked much healthier than most people. Clearly, this phenomenon was a huge fortuitous encounter for her.","“She should be fine now. There might even be an advancement in her cultivation when she regains consciousness,” Eggy remarked.","Chu Feng nodded in agreement. He finally exhaled in relief.","A brilliant red light suddenly glowed from a distant galaxy. Its radiance could be clearly seen even though Chu Feng was a far distance away from its source. It was from the Immortal Sea Galaxy.","“Another phenomenon!” Eggy exclaimed in astonishment.","This phenomenon also spanned the size of a starfield, but it looked even more incredible as the red light converged into a blood-red lotus.","“Is this really just a coincidence?” Chu Feng murmured.","The phenomenon happened to envelop the starfield where the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader resided, as well as where Zi Ling was in closed-door cultivation. He couldn’t help but wonder if this phenomenon was related to Zi Ling.","A phenomenon signified good news, and one that enveloped a starfield would be extremely difficult to track. Even those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect would struggle to track its source.","So, Chu Feng was in no rush to look for Zi Ling. He thought that he should meet up with Wen Xue, Li Wu, and Bai Yunqing first.","But as Feng Ling’s phenomenon had moved along with him earlier, he had been moving in another direction lest Jie Tianran tracked their whereabouts through this. This meant that he had to take a detour to find Wen Xue and the others.","Meanwhile, the experts of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were indeed observing the phenomenon.","“That moving phenomenon is probably related to Chu Feng, but what’s the deal with the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s phenomenon? It doesn’t seem to be from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.”","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists speculated about the situation.","In contrast, the Netherworld Sect wasn’t too concerned about the ongoing phenomena. They were still overwhelmed by their anger from Chu Feng’s escape.","Shortly after, the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s phenomenon faded.","But a more blinding light shone from the Immortal Sea Galaxy right after. This time, the phenomenon shocked not just the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists but the Netherworld Sect’s experts as well.","It was the same phenomenon, but it enveloped the entire Immortal Sea Galaxy this time!","“Three phenomena?” Even Jie Tianran couldn’t remain calm."]},{"number":6561,"title":"Chapter 6561: Chapter 6559: The Legendary Immortal Sea?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6559: The Legendary Immortal Sea?","The consecutive phenomena caught the attention of powerhouses across the world of cultivation. Even powerful entities that had been living in seclusion were paying attention to the situation in the Immortal Sea Galaxy.","As shocking as the moving white light and the red lotus were, they looked like mere appetizers compared to the humongous phenomenon shrouding the Immortal Sea Galaxy. In fact, it went even further than that.","The Immortal Sea Galaxy was shaped like a flowing river, but this phenomenon was like an ocean that devoured the entire river. One could see it clearly with bare eyes without relying on any special means.","Those witnessing this sight were shocked to their core. The sounds of raging waves could be heard even across space. It felt like a true ocean had suddenly appeared in the middle of space, just that it enveloped not a single realm but an entire galaxy.","“This phenomenon is ridiculously huge. Chu Feng, it has to be Little Fishy, right?” Eggy asked.","Little Fishy had induced phenomena before, but it had never been at this scale.","“It’s hard to say, but I hope it’s Little Fishy,” Chu Feng replied.","Meanwhile, the experts inside the formation realm above the Undying Starfield were observing the phenomenon.","“The Immortal Sea Fish Clan,” Jie Tianran suddenly blurted out with a frown.","“Mansion Master, is that phenomenon induced by the Immortal Sea Fish Clan? Could the rumors be true?” Baili Xukong and the other experts of the Netherworld Sect turned to Jie Tianran.","They had heard rumors about the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.","There had been intense fighting in the earlier years of the present era to become the galaxy overlords. Only the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had firmly secured its position as the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s overlord right from the start.","It was said that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had been around since the Ancient Era, but they were just a little-known monstrous beast clan back then. Naturally, they also weren’t known as the Immortal Sea Fish Clan back then.","In the earlier years of the present era, they encountered a mystical golden ocean in the Immortal Sea Galaxy. The golden ocean was said to be enchanting, almost like something that had fallen from the immortal realm. It was an invaluable cultivation ground.","The golden ocean was named the Immortal Sea.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan cultivated in the Immortal Sea until its energy was depleted and its water ran dry. In exchange, they obtained tremendous power. Out of gratitude for this fortuitous encounter, they designated the Immortal Sea as their ancestral ground and sealed it off.","They even renamed themselves as the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.","Since then, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan began their long rule over the Immortal Sea Galaxy. Generations of experts emerged from their ranks and left their marks on history.","While they had never dominated the world of cultivation, they had also never been weak before.","This rumor was the reason most people held great expectations for the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land. There had been plenty of attempts to sneak in—most failed and lost their lives, but some succeeded.","However, what they witnessed was disappointing.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land was a huge pit that stretched to the horizon; there was not the slightest energy left in it.","Back to the present, the Netherworld Sect’s experts turned to Jie Tianran to seek his opinion. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was one of the powers that had successfully infiltrated the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land.","“It is the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. One of their clansmen must have awakened their bloodline,” Jie Tianran said.","“A bloodline awakening induced such a phenomenon? It must be Xianhai Shaoyu or Xianhai Yu’er,” a Netherworld Sectmember said worriedly.","The Netherworld Sect had already put Chu Feng onto their kill list, and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan was known to be on good terms with Chu Feng. It would be extremely disadvantageous to them if the Immortal Sea Fish Clan were to make a comeback.","Jie Tianran ordered six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists to head into the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land to investigate the situation.","“Xiahou Jue, you go as well,” Baili Xukong ordered.","He had only dispatched one person, but that person was a Netherworld Marshal and a rank four Heavenly God.","The six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists turned to look at Jie Tianran.","“It’ll be safer for you to have a Netherworld Sect’s expert tag along, but maintain a low profile and don’t let anyone discover you,” Jie Tianran ordered.","Xiahou Jue and the six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists understood that Jie Tianran wanted to keep this operation a secret. Upon receiving their orders, they immediately set off.","Some time later, the suppression talisman paper powered by the sacred item finally depleted its energy. The suppression power faded, and the Undying Starfield reverted to normal.","Of course, there was no way Jie Tianran would reveal that the suppression talisman paper had run out of power. He claimed credit for the unraveling of the suppression power instead.","“That wretched Chu Feng! Fortunately, we have the Mansion Master here!”","Oblivious to the truth, the Netherworld Sect’s experts expressed their gratitude to Jie Tianran.","“I’m ashamed. I have purged Chu Feng’s destruction formation from the sacred item, but his formation has still inflicted considerable damage to it. I’ll have to repair it first, and this means that I won’t be able to awaken its power any time soon. Please be mentally prepared.","“For the time being, I’ll leave a formation to continue the repairs. Once the sacred item is fully repaired, I’ll awaken it. However, this ordeal has cost our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion quite a lot of treasures, and this is a cost that we cannot bear,” Jie Tianran said.","Baili Xukong replied, “Rest assured, Mansion Master. Since our Netherworld Sect has requested your help, we will not take advantage of you. We might not be able to return to you the treasures you have depleted, but we’ll offer you something of equivalent value.”","No one refuted Baili Xukong’s declaration. They already knew that their Netherworld Sect would have to foot the bill from the moment Jie Tianran pulled out his precious talisman papers.","Jie Tianran didn’t stand on ceremony. He took out a scroll and tossed it over to Baili Xukong.","Baili Xukong unfurled the scroll. Cang Li and the others glanced over. Despite being mentally prepared, they still felt a tight clench in their hearts. The list was filled with extraordinary items. This would be a huge strain on them, even with the Netherworld Sect’s massive wealth.","“You have seen for yourself. The talisman papers I have thrown into the formation were all invaluable treasures, and I’ll require even more precious talisman papers to repair the sacred item,” Jie Tianran explained.","“Rest assured, Mansion Master. We’ll quickly gather the items on this list.”","Baili Xukong and the others had no choice but to take on the responsibility even though their hearts were bleeding. Nothing was more important to them than the awakening of their sacred item.","However, this only further fanned their hatred for Chu Feng. He was the cause of this."]},{"number":6562,"title":"Chapter 6562: Chapter 6560: I’m Here For Your Lover","paragraphs":["Chapter 6560: I’m Here For Your Lover","Even the most amazing phenomenon eventually faded.","Chu Feng noticed that Eggy had gone silent. He projected his consciousness into his World Spirit Space and saw that she had resumed cultivation.","Ever since receiving her benefit from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, she had been cultivating whenever she had time. This made Chu Feng more curious about what benefit she had received.","He had known her for a long time now, but aside from special circumstances, this was the first time she was so diligent with her cultivation.","...","Chu Feng soon arrived at the agreed location with Wen Xue and the others.","Bai Yunqing had constructed a hidden space in the vicinity, but Chu Feng could enter without any impediment. When he entered, he saw that Bai Yunqing had already prepared a recovery formation and was treating Li Wu.","Wen Xue was standing in the distance, looking bored. She was the first to notice Chu Feng.","“You’re back, junior.” Wen Xue excitedly ran up to Chu Feng.","Her exclamation caught Li Wu and Bai Yunqing’s attention.","“Big brother!” Bai Yunqing was overjoyed to see Chu Feng.","Li Wu rushed out of the recovery formation and knelt to Chu Feng.","“What are you doing, sister-in-law?” Chu Feng hurriedly pulled her up to her feet.","Li Wu was in a terrible state. She had paid a hefty price channeling her curse energy to help Chu Feng’s formation permeate the sacred item. Even so, she refused to get up and instead began to tear up.","“I know the phenomenon was induced by Feng Ling. Chu Feng, no words can repay the debt I owe you, but please accept my kowtow.”","Li Wu kowtowed to Chu Feng. Even though she hadn’t met Feng Ling yet, she could already tell from the earlier phenomenon that he had successfully rescued Feng Ling.","From this, Chu Feng could tell how deep their sisterly bond was, so he didn’t stop her. Instead, he reached into his formation realm and pulled Feng Ling out.","Li Wu rushed forward to embrace Feng Ling.","Feng Ling was still unconscious, but it was evident from her state that she had made a full recovery and even obtained a fortuitous encounter from that.","“Feng Ling had been tortured by the Netherworld Sectmembers. I have helped her recover, but it’ll take some time before she regains consciousness. Don’t worry, she should be all right now,” Chu Feng replied.","“Who did it?” Killing intent flared from Li Wu.","“His name is Zhao Feng. He’s dead. I killed him,” Chu Feng replied.","Li Wu’s killing intent dissipated, but it was replaced with shame. She knew that it would have been no easy task for Chu Feng to rescue Feng Ling and avenge her at the same time.","Li Wu and Bai Yunqing had been observing the Undying Starfield; they had witnessed the terrifying sight of a humongous scroll sealing off the Undying Starfield, as well as the Great Monster Slayer Emperor slashing through the sealing formation.","It must have been a difficult battle.","“Feng Ling and I will repay this favor,” Li Wu said.","“All right.” Chu Feng nodded.","He knew that Li Wu wasn’t the type to speak empty words; her words carried her conviction. Turning down her offer would only make her feel conscience-stricken.","“Big brother, I saw a huge soul entity tearing through the sealing formation that enveloped the Undying Starfield. Is that your doing?” Bai Yunqing asked with glowing eyes.","They had sensed the intense pressure from the soul entity, but they couldn’t tell who that soul entity was.","“It was the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s soul entity,” Chu Feng replied.","“Big brother, have you obtained his legacy?” Bai Yunqing asked.","Chu Feng had previously told Wen Xue about the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s tomb. By now, the whole group knew about Chu Feng’s motive for sneaking into the Undying Starfield.","“Yes.” Chu Feng nodded.","“That’s great! The journey was fraught with danger, but at least everything ended well,” Bai Yunqing replied.","“Junior Chu Feng, what are your plans? Do you intend to head to the Immortal Sea Galaxy?” Wen Xue asked.","They had witnessed the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s phenomenon, and they suspected that the phenomenon was related to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. Considering how much Chu Feng cared about his friends, he would want to investigate the situation.","“Yes, I’m intending to go take a look,” Chu Feng replied.","“I won’t be accompanying you,” Wen Xue said.","“Senior, what is your plan?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’ll first return to the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect to visit my master before heading into the Ninth Galaxy. I was thinking of inviting you to come with me, but it looks like you’ll be staying here a while more.”","“I’ll see you in the Ninth Galaxy, senior.”","“Sure thing. I’ll first head over and secure a foothold so that you’ll have backing when you finally come over.” Wen Xue smiled.","“Deal,” Chu Feng replied with a chuckle.","Wen Xue bade the group farewell and left.","“Big brother Chu Feng, Miss Li Wu is still in a dangerous condition, so I’ll help her recuperate first. I’ll look for you once her condition has stabilized,” Bai Yunqing said.","“Miss Li Wu’s safety takes precedence. Furthermore, Feng Ling remains unconscious even though she has induced a phenomenon. You might need to help her regain consciousness. For now, your job is to take care of them. You can look for me once they are faring better.”","Chu Feng handed a location talisman to Bai Yunqing. Through it, Bai Yunqing would be able to locate Chu Feng as long as he was within a set radius of the latter.","Following that, Chu Feng took his leave and made his way to the Immortal Sea Galaxy. He intended to first look for Zi Ling before checking out the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.","Meanwhile, Bai Yunqing stayed behind and continued treating Li Wu.","Shortly after Chu Feng left, Bai Yunqing sensed something from Chu Feng’s location talisman and hurriedly took it out. He was worried that something had happened to Chu Feng.","Upon careful examination, he noticed that Chu Feng had embedded something inside the location talisman. It contained a storage space. He opened the storage space and found that it was filled with valuable herbs.","Li Wu was stunned.","Bai Yunqing laughed. “These are invaluable natural oddities that are all beneficial to Miss Li Wu’s condition. Big brother must be worried that you won’t accept them, so he hid them in the location talisman.”","“Your big brother is a meticulous man. You should learn more from him,” Li Wu said.","“Of course. That’s the man who granted me a new lease of life. He’s my role model.” Bai Yunqing smiled.","He fused the herbs into the recovery formation, and the recovery formation’s potency shot up. That gave him more confidence in treating Li Wu. He was about to channel the formation when a person suddenly walked in.","“Miss Wen Xue?”","Bai Yunqing and Li Wu were startled.","“Are you here to look for my big brother? He has already left for the Immortal Sea Galaxy.”","Wen Xue smiled. “No, I’m here for your lover.”"]},{"number":6563,"title":"Chapter 6563: Chapter 6561: The Conflicted Wen Xue","paragraphs":["Chapter 6561: The Conflicted Wen Xue","“Miss Wen Xue, do you... need something from Miss Li Wu?” Bai Yunqing asked as he glanced at the figure behind Wen Xue—Wuma Hanshuang.","“What do you want?” Li Wu coldly asked.","“I’ll trade two lives for Miss Li Wu’s life. How does that sound?” Wen Xue asked.","Li Wu’s eyes immediately turned cold. She could tell right away that Wen Xue was up to something terrible.","Bai Yunqing remained unguarded toward Wen Xue because the latter was Chu Feng’s friend.","Before Bai Yunqing could finish his words, Wen Xue’s left hand shot for Bai Yunqing’s neck.","Without any hesitation, Li Wu thrust her palm toward Wen Xue, unleashing a powerful wave of black aura. This was not just a simple execution of martial skill, for it harnessed curse energy.","But the gush of curse energy visibly diminished as it approached Wen Xue. Eventually, it shrunk into a weak bundle of black aura and landed in Wen Xue’s right palm.","“Mmm, what a pure taste. I love it.” Wen Xue leaned in to sniff the black aura on her palm before revealing a satisfied look.","Li Wu instinctively pulled Feng Ling behind her while looking at Bai Yunqing with worried eyes. However, she didn’t continue her attack, for it had become apparent that Wen Xue was not only stronger than her but Wuma Hanshuang as well.","Wen Xue had been hiding her true strength all along.","“Who are you?” Bai Yunqing endured the pain and questioned.","“Who am I? I am Wen Xue,” Wen Xue smiled.","Bai Yunqing was dazed. His mind had gone blank. He thought the other party had impersonated Wen Xue, but it seemed unnecessary for her to do so, considering how strong she was. In other words, she was most likely Wen Xue.","“Miss Wen Xue, why are you doing this to us?” Bai Yunqing asked.","Despite being held hostage, Bai Yunqing’s tone became softer after confirming that Wen Xue was not an impostor.","“Are you dumb? She’s a natural oddity as well! She wants my power! The two lives she mentioned refer to you and Feng Ling. She’s using you and Feng Ling to threaten me!” Li Wu exclaimed.","“Indeed. Miss Li Wu is sharp-witted,” Wen Xue said with a grin.","“This can’t be true. Miss Wen Xue, you’re just joking with us, right? Aren’t you my big brother’s friend? Weren’t you the one who brought us here?” Bai Yunqing asked.","“That’s why I needed Chu Feng to ascertain your safety before making a move. Otherwise, he’ll suspect that I’m behind your deaths.”","Boom!","A surge of teleportation energy suddenly enveloped Bai Yunqing, allowing him to escape from Wen Xue’s clutches. It was Bai Yunqing’s protection treasure.","However, it only teleported him not too far away from where Wen Xue was.","“I’ve already sealed off the area. You can’t escape even with a teleportation formation,” Wen Xue pointed out.","Bai Yunqing kneeled to Wen Xue and said, “Miss Wen Xue, kill me if you want to, but please spare Miss Li Wu. I know that my words mean nothing to you, but won’t you at least do it on my big brother Chu Feng’s account?”","Bai Yunqing knew that neither he nor Li Wu was a match for Wen Xue, so he resorted to begging her. His attitude was so earnest that it seemed like he truly intended to trade his life for Li Wu’s.","Wen Xue looked at Bai Yunqing with hesitant eyes. A moment later, she laughed.","She turned to Li Wu and said, “Miss Li Wu, Bai Yunqing might be a blockhead, but he’s worth entrusting your life to. May we meet again. No, it’ll be better if we never meet again.”","With that, Wen Xue left with the puppet Wuma Hanshuang.","“Miss Wen Xue? Miss Wen Xue?” Bai Yunqing instinctively followed Wen Xue out, only to find that she had left. He stood still on the spot, his mind in a complete mess. He struggled to make sense of the situation.","Soon, Li Wu flew out of the formation realm.","“Was Miss Wen Xue testing me to see if I’d be willing to lay down my life for you?” Bai Yunqing asked Li Wu.","“What does she stand to gain from that?” Li Wu asked.","“Maybe she’s a warm-hearted person?”","Li Wu rolled her eyes. She looked at Bai Yunqing as if he were an utter fool. “You still trust her even though she had her hand around your neck? You even asked if she was joking.”","“I don’t trust her. I trust my big brother. My big brother is a good judge of character. I trust his friends,” Bai Yunqing replied.","“Perhaps we should thank Chu Feng for this,” Li Wu said.","“Ah?” Bai Yunqing still hadn’t figured out the situation.","“I was observing her closely. Her killing intent didn’t waver in the slightest when you kneeled and begged her. She only changed her mind when you mentioned Chu Feng.”","“You’re saying that she really coveted your energy?”","“Yes, and I think she only stopped because of Chu Feng. She knows that you’re an important friend to Chu Feng and that he would investigate your death. There is a good chance that he might uncover her as the culprit. Or maybe she feels that Chu Feng entrusted us to her because he trusts her, and she doesn’t want to let down his trust. Either way, she changed her mind because of Chu Feng,” Li Wu said.","“Let’s hurry up and leave then! It’ll be terrible if she changes her mind and returns,” Bai Yunqing exclaimed. He quickly stowed away the formation realm and fled with Li Wu.","Little did he know that a gaze was tracking them. It was Wen Xue.","She hadn’t completely left the area. There was a conflicted look on her face, and it only deepened as she watched them become smaller in her gaze. It eventually reached a point where her little face warped.","Pah!","Wen Xue slapped herself.","“What are you doing? What are you doing! They are just Chu Feng’s friends! There is no reason to let such top-quality curse energy go. Feng Ling has quite the amazing bloodline as well. It’s unlikely that I’ll find a natural oddity with such a bloodline even in the Ninth Galaxy.","“Wen Xue, are you a fool? Why are you hesitating? When did you become so wishy-washy? It’s one thing to go easy on Chu Feng, but you’re going easy on his friends, too. You’re a disappointment!","“Argh!!!!”","Wen Xue stomped her feet while ranting erratically like a lunatic. Despite being so conflicted that she was on the verge of a rampage, she didn’t pursue them."]},{"number":6564,"title":"Chapter 6564: Chapter 6562: Zi Ling’s Gains","paragraphs":["Chapter 6562: Zi Ling’s Gains","A moment later, Wen Xue calmed down. “Choices weigh heavier than hard work in life. I believe that I have made the right choice.”","Having come to a self-compromise, she turned to Wuma Hanshuang and formed a hand seal.","The statue-like Wuma Hanshuang’s eyes suddenly regained some spirit. She was momentarily dazed, but as soon as her eyes fell on Wen Xue, intense killing intent burst forth from her.","But before she could make a move, the space around her shattered.","It was the result of overwhelming oppressive might, but it was not from her. It was Wen Xue.","“Master, you aren’t my match,” Wen Xue remarked.","“What kind of monster are you? What did you do to me?” Wuma Hanshuang roared with a mixture of fear and trepidation in her eyes.","“I merely used your body to handle some stuff. The job is done, so I decided to return your freedom. I am someone who knows gratitude, after all. You were using me as well, but I can tell whether you earnestly cared for me or not. That’s why I’ll allow you to leave, master.","“However, I’ll advise you against returning to the Netherworld Sect. You are now viewed as a traitor there,” Wen Xue said before vanishing into thin air.","Wuma Hanshuang stood on the spot with a complicated expression.","She knew something must have happened, but she didn’t have the slightest memory of what happened after she was controlled by Wen Xue. She first inspected her dantian. She confirmed that the gu Wen Xue had previously placed in there was gone.","She should be truly free now.","After some thought, she still decided to make her way toward the Undying Starfield.","...","Traversing through the Nine Realms Secret Domain on Qin Jiu’s boat, it didn’t take long for Chu Feng to arrive at the hideout of the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader. He was about to step in when the guild leader appeared in front of him.","“You’re finally back,” the guild leader remarked.","“I wasn’t gone for a long time,” Chu Feng pointed out with a smile.","“That might be true, but many things have happened in the meantime. Why do I see your shadow in every incident?”","“I did go to some places.”","Chu Feng scratched his head awkwardly. He could tell that the guild leader was accusing him of causing trouble everywhere","“Haaa!”","The guild leader sighed. Chu Feng was the future of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, so how could she not worry about him? She knew that a cultivator’s path was bound to be fraught with danger, but Chu Feng’s path seemed exceptionally precarious. Danger seemed to follow him wherever he went.","“It’s good that you’re fine. I know why you returned. Come with me,” the guild leader said as she led Chu Feng deeper into the realm.","Some time later, they arrived before a stone tower.","“It looks like Zi Ling was indeed behind that phenomenon,” Eggy said in delight.","Chu Feng smiled as well.","Zi Ling was undergoing closed-door training in the stone tower, and the stone tower was currently enveloped by a blood-red lotus. The blood-red lotus was small, but it emanated a formidable aura. It was the same lotus from the phenomenon that enveloped this starfield.","Chances were that Zi Ling had reaped huge rewards from her closed-door training.","“You must have returned because you saw Zi Ling’s phenomenon,” the guild leader stated.","“That’s right.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Zi Ling carries a huge fortuitous encounter. Her closed-door training this time is very different from before. I sensed her aura right before the phenomenon appeared. Do you know what her cultivation was then?”","“What is it?”","“I know you’re close with Zi Ling, but you should be mentally prepared. This completely defies common sense. Don’t feel disheartened by her progress, lest it hinder your cultivation.”","“Elder, hurry up and tell me.”","“Rank nine True God.”","“She grew so fast?”","Chu Feng was both surprised and delighted by the revelation. Zi Ling had been at pinnacle Half-God level prior to her closed-door training, and she was aiming to reach True God level. Who could have thought that she would make such huge progress within a short span?","She hadn’t even emerged from her closed-door training, but she was already at rank nine True God level!","Chu Feng worried that Zi Ling’s foundation would be unstable as a result of her swift progress.","“Shocking, isn’t it? I have never seen anything like this. Chu Feng, you shouldn’t feel burdened by her progress. With your talent, it’s only a matter of time before you reach rank nine True God level,” the guild leader said. She was worried that this would affect Chu Feng’s state of mind.","“What are you saying, elder? I’m just worried that Zi Ling’s swift progress will destabilize her foundation,” Chu Feng replied.","He had also reached rank nine True God level, but he had progressed a step at a time through different fortuitous encountersencounters, so his foundation was still sturdy. Of course, there were fortuitous encounters that raised one’s cultivation without affecting one’s foundation, but he wouldn’t know whether that was the case for Zi Ling until he finally met her.","Till then, he was bound to be worried.","“I see. You don’t need to worry about her. Her aura was extremely stable when I sensed her rank nine True God level cultivation,” the guild leader replied.","That put Chu Feng’s heart at ease.","“Chu Feng, Zi Ling’s fortuitous encounter is related to the tower she obtained from your father, right?” Eggy asked out of curiosity.","“It should be.”","Chu Feng’s father had taken Zi Ling as his disciple and gifted her the blood-red ancient tower. The blood-red ancient tower consisted of three levels, and there was a door on each level. The blood-red ancient tower was likely the reason behind Zi Ling’s growth spurt.","However, the blood-red tower came with a massive downside. She had to open all three doors within a time limit, or else she would suffer a backlash from it.","The blood-red lotus shrouding the stone tower was identical to that of the phenomenon, but unlike the phenomenon, it was not a simple manifestation but a pure accumulation of power. This power emanated a similar aura to the woman he had once conversed with on the first level of the blood-red ancient tower.","Zi Ling must have gained the acknowledgment of that woman. That was why her cultivation surged to rank nine True God level, and chances were that she would reach rank one Heavenly God before she emerged from her closed-door training.","If this was the reward from unlocking the first level, he couldn’t imagine what the rewards for the second level and the third level would be.","The blood-red ancient tower was more terrifying than Chu Feng had expected.","“Don’t worry too much. Your father might have left you in the lurch, but he’s still quite reliable when it comes to treasures and powers. He is the god of tomb raiding, after all,” Eggy said.","“Um...” Chu Feng agreed that his father was an unfathomable individual, but Eggy’s remark felt a little off."]},{"number":6565,"title":"Chapter 6565: Chapter 6563: Heading to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Ancestral Land","paragraphs":["Chapter 6563: Heading to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Ancestral Land","“Elder, are you able to gauge how potent the power shrouding the stone tower is?” Chu Feng asked the guild leader.","His perception told him that the stone tower couldn’t be moved, but this place was not necessarily safe anymore after the phenomenon. He still remembered how a lunatic had once found this place[1].","If Jie Tianran sent his underlings to investigate the phenomenon, there was a good chance they could find this place.","Fortunately, the manifested blood-red lotus was protecting the stone tower. The only question left in his mind was whether the blood-red lotus was strong enough to ensure Zi Ling’s safety.","“As expected of a prodigy. You noticed that the blood-red lotus wields defensive capabilities as well. I only realized it when I came into contact with it. Well, I’m unable to gauge how potent the power is, but... Maybe you should take a look yourself,” the guild leader said.","The guild leader whipped out her God Armament and unleashed her aura as a rank one Heavenly God level cultivator. She channeled her martial power and executed a God Taboo Martial Skill at the stone tower where Zi Ling was undergoing closed-door training.","But the blood-red lotus devoured the attack whole.","“Rank one Heavenly Gods can’t get close at all. I suspect rank three Heavenly Gods won’t be able to faze it,” the guild leader said.","“In my view, even rank five Heavenly Gods won’t be able to faze it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Rank five Heavenly Gods?”","The guild leader narrowed her eyes. The first thought that came to her mind was who had reached such a level, since she had never encountered a rank five Heavenly God before. She turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Have you met a rank five Heavenly God before?”","“I have. The present Netherworld Sect has rank five Heavenly Gods,” Chu Feng replied.","“I knew it. You wouldn’t have been able to make this judgment otherwise. Were you involved with the situation over at the Undying Starfield?” the guild leader asked in astonishment. She had guessed as much, but it still shook her to have her deduction confirmed.","“Yes.” Chu Feng told the guild leader about what happened.","The guild leader was silent for a long while. “You are a brazen one. You had the guts to venture into a place like that. But at least you obtained the Great Monstrous Slayer Emperor’s legacy, so your trip wasn’t in vain.”","A second later, her pupils suddenly widened. “Hold on. You mentioned that you have reached rank nine True God level as well?”","“Indeed.” Chu Feng nodded. He revealed his aura as a rank nine True God level cultivator.","“No, this... You two... What the hell! Are you still juniors? You have only spent decades cultivating, and advancing in True God level should have been much harder than in Half-God level. How are you two making breakthroughs so easily? Do you know how long I spent to reach rank nine True God level? I was a prodigy as well!","“Ugh, this is so frustrating. At least this is good news for us,” the guild leader remarked with a tinge of shock and delight.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect had displayed overwhelming strength. Under normal circumstances, the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect wouldn’t stand a chance against these powers.","But Chu Feng and Zi Ling’s swift growth brought hope to them.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect might be beyond their means right now, but with enough time, they would be able to catch up with and even surpass them.","At this point, the guild leader suddenly remembered another matter and remarked, “I wonder which of the two prodigies of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan has awakened their bloodline, inducing a phenomenon even larger than Zi Ling’s.”","“Elder, are you sure that is a phenomenon from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan? Why does it look different from the phenomena they have previously induced?” Chu Feng asked.","“It looks like you lack understanding about the Immortal Sea Fish Clan despite your close ties with them,” the guild leader said with a smile.","She shared the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s origin story with Chu Feng.","Only then did Chu Feng learn that the phenomenon that had enveloped the Immortal Sea Galaxy was the legendary Immortal Sea. It was for that reason the guild leader was certain someone from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had awakened their bloodline.","“Elder, do you know where the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land is?”","Chu Feng thought he should check out the situation at Little Fishy’s side since Zi Ling was fine for the time being.","“I do. Are you planning to head there?” the guild leader asked.","“That’s my plan,” Chu Feng replied.","“Let’s head there together.”","“Elder, I can head there myself.”","“I’m not tagging along for your sake. There’s an unawakened sentient natural oddity in the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land. The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s clan chief promised it to me after I did him a favor. That natural oddity is very beneficial to older cultivators like me, but it has to flower first before I can use it for my cultivation.","“Actually, I didn’t have high hopes for it. The natural oddity thrives off the Immortal Sea, but it has been many years since the Immortal Sea dried up. The natural oddity has stopped growing altogether. It’s not entirely impossible for the natural oddity to flower, but the chances are slim.","“But things are different now that an Immortalan Sea Fish Clansman has awakened their bloodline. My guess is that there is a change in the Immortal Sea. I’m hoping that the change has led to the flowering of my natural oddity. In any case, I’m just trying my luck,” the guild leader said.","“All right, elder. Let’s head there together.”","But Chu Feng didn’t make a move right away. Instead, he began constructing a formation.","He didn’t think a rank five Heavenly God could faze the stone tower, but he wasn’t about to let his guard down, since Zi Ling’s safety was at stake. So, he constructed two formations in the vicinity. The first formation concealed the stone tower, whereas the second formation detected intruders.","As long as Chu Feng was still in the Immortal Sea Galaxy, he would be able to sense the intruder.","Only after he completed the formation did he and the guild leader depart for the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land.","What Chu Feng didn’t know was that Jie Tianran was not concerned about Zi Ling’s phenomenon and didn’t dispatch anyone to investigate it. Instead, he had dispatched people to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land.","1. Chapter 6113. A ‘madwoman’ who snubs the galaxy overlords came to this realm after making a breakthrough to Heavenly God level to attack the guild leader for having once evicted her from the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s premises. The madwoman later backed down upon learning that Chu Feng was Chu Xuanyuan’s son ☜"]},{"number":6566,"title":"Chapter 6566: Chapter 6564: Meeting Acquaintances","paragraphs":["Chapter 6564: Meeting Acquaintances","Chu Feng and the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader boarded Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat, and it didn’t take them long to arrive at the perimeter of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land.","“Something is amiss,” the guild leader suddenly said with a frown.","“Elder, there should have been a formation here, right?” Chu Feng asked.","He could tell that there should have been a formation around the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land, but the formation had disappeared. In fact, he wouldn’t have known better if he hadn’t used Heaven’s Eyes.","“Of course. This is the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land, after all!","“The natural energies here are extremely thin, perhaps due to the Immortal Sea, so the environment is not suited for cultivation. That’s why there are hardly any cultivators in this realm, and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan didn’t station their headquarters here.","“Even so, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan still stations many experts here. In fact, its headquarters is located at a nearby realm,” the guild leader said, revealing the high regard the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had for its ancestral land.","“I don’t think the formation was destroyed. It feels like something has absorbed it instead,” Chu Feng said.","“That’s bizarre.” The guild leader frowned.","“Indeed. I gave Yu’er and Brother Shaoyu a location talisman paper each before we parted ways, but I can’t sense their location talisman papers at all. Have they already left this place?” Chu Feng murmured.","“Probably. Chu Feng, you don’t have worry too much about them. They will be fine. The phenomenon must be something good. They probably left this place because they knew that the phenomenon would draw the attention of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” the guild leader said.","“You’re right.” Chu Feng nodded.","They continued traveling while conversing.","They were still far from their destination, but they could already spot a boundless hole in their vision. That hole was where the Immortal Sea used to exist. It was rumored that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan used to cultivate there till they depleted all its energy, causing the sea to dry up.","“Indeed, something has changed,” the guild leader exclaimed in astonishment.","She had been to the Immortal Sea before, and back then, there was nothing noteworthy here except for the size of the hole. The Immortal Sea was still dry now, but a concentrated, sacred aura was being emanated somewhere from the boundless hole.","“Chu Feng, there’s hope! My natural oddity might just blossom under such conditions,” the guild leader told Chu Feng excitedly.","“Elder, do you know where the natural oddity is?” Chu Feng asked.","He was planning to first find the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, but he couldn’t find any signs of them despite already being in the vicinity of their ancestral land. Furthermore, there was no response from Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s location talismans.","This led him to think that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had already left this area.","He was perplexed, since he didn’t think that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan would leave their ancestral land unguarded. Even if their protective formation had been absorbed for whatever reason, they should have at least left some means or stationed some guards behind.","“It’s a bit far away. It’s on the opposite side,” the guild leader said.","The Immortal Sea was massive, but they were riding on Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat. It was capable of moving at speeds surpassing that of ordinary teleportation formation. Thanks to that, it didn’t take them long to arrive at the opposite end of the Immortal Sea.","Along the way, they didn’t see any signs of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. However, Chu Feng did sense a peculiar aura.","“Do you sense it too, Chu Feng?” The guild leader grew increasingly excited.","“Elder, the aura wasn’t this concentrated before, right?” Chu Feng asked. He deduced that the aura was coming from the guild leader’s natural oddity.","“Of course not. That’s why I think it’s hopeful. This trip is not in vain!”","The guild leader was so excited that she beamed a wide grin. It contrasted starkly with her usual solemn demeanor. This showed how much she wanted to advance her cultivation.","But as they approached the aura, their eyes began to widen. Their gazes peered across space to lock onto the natural oddity.","The natural oddity resembled an immortal spirit grass, but it was much larger than any spirit grass, standing at over thirty meters in height like a towering tree. It emanated waves of light, and a massive flower had blossomed on its crown.","It was mature.","But a woman stood beneath the natural oddity.","She had white hair and exquisite features, but her complexion was as pale as a ghost. In particular, her eyes didn’t seem to belong to a human. Her disposition felt so eerie that not even her beauty could compensate for it.","She felt like a menace that ought to be avoided at all costs.","This woman was famously unreasonable and vicious in the world of cultivation, which was why she became known as a lunatic. Those who had heard of her would flee from her at first sight, fearing for their lives. Even galaxy overlords were hesitant to cross her.","But this lunatic was acquainted withwith Chu Feng’s father, and it seemed like there was quite a history between them.","She had a grudge with the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader, but she spared the latter and backed off on Chu Feng’s account.","Later, when Chu Feng was competing with Baili Zilin in the Luck Saint Realm, that lunatic rushed to the scene to back him up. It was due to her presence that the Netherworld Sect’s Jimo Qianzhou dared not make a reckless move on Chu Feng.","As Chu Feng and the guild leader approached, the lunatic also noticed them and looked over with murderous eyes. However, when she noticed Chu Feng, her killing intent dissipated right away.","Soon, the bamboo boat arrived before the natural oddity. The guild leader leaped off the bamboo boat and rushed to the natural oddity.","“What are you doing here?” the guild leader asked grimly.","“None of your business,” the lunatic scoffed. Her tone was so sharp that it felt like she wouldn’t hesitate to go on a massacre if the guild leader were to annoy her.","“Elder, it has been a while.” Chu Feng stepped forward and greeted the lunatic.","“Are you here because of the phenomenon too?” the lunatic asked. Her expression remained impassive, but her tone was conspicuously gentler."]},{"number":6567,"title":"Chapter 6567: Chapter 6565: A God’s True Body?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6565: A God’s True Body?","Before Chu Feng could reply, the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader pointed at the natural oddity and said, “We came for this thing.”","She had a feeling the lunatic had come for the natural oddity, so she was proclaiming her ownership of it first.","“First come, first served,” the lunatic said.","“It belongs to me,” the guild leader replied with a displeased frown. Just my luck. That lunatic is here to take my natural oddity.","“I don’t see your name on it,” the lunatic pointed out.","“You want to fight?”","Anxious, the guild leader unleashed her rank one Heavenly God level cultivator aura.","The lunatic glared at the guild leader while unleashing her oppressive might as well. She, too, was ready for a fight.","“Elder, we have indeed come for the natural oddity, and the natural oddity already has an owner,” Chu Feng hurriedly interjected to defuse the situation.","All of a sudden, the trio turned their gazes in the same direction while activating treasures that reinforced their observation prowess. They vaguely heard voices, but those voices didn’t seem to be coming from this realm.","It sounded like a summons from afar.","Their gazes, reinforced with treasures, peered across vast space toward God’s Era. There was a change in God’s Era, and this time, it was larger than before.","God’s Era’s silhouette was humongous and majestic, but it had always been blurry, resembling a mix between a human and a beast. But at this very moment, the silhouette had started peeling off like a layer of dirt, revealing its true appearance.","It was an entity dressed in an imposing armor. It looked vaguely humanoid, but the full body armor made it impossible to tell whether it was a human or a beast.","Of the armor, the helmet particularly stood out. It resembled a crown.","On the whole, the entity didn’t feel like a veteran general on the battlefield but a conqueror who had united the world with its sheer strength.","At the same time, the three doors that had previously manifested near God’s Era, which boasted sizes comparable to starfields, grew increasingly distinct.","“God’s Era has revealed its true form. Is it going to open for good?” the guild leader remarked.","The lunatic appeared calm, but her eyes divulged her astonishment.","This was an unprecedented phenomenon in the world of cultivation, and the aura it emanated left cultivators feeling expectant, no matter who or where they were.","“Chu Feng, that entity feels overwhelmingly powerful despite being a mere silhouette. It feels almost like a god who towers over all beings, but it feels different from what I envisioned gods to be,” Eggy said.","“What do you envision gods to be?” Chu Feng asked.","“Someone covered in a halo that obscures his face, but actually, he is just an extremely old person who has lived through the ages.”","“Even if gods exist, they are still mortal at their core, just that they have obtained powers far surpassing everyone else. It’s similar to how Upper Realms’ cultivators are as good as gods to Lower Realms’ cultivators, but in truth, they are mortals as well,” Eggy revealed her thought.","“My thoughts exactly,” Chu Feng replied.","“Look, Chu Feng! That fellow is moving!” Eggy exclaimed.","Chu Feng’s gaze had never drifted away from God’s Era. He watched as the humongous silhouette grabbed those three doors with its left hand and pulled them open with its right hand. Three bundles of light emerged from the doors.","These three light bundles started small, but they enlarged as power converged in the silhouette’s right hand. They grew to a size comparable to the three doors, resembling behemoths that could envelop an entire starfield.","Even from a far distance away, Chu Feng could sense their extraordinary nature. The same went for any cultivator who had reached a certain level of accomplishment.","“Chu Feng, what’s the light bundle in that silhouette’s right hand? Could it be God’s Era’s final power?” the guild leader asked.","The lunatic’s ears twitched upon hearing that question. She was also listening in.","They both knew about Chu Feng’s extraordinary observation prowess. He could discern things at a far deeper level.","“Elder, I can’t discern anything special from the silhouette for now, but I personally don’t think that is God’s Era’s final power,” Chu Feng replied.","“Oh? What could that be then? It’s my first time witnessing such a sight. It feels as if even the slightest move from that humongous silhouette can reshape the entire world of cultivation. I feel nervous just looking at it,” the guild leader said.","Meanwhile, everyone who possessed observation means was watching God’s Era’s transformation. This included Jie Tianran and the Netherworld Sect’s experts.","“Jie Tianran, it looks like God’s Era is about to open once more. That was an interesting phenomenon; it’s a move to draw attention. There will be an intense fight over God’s Era’s power,” the old entity inside Jie Tianran said.","“It’s fine. I have already claimed the initiative. Anyone who stands in my way will only end up as my stepping stone,” Jie Tianran proudly declared.","“That grandson of yours isn’t to be underestimated. He’ll surely join the fray after witnessing that phenomenon. You mustn’t lose to him,” the old entity said.","“He’ll only end up as my stepping stone as well.”","Meanwhile, deep in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, Lord Long Xie and many powerful entities were all observing God’s Era’s transformation.","“Lord Long Xie, what is God’s Era? How can it emanate such a powerful aura? It isn’t oppressive might, but I feel all jittery just looking at it,” the monstrous old man asked Long Xie.","“I don’t know. God’s Era has never been conquered in the Ancient Era, and it has never shown such a phenomenon, either.” Even the knowledgeable and powerful Long Xie was very curious about God’s Era’s silhouette.","“That is quite the transformation. It looks like God’s Era is going to open for good. Could the prophecy be true? Is someone from this era going to obtain its final power? Could it be that fellow, Chu Feng?” the monstrous old man asked excitedly.","“It’s not that simple.”","Unlike the monstrous old man and the other entities, Long Xie didn’t think it would be that easy to obtain God’s Era’s final power.","Just then, everyone’s gazes turned severe.","The silhouette’s right hand quivered. The light bundle in its right hand rose into the sky and transformed into a meteor storm that whizzed toward the Seven Realms Galaxy."]},{"number":6568,"title":"Chapter 6568: Chapter 6566: The Lunatic’s Name","paragraphs":["Chapter 6566: The Lunatic’s Name","A resplendent meteor storm of unprecedented size whizzed across space. This incredible phenomenon wowed the world of cultivation, but more importantly, it also symbolized a huge fortuitous encounter of boundless possibilities.","The meteor storm moved at an astonishing speed. It only took moments for it to enter and scatter all over the Seven Realms Galaxy. It didn’t cause any damage; instead, it seemed to blend right into the galaxy, as if they were one.","“Chu Feng, was that energy bestowed upon the Seven Realms Galaxy? Did the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master obtain God’s Era’s power?” the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader asked worriedly.","“That power might have entered the Seven Realms Galaxy, but it looks like anyone can claim them,” the lunatic said. Neither the guild leader nor Chu Feng expected her to voice her opinion.","“I also think the energy can be claimed by anyone,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng, let’s go to the Seven Realms Galaxy,” the guild leader said.","“Hold on. Let’s see where the other two light bundles are heading first,” Chu Feng replied.","He was still observing God’s Era’s massive silhouette, particularly the two remaining light bundles in its right palm.","But God’s Era’s silhouette began fading with the two light bundles in its right palm. Only the three doors on its left hand remained tangible. This seemed to imply that only the three doors would remain.","“It looks like the remaining two light bundles aren’t going anywhere for now.” Chu Feng retracted his gaze.","“Chu Feng, should we head to the Seven Realms Galaxy now?” the guild leader asked.","“You wish to go?” Chu Feng asked.","“God’s Era is a huge fortuitous encounter. I thought that I had no business with it, since it is prophesied that its power will be obtained by a junior, and older powerhouses like Jie Tianran are competing for it as well. However, it looks like we can all get a slice of the pie.","“Besides, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has been trying to kill you. As your elder, I’m obliged to teach them a lesson on your behalf. Why don’t we steal some of God’s Era’s benefits that have fallen in the Seven Realms Galaxy?” the guild leader asked.","“I would have gone even if you didn’t want to. I’d be more than happy to have you accompany me,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“What about you?” The guild leader turned her gaze to the lunatic.","There was a moment of silence before the lunatic coldly replied, “I’ll go.”","“Are you coming with us? We can surely take the lead with Chu Feng around,” the guild leader said.","“Sure,” the lunatic replied.","“Let me quickly assimilate the natural oddity. We’ll make a move right after,” the guild leader said.","She released her energy in preparation to assimilate the natural oddity, but before proceeding ahead, she shot a glance at the lunatic, fearing that the latter would get in her way. The lunatic was known to be unreasonable, after all, not to mention that they had a conflict in the past.","“Go ahead, but it won’t be easy. I have examined the natural oddity. There is more than meets the eye. If you can’t do it, I’ll take it,” the lunatic said.","“You don’t need to worry about it. I can handle this natural oddity. You can sit back and relax. I’ll make it up to you over at the Seven Realms Galaxy.”","The guild leader crossed her legs and sat down on the ground. She extended her assimilation energy toward the natural oddity and began absorbing its energy.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng bowed to the lunatic.","The lunatic tilted her head confused, not understanding the meaning behind Chu Feng’s gesture.","“Elder, I’m grateful for your help in the Luck Saint Realm,” Chu Feng replied.","Back then, the lunatic had left before he could thank her.","“Mm.” The lunatic nodded impassively.","“Elder, is there anything I can do to repay the favor? I have some God Armaments. Is there anything that catches your eye?” Chu Feng took out dozens of God Armaments with a wave of his sleeves.","The lunatic glanced at the God Armaments, but she eventually replied, “No need.”","“Elder, I’ll be too embarrassed to ask for your help again if you don’t take anything. Why don’t you take these two? I think they fit your disposition.”","Chu Feng took out two God Armaments, put them in a Cosmos Sack, and presented them to the lunatic with both hands. He noticed the lunatic’s gaze lingering on those two, a sign that she was fond of them, just that she was embarrassed to accept them.","God Armaments were valuable gifts, after all.","“Elder, please accept them,” Chu Feng insisted.","At Chu Feng’s insistence, the lunatic took the Cosmos Sack. She added, “Look for me if you need help.”","“Definitely. Besides, we’re heading to the Seven Realms Galaxy afterward, so I’ll be counting on you to look after me,” Chu Feng replied with a chuckle.","The lunatic didn’t reply. Thinking that she wasn’t fond of chatting, Chu Feng didn’t continue the conversation so as not to put her in a spot.","However, the lunatic turned to Chu Feng and remarked, “I heard the Immemorial Domain of Gods is the true world of cultivation. The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion has already moved in there. Are you aware of this matter?”","“Yes, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion has moved into the Ninth Galaxy. I have also heard rumors about the Ninth Galaxy. For some reason, the present eight galaxies are nothing like they were in the Ancient Era. Only the Ninth Galaxy has retained its condition from the Ancient Era.","“The realms there are much larger, some even spanning the sizes of our starfields. More importantly, the natural energies there are much more concentrated, making the environment more favorable for cultivation,” Chu Feng replied.","“Why don’t you enter the Ninth Galaxy? Is it to compete for God’s Era’s power? Or is it due to your grudge with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?” The lunatic didn’t doubt the credibility of Chu Feng’s news; she was only curious why Chu Feng didn’t head into the Ninth Galaxy.","“Both are true. I want to obtain God’s Era’s power, and I also wish to resolve my grudge with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. There are other reasons, too.”","Chu Feng was also worried about the Chu Heavenly Clansmen and his friends in the Lower Realm.","“Elder, do you intend to head there soon?”","“Yes,” the lunatic replied.","“Elder, I have known you for a while now, but I still don’t know your name,” Chu Feng said.","The lunatic was feared throughout the world of cultivation for her capricious and vicious nature, but no one knew anything about her past or her name.","“My family name is Liu.” The lunatic briefly paused before adding, “Liu Qingqiu.”","“That’s a beautiful name,” Chu Feng said.","“Is it?” The lunatic showed a rare hint of surprise.","“Of course it is. It complements you well—cold, but beautiful.”","“The last person to ask about my name was your father. When I replied Liu Qingqiu, I found those words foreign. It had been a long time since anyone asked about my name,” the lunatic replied.","It suddenly occurred to Chu Feng that the lunatic wasn’t as cold and heartless as she appeared on the surface. Perhaps she needed friends as well."]},{"number":6569,"title":"Chapter 6569: Chapter 6567: The Natural Oddity is a Demonic Item","paragraphs":["Chapter 6567: The Natural Oddity is a Demonic Item","Wu!","The Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader suddenly let out a groan. Looking over, her face was already warped in pain.","“What’s wrong, elder?” Chu Feng asked anxiously, but the latter didn’t seem to hear him.","He placed his hand on her forehead to inspect her condition. Soon, he realized that she had been caught in an illusion, and it wouldn’t be easy to pull her out of it.","This prompted him to turn his attention to the natural oddity. He suspected it to be the culprit.","In contrast, the lunatic remained impassive.","“I won’t hold back since she’s unable to do it.” The lunatic sat down and prepared to assimilate the natural oddity as well.","“Elder, there’s something amiss about the natural oddity,” Chu Feng advised.","“I know.”","The lunatic closed her eyes and began assimilating the natural oddity. Soon, she began frowning in pain just like the guild leader.","Chu Feng tried several ways to rescue them, including constructing formations, but he couldn’t sever their connection with the natural oddity. Watching their auras grow weaker, he made up his mind.","“I’ll have to destroy the natural oddity.”","But he didn’t make a move right away. He grabbed the Monster Slayer Sword and utilized its power to raise his cultivation up to rank one Heavenly God level. To avoid any accidents, he decided to go all out.","As soon as he swung his blade, he realized that the situation was worse than he had expected.","The Monster Slayer Sword struck the natural oddity with a loud clang. The seemingly frail treasure turned out to be unbelievably resilient! Not even the power of the Monster Slayer Sword could faze it in the least.","“Why is that natural oddity so hard? Chu Feng, do you need my help?” Eggy asked.","“Something is very wrong with this natural oddity. I don’t think it’ll work even if you make a move. We’ll have to try something else.”","Chu Feng sat down and began assimilating the natural oddity as well.","Since external means didn’t work, he could only head inside the natural oddity and see if he could rescue the guild leader and the lunatic from within.","The natural oddity’s energy flowed into his body, but it wasn’t energy he could use for cultivation. Instead, it transported his consciousness into another space. This was within Chu Feng’s expectations.","It appeared to be a huge space, but Chu Feng wasn’t certain as the area was shrouded in a golden aura. The golden aura looked beautiful, but it clouded one’s mind. The only way to not be affected by it was to maintain one’s composure.","Those who failed to maintain their composure would be slowly devoured by the golden aura until death.","“Elder?”","Chu Feng soon noticed the lunatic.","She was sitting with crossed legs not too far away. A golden aura shrouded her, devouring her life force, bloodline, and cultivation. The rate of devouring was slow, but she would surely die if this went on.","Needless to say, she didn’t respond to Chu Feng’s call.","Chu Feng walked up to the lunatic and placed his hand on her forehead. It was fortunate that he could still utilize his means even though this wasn’t his real body.","He channeled his spirit power to break the link between the lunatic and this place, thus awakening her from her trance. He proceeded to fortify her mental resilience lest she succumbs to the golden aura again.","The lunatic’s first response upon regaining consciousness was horror. However, she soon heaved a sigh of relief when she saw Chu Feng. She knew how close she had come to death earlier. Anyone in her place would have been frightened.","Hu!","The golden aura soon enveloped the lunatic once more, causing her face to warp in pain.","For some reason, she was unable to maintain her composure. In this place, anyone whose composure was shattered would be immediately afflicted by the golden aura.","This time, it took Chu Feng longer to awaken her.","“Elder, I think you have to leave this place,” he said.","“Thank you.”","The lunatic understood the plight she was in. She thanked Chu Feng before disappearing from this space. She had severed her own connection with the natural oddity.","Chu Feng ventured deeper into the space and soon found the guild leader. She was in worse condition than the lunatic.","Fortunately, Chu Feng was able to awaken her and inform her about the dangers of this place.","“How bizarre. The natural oddity should have been a cultivation resource, so how did it transform into a demonic item that devours people? Was I deceived by the Immortal Sea Fish Clan?”","The guild leader’s first response upon regaining consciousness was anger. This natural oddity was a gift from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, after all.","“Elder, I suspect that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan doesn’t know much about this item, either,” Chu Feng replied.","“Yes, I might be thinking too much into it. It could also be that the changes in the Immortal Sea have corrupted the natural oddity,” the guild leader muttered.","Right after she said those words, the golden aura assaulted her once more, plunging her into a painful illusion.","Chu Feng had to awaken her once more.","“Elder, you should leave this place first. We’ll talk later.”","“There’s something sinister about this place. It’d be best not to linger here,” the guild leader voiced her agreement. A second later, she suddenly turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Wait, do you intend to stay here?”","“Elder, this natural oddity does appear to be a cultivation resource that is highly beneficial to cultivators with deep accumulation like you. As you have said earlier, it might just be corrupted. As long as we purge the corruption, it might still be usable.","“Elder, I have a bold request to make. If I am able to purge the corruption, can you share half of the natural oddity with Elder Liu?” Chu Feng said.","“Elder Liu? You’re talking about that lunatic?” the guild leader asked.","“Yes.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Not bad, you rascal! You actually got that lunatic’s family name. No one has ever gotten that from her. Oh no, I can feel it setting in again. I’ll have to leave now. I’ll share half of it with her if you can purge the corruption. Be careful, all right? Don’t hesitate to sever your connection if things go awry,” the guild leader said before hurriedly severing her link with the natural oddity.","When she regained her consciousness, she found the lunatic sitting not too far away.","Her pale face and shaken pupils made her realize that the lunatic had attempted to assimilate the natural oddity as well, just that she was first saved by Chu Feng.","“Looks like you failed as well,” the guild leader snorted.","The lunatic ignored the guild leader. She looked at Chu Feng with worried eyes.","“You don’t have to worry about Chu Feng. He’ll be fine,” the guild leader said, though her eyes also reflected her worry.","The natural oddity was too sinister. It clearly wasn’t a cultivation resource but a monster that devoured people. Even though Chu Feng appeared unfazed inside the natural oddity, there was no guarantee that he wouldn’t meet with danger.","The two of them were lucky to have Chu Feng to save them, but Chu Feng wouldn’t have anyone to save him."]},{"number":6570,"title":"Chapter 6570: Chapter 6568: I’ll Let You Look All You Want","paragraphs":["Chapter 6568: I’ll Let You Look All You Want","Chu Feng explored the realm inside the natural oddity. His vision was obscured by the golden aura, but fortunately, he could still gather some information using his enhanced Heaven’s Eyes.","The golden aura was coming from somewhere.","So, Chu Feng began making his way toward the origin of the golden aura. The deeper he went, the greater the interference from the golden aura. He needed to stop from time to time to calm down before marching on.","Fortunately, it didn’t take him long to stumble upon a formation at the center of this realm. It appeared to be naturally formed. This formation comprised of multiple layers.","The first layer was for storage.","The second layer was for refinement.","The third layer was beyond Chu Feng’s means to decipher, but he sensed condensed aura within.","The fourth layer was even more enigmatic to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng deduced there should be a fifth layer or perhaps even more.","He had a feeling that what he was seeing right now was just the tip of the iceberg. There must be a behemoth hidden deep underneath. This formation was likely to be stronger than he could have imagined.","Two familiar auras were stored on the first level—they were from the guild leader and the lunatic. These were their devoured energies.","Chu Feng figured that he could help the two elders recover if he could retrieve their energies.","So, he constructed a formation and successfully retrieved their energies from the formation. Then, he used his body as a medium to transport the energies out.","Meanwhile, the two ladies recuperating outside opened their eyes at the same time.","“This feeling...” the guild leader murmured.","It was the life force, cultivation, and bloodline power that the natural oddity had devoured from her earlier. It would have taken her much more effort to recover under normal circumstances, but if she could reabsorb her energy, her body could immediately recover by at least half.","It would only take a bit more conditioning afterward for her to make a full recovery.","“It’s Chu Feng,” the lunatic stated.","She didn’t think that the energy could have come from nowhere. Something must have happened, and the only one who could have done anything here was Chu Feng.","“It must be him. That fellow is truly capable. No wonder he’s able to reach rank nine True God level as a junior,” the guild leader remarked.","“Chu Feng has reached rank nine True God level?” the lunatic asked in surprise.","“It’s ridiculous, isn’t it? I was shocked when I heard about it. I am a prodigy as well. It took me tremendous effort to reach rank nine True God, but he only took less than a century. It feels like I’m trash compared to him.","“I was indignant at the start, but I have no choice but to concede it now. There is a huge gap between us,” the guild leader said with a resigned smile.","It could be because she was in a good mood from having regained her cultivation, life force, and bloodline power, but she spoke to the lunatic with a smile despite their earlier misgiving.","The lunatic didn’t reply, but the shock in her eyes remained.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng stood before the formation hesitantly. He had a feeling that a secret was hidden inside the formation. It might look safe on the surface, but there was no telling what was lurking beneath it.","His danger sense was tingling. That was why he hesitated to take a step forward despite believing in seeking opportunities amid danger.","“What’s wrong, Chu Feng? Are you worried about the formation? You don’t need to be. I’ll protect you if anything happens,” Eggy said.","The Divine Deer also spoke up, “Feel free to enter if you wish to, Chu Feng. I’ll make a move if there is danger.”","Chu Feng was delighted to hear their voices. “You’re still able to maintain contact with me even when I’m in this state?”","He had thought that Eggy and the Divine Deer wouldn’t be in this realm, as he hadn’t entered it with his real body.","“Of course. I am always with you. I merely kept my silence to not disturb you,” Eggy said.","The Divine Deer didn’t say anything else, but it had already made its stance clear. That bolstered Chu Feng’s confidence.","“There’s nothing to worry about since the two of you are here with me. Let’s do it! There might be a considerable fortuitous encounter here,” Chu Feng said as he stepped into the formation.","As he ventured deeper into the formation, he realized there were more than four levels to the formation. His journey was smooth sailing, so it didn’t take him long to reach the deepest area of the formation, where the golden aura was the thickest.","It turned out that the golden aura came from a golden pool that emanated a divine aura. It resembled the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s bloodline, but more concentrated.","“Chu Feng, this pool... Is it the remnants of the legendary Immortal Sea?” Eggy asked.","“It’s possible,” Chu Feng replied.","“Why are you still standing around? Hurry up and stow it all away! I’m sure it’ll be highly beneficial to Little Fishy’s cultivation!” Eggy exclaimed excitedly.","This cultivation resource was unlikely to be useful to Chu Feng, but since it was connected to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, the odds were that it would be useful to Little Fishy.","“All right.”","Chu Feng took out a formation gourd and uncorked it. The golden pool water rose into the air and flowed into the gourd.","As the pool water dipped, a woman suddenly appeared.","She had long golden hair of over ten meters, and it floated in the air as if it had a spirit of its own. She looked to be in her twenties, but she was stunning and only paled slightly in comparison to top-notch beauties like Eggy, Little Fishy, and Zi Ling.","In particular, her golden eyelashes looked particularly charming.","As the pool water continued to dip, Chu Feng’s heart thumped rapidly. He realized that the woman was unclothed.","Shoosh!","Just then, the woman suddenly opened her eyes.","Chu Feng froze like a statue. He was mesmerized by her eyes, which radiated faint golden lights. It felt as if there were countless stars in each of her eyes, harnessing not just great power but unknown secrets as well.","Soon, he realized that he was not just charmed; he was indeed immobilized.","The golden-haired woman looked at Chu Feng with a devilish smile. “I’ll let you look all you want since you seem to enjoy it so much.”"]},{"number":6571,"title":"Chapter 6571: Chapter 6569: Unprecedented Danger","paragraphs":["Chapter 6569: Unprecedented Danger","The golden-haired woman’s smile was not only devilish but bewitching as well.","“Oh? What a familiar sight,” the Divine Deer spoke mirthfully. It had spoken to Chu Feng in the same tone during their first meeting.","“Is it another divine skill?” Eggy asked in excitement.","The Divine Deer had tested Chu Feng in this manner during their first meeting. Perhaps this was a convention among divine skills.","But while Eggy was feeling excited, Chu Feng was feeling worried.","The golden-haired woman said that she would let Chu Feng see all he wanted, and she did rise from the golden pool to reveal herself, but the golden aura had obscured most parts of her body. Chu Feng could hardly see anything at all.","More importantly, the golden-haired woman was looking at him with the eyes of a predator.","“This god was the one who let you in, but you are still quite the capable one to find your way here.","Those words further fanned Eggy’s excitement. “See! She calls herself a god. She must really be a divine skill!”","The golden-haired woman walked up to Chu Feng and said, “Chu Feng, you do live up to your reputation.”","She placed her fair, delicate hand on Chu Feng’s head before slowly sliding it down. Her touch felt sensual. It moved down Chu Feng’s hair, his cheeks, his neck, his shoulder, and his chest.","However, Chu Feng was in no mood to enjoy the sensation. He had a strong feeling that this didn’t bode well. The person before him harbored malevolent intent.","“Elder, do you know me?” Chu Feng composed himself and asked respectfully.","“There is no junior world spiritist more famous than you in these eight galaxies. I’m bound to have heard about you,” the golden-haired woman said as her hand slid to Chu Feng’s dantian and stopped there.","“But what I’m more interested in is your Heavenly Lightning Bloodline.”","She raised her gaze from Chu Feng’s abdomen to meet his eyes. Her eyes were even more beautiful up close, but the sharp glint in them sent shivers down his spine.","“Elder, what do you mean? I don’t understand,” Chu Feng asked.","The golden-haired woman’s smile widened. Chu Feng shuddered. He felt strong killing intent coming from her.","“It’s a malevolent entity,” the Divine Deer murmured, having realized that the golden-haired woman was not a fortuitous encounter. It quickly channeled its power to bring Chu Feng out of this place.","“You’re courting death!”","At the same time, a surge of spirit power gathered beside Chu Feng. Eggy was trying to leave the World Spirit Space to deal with the golden-haired woman, but the gate refused to form.","“Oh no. Chu Feng!” the Divine Deer exclaimed. To its horror, it couldn’t channel its power.","“Oh? You have some good stuff with you—a powerful world spirit and even a divine skill.”","The golden-haired woman glanced at the surge of spirit power that refused to channel into a gate and smiled mockingly.","Chu Feng tensed up further.","It was one thing for Eggy to be unable to leave his World Spirit Space, but to think that even the Divine Deer would be unable to use its ability. How powerful could the golden-haired woman be then? Just what kind of entity was she?","The golden-haired woman suddenly vanished.","Chu Feng noticed a gaze appearing in his dantian. He projected his consciousness into his dantian world, but the golden-haired woman was nowhere to be found. Even so, he could still sense her gaze.","This unnerved him.","It felt like the gaze was from the outside, looking upon everything like a god.","Chu Feng had encounters with enemies who attempted to enter his dantian to steal his bloodline power, but this was the first time an entity had entered his dantian in this manner. This made him realize that he was in trouble.","“That is...” the golden-haired woman suddenly exclaimed in shock.","Her gaze was locked on the Sacred Tree Seed.","“It really is! To think that it is in your body! You didn’t just obtain the Genesis Bloodline but this as well. You are truly blessed with fortuitous encounters. The world is helping me! This must be fate! Hahaha...”","The golden-haired woman laughed heartily, her gleeful voice reverberating throughout Chu Feng’s dantian as if she had become the ruler here.","“You were able to obtain even this item. Maybe that legendary item might be inside you as well. Let me take a look. If it is, you would have been worthy of my reward,” the golden-haired woman said excitedly.","Chu Feng’s pitch-black dantian world was swiftly inundated by a blinding light.","A golden aura appeared on the horizon of his dantian world and gushed inward like a tsunami, threatening to devour everything. It shook his dantian world so violently that it felt like it would be destroyed at any moment.","But what was even more terrifying was that Chu Feng couldn’t sense the parts of his dantian world that had been devoured by the golden aura. It was as if those parts had been snatched away and no longer were his.","Just then, a humongous pair of eyes opened from the depths of the dantian world, and a deep voice boomed, “Scram!!!”","A barrage of red lightning gushed outward. It took only an instant for it to collide with the tsunami of golden aura. Not only did it halt the golden aura’s advancement, but it even began vaporizing it.","It didn’t take long for the red lightning to drive off the golden aura and vaporize it.","Chu Feng also regained connection with those parts of his dantian world."]},{"number":6572,"title":"Chapter 6572: Chapter 6570: Could She Be Behind the Phenomenon?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6570: Could She Be Behind the Phenomenon?","“Interesting,” the golden-haired woman remarked.","Then, she abruptly vanished. Even her omnipresent gaze vanished from his dantian.","Chu Feng regained control of his body.","Hu!","Chu Feng was so weakened that he nearly stumbled to the ground. He staggered a few steps backward before regaining his balance.","Eggy finally manifested the gate and emerged from his World Spirit Space. She quickly rushed forward to support him. She looked at him worriedly and asked, “What’s wrong, Chu Feng?”","His face was covered in sweat, and his pupils were dilated.","Eggy had a good grasp of Chu Feng, having been with him since their time in the Nine Provinces Continent. He had always remained calm no matter how precarious their situation was. It was rare for him to show such an expression.","“I’m fine. It’s over now.” Chu Feng squeezed out a smile to not worry Eggy.","“What happened, Chu Feng?” the Divine Deer asked.","It could use its powers now, but earlier, the golden-haired woman had sealed off its abilities. This was testament to the golden-haired woman’s terrifying prowess. Since she had displayed her malice, there was no way she would be so kind-hearted as to let him go.","Something must have happened.","“That entity attempted to possess my body and steal my treasures, but my bloodline power fought her off. I don’t know if she is dead or if she has only left. Hold on, let me ask about it.”","Chu Feng knew that the roar inside his dantian earlier had come from the red lightning beast. He projected his consciousness back into his dantian world, and he was awed once more when he saw the red lightning beast’s massive physique.","He knew how powerful his lightning beasts were. Other entities who entered his dantian world before the golden-haired woman suffered terrible plights.","However, the golden-haired woman was different. He could tell that she was in an entirely different class. Yet, an entity of her caliber couldn’t do much against his lightning beasts, either.","“Thank you, elder.” Chu Feng bowed to the red lightning beast.","He had felt powerless before the golden-haired woman’s prowess and panicked earlier. He might have reached pinnacle True God level, but he knew that the ‘god’ in his cultivation rank was merely just a name and was not true godhood.","Rather, the power he had just experienced felt more like a god’s power. It was of a different caliber; he couldn’t even imagine how he could have withstood such power. It was his survival that was at stake, but he felt like he could only watch helplessly as everything unfolded.","It was a huge relief that the lightning beasts were around.","“You don’t need to thank me. This is my turf. You’re on your own for anything that happens in the world of cultivation, but I’ll cripple anyone who causes trouble in my turf,” the red lightning beast said.","“Elder, you’re as majestic as ever!” Chu Feng said.","“Cut the crap and get to the point.”","“Heh, it’s impossible to hide anything from you. Elder, did you manage to kill that golden-haired woman?”","“That fellow is not that simple, but I doubt she’ll dare to return to this dantian world.”","“So, she’s still alive?”","The red lightning beast didn’t reply, but its silence spoke volumes.","“Elder, what was that entity earlier? Is she a natural oddity? It doesn’t seem like it. Is she another powerhouse from the Ancient Era?” Chu Feng pressed on.","But the red lightning beast still didn’t answer. It would always fall silent whenever Chu Feng asked questions that it didn’t want to answer. Knowing how stubborn it could be, he pulled his consciousness back into his main body.","“Chu Feng, is that fellow dead?” Eggy hurriedly asked.","“It seems like she has escaped,” Chu Feng replied.","“Escaped? She must be quite capable to have escaped. But it looks like your bloodline power is still the stronger one here.” Eggy breathed a sigh of relief.","Since the danger was over, she returned to the World Spirit Space.","But Chu Feng remained worried. Many questions floated in his mind.","The water inside the pool resembles the legendary Immortal Sea. Was it the Immortal Sea’s remnant power, or did that woman steal it from the Immortal Sea?","Or does it have nothing to do with the Immortal Sea at all, and is it just energy the woman gathered through her vile formation, just that it resembles the Immortal Sea?","Chu Feng thought that the former two possibilities were more plausible.","The woman’s means resembled the legendary Immortal Sea so much that it was likely that she had obtained a means related to it.","But this brought about more doubts.","Was the woman related to the Immortal Sea, or did she obtain her power by stealing and cultivating with the Immortal Sea’s energy?","Also, could the humongous phenomenon that had enveloped the entire Immortal Sea Galaxy be related to this golden-haired woman?","Chu Feng had previously attributed it to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, particularly Xianhai Yu’er and Xianhai Shaoyu, but he found no traces of them in their ancestral land.","The golden-haired woman might have been behind that phenomenon instead. With her strength, she was more than capable of pulling that off, though Chu Feng thought that it would be a pity if that was the case.","But what worried him the most was that he didn’t think that there was anyone in these eight galaxies who had the power to stop the golden-haired woman.","“Hm?”","Chu Feng suddenly sensed the formation dissipating. Consequently, the natural oddity’s aura began to surface. This made him realize that the root of this disaster was not the natural oddity but the golden-haired woman’s formation.","The natural oddity could be assimilated once the formation had been unraveled.","The formation dissipated so slowly that it would have taken more than a decade if left be, though Chu Feng could hasten the process. But before then, he first raised his formation gourd.","No matter how the golden pool was formed, there was no denying that the fluid inside it was an invaluable cultivation resource. It was just that Chu Feng was in a state of heightened vigilance after what happened earlier.","Fortunately, the golden-haired woman didn’t reappear from the golden pool. She must have really left.","Chu Feng first stowed away the golden water before constructing a formation. He channeled the formation, and the golden-haired woman’s formation began to dissipate at a much faster pace.","Meanwhile, the lunatic and the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader sensed the change in the natural oddity.","“Somehow, it feels like we can cultivate with the natural oddity now. Shall we give it a try?” the guild leader asked the lunatic.","“You can go first,” the lunatic said.","The guild leader rolled her eyes. “Tsk, you aren’t dumb at all. You’re letting me go first because you’re worried that it’ll be dangerous.”","She had wanted the lunatic to go first. The near-death experience she had just been through had truly frightened her."]},{"number":6573,"title":"Chapter 6573: Chapter 6571: The Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief","paragraphs":["Chapter 6571: The Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief","“Hm?”","Both the lunatic and the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader suddenly stood up at the same time as they turned their eyes toward the southeast. The clear sky was being devoured by dark clouds at a rapid pace.","A Heavenly God’s aura could be sensed. It was not a natural weather pattern but the onslaught of a Heavenly God.","Fortunately, the other party was only at rank one Heavenly God.","Shoosh!","The lunatic rose into the air. The powerful winds caused her skirt to flutter furiously, but she wasn’t intimidated in the least. If anything, her eyes reflected murderous intent.","The surrounding space distorted as powerful oppressive might swept outward. The incoming dark clouds appeared to have crashed into an unmoving entity, causing them to dissipate into thin air.","The oppressive might was from the lunatic.","The guild leader also rose into the air and thrust her palm forth. She unleashed her martial power in the form of a towering wave, crashing across space.","This was the power wielded by Heavenly Gods. They could destroy smaller realms like the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm at a whim.","“Gahaha!” An arrogant laughter roared despite the scattering of the dark clouds.","The guild leader immediately realized something was amiss, for the laughter was from an opposite direction from where the dark clouds were coming from.","She looked over and saw yet another bundle of dark clouds forming, but this time, it swiftly covered the entire sky. Amid the billowing dark clouds was a pair of giant red eyes reminiscent of two suns.","It was a startling sight, as if the devil had descended upon the world.","The laughter came from that dark cloud.","“I didn’t expect to stumble upon such a rare natural oddity and two gorgeous women shortly after coming out of seclusion. The world is truly generous to me,” the voice spoke in a sleazy but taunting manner.","Boom!","The lunatic whipped out the God Armament sword she had just received from Chu Feng and swung it, unleashing a golden sword beam. It scattered the dark clouds.","“Gahaha!” The arrogant laughter echoed once more.","Once again, the dark clouds manifested from another direction.","“What a feisty one you are. I love it! Ladies, allow me to introduce myself. I am the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief. It was just days ago that my clansmen and I came out of seclusion. We are seeking to dominate the world of cultivation.","“The two of you have reached Heavenly God level, just like me. Why don’t you marry me and become my wives? Once I conquer the world of cultivation, I’ll bestow each of you with a galaxy. How does that sound?” the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief bragged.","The guild leader scoffed in contempt, “A mere rank one Heavenly God dreams of dominating the world of cultivation? Your Cloud Leopard Clan must have been closed off from the world.”","“Beauty, you don’t seem to be too intelligent. You might think that you’re putting me down, but you’re insulting yourself as well. Aren’t you a rank one Heavenly God as well? You should know that there’s a disparity even among fellow Heavenly Gods, and I... am invincible within the same rank.”","Boom!","Another golden sword beam suddenly tore through the dark clouds. The lunatic had launched another attack. She couldn’t be less interested in his prattling.","It was just that the dark clouds swiftly manifested elsewhere once more.","“My little feisty lady has no patience. Is it because you want to have a taste of my strength?”","Killing intent flared from the dark clouds.","The guild leader whipped out her God Armament while eyeing the dark clouds vigilantly. Even though they could scatter the dark clouds, they hadn’t been able to inflict any tangible damage on the other party, evident from how the dark clouds just reformed themselves right after.","While the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief lacked understanding about the present world of cultivation, he was not an opponent to be underestimated. His killing intent was chilling. He was most likely a veteran fighter.","Soon, two beams of light shot out from the dark clouds. They were two massive bells.","The lunatic and the guild leader stared intently at the two bells.","One of them rang.","Ding!","A piercing sound reverberated across the sky. A cold light pierced through the lunatic’s abdomen.","By the time the guild leader registered what was going on, the cold light had already vanished.","A bloody hole appeared in the lunatic’s abdomen, and she bled profusely.","“How are you feeling?’ the guild leader rushed over and asked.","“There’s something weird about him. Be careful,” the lunatic took out a treasure to stop her bleeding as she spoke.","It was only then that the guild leader realized that the bell that had rung earlier had vanished.","Just then, the other bell rang.","The guild leader immediately formed a hand seal and wrapped herself in a layer of martial power, lest she land in the same fate as the lunatic.","Shoosh!","She only saw a flicker of cold light before her martial power scattered. A bloody hole appeared in her abdomen as well.","“Damn it! Why didn’t I sense anything at all?” the guild leader spat.","She was unable to see through the other party’s attack, and this didn’t bode well.","Boom!","Another golden sword ray sliced through the air. The result was the same as before. The dark clouds were scattered, but they manifested elsewhere right after. Evidently, such attacks didn’t work against their enemy.","“Beauties, do you know what I’m capable of now? Will you submit to me, or do you want to continue this fight?” the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Something is amiss. We shouldn’t push it. Let’s placate him first and take our time to find his weakness. If we die here, Chu Feng will be in trouble as well,” the guild leader told the lunatic via voice transmission.","Shoosh!","Golden martial power enveloped the lunatic, raising her fighting prowess by a considerable extent. The lunatic morphed into a golden light that surged toward the dark clouds.","“Haaa!” The guild leader shook her head helplessly.","She tightened her grip around her God Armament and followed the lunatic in her charge.","But the truth was that she had the same thought as the lunatic. If long-range attacks didn’t work, the next thing to do was to try attacking him at close range."]},{"number":6574,"title":"Chapter 6574: Chapter 6572: A Circus Trick","paragraphs":["Chapter 6572: A Circus Trick","The lunatic and the guild leader wrapped themselves in martial power and charged into the dark clouds. They simultaneously swung their God Armaments, unleashing devastating martial skills.","Cold gleams flashed.","The dark clouds dissipated under their attack, but that only further stoked the guild leader’s unease.","It was the same as before.","The dark clouds had scattered, but they had failed to deal decisive damage to the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief.","“Kikiki...” A sinister laughter echoed as the dark clouds manifested from the opposite direction. “Aren’t the two of you obstinate? Just like untamed mares. I shall beat some obedience into you, until you finally beg for mercy and become tame!”","Lights shot out of the billowing dark clouds, and over a hundred bells appeared.","“Could it be...”","Fear flickered across the guild leader and the lunatic’s eyes.","If each of the bells represented a single attack, they would be crippled, if not dead, by the time all the attacks landed.","“Run!” the guild leader shouted at the lunatic before turning tail and fleeing.","The lunatic also knew that they would be doomed if they remained, so she executed her movement skill and flitted off.","It only took an instant for them to cover a vast distance, but they stopped when they realized that the dark clouds weren’t following them.","A sneer echoed, “Running away? But escape is futile. I have already imprinted your bodies. You can flee to the ends of the world, but I will still find and capture you. Don’t worry, my beauties. I’ll take care of you after I assimilate the natural oddity.”","The guild leader and the lunatic were extremely displeased to hear those words, but this confirmed one thing. As enigmatic as the other party’s attacks were, they had a limited range. They could dodge his attacks by stepping out of his attacking range.","“I’m heading back,” the lunatic said.","“What? Are you out of your mind? You shouldn’t give up your life for resources!” the guild leader exclaimed.","“What will happen to Chu Feng if we don’t return?” the lunatic asked worriedly.","She was not worried about the natural oddity but Chu Feng.","“Chu Feng was behind the chaos in the Undying Starfield. To escape from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect’s Heavenly Gods, he must have some hidden hands up his sleeves,” the guild leader said.","“What hidden hands does he have?” the lunatic asked.","“Um... I’m not sure, but we can only pray that Chu Feng has a way to deal with that fellow. We clearly aren’t a match for him. If we march back there, there will only be two outcomes—we will either be captured or killed by him. That’ll only burden Chu Feng,” the guild leader said.","The lunatic agreed with the guild leader’s words, but she couldn’t bring herself to watch from afar.","Pu! Pu!","Two dull thuds echoed. Another bloody gorge simultaneously appeared in the lunatic and the guild leader’s abdomens.","A laughter cackled from behind.","Only then did the guild leader and the lunatic notice that the dark clouds had dissipated and reappeared behind them. Appearing with the dark clouds were the 98 bells. He had just used two bells to attack them.","“Was I mistaken?”","The guild leader frowned. She thought she had escaped from the other party’s attacking range, but it looked like her judgment was off.","Just then, the remaining 98 bells rang at the same time.","The guild leader and the lunatic were horrified. Despite knowing that it might not be enough to dodge the other party’s attack, their first reaction was still to flee.","Shoosh!","A figure suddenly appeared in front of them—Chu Feng. His aura had risen to rank one Heavenly God level, but the power was coming from the sword in his right hand.","“The Monster Slayer Sword?”","Both the guild leader and the lunatic recognized the sword. It was the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s personal weapon.","However, what caught their attention more than Chu Feng’s cultivation was the silver dagger floating in front of him. Chu Feng had stretched his left hand to grab something, but it wasn’t the silver dagger.","“A mere circus trick.”","Chu Feng clenched his left fist, and the crisp sound of snapping bone echoed.","“AHHHH!!! Stop it stop it stop it! Stop it right now!!!” the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief screamed in agony, but his voice echoed not from the dark clouds but from in front of Chu Feng.","Chu Feng released his spirit power and constructed a formation. A figure was revealed under the formation. It was a two-meter-tall old man with a humanoid, leopard body. He appeared to be born with a single arm, and he was wielding a silver dagger.","Chu Feng was holding the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief by his wrist, which created the illusion of a floating silver dagger earlier.","“The Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief is really a leopard,” the guild leader remarked.","She had no idea how Chu Feng did it, but he had managed to turn the tide.","“You bastard! Do you know who I am?” the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief roared fiercely at Chu Feng. The pain from fracturing his wrist had finally subsided enough for him to speak.","“I can’t care less who you are.”","Chu Feng swung his right arm. With a cold gleam, he lopped off the other party’s only arm.","“GAHHH! Y-you...”","The Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief screamed miserably while glaring at Chu Feng with hateful eyes. He turned around and vanished into thin air."]},{"number":6575,"title":"Chapter 6575: Chapter 6573: Obtaining Two Secret Treasures","paragraphs":["Chapter 6573: Obtaining Two Secret Treasures","After the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief disappeared, Chu Feng executed Heaven Footwork and vanished into thin air. By the time he reappeared, he was already very far away from where he previously was.","He swung his Monster Slayer Sword down on what appeared to be nothing, but blood splattered.","GAH!","The Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief shrieked in pain. His figure reappeared.","Chu Feng’s Monster Slayer Sword had slashed him from his shoulder to his abdomen, slicing him into two pieces.","The excruciating pain caused the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s face to warp, but he swallowed his screams and frantically pleaded for his life, “Young hero, it’s a misunderstanding. It’s all a misunderstanding!”","“A misunderstanding?” Chu Feng sneered.","He exerted a powerful suction force that flowed through the Monster Slayer Sword and enveloped the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief.","“GAHHHHH!”","The Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief let out a blood-curdling cry. His body convulsed ceaselessly from the sheer pain, his eyeballs bulged, and he struggled to utter a word.","Chu Feng was absorbing the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s origin energies, and he was using some method to maximize the pain.","By the time he transferred the origin energies to Eggy in his World Spirit Space, the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief was already on the verge of death. Even so, he continued glaring hatefully at Chu Feng.","If looks could kill, Chu Feng would have withered there and then.","But even so, the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief didn’t utter a word. He wasn’t able to speak earlier due to the sheer pain, but now, he was too weak to talk.","“Don’t do things that will cause misunderstandings in your next life,” Chu Feng sneered as killing intent flickered across his eyes.","Shoosh shoosh!","There were two flashes of cold light. One sliced the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief in half, and the other one decapitated him.","The dark clouds dissipated along with the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s aura.","Neither the guild leader nor the lunatic was surprised by Chu Feng’s decisiveness in killing the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief, but watching him construct a formation to preserve the latter’s carcass gave them chills.","They wondered if Chu Feng had some twisted interest in storing corpses.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal and activated a formation. An aura flowed out of the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s body and converged to form a rune imprint. The rune imprint emanated an extremely old aura that dated even farther back than the Ancient Era.","It was an item from the Immemorial Era.","“What’s that?”","The guild leader and the lunatic’s eyes lit up.","Chu Feng grabbed the rune imprint. He made his way over to the guild leader and the lunatic while explaining, “It’s a treasure. It harnesses formidable concealment power and raises one’s speed.”","Then, he flicked his wrist and whipped out a silver dagger. It was the same silver dagger brandished by the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief earlier. It was not a God Armament but a treasure.","“This dagger wields formidable offensive prowess. It can move at exceedingly fast speeds, making it nigh impossible to avoid when activated at close range. It can also easily pierce most defensive means.","“That old leopard used the rune imprint to first sneak up on you before activating the dagger at close range.”","“Are you saying that he relied solely on those two treasures to attack us earlier? It wasn’t a secret skill? But what was the deal with the dark clouds and the bells then?”","The guild leader had been convinced that the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief had been using secret skills to attack them.","“The bells are a feint. The dark clouds should be a secret skill, but it’s nothing but a circus trick. It doesn’t possess any offensive prowess,” Chu Feng replied.","“I see. The dark clouds and the bells are distractions. He’s merely buying time to secretly approach and attack us.” The guild leader widened her eyes in realization.","“That should be the case. That old leopard was very weak. He has probably been relying on these two treasures for the longest time. It must have taken a lot of practice to fool Heavenly Gods. He might have even sacrificed some things in his cultivation for that, which would explain his weakness.”","Chu Feng had fought against the Netherworld Sect’s rank one Heavenly Gods. He thought they were already weak enough, but this old leopard was even weaker than them.","“I nearly got killed by the likes of that thing. How shameful,” the guild leader said in self-deprecation.","“He might not be strong in the traditional sense, but his combination of skills makes him a tricky enemy. I wouldn’t have been able to find him if I weren’t a world spiritist,” Chu Feng replied.","He had subdued the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief easily because his Heaven’s Eyes happened to curb the latter’s ability. Anyone else in his place would have found themselves rendered helpless.","“You’re right. That old leopard might be nothing much, but his treasures are formidable. Chu Feng, will you be able to tame his treasures?” the guild leader asked.","“It’ll take time, but it shouldn’t be a problem. Elder, are you interested in it?” Chu Feng replied.","“Forget it. It is a formidable treasure, but I have just examined it, and I don’t think it will be easy to control it. I should leave it to a prodigy like you instead,” the guild leader said.","“Elders, the natural oddity can be assimilated now. Please feel free to do so,” Chu Feng said.","The injuries sustained by the guild leader and the lunatic were no big deal, as the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief had avoided their vitals; he was probably trying to scare them into submission. It didn’t get in the way of their cultivation.","The natural oddity couldn’t be taken away, so Chu Feng thought it would be best for them to assimilate it as soon as possible.","“Thank you, Chu Feng. I don’t know how I can repay you for this,” the guild leader said.","“Elder, I still remember the favor you have shown me. It’s only right for me to do this for you,” Chu Feng replied.","“All right. I shan’t stand on ceremony then.” The guild leader smiled. She turned to the lunatic and said, “Let’s go.”","The lunatic looked at the guild leader in confusion.","“It is Chu Feng’s request. He asked me to share half of the natural oddity with you if he can restore it. I am not one to break my promise. I’ll be leaving half for you, whether you take it or not,” the guild leader said as she made her way toward the natural oddity.","The lunatic looked at Chu Feng with moved eyes.","“Go ahead, Elder Liu,” Chu Feng said.","“Mm.” The lunatic nodded before making a move. She might not have thanked Chu Feng, but the emotions rippling in her eyes spoke louder than words."]},{"number":6576,"title":"Chapter 6576: Chapter 6574: Is This Right?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6574: Is This Right?","Chu Feng also made his way to the natural oddity.","The natural oddity’s energy flowed into the guild leader and the lunatic’s body once again, but this time, they didn’t display any discomfort. Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief.","“Chu Feng, I know that those two elders are your benefactors, but you have just saved their lives. Why don’t you negotiate with them to get a share of the natural oddity as well? You need to advance to Heavenly God as soon as possible,” Eggy said.","“The natural oddity is an extraordinary treasure, but its effects differ from person to person. Even if I claim the whole natural oddity for myself, it’s only a drop in the bucket compared to what I require to reach Heavenly God. Besides, this natural oddity complements the two elders much more than me,” Chu Feng replied.","“Fine, fine. I’ll leave you to examine that old leopard’s stuff. I’m going to cultivate.” Eggy sat down, took out the scroll she received from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, and began cultivating.","“Eggy, what are you cultivating?” Chu Feng asked. He couldn’t help but be curious about what Eggy had received from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, for her to cultivate so diligently.","“It’s a secret,” Eggy replied with a sweet smile.","So, Chu Feng turned his attention to the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s two treasures.","The latter had made a trade-off in his cultivation to control these two treasures. Chu Feng figured that there should be a clue in his carcass, which was why he preserved it.","While studying the carcass, he continued to keep an eye on God’s Era for changes in the remaining two bundles of power. He would also occasionally glance at the Seven Realms Galaxy to see if the God’s Era’s power there would manifest into anything.","For the time being, there was nothing noteworthy.","Time passed. The guild leader and the lunatic were finally done assimilating the natural oddity, but they remained seated, focused on their cultivation.","Chu Feng was heartened. From experience, he figured that the two elders must have received an epiphany from this fortuitous encounter.","Soon, a beam of light shot out from the lunatic’s body and gushed into the sky. The same happened to the guild leader moments later. The two beams shot out of the realm and scattered around as an aura, forming two incredible phenomena.","“Did the two elders make a breakthrough?” Chu Feng wondered.","The auras of the guild leader and the lunatic surged to rank two Heavenly God level. With that, they finally opened their eyes and stood up.","“Congratulations on your breakthrough, elders,” Chu Feng said with a smile.","“Chu Feng, it’s all thanks to you,” the guild leader replied with a radiant smile.","It was rare to see her in such high spirits, though it was understandable since it was extremely difficult for someone of her age to take a step forward. Not to mention, this was a breakthrough in Heavenly God level!","“Elder, you’re giving me too much credit. The hardest part about cultivation is not a lack of resources but enlightenment. It’s due to your own abilities that you succeeded in making a breakthrough,” Chu Feng replied with a thumbs up.","Just then, Chu Feng, the guild leader, and the lunatic raised their heads at the same time.","Whoosh!","A jarring sound echoed across space.","Humongous formation chains had appeared from space and were wrapping around the realm, attempting to seal it off. At the same time, a dark red aura also enveloped the realm.","“It’s the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Chu Feng said.","The guild leader and the lunatic drew their God Armaments while scanning their surroundings. They were searching for Netherworld Sectmembers and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists.","“Don’t bother searching anymore,” a voice spoke.","Seven figures appeared in space, They stood in a circle, surrounding Chu Feng and the others. Six of them wore the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritist cloak, whereas the last one was Netherworld Marshal Xiahou Jue.","Shoosh!","The lunatic swung her blade, unleashing a sword ki toward Xiahou Jue.","“Stop, elder!” Chu Feng shouted.","But it was already too late. The sword ki had already reached Xiahou Jue.","Xiahou Jue raised his arm, grabbed the sword ki with his bare hands, and crushed it. At the same time, the lunatic’s abdomen suddenly lurched, and she spewed blood from her mouth. The attack had been transferred through the sword ki to inflict damage directly on the lunatic!","The guild leader hurriedly supported the lunatic while looking at Xiahou Jue with shocked eyes. She murmured in despair, “Rank four Heavenly God?”","She stood no chance against such an opponent, even with her recent breakthrough.","“He’s not just a rank four Heavenly God. He can still raise his cultivation by a rank,” Chu Feng said.","“What?”","The guild leader and the lunatic were flabbergasted. The vast disparity in their strength eroded their fighting will.","“Are these the opponents you faced in the Undying Starfield?” the guild leader asked in horror. She found it difficult to believe, especially now that she was experiencing the strength of a rank four Heavenly God in person.","“Don’t worry. He can’t kill us,” Chu Feng said.","He retreated two steps to stand closer to the guild leader and the lunatic, knowing that he might have to invoke the Divine Deer’s power to escape from this predicament.","Xiahou Jue shot a disdainful glance at the lunatic before turning his attention back to Chu Feng. His eyes became wary even though Chu Feng was far weaker than him.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists also dared not let down their guard. They were so nervous that they could even hear their frantic heartbeats.","That greatly assuaged the guild leader and the lunatic’s nervousness.","“Why do they seem even more nervous than us? Is this supposed to be the case?” the guild leader asked the lunatic.","The lunatic was baffled as well."]},{"number":6577,"title":"Chapter 6577: Chapter 6575: Heavenly God Yu’er","paragraphs":["Chapter 6575: Heavenly God Yu’er","“What kind of monster are you, Chu Feng? You were still in the Bloodline Galaxy not long ago. How did you get here so quickly?” Xiahou Jue questioned.","He had lost the arrogance he had displayed when he first met Chu Feng at the Immemorial Cemetery. It was clearly unwise to underestimate Chu Feng because of his weaker cultivation or spirit power.","Xiahou Jue and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists had rushed here at their fastest speed after receiving orders, but they still arrived here later than Chu Feng.","Even so, they were determined to kill Chu Feng here. It was one thing to be rendered helpless in the Undying Starfield, since Chu Feng had taken control of the sacred item and suppressed their cultivation, but there was no such excuse here.","“Xiahou Jue, don’t waste your breath on him. Kill him,” a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist said. He had only refrained from making a move himself because he was afraid that something would go awry, and he would have to take the blame.","Besides, Xiahou Jue was indeed stronger than him.","But Xiahou Jue looked at them with contemptuous eyes. This was the kind of person he was. He wouldn’t listen to anyone’s orders in the Netherworld Sect except for Baili Xukong and a few lords from the neutral faction, let alone someone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Chu Feng, what’s wrong? Are you scared speechless now that you aren’t holding our sacred item hostage anymore? Or are you scheming something? I’ll offer you some words of advice. I may consider sparing your life if you surrender obediently, but if you dare try anything, I’ll kill you and those two old hags!” Xiahou Jue spat coldly.","A blood-red aura enveloped the realm, forming a cage.","“Xiahou Jue, not even those two old things, Baili Xukong and Jie Tianran, had been able to capture me. Who gave the likes of you guts to utter such brazen words?” Chu Feng scoffed.","“You arrogant twat!”","A Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion couldn’t take it anymore. He formed a hand seal, and a golden light descended through the blood-red aura.","Upon closer examination, it was a humongous golden bell that covered the entire sky. It was so huge that it could easily fill an ocean. It was a powerful sealing formation.","“Damn it!” The lunatic was unnerved. This formation was beyond her means to deal with, but she still raised her sword to fight back.","“You don’t have to do that, elder.”","Chu Feng raised his hand to stop the lunatic. He knew that she didn’t have the power to deal with the descending formation, not to mention Xiahou Jue could raise his cultivation to rank five Heavenly God. He had already given up on this battle.","The Divine Deer would step in when they were truly in danger anyway.","“I’d like to see who dares to touch him!” a woman’s voice suddenly echoed.","The earth shook.","Boom!","A ray of light shot into the blue sky and struck the golden bell, shattering it into countless fragments.","The faces of Xiahou Jue and the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists stiffened up.","“Chu Feng, that voice...” Eggy murmured.","“Yes, it’s Yu’er,” Chu Feng replied affirmatively.","A figure emerged from the light. Indeed, it was Little Fishy, but her aura was no longer at pinnacle True God level but rank one Heavenly God level.","“Xianhai Yu’er? She has reached Heavenly God level?”","The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists recognized Little Fishy, but they breathed a sigh of relief upon seeing her.","The one who had just made a move was a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, which was why they were worried when his attack was unraveled. They thought that a powerful enemy had arrived.","But if the enemy was just a rank one Heavenly God, there would be nothing to fear.","“Xianhai Yu’er, were you the one who induced the earlier phenomenon?” the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist who conjured that golden bell earlier questioned.","But Little Fishy ignored him. Instead, she made her way over to Chu Feng’s side. Her cold expression transformed into a beaming smile so radiant that it could melt away any worries.","“Xianhai Yu’er pays respect to the two elders.” Little Fishy first greeted the guild leader and the lunatic before turning to Chu Feng. She thumped her chest and said, “Big brother, now that I’m here, you don’t need to fear those old things.”","Chu Feng was overjoyed to see Little Fishy, but there was a question bothering him. “Yu’er, were you here all along?”","Even with his keen senses, he hadn’t sensed any traces of Little Fishy in the area, which was why he was convinced that she wasn’t here. He even thought that the earlier phenomenon was induced by the golden-haired woman instead.","But from the looks of it now, Little Fishy likely induced the phenomenon when she made a breakthrough to Heavenly God level. This also indicated that she had been here all along.","“Yes, big brother. I was in the ancestral land all along.” Little Fishy nodded with a smile.","Intense killing intent suddenly flared. It was from the rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist who constructed the golden bell formation earlier.","“Are you pretending that we don’t exist?”","He had a fiery temper, which was why he had blown up earlier when Chu Feng insulted Jie Tianran. He couldn’t stand how Xianhai Yu’er had outright ignored them to engage in idle chatter with Chu Feng.","“Give me a moment, big brother,” Little Fishy said before vanishing into thin air.","The next instant, she appeared beside the rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. Her face was gorgeous, but her eyes emitted bone-chilling frost.","“Were you the one who attacked my big brother earlier?” Little Fishy asked.","Startled, the rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist anxiously retreated while forming hand seals to stack multiple layers of spirit power around him. For a moment there, he vividly felt the threat of death.","But with a swipe, Little Fishy clawed through his defenses as if they were flimsy blobs of tofu. Then, her hand darted forth and grabbed his throat.","Kacha!","Everyone watched in shock as the rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist breathed his last."]},{"number":6578,"title":"Chapter 6578: Chapter 6576: Absolute Contempt","paragraphs":["Chapter 6576: Absolute Contempt","A ship flying the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s flag swiftly traveled through a teleportation passageway linking the Bloodline Galaxy to the Seven Realms Galaxy.","The people onboard the ship were the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists, who had been aiding the Netherworld Sect at the Undying Starfield earlier. Even Jie Tianran was on this ship as well.","Jie Tianran had initially planned for his formation inside the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item to stabilize first before leaving, but the changes in God’s Era left him with no choice but to leave prematurely.","A significant portion of God’s Era’s power had descended upon the Seven Realms Galaxy, and these were likely to be huge fortuitous encounters.","The Netherworld Sect didn’t blame Jie Tianran for leaving, especially since the latter had been clear about his priorities from the start.","On top of that, Jie Tianran had made sure to stabilize the sacred item’s condition to prevent it from deteriorating before leaving. He had also left some world spiritists behind to keep an eye on the sacred item. Above all, the formation he had constructed looked reliable.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists had been excited about returning to the Seven Realms Galaxy. They thought that this was a chance for them to bring their spirit power to a greater height.","Under their Mansion Master’s leadership, their spirit power had already reached a level they dared not imagine before. They did pay a price for it—the shortening of their lifespans—but they believed that their Mansion Master would have a countermeasure for it.","Their potential was unlimited.","But right now, they were all looking at a plate with grim faces, including Jie Tianran.","There were six beads on the plate, and one of them had shattered. These were the life beads of the six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists they had dispatched to the Immortal Sea Galaxy.","“Didn’t Xiahou Jue accompany them to the Immortal Sea Galaxy? How did this happen?”","“Could there be a treasure in the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land, and Xiahou Jue wanted to monopolize it, so he made a move against our people?”","The world spiritists threw out conjectures.","Their first thought was not that the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists had encountered a strong enemy but that Xiahou Jue had backstabbed them.","This was due to their deep-seated prejudice against the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. They didn’t think that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan could possibly kill a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, even if they had induced that galaxy-level phenomenon earlier.","Jie Tianran fell silent.","...","Meanwhile, in the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land, Little Fishy stowed away the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist she had just killed in a unique sphere. Everyone present stared at Little Fishy.","Little Fishy’s appearance had changed. She was shrouded in a layer of blue aura that resembled waves, and her pupils had turned blue like the deep sea. She was as beautiful as ever, but now, she exuded an air of enigma and grandness as well.","A pair of fins resembling majestic wings had sprouted on her back. They were extremely beautiful, as if they had been tailored for Little Fishy.","In her current state, her cultivation was no longer at rank one Heavenly God but rank four Heavenly God.","“She’s able to raise her cultivation by three ranks at Heavenly God level?”","The lunatic and the guild leader stared at Little Fishy in utmost shock.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists and Xiahou Jue were horrified as well. It was extremely rare for any cultivator to be able to raise their cultivation by a rank after reaching Heavenly God level, but Little Fishy was able to raise it by three ranks.","The gap in their talent was despair-inducing. It made them wonder if they were dreaming.","Shoosh!","Little Fishy waved her sleeves, and her blue aura rushed at the other Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","Boom!","A loud explosion followed, and the blue aura vaporized like steam. Xiahou Jue had appeared in front of Little Fishy to stop her attack.","“Looks like you were the one who induced that phenomenon. To think that a monster like you would emerge from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. I would have never believed it if I hadn’t seen it in person.” Xiahou Jue assessed Little Fishy while unleashing his rank four Heavenly God level oppressive might.","It was as if he was telling Little Fishy that he was no pushover, either.","Shoosh!","Little Fishy thrust her palm at Xiahou Jue. Her attack was so fast that the latter had no time to dodge at all.","Pah!","Shockwaves rippled as Xiahou Jue was sent flying into the distance.","At the same time, Little Fishy waved her hand. Her blue aura transformed into a scythe that reaped across space, decapitating the remaining five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","Boom!","A brilliant light suddenly shone in the distance.","Xiahou Jue reappeared on the battlefield unharmed. He was wrapped in formation armor, but the armor was covered in cracks. The formation armor was likely a protection armor, and it had automatically activated earlier to protect him from Little Fishy’s palm strike.","Xiahou Jue whipped out two golden God Armament truncheons. These weapons were the source of the brilliant light.","“That was quite a fast move. Very well, let me see what a junior like you is capable of.”","He crossed the truncheons in front of him before abruptly swinging them.","Whoosh!","An eerie growl shook the world. A humongous blood skeleton rushed at Little Fishy.","But Little Fishy was unfazed. She thrust her palm forth and destroyed the blood skeleton.","A golden light surfaced. Xiahou Jue charged up to Little Fishy and began swinging his golden truncheons like a furious gale.","Little Fishy stepped backward and dodged all the attacks.","Xiahou Jue was unable to pose any threat to Little Fishy even when he was wielding his God Armaments.","...","The ship where Jie Tianran was onboard fell silent.","The crowd fell ghastly silent upon seeing the shattered life beads.","“I’ve underestimated the Immortal Sea Fish Clan,” Jie Tianran broke the silence with a calm remark.","Unlike the others, he didn’t doubt the Netherworld Sect’s Xiahou Jue. Instead, he was certain that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan was behind this.","“Lord Clan Chief, I’m willing to head to the Immortal Sea Galaxy to investigate this matter,” a rank four Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist spoke up.","“Even Xiahou Jue is unable to curb the enemy. Are you heading there to die?” Jie Tianran scoffed.","The other world spiritists fell silent. They were convinced that Xiahou Jue was behind their brethrens’ death, but Jie Tianran was suggesting that someone else was behind this, and that someone had defeated even Xiahou Jue.","If so, the severity of this matter had far surpassed their imagination.","“I’d also like to know what lies in the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land, and I want to exact vengeance for our people as well. But we have more important things at hand. The most important thing at hand for us is to claim God’s Era’s power that has descended into our Seven Realms Galaxy.","“Our Saint-tier elders and the Shadow Corps have their hands full at the moment, so I’ll need you to claim God’s Era’s power scattered over the Seven Realms Galaxy,” Jie Tianran said.","With a wave of his hand, he conjured a map of the Seven Realms Galaxy. Some locations had been marked. These were the places where God’s Era’s power had landed.","“I don’t know what the powers that landed in the Seven Realms Galaxy are, but I want you to secure all of them,” Jie Tianran ordered.","“Understood,” The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists replied.","...","Over at the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land, Xiahou Jue’s offense intensified. He had begun unleashing martial skills, but Little Fishy continued to evade his attacks with ease.","“Junior, why aren’t you drawing your God Armament? Are you looking down on me? You must not know that I haven’t unleashed my full prowess yet.” Xiahou Jue gritted his teeth. He thought that Little Fishy was insulting him.","Clang!","A cold gleam flashed, and Xiahou Jue felt a sharp pain in his right arm.","He glanced over and saw his right arm flying off with his golden truncheon. He turned his gaze back to Little Fishy. Unbeknownst to him, she had drawn a God Armament sword and severed his arm.","“Show me your full prowess,” Little Fishy sneered coldly.","Her gaze sent shivers down Xiahou Jue’s spine. In her beautiful eyes, he saw coldness, confidence, and dominance. She was looking down on him."]},{"number":6579,"title":"Chapter 6579: Chapter 6577: Misjudged","paragraphs":["Chapter 6577: Misjudged","“Chu Feng, does Xianhai Yu’er know what Xiahou Jue is capable of?” the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader asked Chu Feng.","“She knows,” Chu Feng replied.","They had encountered Xiahou Jue together in the Immemorial Cemetery.","“She’s going easy on him despite knowing he can raise his cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level. Does this mean that...”","The guild leader’s eyes lit up. Seeing Xianhai Yu’er’s confidence, an unbelievable conjecture suddenly occurred to her.","“I wouldn’t be surprised if it’s Yu’er,” Chu Feng replied with expectant eyes.","Little Fishy was in no rush to go all out despite knowing that Xiahou Jue could raise his cultivation up to rank five Heavenly God level. That could only mean that she had the power to curb rank five Heavenly Gods as well.","“Hah...” Xiahou Jue suddenly laughed.","He hadn’t been able to react to Little Fishy’s attack at all. If she had the strength to sever his arm, she could have taken his life as well. Yet, she chose not to do so.","Is she looking down on me? Or is she that confident in herself?","“Junior, you have truly opened my eyes today. Very well.” Xiahou Jue took out a teleportation talisman, only to burn it into ashes with his martial power.","The guild leader and the lunatic were baffled by his actions.","“Interesting,” Chu Feng remarked with a chuckle.","He could tell that the teleportation talisman was the real deal. It was likely Xiahou Jue’s emergency escape method should he encounter an opponent that was beyond his means to deal with. He could have escaped with that teleportation talisman, but he chose not to.","“Today, I, Xiahou Jue, will put my life on the line to see how far the top prodigy of this era can go. If I die in your hands, at least it will be an eye-opener for me. But if you die at my hands, don’t blame me for not showing you mercy. If anything... you and Chu Feng should have never stood against our Netherworld Sect,” Xiahou Jue said as he glanced at Chu Feng.","It was a life-and-death battle, but Xiahou Jue didn’t conceal his admiration for Little Fishy and Chu Feng. This changed Chu Feng’s impression of Xiahou Jue.","He doesn’t seem to fear death. If anything, he exudes the airs of a true expert.","“You sure have a lot to say,” Little Fishy snorted.","“Hah...” Xiahou Jue smiled.","A terrifying red embryo surged into the air while expanding, enveloping the sky in the blink of an eye. It was a Netherworld Embryo!","The Netherworld Embryo quickly grew from an infant into an adult. Blood-red armor appeared on its body, making it resemble a war god that had risen from hell.","“Is this the Netherworld Sect’s means?”","Both the guild leader and the lunatic looked unnerved. They had known that Xiahou Jue could raise his cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level, but they didn’t expect him to possess such powerful means on top of that.","This completely overthrew their previous impression of the Netherworld Sect.","Once the Netherworld Embryo was done forming, it returned to Xiahou Jue’s body. His eyes turned blood-red, and he began emanating a blood-red aura. The same blood-red armor that had formed around the Netherworld Embryo earlier also formed around him now.","By this point, his cultivation had already risen to rank five Heavenly God level.","But Chu Feng and the others had their eyes on Little Fishy.","She was also emanating the aura of a rank five Heavenly God. Another pair of finlike wings had appeared on her back, but they were larger and grander this time. It gave her an imposing look.","“To think that someone can raise their cultivation by four ranks in Heavenly God level!” Xiahou Jue remarked with a laugh. His frown loosened up, and he didn’t look as conflicted anymore.","The next moment, powerful teleportation energy enveloped Xiahou Jue.","Little Fishy immediately swung her God Armament sword down on Xiahou Jue, but she was still a step too late. Xiahou Jue had escaped.","“Damn it. I’ve misjudged him.”","Chu Feng had thought that Xiahou Jue had resolved himself to put his life on the line to test Little Fishy out, but it turned out that he had another teleportation talisman in his arsenal. He had merely burned one of his teleportation talismans to make Little Fishy put down her guard, so that he could make his escape.","And it worked.","Xiahou Jue’s voice echoed from the void, “Chu Feng, I’m not afraid of death. I’m curious to see if you’ll show the same flair as this lady when you advance into Heavenly God level... though I wonder if you’ll ever get the chance to do so. The Netherworld Sect will not let you off after what you have done.”","The guild leader rolled her eyes. “He’s still running his mouth even though he has already run away. I thought he was a fearless one.”","Eggy also quickly spoke up, “Chu Feng, the origin energies! Tell Little Fishy to give me those world spiritists’ origin energies.”","Little Fishy stowed away the corpses of those Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists before flitting up to Chu Feng. She apologized with a bow, “I’m sorry, big brother.”","“Yu’er, it’s fine. We’ll get him the next time,” Chu Feng consoled her, thinking that she was feeling self-reproach for letting Xiahou Jue escape.","But Little Fishy shook her head and said, “It’s not that.”","“Oh? What is it then?” Chu Feng asked.","“I know that the beautiful world spirit big sister in your body needs origin energies, but I need these people’s origin energies as well. I’m afraid I can’t hand them over to the world spirit big sister,” Little Fishy said."]},{"number":6580,"title":"Chapter 6580: Chapter 6578: The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Quandary","paragraphs":["Chapter 6578: The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Quandary","“I’ll make it up to that big sister in the future,” Little Fishy said.","“Something is amiss here, Chu Feng. Why would Little Fishy suddenly need origin energies?” Eggy grew vigilant.","Chu Feng also noticed the same problem and asked, “Yu’er, did something happen?”","“Of course not. It’s just...”","LIttle Fishy was about to explain with a radiant smile when Chu Feng interjected, “Yu’er, don’t lie to me.”","Hesitation flickered in her eyes. “Big brother, my clan met with some trouble.”","“It’s fine, Yu’er. I’ll shoulder the burden with you no matter the situation. Tell me what happened,” Chu Feng said gently.","Little Fishy’s eyes reddened. It formed a stark contrast to her powerful aura. She might have grown stronger, but she still had a vulnerable side. Chu Feng’s presence greatly comforted her, especially because she knew that he meant those words.","Little Fishy looked at the guild leader and the lunatic and said, “Elders, my apologies but...”","The guild leader raised her hand to stop her. “I get it. You two speak.”","With that, the guild leader and the lunatic took their leave.","“Big brother, follow me.” Little Fishy made her way to the place where she emerged from.","Chu Feng followed her, and they soon arrived at a natural cavern world located at the bottom of the Immortal Sea. This was where Little Fishy had been undergoing closed-door training.","Chu Feng was perplexed.","This place was rich in the Immortal Sea’s aura, making it an ideal cultivation ground for the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, but there was no isolation barrier here. It didn’t make sense for Chu Feng to have failed to sense Little Fishy earlier.","Just then, Little Fishy opened her mouth, and a bead-sized light sphere floated out from within. This light sphere contained isolation energy that not even Chu Feng could see through.","Little Fishy formed a hand seal, and the light finally receded. Only then did Chu Feng realize that the light sphere was a formation realm. There were countless figures meditating inside the formation realm, including Little Fishy’s parents, grandfather, and older brother, Xianhai Shaoyu.","They were all cultivating, and Chu Feng could sense them improving in real-time. Little Fishy wasn’t the only one who became stronger.","The reason behind their swift growth was the golden aura. The golden aura was coming from the formation realm, and it harnessed the concentrated aura of the Immortal Sea. There was no better cultivation resource than this to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.","This should have been a good thing, but Chu Feng sensed something amiss.","He didn’t rush to voice his concern aloud. Instead, he patiently waited for Little Fishy to share her story.","“Big brother, have you heard about the story of our Immortal Sea Fish Clan and the Immortal Sea?” Little Fishy asked.","She knew that Chu Feng was lacking knowledge about the world of cultivation, particularly because it hadn’t been that long since he emerged from the Eastern Region.","“I only heard about the story after I saw the phenomenon,” Chu Feng replied.","“The story is true. Our Immortal Sea Fish Clan underwent a metamorphosis after absorbing the Immortal Sea’s energy. It paved the way for our ancestors to rise to prominence in the Immortal Sea Galaxy. That was why we set the Immortal Sea as our ancestral land.","“Not long ago, we sensed changes in our ancestral land and realized that it still retains some of its energy. We were able to tap into that energy and benefit from it. On top of that, I discovered something. The energy in our ancestral land isn’t just a cultivation resource; it is alive, sentient, and powerful. It’s similar to a natural oddity, but far stronger.","“I had tried communicating with the ancestral land, but to no avail. This time, it finally worked. My conjecture was right. Our ancestral land is indeed alive and sentient. As a result, I learned some things,” Little Fishy said.","“What is it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Our ancestral land’s energy didn’t disappear because we depleted its energy. Rather, it was devoured by a terrifying monstrous beast who lived in the vicinity,” Little Fishy replied.","Eggy spoke up, “Chu Feng, could that monstrous beast be that golden-haired woman?”","“It is possible,” Chu Feng replied.","He didn’t mention the golden-haired woman right away but instead waited for Little Fishy to continue her story.","“That monstrous beast devoured not just our ancestral land’s energy but life force as well, causing it to wither. To protect itself, our ancestral land sealed off its remaining energy and retreated deep underground. It is summoning us now not just to help us, but also in hopes that we can help it,” Little Fishy said.","“How can we help it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Our ancestral land raises our cultivation, and in return, we’ll use our powers to nourish it and restore its life force. That is what all of my clansmen are doing right now. However, we met with a quandary,” Little Fishy said with a frown.","“Yu’er, there is bound to be a solution to any problem. Tell me what’s going on, and we can brainstorm together. I’m sure we can resolve any problem,” Chu Feng consoled.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan appeared to be in a terrible position, evident from how stressed Little Fishy looked. That was why Chu Feng comforted her while probing for more information. He wanted her to know that she wasn’t alone, and he was here to help.","“Big brother, our goal is to raise our cultivation while nourishing our ancestral land, so we’re using a special cultivation method. It could be because our ancestral land is in a poor condition and is unable to control its energy, but our clansmen are unable to awaken from their cultivation.","“Even I struggled to awaken from my cultivation, even after I made a breakthrough to Heavenly God level and induced a huge phenomenon.","“I suspect that it’s not just the ancestral land’s energy binding us. An external force is at play, too. It’s a power resembling that of the ancestral land, but it is malevolent. I sensed your arrival, big brother, but I couldn’t head over to look for you.","“But for some reason, big brother, moments after you arrived, that energy suddenly vanished. That was how I managed to wake up from my cultivation and arrive in time to rescue you from danger,” Little Fishy said.","“It really is that golden-haired woman!” Eggy exclaimed."]},{"number":6581,"title":"Chapter 6581: Chapter 6579: The Means of the Demonic Path","paragraphs":["Chapter 6579: The Means of the Demonic Path","“Yu’er, since you have managed to establish communication with your ancestral land, did it tell you what the monstrous beast who devoured its energy looks like?” Chu Feng asked.","“The ancestral land doesn’t know what the monstrous beast looks like, but it seems to morph into the form of a golden-haired woman,” Little Fishy replied.","By this point, Chu Feng was certain that Little Fishy’s monstrous beast was the same golden-haired woman who snuck into his dantian.","“Yu’er, I think I have met that monstrous beast.”","“Is that monstrous beast still here?” Little Fishy’s face darkened in horror. She had heard from her ancestral land how powerful the monstrous beast was.","“Don’t worry, Yu’er. It’s unlikely that the monstrous beast will pose a threat to us for the time being, whether she’s still around or not,” Chu Feng replied.","He had made this deduction based on how the golden-haired woman hadn’t made another attempt on him despite coveting the items inside him. It could be because her injuries were too severe or that she was intimidated by the red lightning beast.","He proceeded to tell Little Fishy about what he had gone through.","“That explains the sudden disappearance of the external force! That monstrous beast tried to plunder big brother’s bloodline, only to be injured by your bloodline power. In the end, you were the one who saved me.” Little Fishy breathed a sigh of relief.","At least she was safe for the time being.","“Yu’er, will your clansmen be in danger if they continue cultivating without waking up?” Chu Feng asked.","“If left be, their sense of self may begin to erode. This may lead to them losing their memories or, in more severe cases, suffering a cultivation deviation,” Little Fishy replied.","“Are you collecting origin energies to help them maintain their sense of self?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, that’s my intention.”","Little Fishy flicked her wrist and took out a black bead inscribed with runes. It was a treasure from the Immemorial Era.","“Woah, that’s some good stuff!” Eggy’s eyes lit up. Her intuition told her the black bead was a priceless treasure.","But Chu Feng could tell that the black bead was malevolent in nature.","“Big brother, the ancestral land told me that I can maintain my clansmen’s sense of self by filling this black bead with origin energies.” Little Fishy looked at Chu Feng hesitantly. “Big brother, will you look down on me for resorting to demonic means to protect my clansmen?”","Chu Feng chuckled. “Silly girl. I have siphoned origin energies away from countless people for your world spirit big sister, but I don’t consider myself an unscrupulous person. I have my set of principles, and I only take the lives of those whom I believe deserve death.","“The people whom you have just killed have innocent blood on their hands. Just the fact they had made an attempt on our lives is more than enough reason for us to kill them. Those who seek to kill others should be prepared to die as well. Since their life is forfeit to us, we should get to decide how we want to deal with them.","“I recently killed an old leopard and obtained two rare treasures from him. To decipher those two treasures, I preserved the old leopard’s body and took it with me. In comparison, what you have done isn’t anything much. I’m sure there are people who view me as a heinous villain, but who cares? I’m not bothered by them.”","He even took out the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s corpse to show her.","“Chu Feng, Little Fishy is a young lady. You shouldn’t scare her by showing her something like that,” Eggy replied.","“Is our Eggy afraid of it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course not,” Eggy replied.","“If our Eggy is not afraid, I don’t think Yu’er will be intimidated, either. Haven’t you realized that the two of you are quite similar?” Chu Feng asked.","“How so?” Eggy asked.","“You look harmless as if anyone can walk over you, but those who dare to do so will quickly regret their action when they notice your vicious streak hidden beneath,” Chu Feng replied.","“What did you say? Do I look that weak?” Eggy put her hands on her hips as she exclaimed indignantly. She recalled how imposing Little Fishy was when she dealt with Xiahou Jue, and she added, “But yes, Little Fishy is indeed no pushover.”","In truth, Little Fishy was no weak-willed lady who would squirm at the thought of siphoning the origin energies of others. She was just concerned about what Chu Feng thought about her.","Chu Feng understood that as well, but he couldn’t help but comfort her. He and Eggy had watched Little Fishy grow up, so they felt protective of her. Even when they knew deep down that their protectiveness might be unnecessary, they still couldn’t help but care for her.","Little Fishy stared quietly at the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s carcass for a while before raising her head and beaming a smile at Chu Feng. “Big brother, it’s good to have you around.”","Chu Feng smiled in response. “No matter what you do, your standing in my heart will never change.”","“Mm.” Little Fishy nodded as her smile brightened. Her face looked bright and vibrant as if she had temporarily forgotten all unhappiness and worries she had.","“So, how do we channel this bead?” Chu Feng glanced at the black bead in Little Fishy’s hand.","The black bead appeared to be deactivated.","“The ancestral land said that there’s no way to activate this item, but it’ll awaken on its own accord now and then. Till then, I have to collect enough origin energies to feed it,” Little Fishy replied.","Weng!","The runes on the black bead suddenly glowed, and its structure changed.","“Big brother, did the black bead just awaken?” Little Fishy asked.","“Seems so,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6582,"title":"Chapter 6582: Chapter 6580: Grandmother’s Return","paragraphs":["Chapter 6580: Grandmother’s Return","“We’ll know once we give it a try.”","Little Fishy fused all the origin energies she had collected into the treasure. She looked visibly nervous, for this was the only way she knew that could save her family members.","The fusion went smoothly.","The treasure seemed to be connected to the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen, as the treasure immediately released a peculiar energy into the Immortal Sea’s realm.","While Chu Feng was unable to see through the energy, he did sense the air of bizarreness he felt from the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen lightening considerably. Despite still being petrified in cultivation, their expressions didn’t seem as severe as before.","“Yu’er, what are your plans?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’ll have to collect more origin energies, but I won’t take the lives of the innocent. I’ll only kill those who are hostile to me. I’ll head to the Seven Realms Galaxy,” Little Fishy replied.","The Seven Realm Sacred Mansion had never been on good terms with the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, and they were bound to be wary of them after the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s phenomenon.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion wouldn’t hesitate to make a move on Little Fishy if she appeared before them right now.","“Let’s go together,” Chu Feng replied.","“Hold on, big brother. I know you care deeply about my silly brother and me, but let me handle this matter by myself, all right?” Little Fishy asked. She was worried about implicating Chu Feng.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion carried an alarming level of animosity toward Chu Feng. There was no saying how far they would go to destroy him. Chu Feng would be in danger if he entered the Seven Realms Galaxy now.","“Yu’er, I was already planning to head to the Seven Realms Galaxy. You’re unaware of the changes in God’s Era because you have been busy cultivating,” Chu Feng said.","“There’s a change in God’s Era?” Little Fishy asked.","“You should take a look yourself.”","Little Fishy used her observation means to inspect the changes in God’s Era, and she was surprised by what she saw. She noticed the two bundles of power in God’s Era’s grasp. “Big brother, is that God’s Era’s power?”","“I can’t say for sure yet, but those are definitely fortuitous encounters for us. There were initially three bundles, but one of them had fallen into the Seven Realms Galaxy,” Chu Feng replied.","“Ah! You should have told me earlier, big brother! I wouldn’t have held you up if so,” Little Fishy exclaimed. She could have filled Chu Feng in about the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s plight and the golden-haired monstrous beast along the way.","“It’s fine. We won’t take long to get there anyway. Let’s go,” Chu Feng replied.","“All right.” Little Fishy nodded. She was happy to travel with Chu Feng.","So, the group made its move.","The Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader didn’t probe into the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s situation, though she couldn’t resist her curiosity to ask, “Yu’er, is rank five Heavenly God level your current limit?”","“Yes, rank five Heavenly God level is my current limit. However, I am confident in my fighting prowess. I can stand my ground even against a dozen rank five Heavenly God level cultivators,” Little Fishy hurled her fist as she spoke.","She was no longer a lass, but her demeanor was still childlike. Her eccentricity was adorable.","“That’s amazing. With you accompanying us, we would have nothing to worry about in the Seven Realms Galaxy. I have known all along that it’s only a matter of time before you juniors overtake me, but I didn’t expect the day to come so quickly,” the guild leader remarked.","She patted Chu Feng’s shoulder and added, “Chu Feng, you’ll have to buck up. I’ll be able to rely on you once you reach Heavenly God level.”","“I’ll work hard,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Little Fishy smiled as well. “Elder, you can rely on me, too.”","“Hahaha! Yes, I’m relying on you as well, Yu’er. With you two as my backing, no one will dare to trifle with me anymore!” the guild leader laughed.","Chu Feng looked at the beaming Little Fishy and heaved a sigh of relief. He had been worried that shouldering her clan’s fate would be too much stress on her, but he could tell from her smile that she was still coping well.","Little Fishy had a strong mind. She was able to bear the crushing weight of her responsibilities without suffocating.","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran and his people had arrived at the Seven Realms Galaxy.","Jie Tianran dispatched his world spiritists all over the Seven Realms Galaxy, whereas Jie Tianran himself returned to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. The strongest fragment of power had fallen into the depths of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","But when Jie Tianran returned to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, he received a surprising piece of news.","“What? Nianqing has returned?” Jie Tianran stared at the elder who reported the news in shock.","“Lord Mansion Master, Lord Nianqing has only returned recently, and she has ordered me to inform you to look for her once you return,” the elder said.","“Oh?” Jie Tianran narrowed her eyes.","Jie Nianqing was Chu Feng’s maternal grandmother. Jie Tiannian and Jie Ranqing’s names were taken from Jie Tianran and Jie Nianqing’s names.","She had been residing in the Divine Inheritance Ground, but not too long ago, it had suddenly become inaccessible.","Upon learning of the matter. Jie Tianran headed over to inspect the situation. He was unable to enter the Divine Inheritance Ground as well, but fortunately, those inside were still able to leave the premises.","Through them, he learned an important piece of news.","The Divine Inheritance Ground’s cultivation ground had opened, and Jie Nianqing was cultivating there. He didn’t know that the cultivation ground had opened because of Chu Feng, but he did know it was a huge fortuitous encounter.","Without a doubt, Jie Nianqing must have benefited greatly from it.","“Where is she?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Lord Mansion master, Jie Nianqing is in the Asura Valley,” the elder replied.","“Asura Valley?” Jie Tianran frowned, only to reveal a bizarre smile right after.","With a grand wave of his sleeve, he made his way in the Asura Valley, which was located deep within the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion."]},{"number":6583,"title":"Chapter 6583: Chapter 6581: Jie Tianran’s Secret","paragraphs":["Chapter 6581: Jie Tianran’s Secret","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had seven valleys named after the Seven Spirit Worlds. These valleys harnessed energies that corresponded to the Spirit World they were named after, and world spirits could benefit from cultivating there.","These seven valleys were from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, but after they left for the Ninth Galaxy, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion took control of them. For their convenience, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion moved the seven valleys into their base.","Despite being named as valleys, they were humongous. The largest Asura Valley was even considerably larger than the Lower Ancestral Martial Realm. It had taken quite some time back then for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to move the seven valleys into their base.","Jie Tianran made his way to the center of the Asura Valley, where a dignified old woman stood. She was Chu Feng’s grandmother, Jie Nianqing.","“Congratulations, Nianqing,” Jie Tianran said with a smile. It was rare to see such a fawning expression on his face.","In contrast, Jie Nianqing’s attitude was much colder. “Congratulations? For what?”","“I heard that the Divine Inheritance Ground’s cultivation ground has opened. The rumors must be true, considering how you are no weaker than me now,” Jie Tianran remarked.","Jie Nianqing had made no attempt to conceal her strength as a rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“I was able to make quick progress because of the extraordinary nature of the Divine Inheritance Ground. I stumbled upon a fortuitous encounter that even the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect has failed to obtain.","“Rather, I’m intrigued by how you reached rank five Heavenly Dragon in such a short time without the aid of the Divine Inheritance Ground, Mansion Master. You are an unfathomable figure, aren’t you?” Jie Nianqing remarked.","“You seem unhappy, Nianqing,” Jie Tianran said.","As they were a couple, Jie Nianqing wouldn’t address Jie Tianran as ‘Mansion Master’ in private, unless she was angry.","“Mansion Master, I have a question to ask you,” Jie Nianqing said.","“Feel free to pose your question, Nianqing,” Jie Tianran replied.","“I have heard rumors that Chu Feng is Ranqing’s child, and he has displayed extraordinary talents that have never been seen in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Yet, you refuse to acknowledge him as your grandson. Instead, you declare that you have crippled Ranqing and are planning to plunder Chu Feng’s Ruler’s Bloodline. Is this true?” Jie Nianqing asked.","“Ranqing is my daughter. I’d never hurt her. She has merely entered the Ninth Galaxy. As for Chu Feng, his very existence is a bane to Ranqing. He hinders her future. I have to reclaim his bloodline to help her fulfill her potential,” Jie Tianran replied.","“In other words, the rumors that you are hunting down your grandson is true,” Jie Nianqing asked.","“He’s not worthy of the Ruler’s Bloodline. He is an obstacle to our Ranqing. I’ll be frank with you. I have divined the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s future, and we’ll face a huge calamity in the future. The only one who can stop the calamity is Ranqing.","“Ranqing possesses the purest Ruler’s Bloodline in the world. That’s why she cannot wed anyone, or else it’ll sully her bloodline. The very fact that Chu Feng possesses a strong Ruler’s Bloodline shows that he has siphoned power away from Ranqing.","“If I don’t reclaim his Ruler’s Bloodline and return it to Ranqing, she won’t be able to grow strong enough to protect our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Jie Tianran declared.","Jie Nianqing looked shocked as if she had heard utter nonsense. “Jie Tianran, what rubbish are you spouting? This is the first time I have heard that someone with a strong bloodline shouldn’t wed and bear a child.”","“It doesn’t matter for normal bloodlines, but our Ranqing is different. She possesses the strongest world spiritist bloodline, the unparalleled Ruler’s Bloodline! She’s destined to be different from the masses,” Jie Tianran declared.","“If you believed that, why did you betroth her to Jie Mubai in the first place?” Jie Nianqing asked.","“Jie Mubai? Hmph... It’s not just Ranqing who looks down on him; I feel the same way as well. He might possess some talent, but the likes of him can’t possibly be worthy of our Ranqing. I’m merely placating him because he still has some use to me.”","“Is what you have just said true?”","“Nianqing, I wouldn’t lie to you. This is my greatest secret, and I have only told Ranqing about it. However, she didn’t believe me either.”","“Are you out of your mind? You have always been skeptical about divinations! How can you dictate what’s right and wrong for Ranqing over a mere divination?” Jie Nianqing could hardly believe what she was hearing.","“It is no ordinary divination,” Jie Tianran replied.","Jie Nianqing suddenly recalled something, and her face turned grim. “It’s the Immemorial Divination Art. Your master was planning to impart it to Daoist Starseizer, but it suddenly went missing. You took it.”","“That’s right.” Jie Tianran nodded.","“You used the Immemorial Divination Art’s forbidden skill to craft a prophecy about Ranqing and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?” Jie Nianqing asked.","“That’s right.” Jie Tianran nodded.","JIe Nianqing’s body trembled, and her breathing hastened. She looked conflicted as if she was making a difficult decision. In the end, she hardened her heart and asked the question that she had been wanting to know the answer to but dared not ask.","“Were you behind the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s tragedy back then?”","A tragedy had struck the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion many years ago.","Tens of thousands of households were massacred, but all of these households had a common trait—they had an infant who was less than a year old.","Jie Tianran replied without missing a beat, “That’s right.”"]},{"number":6584,"title":"Chapter 6584: Chapter 6582: Jie Tianran’s Twisted Logic","paragraphs":["Chapter 6582: Jie Tianran’s Twisted Logic","“Jie Tianran, you... Our predecessors trusted you to lead the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion as the Mansion Master! How can you commit such a heinous act over an illogical prophecy? That’s millions of innocent households!” Jie Nianqing trembled as she spoke with a voice quivering with rage and incomprehension.","But Jie Tianran remained calm. “I am the Mansion Master. It goes without saying that I have the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s best interest at heart. Mortal kings wage war for their nations to prosper in the future; mortal soldiers are willing to lay down their lives for their nations’ future.","“Our people enjoy exalted stature because the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is the strongest power in the world of cultivation. For the privileges they enjoy, isn’t it only right for them to make some sacrifices for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion as well?","“Most people are too weak to contribute to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s fighting prowess. If they live out their lifespan and achieve nothing in the process, they are nothing more than maggots leeching off us.","“You may think I’m cruel to sacrifice them to do the divination, but I gave meaning and value to their lives. They should feel honored that they are still able to contribute to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion despite their weakness.”","Jie Nianqing questioned, “What right do you have to take their lives? Did you ask them?”","“I don’t have to ask them. They are obliged to obey me because I am the Mansion Master. I have the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s best interests at heart,” Jie Tianran replied.","“That’s ridiculous! You wouldn’t have to do that secretly if you thought you were right. Deep down, you knew how dirty your actions were. Someone born of flesh and blood should never be able to commit such an atrocity. Even beasts wouldn’t do that. You’re less than a beast,” Jie Nianqing spat.","“Those who seek to achieve great things can’t be bound by morality. Only then can they make the right decisions. No major power in the world has clean hands. Nianqing, you aren’t a child anymore. Surely you should understand this logic?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Jie Tianran, I must have been blind. You are a selfish man. You have never cared about me, our daughter, or the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. You only want to bring the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to the top to fulfill your ego. It has always been all about yourself.” Jie Nianqing glared at Jie Tianran with cold eyes.","“Nianqing, we have been together for many years now. Is this how you view me? You may question my actions in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but you can’t question my feelings for you. Do you still remember Jie Ning?”","Jie Nianqing was taken aback. She asked with narrowed pupils, “What are you trying to say?”","“Jie Ning’s talent and background were above yours. Our elders, including my master, hoped that I could marry Jie Ning instead of you. This is the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s tradition. Through the matrimony of the strong, we can bear outstanding offspring who will prop up the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in the future. You should know that, too,” Jie Tianran said.","“I know. Someone as selfish as you would have never chosen me if Jie Ning hadn’t died a premature death,” Jie Nianqing scoffed.","“Do you know how Jie Ning died?”","“She died in a remnant while on a mission. Those accompanying her lost their lives as well.”","“I did it.”","“What?” Jie Nianqing was horrified.","“The only way I can wed you as my wife is when she’s gone. Otherwise, I can only take you as a concubine. You say that I don’t love you, but I have never taken in another woman despite being the lofty Mansion Master,” Jie Tianran said.","“Weren’t you in closed-door training?” Jie Nianqing questioned.","“I pretended to be. How else can I do it secretly?” Jie Tianran replied.","“You could have just voiced out that you didn’t like Jie Ning. You didn’t need to kill her. She would have become a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist and contributed greatly to our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had she still been around,” Jie Nianqing asked.","“You are truly naive. Things aren’t as simple as you think. We were all living under the elders’ protection then. We didn’t have the right to choose. This is the only way I can wed you as my wife.”","“You’re merely finding excuses for your actions. There are other solutions. You don’t always need to resort to such dirty methods.”","Jie Tianran suddenly laughed. “It’s fine. You can continue being the innocent woman you are. I’m here to protect you anyway.”","But Jie Nianqing only felt disgusted and enraged. She glared at Jie Tianran and roared, “Stop your hypocrisy, Jie Tianran! Ranqing isn’t around to refute your claims, and I’m sure you also feel justified about turning your back against Lord Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer. But what about Tiannian?","“Tiannian is our daughter as well, but you took her bloodline, crippled her cultivation, and even tried to take her life, all because she helped Chu Feng. Are you still a human?”","Jie Tianran flicked his wrist and took out a sphere emanating Jie Tiannian’s aura. It was her bloodline. “Look. I may have taken her bloodline, but it’s all so that she can metamorphosize. I have already planned it out for her, but Chu Feng acted on his own accord to take her away.”","“Screw you! You even ordered Tian’er to kill Tiannian. Do you think I didn’t know that?” Jie Nianqing roared. She was so angry that her face turned pale.","“I was testing him. A true expert needs to be callous. If he truly made an attempt on Tiannian’s life, I’d have stopped him and told him that he mustn’t hurt his kin no matter how callous he is,” Jie Tianran replied.","“A load of bull! You have no credibility!” Jie Nianqing roared.","“Nianqing, you’ll know what kind of person I am in the future. You’re listing my crimes to find a reason to deal with me. You might not understand me, but I know you. Since you have already made up your mind, go ahead and do it.","“No matter what preparations you have made, there’s no way you are a match for me. If you give up right now, I’ll pretend that nothing has happened. But if you insist on making a move, you shouldn’t blame me for hurting you,” Jie Tianran said as his eyes reflected a vicious glint."]},{"number":6585,"title":"Chapter 6585: Chapter 6583: Grandmother’s Strength","paragraphs":["Chapter 6583: Grandmother’s Strength","Boom!","Jie Tianran unleashed his oppressive might. His spirit power had reached rank six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“Think carefully, Nianqing,” he said with a menacing glint in her eyes.","Jie Nianqing’s robe fluttered as she unleashed her spirit power and oppressive might. She wasn’t any weaker than Jie Tianran.","“You also possess heaven-defying battle power?” Jie Tianran was shocked.","It was extremely rare for world spiritists to possess heaven-defying battle power, and Jie Nianqing had never wielded such power before.","“Jie Tianran, I am a member of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I can’t overlook what you have done to my daughter and my grandson, as well as what you have done to the people of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion for your selfish motives.","“We can settle our family issues internally, but you massacred over a million households over a meaningless prophecy. That crime has to be judged by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. In view of our couple ties, I’ll take a step back if you confess to your crimes before the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Otherwise, I’ll capture you and force you to do so,” Jie Nianqing said.","“Couple ties? I’m surprised you know that we’re a couple. A wife ought to support her husband, but the first thing you do after making a breakthrough in the Divine Inheritance Ground is to turn against me,” Jie Tianran snorted.","“Look at what you have done. How am I supposed to support you? Should I turn my back on my kin and commit all kinds of atrocities as well?” Jie Nianqing questioned.","“Nianqing, time will tell whether I was right or not. We have been a couple for many years. You should know what kind of person I am. If you stop right now, I’ll pretend nothing has happened. Otherwise, I won’t go easy on you,” Jie Tianran said.","“Jie Tianran, you still show no remorse for your actions. I’ll capture you and force you to confess to your crimes!”","Jie Nianqing formed a hand seal.","The ground ruptured, and dust gushed into the air. Countless thorned vines covered in purple flowers surged into the air while swiftly expanding in size. It only took an instant for the entire Asura Valley to turn into a sea of gigantic purple flowers.","It looked as if Jie Tianran and Jie Nianqing had stepped into a nation of giants.","But these purple flowers weren’t just big; they harnessed power that matched their sizes.","“It’s the Thorned Flower Sea Formation. Its strength is determined by the color of the flower—from weakest to strongest: white, gray, blue, purple, and gold.","“The stronger the formation, the fewer the flowers one can manifest. Plenty of world spiritists can conjure a sea of white flowers, but only the extraordinarily talented can conjure even ten purple flowers. Yet, you’re able to conjure a sea of purple flowers.","“Nianqing, I can see that the Divine Inheritance Ground lives up to its reputation. Your fortuitous encounter has advanced not just your spirit power but your world spiritist techniques as well. If your bloodline undergoes a metamorphosis as well, you may very well reach my heights,” Jie Tianran remarked leisurely while observing the powerful formation.","But Jie Nianqing was not interested in holding a conversation.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","The countless thorned vines surged around like roaming dragons, but instead of directly attacking Jie Tianran, they continuously formed layers of seals around him. As the seals stacked up, formidable oppressive might began crushing down on Jie Tianran.","This was the unique trait of the Thorned Flower Sea Formation. It heaped pressure on the enemy instead of attacking them directly. The tighter the seal, the stronger the pressure.","Without forming any hand seals, Jie Tianran unleashed 36 surges of spirit power. Each surge manifested into a golden flag that planted into the ground, forming a defensive formation that only spanned ten meters in diameter. It was very humble compared to the Thorned Flower Sea Formation, but it warded off the latter’s offense.","The Thorned Flower Sea Formation continued to stack layers around Jie Tianran, causing the pressure to further intensify, but Jie Tianran remained perfectly calm.","“Nianqing, you seem to have forgotten that I became the Mansion Master on the basis of my strength,” Jie Tianran said.","Jie Nianqing paid him no heed. She intersected her fingers and formed a series of hand seals.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","The thorned vines further increased, causing the pressure to heighten.","“It’s futile, Nianqing. You have constructed an excellent formation, but each formation has its counter. I know the counter to the Thorned Flower Sea Formation. No matter how strong your formation is, you aren’t able to defeat me,” Jie Tianran stated.","The Thorned Flower Sea Formation began emitting a purple light amid buzzing noises. It sounded as if each of the purple flowers had been granted a life of their own. The vines began moving at a faster speed, and the pressure increased at an exponential rate.","This caused Jie Tianran’s defensive formation to distort.","Jie Tianran shook his head and remarked, “Is this your last gambit? The Thorned Flower Sea Formation is very demanding in terms of spirit power, and you’re further raising its output. At this rate, it won’t be long before you deplete your spirit power. Nianqing, I can only say that you’re underestimating me.”","His eyes suddenly narrowed sharply.","A golden light surfaced before Jie Nianqing.","It was a small golden dagger that emanated a divine aura. It was covered in over a hundred golden runes, and each of these runes harnessed immense power.","Jie Tianran recognized the golden dagger right away. It was one of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s strongest slaughter formations, named Weapon of Divine Curse. The formation could be manifested as any weapon, though larger weapons were far harder to manifest.","The crux to the Weapon of Divine Curse lay not in the weapon size but the number of golden runes. The more runes there were, the stronger the formation.","And Jie Nianqing’s Weapon of Divine Curse had over a hundred runes.","This might not seem like much, but it was extremely demanding in terms of spirit power. It consumed even more power than the Thorned Flower Sea Formation.","Jie Tianran thought that the Thorned Flower Sea Formation was enough to deplete Jie Nianqing’s spirit power, but little did he expect her to construct the more potent Weapon of Divine Curse on top of that?","The Divine Inheritance Ground was indeed a huge fortuitous encounter for Jie Nianqing.","“Hah...” Jie Tianran suddenly laughed. “It looks like I underestimated you, Nianqing. The Thorned Flower Sea Formation wasn’t a last gambit but a calculated ploy.”"]},{"number":6586,"title":"Chapter 6586: Chapter 6584: Let the People of the Sacred Mansion Judge","paragraphs":["Chapter 6584: Let the People of the Sacred Mansion Judge","“It looks like you have me cornered. I need my defensive formation to withstand your Thorned Flower Sea Formation’s oppressive might, but if I don’t release my defensive formation, I’ll become a punching bag for your Weapon of Divine Curse,” Jie Tianran calmly remarked.","“Jie Tianran, I don’t want to do this either, but I can’t turn a blind eye after learning about your deeds.” Jie Nianqing channeled her spirit power into her dagger as she prepared to shoot it at Jie Tianran.","Shoosh!","A golden light suddenly pierced through Jie Nianqing’s chest and shattered the dagger before her. Taking a closer look, it was a golden dagger identical to what Jie Nianqing had manifested. However, it had over three hundred golden runes inscribed on its surface.","Jie Nianqing’s Weapon of Divine Curse was manifested with her own strength, whereas, Jie Tianran’s Weapon of Divine Curse was manifested using his treasures. He had prepared this hand a long time ago and was merely waiting for a time to strike.","Shoosh!","A formation chain surged out from the ground and bound Jie Nianqing. It was another treasure that emanated an extremely old aura. It has been buried here for a long time now.","Jie Tianran’s Weapon of Divine Curse morphed into a ray of golden light and swiftly sliced through the Thorned Flower Sea Formation, cutting it open. Then, it returned into his hand.","“Nianqing, I know why you chose to meet me at the Asura Valley. You asked me many years ago why I was reluctant to step in here; I secretly told you that the Asura Valley’s energy curbs me, makes me uncomfortable, and weakens me. You wanted to use the Asura Valley’s energy to one-up me.","“I was lying. The Asura Valley doesn’t affect me in the least. Rather, I have long concealed a Weapon of Divine Curse I constructed using a treasure here. If anyone dares to fight me here, I’d have the advantage,” Jie Tianran said.","“You were already guarded against me back then?” Jie Nianqing was shocked.","They were still a harmonious couple back then. Jie Ranqing wasn’t born yet, so there was no friction between them. Yet, Jie Tianran had already prepared a hand to guard against her.","She suddenly felt all the happiness between them was a lie all along. Perhaps she had never truly understood Jie Tianran before.","“Nianqing, you have become strong. I wouldn’t have been a match for you in a normal fight. Unfortunately, you don’t understand the importance of remaining vigilant, even against your spouse,” Jie Tianran said.","“Have you ever thought of me as your spouse? Cut the hypocrisy! Do whatever you want to me. I’d like to see if you will kill me here, or plunder my bloodline and cripple my cultivation like what you did to our daughter before using me as bait for our grandson,” Jie Nianqing sneered.","Jie Tianran walked up to Jie Nianqing and gently touched her face. His finger flowed down to her neck, her shoulder, and her arm.","But Jie Nianqing stared at him in contempt. “Why bother putting on an act? Don’t you feel disgusted?”","“Hah...” Jie Tianran chuckled, though it was hard to discern what he was feeling.","He took out a talisman paper and plastered it on Jie Nianqing’s left arm. The talisman paper fused into her left arm, and a huge formation that felt even more intimidating than the Weapon of Divine Curse surfaced.","“You...” Jie Nianqing stared at Jie Tianran in shock and fury.","That huge formation was her secret hand, but Jie Tianran had sealed it off with his talisman paper.","“NIanqing, I have underestimated you, but you, too, have underestimated me. Were you planning to commit a double suicide with me?” Jie Tianran asked.","Jie Nianqing glared at Jie Tianran, but she was helpless now.","“Ah, right.”","Jie Tianran hurled a talisman paper into the sky. The talisman paper transformed into a flood of energy that enveloped the world, emanating energy ripples as it searched for something. Under the energy ripples, a sliver of light appeared in the underground.","He reached for the sliver of light. An item rose from the ground and flew into his hand.","It was a mirror.","Jie Tianran formed a hand seal, and the mirror recorded the earlier conversation between him and Jie Nianqing.","“I’m surprised you hid it underground instead of in the sky. How meticulous. Were you planning to use this item to indict me? It’s a pity you have been outmaneuvered.” Jie Tianran clenched his fist and shattered the mirror into bits.","Most world spiritists could easily construct recording formation, but the content of the recording formation could be easily fabricated as well.","This mirror was an immemorial treasure that recorded events, but it could not be tampered with. Anything recorded by the mirror would be taken as the absolute truth. With it, she could expose Jie Tianran’s evil deeds before the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Nianqing, you wanted to have me judged by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but I can tell you right now that they won’t dare to deal with me even if they learn about my deeds. They will only remain subservient to me, for they don’t have the power to oppose me.","“I was the one who bestowed power upon them. They are counting on me to rise to greater heights. The reason I have refrained from revealing the truth is merely because it doesn’t reflect well on me or the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Jie Tianran said.","“Cut the crap! I must have been blind to have ever trusted someone like you. I concede my defeat. Do whatever you want to me,” Jie Nianqing said as she averted her gaze.","“I love you, Nianqing. How can I bear to hurt you? I was forced to do this because you kept trying to corner me, but even so, my feelings for you remain the same. I can’t bring myself to take your life.”","Jie Tianran took out a token and tossed it into the sky. Then, his voice echoed throughout the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","He called for everyone, except for those in essential positions, to gather at the square.","Then, he turned to Jie Nianqing and said, “Nianqing, you believe yourself to be the righteous one. You’d turn against your loved ones for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Let me teach you a valuable life lesson then. We shall see if the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion remembers what you have done for it. Let’s see how they will judge you and determine your fate.”","Jie Tianran carried Jie Nianqing up and began making his way to the square."]},{"number":6587,"title":"Chapter 6587: Chapter 6585: Judgment","paragraphs":["Chapter 6585: Judgment","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s square was filled to the brim, be it the seats below or the sky above it. Juniors and elders alike had worried looks on their faces.","God’s Era’s power had entered the Seven Realms Galaxy. Something huge must have happened for the Mansion Master to gather them at a crucial time like this. They didn’t know whether this gathering would bring good news or bad news.","“Young master Ling Xiao, when did you return?” a sweet voice echoed.","Those words drew countless gazes and caused a stir.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion followed a strict hierarchy. Only those of a higher stature were permitted to take a seat in the square. They were either nobles, powerful experts, or had strong backing.","And Ling Xiao was the most famous prodigy of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion before Jie Tian’s rise to prominence. He had once fought alongside Chu Feng in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith, and the two of them carried admiration for each other.","“I just returned,” Ling Xiao replied politely, but he was feeling troubled.","“Ling Xiao, I heard you have reached rank five True Dragon World Spiritist?” an elder asked with a smile. He addressed Ling Xiao politely despite being a highly-respected elder.","“Yes, elder. I have recently made a breakthrough,” Ling Xiao replied.","“I’d expect no less from our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s renowned prodigy.”","The crowd was awed. Despite having heard rumors about his breakthrough, it still astonished them to hear him speak it aloud.","“I wouldn’t have been able to grow so fast if not for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s resources,” Ling Xiao replied humbly.","“You can’t say that. The Sacred Mansion does have ample resources, but we can’t discount your talent. You’re the most talented prodigy among us aside from young master Jie Tian,” the elder said.","The crowd voiced their agreement.","“I dare not take on that title. Even Jie Baobao’s spirit power has surpassed me,” Ling Xiao said.","“Jie Baobao? Has she reached rank six True Dragon World Spiritist? Did she recently emerge from her closed-door training?”","The crowd was taken aback. Jie Baobao had been known to be a prodigy on par with Ling Xiao, but no one expected her to surpass Ling Xiao.","“She emerged from her closed-door training shortly before I returned,” Ling Xiao said.","The crowd was overjoyed.","Having such prodigies in their ranks was good news for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","While the crowd was conversing, Jie Tianran had already arrived at the square, just that he had decided against revealing himself. He entered a hidden floating palace and watched the crowd from there.","Even though Jie Nianqing was bound, Jie Tianran still settled her down in a chair.","“The show is about to begin, Nianqing,” Jie Tianran said.","His palm emanated a brilliant glow before a person toppled out from within.","“Jie Tianran, why did you capture her?” Jie Nianqing asked nervously.","The person who had dropped out from Jie Tianran’s palm was none other than Shuang Xue, one of Jie Nianqing’s aides. She had tasked Shuang Xue to protect Chu Feng, and Shuang Xue did reach out to Chu Feng, but Chu Feng rejected her protection.","Jie Nianqing had tried contacting Shuang Xue after emerging from her closed-door training, but she was unable to reach the latter. The same went for many of her old aides as well.","But the reason was apparent to her now. Jie Tianran must have picked her aides off.","“Why did I capture her? She, despite being a member of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, sided with a fugitive and secretly aided Chu Feng. Isn’t that more than enough reason for me to apprehend her? There are many more guilty of that crime as well, but I have already executed them,” Jie Tianran said.","“I was the one who issued the order. It has nothing to do with them. Release them!” Jie Nianqing shouted.","“I know that they are working for you, Nianqing, and that Shuang Xue is your aide. It’s on your account that she’s still unharmed now. I did consider sparing her, but you refused to listen to my advice and insisted on fighting me. She could have lived, but Nianqing, you doomed her.","“Don’t bother pleading for her mercy. Your time is better spent on saying farewell to her,” Jie Tianran said.","“Jie Tianran, come at me instead. Let her go!” Jie Nianqing became increasingly agitated, knowing that Jie Tianran wouldn’t hesitate to kill Shuang Xue.","Shuang Xue was not bound, but she made no attempt to escape. Instead, she walked up to Jie Nianqing and kneeled to her. “Lord Nianqing, I was useless. I couldn’t protect young master Chu Feng.”","“Don’t say that, Shuang Xue... Isn’t it the same for me as well?”","Jie Nianqing looked at Shuang Xue with melancholic eyes. She didn’t blame Shuang Xue; even she had stumbled upon Jie Tianran, after all.","Shuang Xue lost control of her emotions and cried.","“It’s about time.” Jie Tianran grabbed Shuang Xue.","“Lord Nianqing, I’m willing to continue serving you if there is an afterworld,” Shuang Xue’s voice echoed in the palace, but she had already been dragged down to the square.","She was forced to kneel at the center of the square as a sinner.","“Lord Shuang Xue?”","The crowd was taken aback, knowing that Shuang Xue was Jie Nianqing’s aide.","“I have called you here today to judge two traitors,” Jie Tianran declared. He proceeded to list Shuang Xue’s crime of secretly protecting Chu Feng.","No one dared to utter a word, considering Shuang Xue’s high stature.","“The punishment for traitors is death. Does anyone object to it?” Jie Tianran shouted.","Only then did the crowd realize what Jie Tianran was up to. They immediately roared in agreement to his verdict.","“Those who betray the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion deserve death, and this is especially true for those who have received the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s grace but still chose to turn their back on us. How should we punish Shuang Xue?”","“Strip her of her cultivation!”","“Grind her bones into powder!”","“Skin her alive and rip out her tendons!”","“We should gouge out her heart to see if it is black!”","“Throw her into a pill cauldron and burn her into ashes!”","All kinds of vicious suggestions and insulting curses were hurled at Shuang Xue."]},{"number":6588,"title":"Chapter 6588: Chapter 6586: The Sacred Mansion’s Voices","paragraphs":["Chapter 6586: The Sacred Mansion’s Voices","Jie Tianran nodded in satisfaction. “Good. That is how our Sacred Mansion sentences traitors. Anyone willing to punish the traitor, regardless of position or cultivation, is free to make a move.”","The crowd fell silent.","Even if Shuang Xue deserved death, who would dare to touch Jie Nianqing’s aide? No one would be able to bear Jie Nianqing’s wrath.","But a roar could suddenly be heard from the sky. “Shuang Xue, how can you betray the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion after accepting its grace? You deserve to die a thousand times over!”","It was a middle-aged woman with a savage face reminiscent of a demon. She unleashed a punishment formation at Shuang Xue, but her spirit power was so weak that she was unable to inflict the slightest damage on the latter’s body.","Shuang Xue was unharmed, but her heart was bleeding. The middle-aged woman who had just attacked her was so humble that most people wouldn’t recognize her, but she did. She had once helped the other party in the spur of the moment, changing her life.","That middle-aged woman had been so grateful to her then, kowtowing to her and vowing to serve her for life. Shuang Xue thought that her intervention was worthwhile then.","Little did she expect the middle-aged woman to be the first one to turn against her as soon as she was in trouble.","The middle-aged woman might be weak, but her action set a precedent.","More people attacked Shuang Xue. Countless formations rained down on her, killing her in a heartbeat and completely obliterating her corpse. Even so, more people continued to join the commotion.","Eventually, it was the minority who didn’t attack Shuang Xue. The crowd understood that this exercise was not a simple gesture to punish a traitor; more than that, it was a way to signal their unyielding loyalty to Jie Tianran.","If they refrained from attacking Shuang Xue, they could be cast under suspicion of betraying the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion as well.","Even so, several people still chose not to make a move. Ling Xiao was one of them.","“Ling Xiao, you should at least launch an attack to make your stance clear. She’s already dead anyway.”","The people around Ling Xiao tried to persuade him, but he still refrained from making a move. He didn’t think that Shuang Xue deserved death. Neither Chu Feng nor Shuang Xue had done anything wrong.","Had Jie Tianran declared Shuang Xue innocent, not a single person would have voiced their objection. But the moment Jie Tianran pronounced Shuang Xue guilty, everyone turned their backs on her, including those whom she had once helped.","Ling Xiao couldn’t accept this. This was not how the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion should be.","Jie Nianqing felt terrible as well. She had seen the people whom Shuang Xue had once helped baring their fangs at her, as if they had a deep-seated grudge against her. Her expression slowly turned impassive as she realized that it was not just Jie Tianran whom she didn’t understand; she had also never understood the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, either.","“Enough,” Jie Tianran announced.","The ridiculous corpse-whipping farce finally came to an end.","“Shuang Xue deserves to die, but the mastermind behind her has received more help from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Don’t you think she deserves death even more?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Of course!”","“She should be severely punished!”","The crowd voiced their agreement and bared their anger despite being unsure about whom Jie Tianran was talking about.","Jie Tianran raised his hand toward the sky and pulled a figure down onto the square. The clamorous square immediately fell silent.","Ling Xiao and the others widened their eyes in disbelief.","The person whom Jie Tianran had apprehended was none other than his wife, Jie Nianqing!","“Lord Nianqing?”","The crowd couldn’t believe their eyes. Jie Nianqing was tightly bound like a sinner, and she had been introduced as the other person who had betrayed the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“What’s wrong? You said she deserves death earlier. Why are you backing down now? Is it because she’s Jie Nianqing, a meritorious subject of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and my wedded wife?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Lord Mansion Master, could there be a misunderstanding?” an elder asked.","“Misunderstanding? Are you saying I’ve gotten senile?” Jie Tianran questioned.","“I was wrong!” the elder hurriedly replied as cold sweat rained from his face.","Those who wanted to persuade Jie Tianran against sentencing Jie Nianqing swallowed their words. They could tell from Jie Tianran’s attitude that he was determined to kill Jie Nianqing today.","“I won’t malign anyone, especially not my wife. However, I also will not protect anyone who undermines the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s interests. Jie Nianqing has obtained the Divine Inheritance Ground’s legacy, advanced to rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, and obtained heaven-defying battle power to surmount one rank.","“Despite receiving so much from the Sacred Mansion, she still sided with an outsider like Chu Feng and attacked me. Don’t you think she deserves death?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Yes, she deserves to die!”","The first one to voice her agreement was the middle-aged woman who attacked Shuang Xue first. Following her, more people spoke up against Jie Nianqing. It was even more clamorous than when they sentenced Shuang Xue to death earlier.","“Nianqing, you shouldn’t blame me for this. This is the people’s will,” Jie Tianran said.","Jie Nianqing maintained an impassive face, not bothering to speak up for herself.","“Hold on,” a voice suddenly echoed over the crowd.","The crowd turned to Ling Xiao, who was sitting by the corner of the square. He was the one who had interjected.","Ling Xiao stood up and first bowed to Jie Tianran before saying, “Lord Mansion Master, Lord Nianqing has contributed greatly to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in the past. Her merits ought to offset her crimes. She doesn’t deserve to die.”","Another elder berated Ling Xiao, “Ling Xiao, what nonsense are you spouting? Jie Nianqing might have contributed greatly to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but anyone who dares to attack the Mansion Master deserves the death penalty!”","More people spoke up to criticize Ling Xiao.","But Ling Xiao paid them no heed and continued vocalizing via an amplification formation, “Lord Mansion Master, even if Lord Nianqing deserves death, our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is currently undergoing a tumultuous period and urgently requires as much manpower as possible.","“Lord Nianqing wields strength comparable to a rank six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. It would be a waste to kill her just like that. I suggest making an exception in view of the current circumstances.”","Ling Xiao looked straight at Jie Tianran, hoping that the latter would spare Jie Nianqing. He knew that the crux of the situation lay with Jie Tianran; as long as Jie Tianran chose to spare Jie Nianqing, no one would object to it.","“I have personally experienced Jie Nianqing’s prowess. She is indeed formidable. If not for my preparations, I might have lost my life to her. However, it’s also because of her formidable strength that it’s dangerous to spare her life. Putting all things aside, who here, other than me, has the power to stop her?” Jie Tianran said.","Fear could be seen in everyone’s eyes. They had just murdered Jie Nianqing’s aide in cold blood, and they had already voiced their agreement to sentence Jie Nianqing to death as well. If Jie Nianqing didn’t die here, they might face her vengeance in the future.","“I have my worries and concerns, but the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion belongs to everyone. Why don’t we hold a vote to decide how we should sentence Jie Nianqing? I’m willing to spare her life if the majority chooses to grant her a second chance. Similarly, I won’t spare her if the majority wants her dead. The procedure shall be fair and square.","“Now, make your stance,” Jie Tianran said.","A buzz broke out in the crowd.","Fearing that Ling Xiao would persuade the crowd to spare Jie Nianqing, many decided to construct voice amplification formations to drown out his voice.","Ling Xiao’s face crumbled in despair. Whether it was to fawn on Jie Tianran or fearing Jie Nianqing’s vengeance, the majority of the people wanted Jie Nianqing dead."]},{"number":6589,"title":"Chapter 6589: Chapter 6587: Refined","paragraphs":["Chapter 6587: Refined","“Such is the will of the people. Everyone, I hereby declare that Jie Nianqing, despite having received the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s grace, has turned their back on us and shall be sentenced to death for her crime. We will reclaim what she has taken from us.","“I shall construct a punishment formation with a treasure to take Jie Nianqing’s bloodline and share the power she obtained from the Divine Inheritance Ground with everyone,” Jie Tianran announced.","He took out a formation plate and over a hundred talisman papers. Each of these talisman papers emanated a powerful and ancient aura.","The formation plate rose into the air and manifested into a massive, glowing formation over the square. It was a formation to refine Jie Nianqing into energy until she breathed her last.","Ling Xiao felt terror from the depth of his soul. This was not just a simple punishment; it was the means of a demonic sect.","“Lord Mansion...” Ling Xiao was about to voice his opposition when a hand grabbed his shoulder, pushing him back down into his seat.","It was Ling Xiao’s grandfather.","He sent a voice transmission to Ling Xiao, “The Mansion Master has already announced his verdict. Our clan will suffer the consequences if you continue opposing the Mansion Master. Xiao’er, you have already done what you can. Do not try to take on more than what you can chew.”","Ling Xiao felt his power and movements being sealed off. He couldn’t even speak now.","“Those who channel the formation can share the Divine Inheritance Ground’s power. There are limited slots, so we’ll go by first come first serve basis,” Jie Tianran said as he rose into the air and stepped away from the formation.","Countless figures rushed into the formation.","In the blink of an eye, the formation, which was large enough to hold over a hundred million people, was filled to the brim. Those who had hesitated had lost their chance to benefit from this opportunity.","None of those who stepped into the formation was of ordinary stature. They were all the stronger ones gathered in this square. This was a competition of speed and strength, after all. Those who weren’t strong enough wouldn’t be able to claim a spot so quickly.","Those who didn’t step into the formation, due to their humble positions, had little interactions with Jie Nianqing, but almost everyone who had stepped into the formation came from clans that had received favors from Jie Nianqing before.","Yet, they still called for Jie Nianqing’s execution, and they would resort to refining her into energy so that they could benefit from the Divine Inheritance Ground’s legacy.","“How can humans be so ugly?” Ling Xiao clenched his teeth.","“The world of cultivation has always been a cruel place where strength reigns almighty. Most people are just wild beasts cloaked in hypocrisy. How many people truly value the bonds they have forged? When interests clash, that’s when they reveal their true colors. They are merely showing their true selves now,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather said.","Weng!","The refinement formation emanated a brilliant light. The anxious crowd had begun channeling the refinement formation.","Jie Nianqing’s body began to crack. Blood flowed out from those cracks, fused into the formation, and was distributed to the formation cores, where the crowd could absorb them. It was hard to imagine the immense pain she must be experiencing.","Yet, Jie Nianqing didn’t frown in the least. She was sneering.","All of a sudden, a blood-red rune imprint appeared on her right arm.","Boom!","The blood-red imprint manifested into a gigantic formation that overlapped the refinement formation.","GAH!!!","Screams of agony followed.","The hundred million world spiritists standing inside the refinement formation screamed in pain. Their energies were being siphoned into Jie Nianqing’s body.","“You were hiding such a hand?” Jie Tianran was taken aback.","It turned out that Jie Nianqing had hidden two cards. The one in her left hand had been sealed by Jie Tianran, but the one in her right hand was far more discreet and powerful... though it was also demonic in nature.","Through the formation in her right hand, Jie Nianqing gained control over the refinement formation, turning her from the punished into the punisher.","Even though there were over a hundred million people gathered in the refinement formation, the strongest of them was only at True Dragon World Spiritist. The true elites were busy carrying out missions outside. Those left here didn’t have the power to oppose Jie Nianqing.","“Save us, Mansion Master!”","Screams filled the air.","The weaker ones exploded into bloodied mist, and their blood flowed into the formation. Others barely held on, but the severe damage to their bloodlines made it impossible for them to survive this ordeal.","“Jie Nianqing, how can you use such cruel means against your fellow members? You truly deserve to die!” Jie Tianran roared.","He took out a talisman paper covered in runes. The talisman paper transformed into an aura that enveloped him, and only then did he step into the refinement formation.","The aura quickly scattered around the refinement formation, and it didn’t take long before Jie Tianran regained control over the refinement formation.","“Jie Nianqing, you are truly stubborn. I shall personally take your life today to enact justice!”","Jie Tianran channeled the refinement formation.","Jie Nianqing’s body shattered, revealing her soul. Even her soul was being absorbed into the refinement formation.","Jie Nianqing didn’t expect Jie Tianran to have such a hand. Despite having prepared several hands, she was still outmaneuvered by Jie Tianran. Looking at the man who had slept beside her for many years, she couldn’t stop tears from flowing down her face.","She could never have thought that she would be killed by the man she loved.","Just then, a voice transmission was relayed to her ears, “Nianqing, it’s only now that you see their vile faces, but I have known all along. I granted them power to swiftly raise their cultivation, but that, in turn, depleted their lifespans. They won’t live for long. They have already paid the price for what they did to you today. So, you can leave in peace.”","Jie Tianran’s eyes hardened in coldness.","He raised his hand, and everyone inside the refinement formation was pulled into his palm. However, not a person voiced their objection. They thought that this was a necessary move for him to turn the tables on Jie Nianqing.","It could be because he had just killed a loved one, but his face was exceptionally cold. He looked at the others gathered in the square with eyes that could murder. No one dared to meet his gaze.","“God’s Era’s power has surfaced. This is a crucial moment for our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I can kill even my wedded wife; I’m sure you know the plight awaiting those who dare betray the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Jie Tianran said.","Many voices erupted in the square.","The crowd declared their unyielding loyalty to Jie Tianran. They seemed to have forgotten that the refinement formation had not just refined Jie Nianqing but a hundred million of their brethren as well. Among them were outstanding juniors who had a bright future ahead of them.","But none of those mattered now. Only their loyalty to Jie Tianran mattered."]},{"number":6590,"title":"Chapter 6590: Chapter 6588: Gathering of the Traitors","paragraphs":["Chapter 6588: Gathering of the Traitors","Shoosh!","Jie Tianran waved his sleeves. Glowing golden pills scattered like a meteor shower into each member's hand. These pills emanated the Immemorial Divine Water’s energy and God’s Era’s aura.","The stronger and more prominent members received more pills.","Everyone’s eyes lit up at the sight of those pills. Even a fool could tell that these were good stuff. It would significantly boost their spirit power.","“Traitors must be punished, but those who remain loyal ought to be rewarded. This is what you deserve,” Jie Tianran said. It was the carrot and the stick.","“Thank you, Lord Mansion Master.”","The crowd bowed.","Jie Tianran smiled. “I’m sure you can tell how formidable these pills are. But this is the tip of the iceberg of what I can give you. God’s Era’s power will only be greater than this.”","The eyes of the crowd lit up.","“Even the fragments that flew into our Seven Realms Galaxy are already formidable. If we can harness them, the benefits will be beyond imagination. Of course, it’ll be completely different if we can completely grasp God’s Era’s power.”","The crowd trembled in excitement.","Jie Tianran had helped the Saint-tier elders and other top experts make a significant leap in their spirit power after returning from God’s Era. That had greatly increased the prowess of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","It could be said that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was at its strongest ever since its ancestors left for the Ninth Galaxy in search of power.","But Jie Tianran was telling them that this was only the start? It left them wondering how far they could reach if they were to truly obtain God’s Era’s power.","“Lord Mansion Master, what kind of power lies within God’s Era?” someone asked.","“That’s the greatest power ever, even when taking the Ancient Era and the Immemorial Era into account. It’s a power that will allow us to metamorphose,” Jie Tianran said.","The mouths of the world spiritists present fell agape. Their eyes gleamed expectantly.","“I can tell you one thing straight now. The Ninth Galaxy is not the Immemorial Purgatory but the Immemorial Domain of Gods. The eight galaxies we live in are only a shell of their former selves due to something that happened in the Ancient Era,” Jie Tianran said.","His revelation sparked intense conversation among the crowd. They were taken aback, since they had never heard about this. They would have never imagined that the world of cultivation they lived in was just a wasteland.","How would the world of cultivation be in the past? And how would the Ninth Galaxy be like?","“What you’re limited by is not your talent but the present world of cultivation. The declining environment has limited your ceiling. However, the Ninth Galaxy retains its original state from the Ancient Era. The natural energies there are many times more concentrated than here, perhaps even a hundred or a thousand times. Cultivation will be smooth-sailing there.","“But we will be faced with powerhouses who have lived through the ages, powerful clans that had dominated the earlier years of the present era, and even true divine beasts like the Dragon Clan, the Phoenix Clan, and the Qilin Clan... They entered the Ninth Galaxy far ahead of us, such that we are lagging far behind them.","“God’s Era shall bridge the gap. I have decided that after obtaining God’s Era’s power, our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion will move into the Ninth Galaxy. We might be upstarts there, but our ancestors have built a foundation for us there. That, together with God’s Era’s power, will allow us to rise to the top of the world.","“By then, we will be trampling on real God Clans, not just pseudo god clans like the Totem Dragon Clan, Totem Phoenix Clan, and the Immortal Sea Fish Clan,” Jie Tianran declared.","His words sparked intense excitement among the crowd. Cheers broke out.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had just lost a hundred million world spiritists, but the melancholy had already scattered, and they were feeling more enthusiastic than ever.","With that, Jie Tianran left the square and ventured into the depths of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to investigate the God’s Era’s power. Meanwhile, the others returned to their posts.","But some people secretly left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, and it was not just Ling Xiao’s clan.","They headed to a space where the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion couldn’t survey.","Ling Xiao’s grandfather took out a token and secretly sent out a signal.","Fifty warships appeared, and they were filled with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists. All in all, there were over fifty thousand people.","These people shared the same values, and they had all received Jie Nianqing’s grace. They were extremely loyal to Jie Nianqing. Ever since God’s Era appeared, they felt that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was straying from their ideals.","They were beginning to fear Jie Tianran.","They were still proud to be members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but they didn’t want to be under Jie Tianran’s rule anymore.","So, they had been secretly planning their escape.","It was just that they couldn’t make up their mind, knowing that escaping from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was a huge crime. Jie Tianran wouldn’t let them off if he caught them.","When Jie Nianqing returned, they subtly expressed their dissatisfaction regarding the present Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to her. Little did they expect her to tell them to leave the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Since even Jie Nianqing had said so, they set aside their reservations and began secretly evacuating their clansmen here.","The last ones to be evacuated were Ling Xiao and the other more noteworthy members. They had an important task to do, and that was to move their assets out of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“How did it go?”","A group of world spiritists rushed out and gathered around Ling Xiao and the others.","They noticed that Ling Xiao and the others had grim faces. That left them wondering if Ling Xiao and the others had failed."]},{"number":6591,"title":"Chapter 6591: Chapter 6589: Supporting Chu Feng?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6589: Supporting Chu Feng?","Among the crowd, an adorable, fair-skinned woman with chubby cheeks walked over.","“Ling Xiao, did... something happen to Lord Nianqing?”","It was Ling Sheng’er, the granddaughter of the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief. On top of her eminent background, she also possessed tremendous talent. She was lauded as a prodigy who could potentially surpass Ling Xiao.","She had met Chu Feng at the Divine Inheritance Ground and became close friends with him. Afterward, she had been accompanying Jie Nianqing in the Divine Inheritance Ground.","Standing behind Ling Sheng’er was her older sister, Ling Mo’er, Jie Nianqing’s aide, Shuang Yu, Jie Yu, and the other people whom Chu Feng met in the Divine Inheritance Ground.","Ling Sheng’er’s words made everyone tense up. She had accompanied Jie Nianqing the most, so she might know things that they were oblivious about.","“Lord Nianqing and Lord Shuang Xue are dead...” Ling Xiao said.","“What?”","That came like a bolt from the blue. Everyone couldn’t believe what they had just heard.","“Audacious, Ling Xiao! How can you joke about Lord Nianqing’s life and death?” someone roared in anger.","“Ling Xiao, you can’t crack such a joke!” someone tried to mediate.","But Ling Sheng’er and the others, who had been accompanying Jie Nianqing since the Divine Inheritance Ground, revealed sorrowful looks.","Shuang Yu clenched her fists and gritted her teeth. Her eyes widened with anger and murderous intent, but she couldn’t stop the tears from flowing down her face.","She had known what Jie Nianqing was planning to do in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. She wanted to tag along, but Jie Nianqing wouldn’t permit it, knowing that this mission would be fraught with danger.","That was how Shaung Yu and Ling Sheng’er knew right away Ling Xiao wasn’t lying.","Jie Nianqing had failed and paid the price.","The others soon realized something was amiss.","Not a single person who returned with Ling Xiao criticized him after he shared the news. Even Ling Xiao’s grandfather had a heavy, grieving expression.","“Hurry up and tell us what happened!” someone urged.","“Jie Tianran killed Lord Jie Nianqing,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather replied.","“I’ll kill them!”","Killing intent flared from many of those present, and some even declared their intention to return to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Ling Xiao’s grandfather snorted, “Are you heading back to die? Do you think Lord Jie Nianqing would want you to make such a meaningless sacrifice?”","The crowd fell silent.","Even Jie Nianqing had failed to defeat Jie Tianran; the rest of them didn’t stand a chance.","“We need to continue living to avenge Lord Jie Nianqing. Only then can we do something for her,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather said.","“What do we do? What can we do?”","The crowd looked at Ling Xiao’s grandfather. They were enraged, but more than that, they felt powerless.","“If only we could contact Chu Feng,” Ling Xiao said with a sigh.","“What did you say? Are you asking us to side with Chu Feng?”","The crowd had conflicted looks on their faces.","Despite having made up their minds to leave, they still viewed themselves as members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They didn’t mind secretly helping Chu Feng out of loyalty to Jie Nianqing, but completely siding with Chu Feng meant taking a stand against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","And that was not a decision they were ready to make yet.","“We should consider Ling Xiao’s suggestion,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather spoke up.","The crowd looked even more conflicted.","“Chu Feng has amassed some influence, and he has many aces up his sleeves as well. Otherwise, our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion wouldn’t have been powerless to do anything about him to date.","“Think about what happened in the Undying Starfield. There were many experts from the Netherworld Sect there, and even Jie Tianran was there as well,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather said.","The crowd nodded in agreement. Many of them possessed observation means, allowing them to see what happened at the Undying Starfield.","The fact that Jie Tianran had been there as well meant that not even he had the power to capture Chu Feng, even when Chu Feng was prancing around right in front of him.","“Chu Feng is an incredible one. He has accomplished many formidable feats. Putting all things aside, he has achieved more than what Ranqing did back then.”","“This era is filled with talents, but none of them shine as brilliantly as Chu Feng.”","Many older ones voiced their agreement.","“All things aside, it has been prophesied that a junior will obtain God’s Era’s legacy. In other words, Jie Tianran’s greatest competitor in God’s Era is Chu Feng. Of course, the present Chu Feng still isn’t strong enough to fight Jie Tianran, but Jie Tianran is unable to do anything about him as well. However, there is no doubt that Chu Feng can surpass Jie Tianran in the future.","“But more importantly, our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has blacklisted Chu Feng and constantly made attempts on his life, but he has refrained from massacring our people on sight.","“You should have heard about how Chu Feng deals with his other enemies. He has been holding back against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, sometimes even befriending some of us. Ling Xiao, Miss Sheng’er, and Jie Yu are examples of that. He chooses people not by their talent or background but by their character,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather said.","“Chu Feng has indeed proven himself to be a principled man.”","“While he is vicious toward enemies, he has never oppressed the weak without reason.”","“Truth be told, I don’t harbor animosity against Chu Feng. I have criticized him, but that was going with the atmosphere. If anything, I do feel respect for him.”","“But... we are still from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.”","The crowd voiced their doubts.","“Elders, what does being a part of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion mean to you?” Ling Sheng’er asked. She was also in grief, but she retained her composure.","“You would pit your lives against Jie Tianran for Lord Nianqing, yet you’re worried about going against Jie Tianran’s will to befriend Chu Feng? I don’t doubt that all of us here love the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but Jie Tianran isn’t the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion!","“Chu Feng isn’t the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s enemy; Jie Tianran merely made it that way. If anything, Chu Feng is Lord Nianqing’s grandson, Lord Ranqing’s son. Were it not for Jie Tianran’s sabotage, he could have become one of the pillars supporting us.","“Chu Feng should have been the future of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but Jie Tianran ruined that for his own warped obsession. Lord Nianqing confronted Jie Tianran to seek justice for Chu Feng, but Jie Tianran would stoop as far as to kill even his wife. He is out of his mind!","“If Lord Nianqing were here, she would spare no effort to support Chu Feng. The best thing we can do for Lord Nianqing right now is to do our best to support Chu Feng as well!” Ling Sheng’er said."]},{"number":6592,"title":"Chapter 6592: Chapter 6590: God’s Era’s Qualification","paragraphs":["Chapter 6590: God’s Era’s Qualification","“Miss Sheng’er voiced my thoughts. I’ll put my all into aiding young master Chu Feng from now on. If your thoughts differ, let’s part ways here on,” Shuang Yu declared with a forceful attitude.","She had tried to kill Chu Feng in the Divine Inheritance Ground when she still didn’t know Chu Feng’s identity. For that, Jie Nianqing imprisoned her and punished her harshly, but she had no complaints.","She had been filled with guilt when she learned that the person she tried to kill was Jie Ranqing’s son, their little young master, and she considered dying to make up for her sins. Had Shuang Xue not stopped her, she would have been dead by now.","From that point on, she considered herself someone who had already died once, and she resolved to dedicate the rest of her life to making it up to Chu Feng.","“Everyone, I need not say more about Jie Tianran’s actions, but putting all things aside, there are too many maggots in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion now. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was founded to bring world spiritists together, so that we can support one another.","“However, the current Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is rife with schemes and politicking. Everyone is just fighting for the interests of their respective clans. We vowed to unite the world of cultivation, but look at how difficult it is for outside world spiritists to join us. We have long forgotten what we stood for.","“At this rate, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion will only be ruined in their hands. It’s time for something to change. Chu Feng is our hope at eliminating those maggots. He is Lord Nianqing’s grandson and Ranqing’s son. He has inherited our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s bloodline. Why should it be a sin for us to support him?” Ling Xiao’s grandfather asked.","The crowd fell silent. They found themselves unable to refute his words.","“But I’ll respect your decision. This is also what Lord Nianqing believes in. Stay if you’re willing to aid Chu Feng and avenge Lord Nianqing. Otherwise, please leave now. Be assured that even if you leave, you can still contact me if you need help. I’ll help you,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather said.","More people expressed their stance.","Some left, but most decided to support Chu Feng. Those who stayed discussed their next course of action before splitting into many teams to contact those who were indebted to Jie Nianqing and Jie Ranqing. They wanted to rally them under Chu Feng to bolster his influence.","Of course, the people they were contacting had to be reliable as well. If a traitor reached out to a Saint-tier elder from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, they could potentially be destroyed.","While gathering more allies, they would also find ways to gather information about Chu Feng. Their ultimate goal was to support him, after all. They knew that there was little they could do to help him at this juncture, but that would be their life from now on.","...","In the meantime, Chu Feng, Little Fishy, the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader, and the lunatic entered the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but they split into three teams.","The guild leader and the lunatic went on their separate ways to other realms, whereas Chu Feng and Little Fishy made their way to an Upper Realm.","Chu Feng remembered where all God’s Era’s power fragments went. The fragment that went into this Upper Realm appeared weak, but looks were deceiving. There was something more to it. He couldn’t put his finger on what it was, but he had a feeling it would be of great importance.","The changes in God’s Era caused a huge uproar in the world of cultivation.","It was not just the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion that dove into action. Some of the bolder powers and cultivators also rushed to the Seven Realms Galaxy, hoping to get something good.","While Chu Feng thought the fragment in this Upper Realm was important, the other larger fragments were important, too. That was why they had split into three groups. The guild leader and the lunatic would go after other fragments, while Chu Feng and Little Fishy investigated the situation here.","Chu Feng constructed a formation from space to observe the Upper Realm. He took turns assessing it using his Heaven’s Eye and Three Realms Divine Eyes to capture the changes in the realm.","“Yu’er, I can protect myself. You don’t have to accompany me. Why don’t you secure the other power fragments instead? I’m worried that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion will beat us to it if we’re late,” Chu Feng said.","He wouldn’t have urged Little Fishy to leave under any other circumstances, but her family was currently trapped in their ancestral land. She needed power right now to save them. The crux of it appeared to be natural energies, but God’s Era’s power might help as well.","“I want to stay with big brother,” Little Fishy replied with a sweet smile. She was worried about Chu Feng despite knowing he had tricks up his sleeves.","“All right. I’m almost done here.”","Chu Feng decided to respect Little Fishy’s decision. Besides, her presence here was indeed reassuring, considering how powerful she was now.","“It’s done. There’s indeed something important hidden here,” Chu Feng exclaimed in excitement.","“What is it, big brother?” Little Fishy asked.","“It’s related to the power inside God’s Era. That power can’t be simply obtained. It demands stature and qualification. There is a way for us to obtain the qualification here. Yu’er, I’ll teach you a method right now. If you can grasp it, you will be qualified to compete for the true power inside God’s Era.”","Chu Feng taught the method he had deciphered from the realm to Little Fishy. Then, he sat down with crossed legs, closed his eyes, and began sensing the realm with his heart.","Little Fishy did the same as well. She quickly realized that Chu Feng was telling the truth.","The Upper Realm felt like a manual, but only those talented enough could decipher it. The manual was not easy at all. Little Fishy was able to scrape the surface, but soon, she had no choice but to concede that it was beyond her means.","So, she gave up and instead quietly observed Chu Feng. A smile slowly formed on her lips as she looked at his serious expression.","As the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s princess, she shouldered the fate of her brethren. She might behave like an eccentric child with no worries or concerns at times, but she had long understood and accepted her fate. She had ambitions as well.","But whenever she was standing before Chu Feng, she felt like those things didn’t matter. As long as she could be with him, nothing else mattered.","...","A massive formation towered in mid-air.","A steady stream of energy seeped out from the underground and flowed into the formation. It was the God’s Era’s power that had landed in the Seven Realms Galaxy, and it could be used for cultivation.","“Yes, it feels right. I can finally use what I obtained from God’s Era,” Jie Tianran said as he took out a copper mirror."]},{"number":6593,"title":"Chapter 6593: Chapter 6591: Claiming the Initiative","paragraphs":["Chapter 6591: Claiming the Initiative","The copper mirror had an unusual design, where nothing could be seen on its reflective surface. It was not that the copper mirror was useless; it was just sealed.","Jie Tianran had been trying to unseal the copper mirror, but to no avail. But now that he had extracted God’s Era’s power, the copper mirror was finally reacting as if it were being summoned by something.","From this, he deduced that the key to unsealing the copper mirror was the God’s Era’s energy.","So, he channeled all of God’s Era’s energy into the copper mirror, and the copper mirror absorbed it all.","“Jie Tianran, is there a need to activate the copper mirror? You should be able to advance your spirit power considerably if you absorb the energy. It might even be enough for you to reach rank six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist,” the old entity inside Jie Tianran asked.","“My goal is God’s Era’s true power, which lies in those three doors. That power is bound to be many times greater than this. This copper mirror is my biggest gain from God’s Era, and it took me some effort to acquire it. If I can unseal it, I dare say that I can obtain far more than just this energy,” Jie Tianran replied.","“Not bad. You’re able to resist immediate temptations and set your eye on the future. I didn’t choose the wrong person,” the old entity replied with a laugh, as if what he had just said was just a test.","The power fragment that dropped into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was the largest one of all power fragments, but it didn’t take long for the copper mirror to absorb all of it. The copper mirror did look brighter than before, but it wasn’t unsealed yet.","“It’s not enough. Are you going to continue?” the old entity asked. The results were unsatisfactory, so he wondered if he should advise Jie Tianran to give up on the copper mirror. However, he posed it as a question to Jie Tianran instead of saying it outright.","“I’ll continue,” Jie Tianran replied.","“Are you sure? Unsealing the copper mirror is probably more important in the long run, but cultivation is all about channeling resources into the right places at the right time. You'll only be wasting your effort if you go down the wrong path. Sometimes, you need to have the flexibility to change paths when the one you’re treading on doesn’t seem right,” the old entity said.","“Don’t worry, elder. I’m certain that the energy is intended to unseal this copper mirror, not for cultivation. This is a test from God’s Era,” Jie Tianran replied.","“All right. Let’s hope you’re right about this,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran decided to personally venture out of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to collect the other power fragments. Just then, an elder suddenly approached him.","“What happened?” Jie Tianran asked.","The elder was one of the elders in charge of observing the changes in God’s Era. Something must have happened to God’s Era.","“Lord Mansion Master, there’s a change in God’s Era. I think it’ll be better for you to take a look yourself,” the elder replied.","He thought that Jie Tianran would head to their observation formation, which was known to be the strongest one in the world of cultivation, but Jie Tianran didn’t have the patience for that.","Jie Tianran took out an observation treasure, channeled it, and pointed it toward God’s Era. What he saw filled him with delight. Something had appeared behind God’s Era’s humongous silhouette, and it shared the same aura as God’s Era. It was still a vague outline, making it hard to make out what it was.","Jie Tianran took out his copper mirror.","The elder looked at the copper mirror and exclaimed in astonishment, “Lord Mansion Master, could it be...”","The item that had appeared behind God’s Era resembled the copper mirror!","“I obtained this from God’s Era. It looks like I have taken the lead in this race,” Jie Tianran declared proudly. He was confident that the changes in God’s Era had arisen from the copper mirror in his hand.","“My deepest respect for the Mansion Master.” The elder bowed deeply to Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran smirked in glee. He asked the old entity, “Elder, do you think I should continue using the power fragments from God’s Era to continue unsealing the copper mirror?”","“It looks like you have made the right bet this time,” the old entity conceded.","Jie Tianran’s smile widened. This proved that his judgment had surpassed the old entity.","...","Meanwhile, Little Fishy’s eyes suddenly lit up.","Chu Feng had begun emanating a powerful, divine aura identical to God’s Era’s. Moments later, the aura seeped back into his body, becoming one with him. Then, he opened his eyes.","“Big brother, did you succeed?” Little Fishy asked.","“I think so,” Chu Feng replied.","“I noticed your body emanating an aura identical to God’s Era. What is that?” Little Fishy asked out of curiosity.","“It’s the thing hidden inside that Upper Realm. I’m not sure what it is for yet, but I should have obtained the qualification to obtain God’s Era’s true power,” Chu Feng replied.","“You must have. I couldn’t even decipher the qualification inside there,” Little Fishy said.","“Ah, it looks like only one person can decipher it.”","Chu Feng sensed the Upper Realm once more, and he realized that he couldn’t decipher it anymore. From that, it was evident that only one person could decipher the hidden qualification. This verified his conjecture that the power hidden in the Upper Realm was the qualification.","“Big brother, where should we head next?” Little Fishy asked.","“Let’s first collect the power fragment here. It might not be much, but it still counts as something,” Chu Feng replied.","“All right.” Little Fishy nodded. “Speaking of which, big brother, I have been thinking that this Upper Realm’s name sounds oddly familiar, and it just occurred to me why.”"]},{"number":6594,"title":"Chapter 6594: Chapter 6592: Mother’s Domain","paragraphs":["Chapter 6592: Mother’s Domain","“Your mother has built a cultivation ground and a palace in this realm. It’s rumored to be gorgeous,” Little Fishy said.","“Oh? I think I know where we are then,” Chu Feng replied.","He had come here in search of the hidden qualification, but one of God’s Era’s power fragments had fallen here as well. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had dispatched its manpower to all the places where the power fragments had fallen to obtain them.","He didn’t bother searching the Upper Realm because he didn’t think much about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion; he figured that he would first obtain the qualification, swipe away the power fragment, and make a clean retreat afterward.","But now that he learned that his mother’s palace was here, his interest was piqued.","So, he began taking a closer look at the Upper Realm via the observation formation. The image slowly grew clearer and clearer.","“Hm? It’s them.”","Chu Feng and Little Fishy were surprised. A formidable defensive formation had enveloped the cultivation ground, and there was a huge army outside the defensive formation.","Someone was invading the cultivation ground.","...","Millions of Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists were stationed inside the cultivation ground, though most of them were juniors. Be them elders or juniors, they were all channeling the defensive formation.","The strongest ones among them were two pinnacle True Dragon World Spiritists. One was a yellow-faced elder, whereas the other was a bearded elder.","Despite having two pinnacle True Dragon World Spiritists holding fort, the defensive formation channeled by millions of world spiritists was still on the brink of collapse.","The cultivation ground was attacked by a huge army that covered not just the ground but the sky as well. They resembled locusts from afar, but they were monstrous beasts—hundreds of millions of them.","There was no lack of True God level cultivators among the monstrous beasts, and over a hundred had reached pinnacle True God level. What made them even more terrifying was their ability to resonate their bloodlines to construct a powerful formation.","This pushed the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists to their limits.","Even the defensive formation Jie Ranqing had personally constructed with a treasure back then had started cracking.","“I don’t know who you are, but I’m guessing you are from an Ancient Era’s race. You might not know that this is the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s turf. Our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is the strongest power in the world of cultivation. You won’t be able to bear the consequences of offending us. However, the ignorant can’t be blamed. If you retreat now, I’ll plead on your behalf to the Mansion Master to let this matter go,” the bearded elder shouted.","He was a more senior member of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and boasted vast knowledge about the world, even though his spirit power had only recently soared to pinnacle True God level.","He didn’t recognize the monstrous beasts. From that, he deduced that the other party might be an Ancient Era’s race that had just emerged from their seclusion. He knew that there was no point in intimidating them, since they still thought that they were bigger than the world.","The only way was to negotiate with them.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng also noticed the monstrous beast army through his observation formation, and he let out a helpless smile. It just so happened that he had met their clan chief not too long ago at the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land.","The monstrous beast army belonged to the Cloud Leopard Clan.","...","The Cloud Leopard Clan was oblivious to Chu Feng’s prying eyes, and they also didn’t know that their clan chief was dead.","Their ambition and pride were swelling, especially since they were on the verge of defeating the considerably strong Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Listen well! We are from the Cloud Leopard Clan,” the leader of the monstrous beast army shouted. “The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, is it? It looks like you aren’t too weak, but you were only able to dominate the world of cultivation because we were in seclusion. Things are different now. Listen well! Soon, your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion will be vanquished from the face of the world. Our Cloud Leopard Clan shall be the one to unite the world of cultivation!”","The leader turned to his clansmen and roared, “My clansmen, the people here are probably of considerable fame. After we breach their formation, we shall kill the men and capture the women to serve as our maids!”","The Cloud Leopard Clansmen responded with thunderous cheers reminiscent of beast howls. Their eyes reddened from zealousness.","In contrast, the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were plunged into despair. They could see what was happening outside the defensive formation, and they could imagine the plights awaiting them once their defensive formation shattered.","The younger women shuddered in fear.","Amid despair, a beautiful, fair-skinned girl reached into her Cosmos Sack and pulled out a dagger. This dagger was imbued with a formation that disintegrated the body of anyone it plunged into.","Yet, she directed that formation dagger at herself. She was ending her own life!","Another woman hurriedly grabbed the dagger and stopped her. “What are you doing?!”","“Lord Fu Xing... I-I don’t want to be sullied by those disgusting beasts. I’d rather end my own life and preserve my honor,” the girl replied while shivering.","Lord Fu Xing was a junior as well, and she was from a noteworthy background. She was a member of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, and she had worked together with Chu Feng during the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s entrance examination. She had her reason for infiltrating the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, and with her talent, she steadily climbed up the ranks and built a reputation for herself.","“Don’t worry, we’ll leave this place alive,” Fu Xing promised.","The girl nodded, though she remained skeptical.","Fu Xing was strong, but only among juniors. This was a situation beyond juniors like them. Practically everyone other than Fu Xing felt hopeless about the situation, including the two pinnacle True Dragon World Spiritists.","More cracks had appeared in the defensive formation in the meantime. Once the defensive formation shatters, they would be powerless before the Cloud Leopard Clan’s onslaught."]},{"number":6595,"title":"Chapter 6595: Chapter 6593: Amid Despair","paragraphs":["Chapter 6593: Amid Despair","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, regardless of background or realm, whipped out their forbidden medicine, talisman papers, and treasures. Some were prepared to fight the Cloud Leopard Clan to the bitter end.","But more were afraid of being captured and tortured, and they would rather end their lives.","The girl closed her eyes, not daring to look at the Cloud Leopard Clansmen’s salivating faces. She tightly clutched her dagger. She was ready to plunge it into herself as soon as she heard the defensive formation shatter.","Boom!","A loud explosion echoed in the distance, prompting the girl to open her eyes.","She looked over and saw a brilliant light pillar falling from the sky upon the Cloud Leopard Clansmen. Blood splattered. Those that came into contact with the light pillar were torn to shreds and reduced to a blood fog.","Upon closer examination, the light pillar was actually a gigantic sword, and it wielded power above that of True Dragons and True Gods.","The girl widened her eyes in disbelief.","For a moment there, she even forgot her fear. Disaster had abruptly befallen the enemy who had struck such deep fear into her.","The gigantic sword was like divine retribution, slaying the Cloud Leopard Clansmen. This horrified not just the Cloud Leopard Clansmen but the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion as well.","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion could tell that this was not their reinforcement, for the gigantic sword of light was not manifested from a formation. It was the means of a cultivator.","“A clan of beasts indeed,” a voice echoed from the sky, overshadowing the Cloud Leopard Clansmen’s roars and screams.","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion looked over, and their faces warped in shock.","“Chu Feng?”","“It’s Chu Feng?”","“That person beside him... Is it Xianhai Yu’er?”","They were conflicted to see Chu Feng here. They didn’t expect Chu Feng to appear here, but even more so, they didn’t expect Chu Feng to save them from the Cloud Leopard Clan. Didn’t Chu Feng have an irreconcilable grudge against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?","“Who are you? How dare you attack us? Do you know who we are?”","The leader of the monstrous beast army glared at Chu Feng, but he couldn’t conceal the fear in his eyes. He could sense the aura of a rank one Heavenly God level cultivator from Chu Feng. That was not a level they could match.","“I know. You are scums from the Ancient Era, the Cloud Leopard Clan, right?” Chu Feng replied with a laugh.","“How dare you make a move on us when you know that we’re from the Cloud Leopard Clan? You must not know how strong we are. Our clan chief is a Heavenly God level expert. He will destroy your clan for daring to harm our clansmen! If you back down now, I’ll talk to our clan chief and ask him to spare your life,” the leader of the monstrous beast army said.","The bearded elder from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was startled. Isn’t that what I just said?","“Your clan chief?” Chu Feng’s smile deepened. “I doubt you’ll recognize him even if he appears in front of you right now.”","He reached into his Cosmos Sack and pulled out the Cloud Leopard Clan’s Clan Chief’s carcass.","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion widened their eyes in realization. They could tell that the carcass belonged to a Cloud Leopard Clansmen. Chu Feng must have beef with the Cloud Leopard Clan as well. He isn’t here to help us; he’s just after them.","However, the Cloud Leopard Clan reacted more vehemently.","“Lord Clan Chief!”","Cries filled the air. Some of them even burst into tears. It was just a carcass, but they could still recognize at a glance that it was their clan chief.","“Good eyes. I didn’t expect you to recognize him like that,” Chu Feng said mockingly.","By now, it had become clear to the Cloud Leopard Clansmen that Chu Feng had murdered their clan chief.","Their leader roared in anger, “He killed our clan chief! We must avenge him!”","But what happened next was that most of the Cloud Leopard Clansmen scattered in all directions. Only a small handful of them charged at Chu Feng; most of them had chosen to flee.","Chu Feng swung his Monster Slayer Sword.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","Humongous sword arcs rippled one after another, massacring the Cloud Leopard Clansmen in masses. In a matter of moments, the hundreds of millions of Cloud Leopard Clansmen were all devoured by the sword arcs and vanished.","There was not a single survivor.","“Heavens. This is Chu Feng...”","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were stupefied, especially the juniors. Goosebumps covered their bodies as their hearts shuddered in shock. They had long heard about Chu Feng’s strength, but they didn’t expect him to be this powerful.","To think that he had surpassed True God level! The Cloud Leopard Clansmen had felt like insurmountable obstacles to them, but he killed them with such ease.","But Chu Feng couldn’t care less about their thoughts. The Cloud Leopard Clansmen were a small deal to him. He formed a hand seal, and the devastating sword arcs converged into two small bundles of light that flew into his hands.","One contained the Cloud Leopard Clansmen’s treasures. Chu Feng stowed it away.","The other contained the Cloud Leopard Clansmen’s origin energies.","“Yu’er.” Chu Feng handed the origin energies to Little Fishy.","“Big brother, you should give it to big sister instead. You were the one who dealt with them. I can gather the origin energies I need myself...”","But Chu Feng stuffed the origin energies into Little Fishy’s hand. “This is also what your big sister wants.”","To prove that he wasn’t lying, a world spirit gate opened, and Eggy’s voice echoed from within, “Be good, Yu’er. These origin energies aren’t very useful to me. You should take them instead.”","Eggy’s voice was gentler than usual. It was rare for her to speak so gently, even to Chu Feng. This showed how much she liked Little Fishy.","Little Fishy smiled sweetly upon hearing those words. “Thank you, big sister, big brother.”","She finally accepted the origin energies with a grin. However, she also marked down this debt so that she could repay this favor several times in the future.","With this, Chu Feng finally turned his gaze to the cultivation ground."]},{"number":6596,"title":"Chapter 6596: Chapter 6594: Troublemaker","paragraphs":["Chapter 6594: Troublemaker","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion trembled in fear under Chu Feng’s gaze. Most of them averted their eyes; very few dared to meet his gaze. They had long heard about Chu Feng’s means, but the sight of him massacring hundreds of millions of lives without blinking made them realize just how callous he could be.","And this was the man wanted by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Could they possibly survive this encounter?","“Thanks, Chu Feng,” a familiar voice echoed from the cultivation ground. It was Fu Xing.","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion turned to look at Fu Xing. Her words suggested that Chu Feng was here to rescue them.","“I’m not here to save you. I don’t want them to ruin my mother’s palace,” Chu Feng replied.","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were taken aback. It turned out that Chu Feng didn’t attack the Cloud Leopard Clan because of the grudge between them; it was simply because they attacked this place.","Shoosh!","Chu Feng landed in the cultivation ground.","“Are you going to preserve this defensive formation by letting me in, or shall I split it open and enter by myself?” Chu Feng asked with the Monster Slayer Sword in hand.","“You...”","The pinnacle True Dragon yellow-faced elder was infuriated to hear such arrogant words. He wanted to berate Chu Feng, but the sight of the other party’s Monster Slayer Sword made him swallow his words.","He dared not even express his anger at Chu Feng and averted his eyes.","The bearded elder took out a token and formed a hand seal, opening a door for Chu Feng to pass through.","No one voiced their complaint. They knew that this defensive formation couldn’t stop Chu Feng. The wiser decision was to let him in.","The moment Chu Feng stepped in, he formed a hand seal, and a sacred aura rose from the ground. This was the God’s Era’s power fragment that had fallen into this realm.","The faces of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members darkened. They had known that a God’s Era’s power fragment had fallen into this realm, and they had been racking their brains for a way to extract it. However, nothing worked.","They didn’t expect Chu Feng to pull off something that had confounded them so easily. Seeing him taking away such a valuable resource pained their hearts, but they did not attempt to stop him, including the yellow-faced elder.","“You’re free to make a move if you have dissatisfactions,” Chu Feng specifically looked at the two pinnacle True Dragon elders as he said those words.","Both the bearded elder and the yellow-faced elder kept their heads lowered.","But Chu Feng didn’t let things slip just like that. He swiped away the defensive formation’s token in the bearded elder’s hand, saying, “The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is not worthy of taking what my mother has left behind.”","He waved his sleeves, and a powerful wind rose from the ground. All of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members, regardless of spirit power, were blown out of the cultivation ground like autumn leaves.","Only Fu Xing managed to land gracefully, but she knew that this was not because of her skills. Chu Feng had gone easy on her.","After evicting the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members from the cultivation ground, Chu Feng flew into the air and constructed a spatial formation. The spatial formation descended from the sky and enveloped the cultivation ground, overlapping with it.","Everyone knew what Chu Feng was up to. The yellow-faced elder harrumphed. “He thinks that he can just take our cultivation ground. He must not know about our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s means. This land shall either remain here or be destroyed. There’s no way he can take it away.”","Right after those words were spoken, the yellow-faced elder stiffened up.","Chu Feng’s spatial formation fused impeccably with the cultivation ground. Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and the massive cultivation ground vanished into thin air—or to be more exact, it had been compressed into a small bead and fell into Chu Feng’s hand.","He had succeeded!","He was planning to leave after stowing away his mother’s cultivation ground and palace, only to stop upon hearing a feminine voice.","“Thank you, Chu Feng.”","It was the girl who had attempted suicide. Her face was covered in dust due to Chu Feng’s earlier eviction, but she didn’t look angry in the least. Rather, she bowed deeply to Chu Feng.","“Thank you for saving us, Chu Feng.”","“You have my gratitude.”","More people thanked Chu Feng afterward. Most of them were juniors, but there were some elders as well.","“Audacious! You all...”","The yellow-faced elder was going to berate the girl and the others, but the bearded elder stopped him and shook his head.","“We would have been dead if not for Chu Feng. If he wanted to, he could have killed us even now,” the bearded elder said.","The yellow-faced elder sighed. There was no denying that Chu Feng had saved them.","Chu Feng was surprised by their gratitude, but he didn’t respond. He merely glanced at them before flitting off. He didn’t leave the realm, instead heading to a place some distance away from the cultivation ground.","He was alone now.","Moments later, a familiar figure appeared in front of him. It was Fu Xing.","They might not have talked out loud earlier, but they had secretly exchanged voice transmissions. Fu Xing wanted to have a chat with Chu Feng.","Chu Feng hadn’t interacted much with Fu Xing, but they had worked together for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s entrance examination and exchanged secrets while facing the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s trial. This experience led him to view Fu Xing as a friend.","That was also why he was moving alone now. He trusted Little Fishy, but he had also promised Fu Xing to keep her identity as the successor of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect a secret.","“It’s been a while,” Chu Feng said with a smile.","“Yes, it has been a while,” Fu Xing replied. “Actually, it hasn’t been that long, but many things have happened since. I thought you wreaking havoc in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was already ridiculous as it is, but you did far more afterward. You really are a troublemaker.”"]},{"number":6597,"title":"Chapter 6597: Chapter 6595: Joining Hands with the Celestial Master Sacred Sect?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6595: Joining Hands with the Celestial Master Sacred Sect?","“Haha!” Chu Feng laughed the remark off before asking, “What about you? Did you obtain what you wanted?”","Fu Xing had never revealed her agenda, but for the successor of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect to join their nemesis, she was bound to have an ulterior motive.","“Yes, and I’m ready to leave the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Fu Xing replied.","“Were you the one who took away the treasure in my mother’s cultivation ground?” Chu Feng suddenly asked.","Fu Xing frowned with a hint of guilty conscience, but she still asked, “How did you know?”","“That cultivation ground is supported by a treasure, and the loss of the treasure will lead to it being crippled within a hundred years. I’ve never seen the treasure before, but I can tell it has only been recently removed. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has no reason to do that out of a whim. You are the biggest suspect,” Chu Feng replied.","“My apologies, Chu Feng. I know Elder Jie Ranqing means a lot to you, and you cherish the things she left behind, but this item is important to me. I can compensate you in other ways,” Fu Xing said apologetically. She took out a Cosmos Sack and handed it to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng didn’t take the Cosmos Sack. “Fu Xing, do you consider us friends?”","Fu Xing took a moment to think about it before nodding. “I do.”","“Then say nothing more. Since you need it, I’ll make a decision on my mother’s behalf and give the treasure to you,” Chu Feng replied.","Fu Xing was taken aback. She thought that Chu Feng would fault her for taking away the treasure, but the outcome was completely unexpected. This showed that Chu Feng truly saw her as a friend, and it was not just lip service.","It was only now that she felt the weight of what it meant to be Chu Feng’s friend.","“Thank you, Chu Feng,” Fu Xing said.","“You already said that we are friends. There’s no need to thank me,” Chu Feng replied nonchalantly.","What he didn’t know was that Fu Xing was not thanking her for not pursuing this matter but for viewing her as a friend.","“Chu Feng, I’ll tell you the truth then. I infiltrated the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to retrieve our Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s treasures. These treasures are important for my elders’ recovery. The treasure that Elder Jie Ranqing used to construct the cultivation ground belongs to our Celestial Master Sacred Sect as well.","“I don’t mean to blame anyone by saying this. I know that Elder Jie Ranqing is a good person. I’m just saying that my master and the other elders of my Celestial Master Sacred Sect should be able to recover soon with the aid of the treasure. There aren’t many of us, but we are still a sizable force. We might be able to join forces against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Fu Xing said.","“Of course. If a chance arises, let’s work together,” Chu Feng replied.","He sensed that Fu Xing was currently moving under orders, so it would be hard for her to call the shots on matters like this. While he had a good impression of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, that didn’t mean that their sectmembers were good people.","He had to first interact with them to know for sure.","“Chu Feng, how do I contact you?” Fu Xing asked.","“You can relay your message to me at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city,” Chu Feng replied.","He was constantly on the move, and the other channels to contact him weren’t as reliable. The most reliable way was through the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect, as not even Jie Tianran was able to do anything about it.","“Looks like the rumors are true. You have snatched the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy from Jie Tianran,” Fu Xing remarked.","She might have joined the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but that didn’t mean she was privy to its secrets, especially when it came to news that painted Jie Tianran in a bad light. She had only heard rumors about it, but she couldn’t confirm it since it was too shocking.","Chu Feng nodded. “Mm.”","“Your rank one Heavenly God level cultivation comes from that sword, right?” Fu Xing asked.","“That’s right.” Chu Feng nodded.","“What’s your current cultivation level then?” Fu Xing was intrigued.","They had been prodigies on the same level back then, so she was curious to know if there was a gap between them right now.","Chu Feng unleashed his martial power and spirit power simultaneously.","“How in the world do you cultivate so quickly? And in both spirit power and cultivation as well!” Fu Xing widened her eyes in disbelief. Even someone as composed as her was shaken up upon sensing Chu Feng’s current strength.","Despite knowing that Chu Feng would pull ahead of her, she didn’t expect him to have reached pinnacle True Dragon and pinnacle True God. That dealt a blow to her.","Chu Feng had reached the peak of what everyone thought was possible before God’s Era opened. Even now, it was still a considerable level. Had it been years ago, no one would have believed that a junior could reach this level.","“What about you?” Chu Feng asked.","“You can already feel it, right?” Fu Xing released her aura—rank two True Dragon.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion hasn’t been treating you well,” Chu Feng remarked.","Given Fu Xing’s talent, she should have been able to pull even further ahead with sufficient resources.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion did distribute good resources to me, but I sensed something amiss and dared not use them. Maybe I was thinking too much into it. Chu Feng, won’t you help me take a look at them?” Fu Xing passed a few pills to Chu Feng.","These pills were cultivation resources harnessing tremendous energy. They contained a huge amount of Immemorial Divine Water.","“Did the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion give it to you?” Chu Feng asked.","“Jie Tianran forged them after returning from God’s Era. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders made huge progress in their spirit power thanks to them. Juniors aren’t entitled to them, and I only received them by special exception,” Fu Xing said.","“Special exception? Are Ling Xiao and the others using this cultivation resource as well?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’m not sure, but I’m the only one among the juniors I know to receive them,” Fu Xing replied.","“These pills contain a huge amount of Immemorial Divine Water. It is beneficial to raising one’s spirit power, but it comes with huge side effects. Taking in so much Immemorial Divine Water is bound to be detrimental to your body. Jie Tianran should be aware of that.”","As much as Chu Feng detested Jie Tianran, he had to acknowledge the latter’s capability."]},{"number":6598,"title":"Chapter 6598: Chapter 6596: Refining With Heavenly Lightning","paragraphs":["Chapter 6596: Refining With Heavenly Lightning","“Is Jie Tianran in such a rush? “","Chu Feng was confused. These things were detrimental to the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, after all.","To be certain, he constructed a formation to do a closer examination of the pills. He even resorted to his Heaven’s Eyes. The result surprised him.","“Is Jie Tianran out of his mind?” Chu Feng exclaimed.","“Is it really harmful?” Fu Xing asked.","“It greatly shortens a person’s lifespan, and the effects are irreversible. You can think of it as a more potent forbidden medicine. Forbidden medicine causes a backlash, but it will be fine once you get through it. But these pills permanently reduce a person’s lifespan,” Chu Feng replied.","“How much does it reduce a person’s lifespan by?”","“Depends on their talent. A talented person who consumes a huge amount of these pills won’t live more than ten years.”","“Ten years for the talented? What about the untalented?” Fu Xing was horrified.","“It’s hard to say. Some might not last a year. Some might even die while assimilating the pills,” Chu Feng replied.","“Jie Tianran is out of his mind!” Fu Xing stared at the cultivation resources with fearful eyes.","She had hesitated for a long time before giving up on these pills. It was hard to resist the temptation after seeing how quickly other members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion grew after consuming the pills.","“It’s good that you didn’t consume them. Can you give them to me?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course, but what do you want them for? Are you planning to use them for your cultivation? Or are you able to remove the harmful side effects of the pills?” Fu Xing asked. Her impression of Chu Feng was someone who didn’t hesitate to take risks.","“I’ll find a way to expose Jie Tianran’s evil deeds and shatter his reputation,” Chu Feng replied.","“It’s useless. I have been in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion for some time now, and the people there blindly worship him. Jie Tianran just needs to find a random excuse, and those people will buy it without any hesitation.”","“That’s up to them, but I still feel obliged to reveal the truth.”","“You’re right. It’s up to them to decide what to do after hearing the truth. Chu Feng, if my master and the others are willing to join hands with you, I’ll head to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect to inform you. Just you wait! You might be ahead of me now, but I’ll surely catch up with you!”","“I know.” Chu Feng figured that Fu Xing already had a plan in mind, not to mention she was indeed extremely talented.","He parted ways with Fu Xing and reunited with Little Fishy.","The guild leader and the lunatic had been busy obtaining God’s Era’s power fragments. Now that Chu Feng had obtained his qualification, it was time for him to start doing the same as well. He was particularly excited about it because he was in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","While traveling, he took out the power fragment he had extracted from the cultivation ground.","“What peculiar energy.” Little Fishy’s eyes lit up.","“Indeed. It can be used for cultivation, and it might be able to help your clansmen as well,” Chu Feng replied.","“Big brother, is this energy similar to origin energies?” Little Fishy asked.","“It’s not origin energies, but it’s of a similar nature.”","“Doesn’t that mean that big sister can cultivate it?” Little Fishy asked cheerily.","“I think so. Eggy, why don’t you give it a try?”","Chu Feng opened his world spirit gate to transfer the power fragment into his World Spirit Space, but surprisingly, Eggy came out.","Little Fishy made her way up to Eggy and stared unblinkingly at the latter’s nearly perfect face. Her eyes glowed like wonderment. She earnestly admired Eggy’s beauty.","“You’re beautiful too, Yu’er,” Eggy replied with a smile as she reached out to pinch Little Fishy’s cheeks. “It’s good to be young. Your face is so supple.”","“You’re both very beautiful, so stop buttering each other up and get to work,” Chu Feng interjected.","Eggy would have been annoyed under other circumstances, but they did have more important matters to deal with at hand. She raised her hand, and the power fragment flew into her palm. Moments later, she shook her head.","“I can’t cultivate this.”","“You can’t?” Chu Feng felt regretful.","“While this energy resembles origin energies, it ultimately isn’t it. However, it should be useful to Yu’er’s family members,” Eggy said.","“I have examined it earlier. The power fragment can become more potent by refining it with a powerful bloodline. You might be able to cultivate it after I refine it,” Chu Feng said.","“Refinement? I’m skeptical, but we can give it a try,” Eggy replied as she sat down on the floor.","“Yu’er, I am busy steering the bamboo boat, so why don’t you give it a try?” Chu Feng asked as he casually constructed a refinement formation.","The formation could be channeled by both world spiritists and cultivators. Little Fishy tried channeling the formation, but the effects were less than ideal.","“Let me give it a try.” Chu Feng tried to refine the power fragment with his bloodline. Soon, the power fragment began to transform.","“Incredible, big brother. It looks like my bloodline is lacking compared to yours,” Little Fishy said, though she didn’t look disappointed in the least. She was happy for him.","“Yu’er, your bloodline is no weaker than mine. It’s just that my Heavenly Lightning Bloodline’s nine-colored lightning is more suited for refinement,” Chu Feng replied. He turned to Eggy and asked, “Can you cultivate with it now?”","But Eggy shook her head and replied, “It’s still a no.”","Chu Feng sighed regretfully.","He always wanted to get the best things for Eggy, even if it meant putting his life on the line. God’s Era’s power fragment was an extraordinary cultivation resource. It was a pity that she couldn’t use it.","So, after refining the power fragment, he gave it to Little Fishy. “Yu’er, you cultivate first.”"]},{"number":6599,"title":"Chapter 6599: Chapter 6597: Jie Baobao In Danger?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6597: Jie Baobao In Danger?","“Big brother, I’m going to cry out of shame at this rate. You can’t give everything to me. You also need to cultivate as well!” Little Fishy exclaimed.","“Why don’t we each take half then? We’ll do the same for the other power fragments we obtain as well.” Chu Feng sliced the power fragment in half and took one portion.","“Fine.” Little Fishy took the other portion.","Both of them began absorbing the power fragment while making their way to the next realm.","The power fragment in the next realm wasn’t too big, either. It was around two times what they had just obtained. However, Chu Feng chose this as their next destination because it was close by.","What he didn’t know was that there was a familiar face in that realm—Jie Baobao.","Her original name was Jie Bao, but she didn’t like that name, so she changed it to Jie Baobao. She maintained a low profile, but the truth was that she was a prodigy on par with Ling Xiao. She had worked together with Chu Feng in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith and had proven herself to be a credible and reliable person.","Chu Feng had a good impression of her.","Jie Baobao had just come out of closed-door training, and she had surpassed Ling Xiao and reached rank six True Dragon World Spiritist. However, she wasn’t in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s cultivation ground but a discreet area.","Hundreds of other Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists were gathered around her, but they had conflicted looks on their faces. Some looked troubled, but others looked excited as if they had been granted a new lease of life.","“We have obtained the stuff. Let’s wait for Ling Xiao and the others to arrive,” an old woman said. She was a rank seven True Dragon World Spiritist, the strongest one in this group.","“Oh no.” Jie Baobao’s face suddenly darkened.","“What’s wrong?” someone asked.","“I forgot to bring something important with me. I need to make a return trip,” Jie Baobao said.","“You can’t,” the old woman objected. “Elder Ling Kun is gathering everyone to channel the extraction formation to obtain God’s Era’s power fragment. He is bound to notice that so many of us have gone missing with our wealth. If you get discovered now, you won’t be able to come out anymore.”","“Don’t worry, elder. I’ll be fine. I won’t divulge your whereabouts even if I get caught,” Jie Baobao said.","“I’m not worried about you betraying us, Baobao. I’m worried about your safety. The Sacred Mansion is not the same place as it was before. Everyone is tense.","“Besides, there are rumors that you and Ling Xiao are on close terms with Chu Feng. I heard that Elder Ling Kun came here not just for God’s Era’s power fragment but also to investigate you. On top of that, his granddaughter has been jealous of you for a while now, but she has been unable to do anything because of your exceptional talent.","“But the tides have changed. Elder Ling Kun has made a breakthrough to rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist and is highly regarded by the Mansion Master, and his granddaughter is the kind to oppress others. I don’t think it’s safe for you to return now,” the old woman replied.","“I did work with Chu Feng on the Nine Heavens’ Zenith, but only I, Ling Xiao, and Chu Feng know about that. Outsiders can’t possibly know that. The rumors floating in the Sacred Mansion are mere rumors. They don’t have evidence; I have nothing to fear.","“Besides, we are only absent. We are bound to have our own private matters to attend to; they wouldn’t think that we are planning to leave the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Even if they do suspect something, they can’t possibly punish me if I feign ignorance.","“I have to return to retrieve the item. Pardon me, elder.”","Jie Baobao rose into the sky to leave.","A barrier suddenly sealed off the surroundings, blocking Jie Baobao’s path. The old woman was stopping Jie Baobao from leaving.","But Jie Baobao’s spirit power pierced right through the barrier. She might be a rank six True Dragon World Spiritist, but she possessed heaven-defying battle power capable of surmounting a rank. The old woman wasn’t a match for her.","“Forget it, elder. We might be too nervous because we’re feeling guilty for leaving the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Baobao is right. It’s unlikely that anyone will think that we are fleeing from the Sacred Mansion. They are busy extracting the power fragment right now; it’s unlikely that they will notice us,” someone said.","“Let’s hope I’m overthinking it,” the old woman remarked with a sigh.","Jie Boabao returned to the cultivation ground. It was inferior compared to Jie Ranqing’s cultivation ground, but it was larger and could accommodate more people. It was reminiscent of a little country.","However, the tens of millions of world spiritists residing here were making their way into the innermost depths of the cultivation ground to extract God’s Era’s power fragment.","Jie Baobao made her way to the chamber where she had previously been in closed-door training. It was her private chamber, imbued with a formation that only allowed her to enter.","She soon left the chamber holding something with a relieved smile. That was the important item she had forgotten to take.","All of a sudden, she narrowed her eyes.","Several figures had appeared in the sky above her. All of them were at least late True Dragon World Spiritists, and there were even a couple of pinnacle True Dragon World Spiritists.","The one leading the group was a white-haired elder who had reached rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. He was Ling Kun.","He had been at the Undying Starfield, and he had witnessed Chu Feng wreaking havoc there. Later, he returned to the Seven Realms Galaxy together with Jie Tianran after witnessing God’s Era’s power fragments scattering all around the Seven Realms Galaxy.","Jie Tianran tasked him to extract the power fragment here.","“Paying respect to the elders,” Jie Baobao said with a bow.","Ling Kun didn’t respond. His face was livid. With a wave of his hand, he bound Jie Baobao with an invisible rope."]},{"number":6600,"title":"Chapter 6600: Chapter 6598: Abusing Power","paragraphs":["Chapter 6598: Abusing Power","“Elder Ling Kun, what are you doing?” Jie Baobao asked in confusion.","“Jie Baobao, I am doing this for you. You and Ling Xiao are the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion's future. The Sacred Mansion has spared no effort in nurturing you. However, there have been rumors that you are colluding with Chu Feng. For your reputation, it is best that you clarify it in front of everyone.”","Ling Kun pulled Jie Baobao into the sky. Before Jie Baobao could react, she was already brought before a massive golden formation resembling a small city.","The tens of millions of world spiritists residing on this cultivation ground were gathered here. There were people everywhere one looked.","Ling Kun’s arrival with Jie Baobao caught the crowd’s attention.","“I have heard rumors regarding Jie Baobao circulating within the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I have investigated the matter, and it seems like the cause stems from Jie Baobao speaking up for Chu Feng when someone insulted him. Jie Baobao, is that true?” Ling Kun asked.","Jie Baobao didn’t answer.","“Grandfather, she didn’t just speak up for Chu Feng. She even hit me! Look, there’s still her palm print on my face!” a woman rose into the sky and said.","She had a slender figure, but half of her face was swollen like a pig’s head. There was a clear palm print on her cheek. She was Ling Tiantian, Ling Kun’s granddaughter.","“Lord Ling Kun, we can testify to that.”","Several more figures rose into the sky. They were all juniors. Most of them were injured, especially the men.","“We were discussing Chu Feng’s misdeeds with Miss Tiantian when Jie Baobao suddenly appeared out of nowhere and framed us for spreading false rumors. We tried to reason with her, but she attacked us,” one of the juniors said.","“This...”","The accusations sparked intense discussions from the crowd.","Jie Baobao was of a high stature in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, being one of its most talented prodigies, but Chu Feng was a special case. It would be a huge case if she had beaten up her brethren over Chu Feng.","“Jie Baobao, I don’t want you to say that I’m biased. My granddaughter isn’t the only one accusing you now. You should explain yourself,” Ling Kun said.","“Elder Ling Kun, your granddaughter is a jealous woman. She has been oppressing others using your name. Many have suffered under her tyranny, and it looks like she has set her eyes on me now. You must have already chosen to pamper her, considering how you dragged me here to question me in public,” Jie Baobao replied with a seething tone.","While Ling Kun was a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist now, he had been a mere late True Dragon World Spiritist before God’s Era, and he wasn’t close to reaching pinnacle. There were many world spiritists like Ling Kun in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","But true prodigies like Jie Baobao still numbered in the minority. For that reason, she didn’t fear Ling Kun. Besides, Ling Kun was clearly using his power to oppress her right now.","“What? Elder Ling Kun dragged Jie Baobao here?”","Jie Baobao’s words changed the public sentiment. To the crowd, Jie Baobao’s stature was higher than Elder Ling Kun’s.","“I am merely following the rules.” Ling Kun didn’t deny the matter, though he stowed away the invisible ropes he had bound Jie Baobao with. “Jie Baobao, you shouldn’t make unsubstantiated claims. You claim that my granddaughter is oppressing others, but I have heard no such news before. If you have evidence, bring it out.”","“You want evidence? Those who have been bullied by Ling Tiantian, step forth!” Jie Baobao looked at the people who had been oppressed by Ling Tiantian, but those people lowered their heads, not daring to step forward.","“It looks like you don’t have evidence. Jie Baobao, you have to give everyone an explanation right now lest others misunderstand,” Ling Kun said.","“What is there to explain? It didn’t happen. I have nothing to say if you can accuse me of colluding with Chu Feng just by pulling several people out,” Jie Baobao replied.","“What about my granddaughter? Your aura lingers on her face.”","“Your granddaughter deserves to be beaten up.”","“You!” Ling Kun was enraged by Jie Baobao’s arrogance.","Several elders stepped forward and interjected.","“Forget it, Elder Ling Kun. It’s just a fight among the kids. It will pass in due time. There’s no need to dig too deeply into it.”","“Indeed. Isn’t that how we grew up as well? We’re all from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. We shouldn’t be holding grudges against one another.”","They were all speaking up for Jie Baobao.","But their words only caused Ling Tian’s face to further darken.","“You’re disrespecting not just me, Ling Kun, but Lord Mansion Master.” Ling Kun took out a token with a flick of his wrist. The token unleashed a humongous formation that covered the sky. “This is Lord Mansion Master’s Enforcement Token. Standing before the token is equivalent to standing in the presence of Lord Mansion Master.”","The crowd was stunned. Even Jie Baobao was taken aback. She couldn’t believe that someone of Ling Kun’s stature would be granted the Enforcement Token.","But the Enforcement Token’s formation couldn’t be faked. Not only was the token real, but it was clearly inscribed on it that it was bestowed upon Ling Kun.","“I didn’t expect Ling Kun to be so highly regarded by Lord Mansion Master. No wonder Lord Mansion Master entrusted this important task to him.”","“It’s a different era now. Jie Baobao is in trouble.”","The crowd stirred again, but the tides had changed. Those who had sided with Jie Baobao earlier were hoping to get in her good graces, but no one dared to speak up for her anymore.","Those elders who had spoken up for Jie Baobao turned livid. They regretted getting involved. The Enforcement Token showed that Elder Ling Kun was favored by Jie Tianran, and it gave him the authority to kill anyone he deemed guilty.","The future might be important, but it would be for naught if they were to be executed right now.","Ling Kun’s anger subsided upon seeing the crowd’s expression. Power was ever so intoxicating."]}]);
